UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'The outbreak of swine flu that was first detected in Mexico was declared a global epidemic on June 11, 2009. It is the first worldwide epidemic [1] by the World Health Organization in 41 years.\n\nThe heightened alert [2] an emergency meeting with flu experts in Geneva that assembled after a sharp rise in cases in Australia, and rising [3] in Britain, Japan, Chile and elsewhere.\n\nBut the epidemic is "[4]" in severity, according to Margaret Chan, the organization\'s director general, [5] the overwhelming majority of patients experiencing only mild symptoms and a full recovery, often in the [6] of any medical treatment.\n\nThe outbreak came to global [7] in late April 2009, when Mexican authorities noted an unusually large number of hospitalizations and deaths [8] healthy adults. As much of Mexico City shut down at the height of a panic, cases began to [9] in New York City, the southwestern United States and around the world.\n\nIn the United States, new cases seemed to fade [10] warmer weather arrived. But in late September 2009, officials reported there was [11] flu activity in almost every state and that virtually all the [12] tested are the new swine flu, also known as (A) H1N1, not seasonal flu. In the U.S., it has [13] more than one million people, and caused more than 600 deaths and more than 6,000 hospitalizations.\n\nFederal health officials [14] Tamiflu for children from the national stockpile and began [15] orders from the states for the new swine flu vaccine. The new vaccine, which is different from the annual flu vaccine, is [16] ahead of expectations. More than three million doses were to be made available in early October 2009, though most of those [17] doses were of the FluMist nasal spray type, which is not [18] for pregnant women, people over 50 or those with breathing difficulties, heart disease or several other [19]. But it was still possible to vaccinate people in other high-risk groups: health care workers, people [20] infants and healthy young people.' WHERE id = '19086b51-2fc9-5e9e-9532-de29c847cea6'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'I was addressing a small gathering in a suburban Virginia living room — a women\'s group that had invited men to join them. Throughout the evening, one man had been particularly talkative, frequently offering ideas and anecdotes, while his wife sat silently beside him on the couch. Toward the end of the evening, I commented that women frequently complain that their husbands don\'t talk to them. This man quickly nodded in agreement. He gestured toward his wife and said, “She\'s the talker in our family.” The room burst into laughter; the man looked puzzled and hurt. “It\'s true,” he explained. “When I come home from work I have nothing to say. If she didn\'t keep the conversation going, we\'d spend the whole evening in silence.”\n\nThis episode crystallizes the irony that although American men tend to talk more than women in public situations, they often talk less at home. And this pattern is wreaking havoc with marriage.\n\nThe pattern was observed by political scientist Andrew Hacker in the late 1970s. Sociologist Catherine Kohler Riessman reports in her new book Divorce Talk that most of the women she interviewed — but only a few of the men — gave lack of communication as the reason for their divorces. Given the current divorce rate of nearly 50 percent, that amounts to millions of cases in the United States every year — a virtual epidemic of failed conversation.\n\nIn my own research, complaints from women about their husbands most often focused not on tangible inequities such as having given up the chance for a career to accompany a husband to his, or doing far more than their share of daily life-support work like cleaning, cooking and social arrangements. Instead, they focused on communication: “He doesn\'t listen to me.” “He doesn\'t talk to me.” I found, as Hacker observed years before, that most wives want their husbands to be, first and foremost, conversational partners, but few husbands share this expectation of their wives.\n\nIn short, the image that best represents the current crisis is the stereotypical cartoon scene of a man sitting at the breakfast table with a newspaper held up in front of his face, while a woman glares at the back of it, wanting to talk.' WHERE id = 'dd0032cd-49b1-5080-a113-c94645819c15'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'Over the past decade, many companies had perfected the art of creating automatic behaviors — habits — among consumers. These habits have helped companies earn billions of dollars when customers eat snacks or wipe counters almost without thinking, often in response to a carefully designed set of daily cues.\n\n“There are fundamental public health problems, like dirty hands instead of a soap habit, that remain killers only because we can\'t figure out how to change people\'s habits,” said Dr. Curtis, the director of the Hygiene Center at the London School of Hygiene & Tropical Medicine. “We wanted to learn from industry how to create new behaviors that happen automatically.”\n\nThe companies that Dr. Curtis turned to — Procter & Gamble, Colgate-Palmolive and Unilever — had invested hundreds of millions of dollars finding the subtle cues in consumers\' lives that corporations could use to introduce new routines.\n\nIf you look hard enough, you\'ll find that many of the products we use every day — chewing gums, skin moisturizers, disinfecting wipes, air fresheners, water purifiers, health snacks, teeth whiteners, fabric softeners, vitamins — are results of manufactured habits. A century ago, few people regularly brushed their teeth multiple times a day. Today, because of shrewd advertising and public health campaigns, many Americans habitually give their pearly whites a cavity-preventing scrub twice a day, often with Colgate, Crest or one of the other brands.\n\nA few decades ago, many people didn\'t drink water outside of a meal. Then beverage companies started bottling the production of far-off springs, and now office workers unthinkingly sip bottled water all day long. Chewing gum, once bought primarily by adolescent boys, is now featured in commercials as a breath freshener and teeth cleanser for use after a meal. Skin moisturizers are advertised as part of morning beauty rituals, slipped in between hair brushing and putting on makeup.\n\n“Our products succeed when they become part of daily or weekly patterns,” said Carol Berning, a consumer psychologist who recently retired from Procter & Gamble, the company that sold $76 billion of Tide, Crest and other products last year. “Creating positive habits is a huge part of improving our consumers\' lives, and it\'s essential to making new products commercially viable.”\n\nThrough experiments and observation, social scientists like Dr. Berning have learned that there is power in tying certain behaviors to habitual cues through ruthless advertising. As this new science of habit has emerged, controversies have erupted when the tactics have been used to sell questionable beauty creams or unhealthy foods.' WHERE id = 'b2d9b6c3-a8ff-5443-bb21-d8be1d29454b'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'Copying Birds May Save Aircraft Fuel\n\nBoth Boeing and Airbus have trumpeted the efficiency of their newest aircraft, the 787 and A350 respectively. Their clever designs and lightweight composites certainly make a difference. But a group of researchers at Stanford University, led by Ilan Kroo, has suggested that airlines could take a more naturalistic approach to cutting jet-fuel use and it would not require them to buy new aircraft.\n\nThe answer, says Dr. Kroo, lies with birds. Since 1914, scientists have known that birds flying in formation — a V-shape — expend less energy. The air flowing over a bird\'s wings curls upwards behind the wingtips, a phenomenon known as upwash. Other birds flying in the upwash experience reduced drag, and spend less energy propelling themselves. Peter Lissaman, an aeronautics expert who was formerly at Caltech and the University of Southern California, has suggested that a formation of 25 birds might enjoy a range increase of 71%.\n\nWhen applied to aircraft, the principles are not substantially different. Dr. Kroo and his team modeled what would happen if three passenger jets departing from Los Angeles, San Francisco and Las Vegas were to assemble over Utah, assume an inverted V-formation, occasionally change places so all could have a turn in the most favourable positions, and proceed to London. They found that the aircraft consumed as much as 15% less fuel (coupled with a reduction in carbon-dioxide output). Nitrogen-oxide emissions during the cruising portions of the flight fell by around a quarter.\n\nThere are, of course, knots to be worked out. One consideration is safety, or at least the perception of it. Would passengers feel comfortable travelling in companion? Dr. Kroo points out that the aircraft could be separated by several nautical miles, and would not be in the intimate groupings favoured by display teams like the Red Arrows. A passenger peering out of the window might not even see the other planes. Whether the separation distances involved would satisfy air-traffic-control regulations is another matter, although a working group at the International Civil Aviation Organisation has included the possibility of formation flying in a blueprint for new operational guidelines.\n\nIt remains to be seen how weather conditions affect the air flows that make formation flight more efficient. In zones of increased turbulence, the planes\' wakes will decay more quickly and the effect will diminish. Dr. Kroo says this is one of the areas his team will investigate further. It might also be hard for airlines to co-ordinate the departure times and destinations of passenger aircraft in a way that would allow them to gain from formation flight. Cargo aircraft, in contrast, might be easier to reschedule, as might routine military flights.\n\nAs it happens, America\'s armed forces are on the case already. Earlier this year the country\'s Defence Advanced Research Projects Agency announced plans to pay Boeing to investigate formation flight, though the programme has yet to begin. There are reports that some military aircraft flew in formation when they were low on fuel during the Second World War, but Dr. Lissaman says they are unsubstantiated. “My father was an RAF pilot and my cousin the skipper of a Lancaster lost over Berlin,” he adds. So he should know.' WHERE id = 'fe06d440-a01e-535a-a208-7a3d9b23f27e'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [7] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "reality", "content": "reality"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "phenomenon", "content": "phenomenon"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "concept", "content": "concept"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "notice", "content": "notice"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］固定搭配与上下文语境。\n［解题思路］come to global notice 为核心固定搭配，意为“引起全球关注、进入全球公众视野”。4 月下旬墨西哥出现大量严重住院及死亡病例并迅速引起世界关注，使此次疫情成为焦点，故选［D］。\n［错项排除］［A］reality（现实，come to reality 意为“成为现实”而非“引起关注”）、［B］phenomenon（现象）、［C］concept（概念）均无法与 come to global... 构成习惯搭配以传达进入大众舆论视野之意。' WHERE id = '424d3727-04b0-583d-92eb-618f6d71cdd6'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [8] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "over", "content": "over"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "for", "content": "for"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "among", "content": "among"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "to", "content": "to"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］方位与范围介词辨析。\n［解题思路］空格前后分别为“重症住院及死亡病例”和“原本健康的成年人群（healthy adults）”。among 强调在特定同类群体的成员之间，准确表达病毒突破免疫防线、竟在体质原本强健的青壮年人群之中引发大量重症乃至死亡病例的反常疫情态势，故选［C］。\n［错项排除］［A］over（在……上方/超越）、［B］for（对于、为了）与［D］to（面向、对于）均无法准确表示流行病病例具体“发生在某一人群范围内部”的归属关系。' WHERE id = 'd06c9c1f-791e-5b73-b28d-34946e7a5d37'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [9] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "stay up", "content": "stay up"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "crop up", "content": "crop up"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "fill up", "content": "fill up"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "cover up", "content": "cover up"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］动词短语辨析与疫情扩散语境。\n［解题思路］上文提及墨西哥城已陷入恐慌并关闭公共场所，空格句紧接着指出新病例开始在纽约市、美国西南部乃至全球各地接连“[9]”。crop up 为高频短语，意为“突然出现、意外冒出”，生动刻画疫情散发病例在多点零星突现的紧迫态势，故选［B］。\n［错项排除］［A］stay up（熬夜、不睡觉；坚持不倒）、［C］fill up（填满、充盈）以及［D］cover up（掩盖真相、隐瞒）均严重偏离病毒病例相继涌现的语境。' WHERE id = 'b653b64a-7135-5cc1-a803-97203673bacb'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [13] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "imparted", "content": "imparted"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "immersed", "content": "immersed"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "injected", "content": "injected"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "infected", "content": "infected"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］动词词义与动宾语义搭配。\n［解题思路］空格后接宾语 more than one million people（逾百万民众），后半句并列呈现 and caused more than 600 deaths（并导致逾 600 人死亡）。infect 在医学传染语境中专指“感染、传染（某人）”，指该新型流感病毒已在美国感染超百万人，故选［D］。\n［错项排除］［A］imparted（传授知识、赋予品质）、［B］immersed（将……浸泡于或专心沉浸于）与［C］injected（注射药物或注入液体）均无法构成“病毒波及人群引发感染”的合理主谓宾逻辑。' WHERE id = '4e6fbd5c-84c0-5151-bba2-afa654dbbb78'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [14] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "released", "content": "released"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "relayed", "content": "relayed"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "relieved", "content": "relieved"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "remained", "content": "remained"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］动词词义辨析与应急行政调配语境。\n［解题思路］全句指出：联邦卫生官员从国家应急储备库（national emergency stockpiles）中为儿童专门“[14]”了一大批抗病毒药物达菲（Tamiflu）。release 在此取“公开投放、紧急调拨发放”之意，准确契合政府解封战备物资流向医院药房的举措，故选［A］。\n［错项排除］［B］relayed（转播信号、传递口信）、［C］relieved（缓解疼痛、解救负担）与［D］remained（停留、保持，不及物）均无法与“从国家库存中调拨药物”匹配。' WHERE id = '2b7a809c-6be6-5386-96ff-3211ece1935b'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'In the following part immediately after this text, the author will most probably focus on ________.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "a vivid account of the new book Divorce Talk", "content": "a vivid account of the new book Divorce Talk"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "a detailed description of the stereotypical cartoon", "content": "a detailed description of the stereotypical cartoon"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "other possible reasons for a high divorce rate in the U.S.", "content": "other possible reasons for a high divorce rate in the U.S."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "a brief introduction to the political scientist Andrew Hacker", "content": "a brief introduction to the political scientist Andrew Hacker"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［精准定位］末段独句成段，勾勒了一幅男人坐在早餐桌旁把报纸举在脸前、女人怒视报纸背面渴望交谈的典型漫画场景，作为前文“男女沟通模式差异”的收束与下段伏笔。\n［命题解密］根据篇章的一致性与连贯性原则，作者既然在末段结尾专门引出“stereotypical cartoon scene”这一具体意象，紧接着的段落最有可能围绕该漫画场景展开进一步刻画，故［B］a detailed description of the stereotypical cartoon 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］《离婚谈》仅在第三段提及，后文未再延续该书；［C］探讨高离婚率的其他原因虽与第三段数据相关，但末段焦点已转至夫妻日常沟通漫画，下文不会突兀跳回离婚率成因；［D］政治学者 Andrew Hacker 仅作为佐证人物在第三、四段出现，并非全文论述焦点。\n［技巧总结］段落衔接预测题的核心在于紧盯末段末尾的新引入意象或话题焦点，优先选择与末段直接顺承且不偏离全文主旨的选项。' WHERE id = '5b884675-9939-5687-9571-181f35115160'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'It has been documented that during World War II, America\'s armed forces once tried formation flight to save fuel.', options = E'[{"key": "T", "value": "T", "text": "True", "content": "True"}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "False", "content": "False"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'F', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干关键词 documented、World War II 及 America\'s armed forces 定位至文章最后一段后半部分：There are reports that some military aircraft flew in formation when they were low on fuel during the Second World War, but Dr. Lissaman says they are unsubstantiated.（有报道称二战期间一些军用飞机在燃油不足时曾编队飞行，但利萨曼博士表示这些说法并未得到证实。）\n［命题解密］原文明确用 reports（传闻/报道）并强调 Dr. Lissaman says they are unsubstantiated（未经证实，缺乏事实依据）。题干却声称“It has been documented（已有文献/档案明确记载证实）”，与原文“未经证实”完全相悖，故判断为［False］。' WHERE id = 'd9861d51-6bbb-5d02-941f-af02b694ff91'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'The Internet affords anonymity to its users, a blessing to privacy and freedom of speech. But that very anonymity is also behind the explosion of cyber-crime that has [1] across the Web.\n\nCan privacy be preserved [2] bringing safety and security to a world that seems increasingly [3]?\n\nLast month, Howard Schmidt, the nation\'s cyber-czar, offered the federal government a [4] to make the Web a safer place — a "voluntary trusted identity" system that would be the high-tech [5] of a physical key, a fingerprint and a photo ID card, all rolled [6] one. The system might use a smart identity card, or a digital credential [7] to a specific computer, and would authenticate users at a range of online services.\n\nThe idea is to [8] a federation of private online identity systems. Users could [9] which system to join, and only registered users whose identities have been authenticated could navigate those systems. The approach contrasts with one that would require an Internet driver\'s license [10] by the government.\n\nGoogle and Microsoft are among companies that already have these "single sign-on" systems that make it possible for users to [11] just once but use many different services.\n\n[12], the approach would create a "walled garden" in cyberspace, with safe "neighborhoods" and bright "streetlights" to establish a sense of a [13] community.\n\nMr. Schmidt described it as a "voluntary ecosystem" in which "individuals and organizations can complete online transactions with [14], trusting the identities of each other and the identities of the infrastructure [15] which the transaction runs."\n\nStill, the administration\'s plan has [16] privacy rights activists. Some applaud the approach; others are concerned. It seems clear that such a scheme is an initiative push toward what would [17] be a compulsory Internet "driver\'s license" mentality.\n\nThe plan has also been greeted with [18] by some computer security experts, who worry that the "voluntary ecosystem" envisioned by Mr. Schmidt would still leave much of the Internet [19]. They argue that all Internet users should be [20] to register and identify themselves, in the same way that drivers must be licensed to drive on public roads.' WHERE id = 'b54de55f-5c38-51b9-b88a-3bf1e0ebc62f'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'Ruth Simmons joined Goldman Sachs\'s board as an outside director in January 2000; a year later she became president of Brown University. For the rest of the decade she apparently managed both roles without attracting much criticism. But by the end of 2009 Ms. Simmons was under fire for having sat on Goldman\'s compensation committee; how could she have let those enormous bonus payouts pass unremarked? By February the next year Ms. Simmons had left the board. The position was just taking up too much time, she said.\n\nOutside directors are supposed to serve as helpful, yet less biased, advisers on a firm\'s board. Having made their wealth and their reputations elsewhere, they presumably have enough independence to disagree with the chief executive\'s proposals. If the sky, and the share price, is falling, outside directors should be able to give advice based on having weathered their own crises.\n\nThe researchers from Ohio University used a database that covered more than 10,000 firms and more than 64,000 different directors between 1989 and 2004. Then they simply checked which directors stayed from one proxy statement to the next. The most likely reason for departing a board was age, so the researchers concentrated on those "surprise" disappearances by directors under the age of 70. They found that after a surprise departure, the probability that the company will subsequently have to restate earnings increases by nearly 20%. The likelihood of being named in a federal class-action lawsuit also increases, and the stock is likely to perform worse. The effect tended to be larger for larger firms. Although a correlation between them leaving and subsequent bad performance at the firm is suggestive, it does not mean that such directors are always jumping off a sinking ship. Often they "trade up," leaving riskier, smaller firms for larger and more stable firms.\n\nBut the researchers believe that outside directors have an easier time of avoiding a blow to their reputations if they leave a firm before bad news breaks, even if a review of history shows they were on the board at the time any wrongdoing occurred. Firms who want to keep their outside directors through tough times may have to create incentives. Otherwise outside directors will follow the example of Ms. Simmons, once again very popular on campus.' WHERE id = '337ffcfc-8821-54c5-b187-c65066c983b8'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'We tend to think of the decades immediately following World War II as a time of prosperity and growth, with soldiers returning home by the millions, going off to college on the G. I. Bill and lining up at the marriage bureaus.\n\nBut when it came to their houses, it was a time of common sense and a belief that less could truly be more. During the Depression and the war, Americans had learned to live with less, and that restraint, in combination with the postwar confidence in the future, made small, efficient housing positively stylish.\n\nEconomic condition was only a stimulus for the trend toward efficient living. The phrase "less is more" was actually first popularized by a German, the architect Ludwig Mies van der Rohe, who like other people associated with the Bauhaus, a school of design, emigrated to the United States before World War II and took up posts at American architecture schools. These designers came to exert enormous influence on the course of American architecture, but none more so than Mies.\n\nMies\'s signature phrase means that less decoration, properly organized, has more impact than a lot. Elegance, he believed, did not derive from abundance. Like other modern architects, he employed metal, glass and laminated wood — materials that we take for granted today but that in the 1940s symbolized the future. Mies\'s sophisticated presentation masked the fact that the spaces he designed were small and efficient, rather than big and often empty.\n\nThe apartments in the elegant towers Mies built on Chicago\'s Lake Shore Drive, for example, were smaller — two-bedroom units under 1,000 square feet — than those in their older neighbors along the city\'s Gold Coast. But they were popular because of their airy glass walls, the views they afforded and the elegance of the buildings\' details and proportions, the architectural equivalent of the abstract art so popular at the time.\n\nThe trend toward "less" was not entirely foreign. In the 1930s Frank Lloyd Wright started building more modest and efficient houses — usually around 1,200 square feet — than the spreading two-story ones he had designed in the 1890s and the early 20th century.\n\nThe "Case Study Houses" commissioned from talented modern architects by California Arts & Architecture magazine between 1945 and 1962 were yet another homegrown influence on the "less is more" trend. Aesthetic effect came from the landscape, new materials and forthright detailing. In his Case Study House, Ralph Rapson may have mispredicted just how the mechanical revolution would impact everyday life — few American families acquired helicopters, though most eventually got clothes dryers — but his belief that self-sufficiency was both desirable and inevitable was widely shared.' WHERE id = 'cb4476ba-09e6-5bbf-b904-9b83edf5bb4f'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'Will the European Union make it? The question would have sounded strange not long ago. Now even the project\'s greatest cheerleaders talk of a continent facing a "Bermuda triangle" of debt, population decline and lower growth.\n\nAs well as those chronic problems, the EU faces an acute crisis in its economic core, the 16 countries that use the single currency. Markets have lost faith that the euro zone\'s economies, weaker or stronger, will one day converge thanks to the discipline of sharing a single currency, which denies uncompetitive members the quick fix of devaluation.\n\nYet the debate about how to save Europe\'s single currency from disintegration is stuck. It is stuck because the euro zone\'s dominant powers, France and Germany, agree on the need for greater harmonisation within the euro zone, but disagree about what to harmonise.\n\nGermany thinks the euro must be saved by stricter rules on borrowing, spending and competitiveness, backed by quasi-automatic sanctions for governments that do not obey. These might include threats to freeze EU funds for poorer regions and EU mega-projects, and even the suspension of a country\'s voting rights in EU ministerial councils. It insists that economic co-ordination should involve all 27 members of the EU club, among whom there is a small majority for free-market liberalism and economic rigour; in the inner core alone, Germany fears, a small majority favour French interference.\n\nA "southern" camp headed by France wants something different: "European economic government" within an inner core of euro-zone members. Translated, that means politicians intervening in monetary policy and a system of redistribution from richer to poorer members, via cheaper borrowing for governments through common Eurobonds or complete fiscal transfers. Finally, figures close to the French government have murmured, euro-zone members should agree to some fiscal and social harmonisation: e.g., curbing competition in corporate-tax rates or labour costs.\n\nIt is too soon to write off the EU. It remains the world\'s largest trading block. At its best, the European project is remarkably liberal: built around a single market of 27 rich and poor countries, its internal borders are far more open to goods, capital and labour than any comparable trading area. It is an ambitious attempt to blunt the sharpest edges of globalisation, and make capitalism benign.' WHERE id = 'd3856130-805e-5b49-b990-d78b02d3300f'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'Leading doctors today weigh in on the debate over the government\'s role in promoting public health by demanding that ministers impose "fat taxes" on unhealthy food and introduce cigarette-style warnings to children about the dangers of a poor diet.\n\nThe demands follow comments made last week by the health secretary, Andrew Lansley, who insisted the government could not force people to make healthy choices and promised to free businesses from public health regulations.\n\nBut senior medical figures want to stop fast-food outlets opening near schools, restrict advertising of products high in fat, salt or sugar, and limit sponsorship of sports events by fast-food producers such as McDonald\'s.\n\nThey argue that government action is necessary to curb Britain\'s addiction to unhealthy food and help halt spiraling rates of obesity, diabetes and heart disease. Professor Terence Stephenson, president of the Royal College of Paediatrics and Child Health, said that the consumption of unhealthy food should be seen to be just as damaging as smoking or excessive drinking.\n\n"Thirty years ago, it would have been inconceivable to have imagined a ban on smoking in the workplace or in pubs, and yet that is what we have now. Are we willing to be just as courageous in respect of obesity? I would suggest that we should be," said the leader of the UK\'s children\'s doctors.\n\nLansley has alarmed health campaigners by suggesting he wants industry rather than government to take the lead. He said that manufacturers of crisps and candies could play a central role in the Change4Life campaign, the centrepiece of government efforts to boost healthy eating and fitness. He has also criticised the celebrity chef Jamie Oliver\'s high-profile attempt to improve school lunches in England as an example of how "lecturing" people was not the best way to change their behaviour.\n\nStephenson suggested potential restrictions could include banning TV advertisements for foods high in fat, salt or sugar before 9 pm and limiting them on billboards or in cinemas. "If we were really bold, we might even begin to think of high-calorie fast food in the same way as cigarettes — by setting strict limits on advertising, product placement and sponsorship of sports events," he said.\n\nSuch a move could affect firms such as McDonald\'s, which sponsors the youth coaching scheme run by the Football Association. Fast-food chains should also stop offering "inducements" such as toys, cute animals and mobile phone credit to lure young customers, Stephenson said.\n\nProfessor Dinesh Bhugra, president of the Royal College of Psychiatrists, said: "If children are taught about the impact that food has on their growth, and that some things can harm, at least information is available up front."\n\nHe also urged councils to impose "fast-food-free zones" around schools and hospitals — areas within which takeaways cannot open.\n\nA Department of Health spokesperson said: "We need to create a new vision for public health where all of society works together to get healthy and live longer. This includes creating a new \'responsibility deal\' with business, built on social responsibility, not state regulation. Later this year, we will publish a white paper setting out exactly how we will achieve this."\n\nThe food industry will be alarmed that such senior doctors back such radical moves, especially the call to use some of the tough tactics that have been deployed against smoking over the last decade.' WHERE id = '517dfc17-31a9-52c5-9494-6876dc844578'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [1] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "swept", "content": "swept"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "skipped", "content": "skipped"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "walked", "content": "walked"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "ridden", "content": "ridden"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义 + 常识 + 固定搭配。\n［解题思路］首段先指出互联网匿名制有利于保护隐私和言论自由，第二句转折指出“但恰恰是这种匿名制导致了席卷互联网的网络犯罪激增”。sweep across 意为“席卷，横扫”，“has swept across the Web”既与前文 explosion（激增）相呼应，又凸显网络犯罪传播之广、影响之大，故［A］正确。\n［错项排除］［B］skipped（蹦跳着穿过）；［C］walked（步行穿过）；［D］ridden（乘车或骑马穿过）。三者虽可与表示实体的网（如蜘蛛网）搭配，但无法与虚拟的互联网（the Web）及抽象主语 cyber-crime 构成“主体—动作”逻辑，故排除。' WHERE id = '627af5e4-bb00-5a59-adc3-69349e681bf6'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [2] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "for", "content": "for"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "within", "content": "within"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "while", "content": "while"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "though", "content": "though"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内逻辑关系 + 过渡段承上启下功能。\n［解题思路］第二段（独句过渡段）提出疑问：能否在保护隐私的同时，给似乎越来越不受法律约束的互联网世界带来安全感？此处“privacy be preserved”与“bringing safety and security to a world”分别对应首段匿名制的两面，需要表示“同时，兼顾”的连词衔接。while 可引导时间/对比状语从句（从句主语与主句一致时可省略主语与 be 动词），体现“保护隐私与保障安全并存”，故［C］正确。\n［错项排除］［A］for 表目的或原因，但隐私与安全属于并存诉求，并非“方法—目的”或“果—因”关系；［B］within 后应接名词，不能直接衔接分词短语 bringing；［D］though 表让步，“尽管带来安全感，隐私能否被保护”逻辑不通。' WHERE id = 'f5d1f29a-331f-5fe9-8be6-c67d8c9cab45'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [3] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "careless", "content": "careless"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "lawless", "content": "lawless"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "pointless", "content": "pointless"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "helpless", "content": "helpless"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义 + 上下文呼应。\n［解题思路］空格位于定语从句“that seems increasingly [3]”中修饰 a world（指互联网世界）。结合句中“带来安全感（bringing safety and security）”及首段“网络犯罪激增、席卷互联网”，可知目前的互联网世界缺乏法制与安全保障。lawless 意为“无法无天的，不受法律约束的”，精准概括当前网络世界的混乱与危险，故［B］正确。\n［错项排除］［A］careless（粗心的，疏忽的），不能用于修饰“网络世界”本身；［C］pointless（无意义的，无目标的）与［D］helpless（无助的，无望的）均与后文积极寻求安全解决方案的基调不符，且偏离“缺乏法律与安全秩序”的语境。' WHERE id = 'd8f553c9-3b5d-541c-876f-0ff2810d0e45'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [4] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "reason", "content": "reason"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "reminder", "content": "reminder"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "compromise", "content": "compromise"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "proposal", "content": "proposal"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义 + 上下文逻辑。\n［解题思路］空格句指出，上月美国国家网络安全顾问霍华德·施密特向联邦政府提交了一项旨在让网络更安全的[4]——即建立“自愿的可信身份”系统。由 offer sb. sth. 结构及破折号后的同位语内容可知，这是针对网络安全的正式“提议，提案”（proposal），故［D］正确。\n［错项排除］［A］reason（理由，原因），不能以具体系统方案作同位语；［B］reminder（提醒物），不符合向政府提交具体制度方案的语境；［C］compromise（妥协，折中方案），文中并未提及这是多方退让后的折中产物，下文完全围绕该方案的功能与价值展开。' WHERE id = '00b2b92e-ef12-52bd-9218-fbe3ae1c9911'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [5] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "information", "content": "information"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "interference", "content": "interference"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "entertainment", "content": "entertainment"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "equivalent", "content": "equivalent"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义 + 比喻对应。\n［解题思路］定语从句指出，“自愿的可信身份”系统将是实物钥匙、指纹和带照片身份证的高科技[5]。“实物钥匙、指纹、身份证”均是线下验证身份的工具，因此线上虚拟的身份系统与它们在功能上属于“等同物，等效替代品”（equivalent），故［D］正确。\n［错项排除］［A］information（信息）与［C］entertainment（娱乐）均无法概括“钥匙、指纹、身份证”的身份认证功能；［B］interference（干涉，干扰）带有消极阻碍含义，与“提升网络安全”相悖。' WHERE id = 'b5e6a348-d78d-5553-a2f8-3dca3a1a8eb6'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [6] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "by", "content": "by"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "into", "content": "into"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "from", "content": "from"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "over", "content": "over"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义 + 固定搭配。\n［解题思路］逗号后的分词短语“all rolled [6] one”补充说明前文的“实物钥匙、指纹和带照片身份证”与该系统之间的关系。all rolled into one 为固定习语，意为“把多种特性集于一身，融为一体”，强调该高科技系统集多种线下验证功能于一体，故［B］正确。\n［错项排除］［A］by 表被动施动者；［C］from 表来源；［D］over 表在……上方或翻越。三者均不能与 rolled...one 构成“融为一体”的惯用表达，代入后逻辑均不通。' WHERE id = '10f65b97-e299-5bb4-a971-57bbc376e37d'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [7] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "linked", "content": "linked"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "directed", "content": "directed"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "chained", "content": "chained"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "compared", "content": "compared"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义 + 固定搭配。\n［解题思路］句子指出该系统可使用智能身份证，或[7]到特定计算机的数字证书，在各类在线服务中验证用户身份。只有当数字证书与特定计算机“连接、绑定”时才能发挥验证作用。linked to 意为“与……相连/关联”，符合技术常识与上下文，故［A］正确。\n［错项排除］［B］directed to（指向，对准），无法体现证书与计算机的绑定；［C］chained to 含“被束缚、难以脱身”的消极语义，不符语境；［D］compared to（与……相比），“证书”与“计算机”并非同类可比对象。' WHERE id = '94262dde-9cbd-526b-b168-77cc99f5dee0'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [8] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "dismiss", "content": "dismiss"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "discover", "content": "discover"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "create", "content": "create"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "improve", "content": "improve"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义 + 动词辨析。\n［解题思路］本句承接上段提交的新提案，进一步阐释该系统的构建理念：其想法是[8]一个私人在线身份系统联盟（a federation of private online identity systems）。由于该系统是针对网络安全问题提出的新方案，应表示“创建，建立”（create），引出下文用户的操作流程，故［C］正确。\n［错项排除］［A］dismiss（摒弃，不予考虑）与构想新系统的态度相反；［B］discover（发现已存在之物）与新提案尚待构建的属性不符；［D］improve（改善已有事物）同样不符合首次提出新系统的语境。' WHERE id = '2caf681a-fb5c-5dc1-bff0-416b2c08ec9a'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [9] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "recall", "content": "recall"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "suggest", "content": "suggest"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "select", "content": "select"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "realize", "content": "realize"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义 + 动作逻辑。\n［解题思路］前句说明要创建由多个私人在线身份系统组成的“联盟”，本句接着说明操作流程：用户可以[9]要加入哪一个系统，并且只有身份经过验证的注册用户才能访问这些系统。既然存在多个并行系统，用户自然拥有自主“选择，挑选”（select）的权利，故［C］正确。\n［错项排除］［A］recall（回忆，记起），加入新系统并非过去发生的事；［B］suggest（建议），用户是系统使用者，此处决定权在于挑选而非提议；［D］realize（意识到），前文未给出供认知发现的前提信息。' WHERE id = 'e11921cc-e636-5ffc-89ea-9a171c6b5a4d'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [10] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "released", "content": "released"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "issued", "content": "issued"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "distributed", "content": "distributed"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "delivered", "content": "delivered"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义 + 常识 + 动宾搭配。\n［解题思路］本句将该新方案与“需要由政府[10]网络驾照（即网络通行证）”的方案进行对比。在英语中，官方机构正式签发、颁发证件（passports / visas / licenses）的标准动词为 issue，此处过去分词 issued 作后置定语，故［B］正确。\n［错项排除］［A］released（发布消息、释放）；［C］distributed（分发物品给大众，如赈灾物资）；［D］delivered（投递信件包裹或发表演讲）。三者均不与 official license 构成“签发证件”的标准搭配。' WHERE id = 'dcc0ec6b-9c8b-5cce-842f-51a2b1f0d014'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [11] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "carry on", "content": "carry on"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "linger on", "content": "linger on"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "set in", "content": "set in"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "log in", "content": "log in"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义 + 固定短语辨析。\n［解题思路］句中引号提示的“single sign-on” systems（单点登录系统）是解答关键：谷歌、微软等公司已拥有这类系统，使用户只需[11]一次就能使用多种不同服务。“log in”为计算机专用词组，意为“登录，登入（系统）”，与 single sign-on 形成直接语义复现，故［D］正确。\n［错项排除］［A］carry on（继续进行）和［B］linger on（逗留，继续存留）均表示动作持续，与 just once（仅一次）矛盾；［C］set in（坏事开始并持续）无“登录系统”之意。' WHERE id = 'abbec421-daed-5dde-8735-9faf327fcc9d'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [12] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "In vain", "content": "In vain"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "In effect", "content": "In effect"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "In return", "content": "In return"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "In contrast", "content": "In contrast"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］段间逻辑关系 + 副词短语辨析。\n［解题思路］第五段说明系统可“单点登录”，第六段紧接着用比喻揭示其效果：[12]，这种方式将在网络空间中创建一个“围墙花园”，用安全的“街区”和明亮的“路灯”营造安全感。前后段属于对同一方案功能的递进阐释与实质总结，In effect（实际上，事实上）恰能引出其实质作用，故［B］正确。\n［错项排除］［A］In vain（徒劳地）含负面色彩，与建立安全环境相悖；［C］In return（作为回报）强调等价交换，两段间不存在交换关系；［D］In contrast（相比之下）表对比，但第六段与第五段谈论的是同一个系统（the approach）。' WHERE id = 'b430e7ef-5f58-5909-85a6-d762c0ea5c8a'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [13] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "trusted", "content": "trusted"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "modernized", "content": "modernized"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "thriving", "content": "thriving"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "competing", "content": "competing"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义 + 主旨呼应。\n［解题思路］第六段用“围墙花园（walled garden）”“安全街区（safe neighborhoods）”“明亮路灯（bright streetlights）”构建安全可靠的隐喻场景，目的在于营造一种[13]社区感。trusted（可信的，可靠的）不仅契合该隐喻，也与第三段“voluntary trusted identity”形成词汇复现，故［A］正确。\n［错项排除］［B］modernized（现代化的）、［C］thriving（繁荣兴旺的）、［D］competing（相互竞争的）虽可修饰 community，但均偏离了全文围绕“网络信任与安全”的核心语境。' WHERE id = '9008e374-6d0c-53de-844b-cbe71135f365'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [14] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "caution", "content": "caution"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "delight", "content": "delight"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "confidence", "content": "confidence"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "patience", "content": "patience"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义 + 上下文逻辑。\n［解题思路］第七段引述施密特的描述：在这个“自发生态系统”中，个人和组织能够[14]地完成在线交易，彼此信任对方的身份以及交易运行平台的身份。由后文伴随状语“trusting the identities...”可知，这种信任机制让交易双方得以“满怀信任地、放心地”（with confidence）完成交易，故［C］正确。\n［错项排除］［A］caution（谨慎小心）意味着对系统安全仍有戒心，与“trusting”矛盾；［B］delight（高兴）偏离“信任与安全”主线；［D］patience（耐心）暗示流程繁琐耗时，文中并无体现。' WHERE id = '07c878af-cf6d-5686-9863-f04c5ea71f58'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [15] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "on", "content": "on"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "after", "content": "after"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "beyond", "content": "beyond"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "across", "content": "across"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义 + 介词搭配。\n［解题思路］定语从句“[15] which the transaction runs”修饰 the infrastructure（此处指网络基础设施/平台），还原语序为“the transaction runs [15] the infrastructure”。英语中表示交易、程序“在某平台/系统上运行”，固定搭配为 run on，故［A］正确。\n［错项排除］［B］run after（追逐）；［C］run beyond（超越，脱离），交易脱离平台无法体现平台安全；［D］run across（偶然遇见，跑过），均不符合“交易在基础设施上运行”的语义。' WHERE id = '17cf8709-d8d3-5195-b569-19dcfdf5a348'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [16] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "divided", "content": "divided"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "disappointed", "content": "disappointed"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "protected", "content": "protected"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "united", "content": "united"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义 + 动词辨析。\n［解题思路］第八段开头 Still（尽管如此）笔锋一转，由前文介绍系统优势转向引发的争议。紧接着下句指出“Some applaud the approach; others are concerned”（有人赞同，有人担忧）。可见该计划在隐私权活跃分子中“造成了意见分歧”，divided（使产生分歧）恰能概括后句两极反应，故［A］正确。\n［错项排除］［B］disappointed（使失望）仅能覆盖担忧者，无法涵盖赞同者（applaud）；［C］protected（保护）脱离讨论主题；［D］united（使团结）与“有人赞同、有人担忧”的分歧现状完全相反。' WHERE id = 'ec1a7d04-af7f-5ca9-b22b-9f7dfb758515'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [17] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "frequently", "content": "frequently"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "incidentally", "content": "incidentally"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "occasionally", "content": "occasionally"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "eventually", "content": "eventually"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义 + 逻辑呼应。\n［解题思路］句中“an initiative push（最初的推动）”与后文“a compulsory Internet \'driver\'s license\' mentality（强制性的网络通行证模式）”构成“起点—终点”的演变链条，说明隐私权活跃分子担忧该计划“最终、归根结底”（eventually）会滑向强制性网络驾照制度，故［D］正确。\n［错项排除］［A］frequently（频繁地）、［B］incidentally（偶然地，附带地）、［C］occasionally（偶尔地）均描述动作频率或偶发性，既无法与 initiative 构成演进呼应，也不符合对尚未全面推行的政府计划的趋势预测。' WHERE id = 'cc016d5f-f8dc-514b-841d-b6153297eb1e'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [18] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "skepticism", "content": "skepticism"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "tolerance", "content": "tolerance"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "indifference", "content": "indifference"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "enthusiasm", "content": "enthusiasm"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］段间并列关系 + 句内语义。\n［解题思路］第九段开头 also 提示与第八段形成并列，继续阐述另一群体对政府计划的负面反应：该计划也受到一些计算机安全专家的[18]，他们担心（worry）该系统仍会使互联网大部分区域处于危险之中。由 worry 可知专家们持“怀疑、质疑”（skepticism）态度，故［A］正确。\n［错项排除］［B］tolerance（容忍，虽有不满但仍接受）；［C］indifference（漠不关心）与 worry 所体现的关切相悖；［D］enthusiasm（热情支持）属于积极态度，与专家们的担忧正相反。' WHERE id = '733e1cb8-82c9-544e-bf6e-3d5e7ec61bbc'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [19] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "manageable", "content": "manageable"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "defendable", "content": "defendable"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "vulnerable", "content": "vulnerable"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "invisible", "content": "invisible"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义 + 情感色彩一致。\n［解题思路］安全专家担心（worry）施密特设想的“自发生态系统”仍然（still）会使大部分互联网处于[19]的状态。“still”呼应首段网络犯罪猖獗的现状，因此此处应填入消极词，表示“易受攻击的，脆弱的”（vulnerable），故［C］正确。\n［错项排除］［A］manageable（可管理的）与［B］defendable（可防御的）均为正面评价，与安全专家的担忧态度冲突；［D］invisible（无形的）虽符合互联网物理属性，但并非专家担心的安全隐患。' WHERE id = 'd8a68d21-ed48-5ed5-bc31-7907e104482c'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [20] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "invited", "content": "invited"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "appointed", "content": "appointed"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "allowed", "content": "allowed"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "forced", "content": "forced"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义 + 类比推理。\n［解题思路］末句通过“in the same way that drivers must be licensed...”进行类比：既然司机“必须（must）”考取驾照才能上路，那么这些持质疑态度的安全专家就主张所有互联网用户都应该被[20]注册并验证身份。forced（被强制，被迫）与 must 语义一致，体现强制性监管，故［D］正确。\n［错项排除］［A］invited（被邀请）与［C］allowed（被允许）均不具备强制力；［B］appointed（被委任，指派担任职务），对象通常是特定人员而非全体网民。' WHERE id = '83c96901-b8c1-5423-8965-422b29bd69a4'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to Paragraph 1, Ms. Simmons was criticized for', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "gaining excessive profits", "content": "gaining excessive profits"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "failing to fulfill her duty", "content": "failing to fulfill her duty"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "refusing to make compromises", "content": "refusing to make compromises"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "leaving the board in tough times", "content": "leaving the board in tough times"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干关键词 Paragraph 1、Ms. Simmons 及 criticized 定位至第一段第三句。\n［命题解密］该句先以“was under fire for having sat on Goldman\'s compensation committee”点明西蒙斯在高盛薪酬委员会任职期间遭受猛烈抨击，随后分号后的反问句“how could she have let those enormous bonus payouts pass unremarked?”点破批评实质：她本应监督高管薪酬，却放任巨额奖金支出毫无察觉地通过，即“未能履行自身职责（failing to fulfill her duty）”，故［B］正确。\n［错项排除］［A］“gaining excessive profits”将“放任高盛发放巨额奖金”偷换为“她自己获取超额收益”；［C］“refusing to make compromises”是对“let...pass unremarked”的望文生义；［D］“leaving the board in tough times”因果倒置，离开董事会是遭受抨击后的结果而非受批评的原因。' WHERE id = '15193817-a726-5487-85c4-8f4ef2614c17'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'We learn from Paragraph 2 that outside directors are supposed to be', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "generous investors", "content": "generous investors"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "unbiased executives", "content": "unbiased executives"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "share price forecasters", "content": "share price forecasters"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "independent advisers", "content": "independent advisers"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干关键词 Paragraph 2 及 outside directors are supposed to be 定位至第二段第一、二句。\n［命题解密］第二段首句直接指出“Outside directors are supposed to serve as helpful, yet less biased, advisers on a firm\'s board”（外部董事应当在公司董事会中担任有益且较少偏见的顾问），第二句补充说明他们拥有足够独立性（enough independence）去质疑首席执行官的提案。综合可见，外部董事应是“独立的顾问（independent advisers）”，故［D］正确。\n［错项排除］［A］“generous investors”曲解了第二句中“made their wealth...elsewhere”（在别处已积累财富）的含义；［B］“unbiased executives”将“advisers（顾问）”偷换为“executives（高管）”；［C］“share price forecasters”属于无中生有，第三句仅指“股价下跌时提供建议”，而非“预测股价”。' WHERE id = 'eb6cea2d-355b-5d0a-9b83-422502aab341'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to the researchers from Ohio University, after an outside director\'s surprise departure, the firm is likely to', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "become more stable", "content": "become more stable"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "report increased earnings", "content": "report increased earnings"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "do less well in the stock market", "content": "do less well in the stock market"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "perform worse in lawsuits", "content": "perform worse in lawsuits"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干关键词 researchers from Ohio University 及 surprise departure 定位至第三段第四、五句。\n［命题解密］这两句明确列举了外部董事突然离职后的三项后果：公司不得不重申盈利的概率上升近 20%、被列入联邦集体诉讼的可能性增加，以及公司股票表现可能更差（the stock is likely to perform worse）。［C］“do less well in the stock market”是对“the stock is likely to perform worse”的精准同义改写，故［C］正确。\n［错项排除］［A］“become more stable”张冠李戴，原文末句指外部董事往往跳槽前往更稳定的大公司（more stable firms），而非原公司变稳定；［B］“report increased earnings”将“restate earnings（被迫重申盈利）”曲解为“报告盈利增长”；［D］“perform worse in lawsuits”偷换主语且过度推理，原文仅说被卷入集体诉讼的可能性增加，且“perform worse”针对的是公司股票而非诉讼表现。' WHERE id = '482fc379-7b90-593a-8741-bff0fdeeb3a3'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'It can be inferred from the last paragraph that outside directors', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "may stay for the attractive offers from the firm", "content": "may stay for the attractive offers from the firm"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "have often had records of wrongdoings in the firm", "content": "have often had records of wrongdoings in the firm"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "are accustomed to stress-free work in the firm", "content": "are accustomed to stress-free work in the firm"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "will decline incentives from the firm", "content": "will decline incentives from the firm"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干关键词 the last paragraph 定位至第四段第二、三句。\n［命题解密］末段指出，由于外部董事在坏消息曝光前离职更容易保住声誉，因此“Firms who want to keep their outside directors through tough times may have to create incentives”（想要在艰难时期留住外部董事的公司或许必须制定激励措施），否则他们就会像西蒙斯一样离开。由此合理推知，若公司提供有吸引力的条件（attractive offers 对应 incentives），外部董事可能会选择留下，故［A］正确。\n［错项排除］［B］“have often had records of wrongdoings”偷换主语，原文“any wrongdoing occurred”指公司发生不当行为时董事刚好在职，并非董事自身有劣迹；［C］“stress-free work”曲解了“have an easier time of avoiding a blow to their reputations”（更容易避免声誉受损）；［D］“will decline incentives”与末两句“靠激励留人，否则就走（Otherwise...）”的逻辑正好相反。' WHERE id = '2109c2db-f4c8-5cc7-b68f-314a942a76bf'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The author\'s attitude toward the role of outside directors is', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "permissive", "content": "permissive"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "positive", "content": "positive"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "scornful", "content": "scornful"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "critical", "content": "critical"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［精准定位］本题考察作者对全文核心对象 outside directors 的态度，综合定位第二至四段。\n［命题解密］第二段肯定外部董事能作为有益、少偏见、独立的顾问在危机中建言献策；第三段虽指出其突然离职会给公司带来负面冲击，但也特意澄清这并不意味着他们都在“跳离沉船”，而是常常正常“另谋高就”；第四段更是建议公司在艰难时期创设激励机制留住外部董事。可见作者充分肯定其价值与正面作用，持肯定态度（positive），故［B］正确。\n［错项排除］［A］“permissive（放任纵容的）”属于无中生有，作者主张用激励制度留住外部董事，并非纵容不负责任；［C］“scornful（蔑视的）”与［D］“critical（批评的）”均以偏概全，仅着眼于外部董事为避嫌而离职的现象，忽视了作者在第二、四段对其作用的正面肯定。' WHERE id = '26b5dac4-1e0e-50a8-9b00-3f122fdd1019'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'By saying "Newspapers like... their own doom" (Lines 3-4, Para. 1), the author indicates that newspapers', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "neglected the sign of crisis", "content": "neglected the sign of crisis"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "failed to get state subsidies", "content": "failed to get state subsidies"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "were not charitable corporations", "content": "were not charitable corporations"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "were in a desperate situation", "content": "were in a desperate situation"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干定位至第一段第四句“Newspapers like the San Francisco Chronicle were chronicling their own doom”。\n［命题解密］首段开篇先点明一年前（A year ago）报业末日似乎近在咫尺（the end seemed near），经济衰退差点夺走仅存的广告与读者，随后以《旧金山纪事报》“都在记录着自己的末日/劫数”为例，形象说明一年前报业曾深陷绝境（in a desperate situation），以此反衬如今形势的逆转，故［D］正确。\n［错项排除］［A］“neglected the sign of crisis”将第二段首句“现在几乎看不到危机的迹象（little sign of crisis）”篡改为“报业忽视危机迹象”；［B］“failed to get state subsidies”与［C］“were not charitable corporations”均曲解了后文联邦贸易委员会的设问“Should they become charitable corporations? Should the state subsidize them?”，把讨论中的拯救方案误作既定否定事实。' WHERE id = '8380a95f-6bf9-5898-9d07-c8aa8ce4d998'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Some newspapers refused delivery to distant suburbs probably because', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "readers threatened to pay less", "content": "readers threatened to pay less"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "newspapers wanted to reduce costs", "content": "newspapers wanted to reduce costs"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "journalists reported little about these areas", "content": "journalists reported little about these areas"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "subscribers complained about slimmer products", "content": "subscribers complained about slimmer products"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干关键词 refused delivery to distant suburbs 定位至第三段第四句，并结合上下句语境分析。\n［命题解密］第三段指出，多家报纸为了维持运营（stayed afloat）不惜大幅裁员、涨价瘦身，甚至“胆敢拒绝向偏远郊区投递报纸”，紧接着第五句将这些举措称为“不得已的求生举措（desperate measures）”，且证明行之有效。由于偏远郊区投递成本高、利润低，报社拒绝配送显然是为了“削减成本（reduce costs）”以求生存，故［B］正确。\n［错项排除］［A］“readers threatened to pay less”与前句“Readers are paying more”（读者付出更多）正相反；［C］“journalists reported little about these areas”无中生有，文中未提及郊区新闻报道量少；［D］“subscribers complained about slimmer products”将“瘦身”和“拒送郊区”两项并列自救措施强行拼接为因果关系，且文中并未提及订户抱怨。' WHERE id = '9f95cdbd-d5d5-555f-9a80-25d1a27a6dec'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Compared with their American counterparts, Japanese newspapers are much more stable because they', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "have more sources of revenue", "content": "have more sources of revenue"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "have more balanced newsrooms", "content": "have more balanced newsrooms"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "are less dependent on advertising", "content": "are less dependent on advertising"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "are less affected by readership", "content": "are less affected by readership"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干关键词 Japanese newspapers are much more stable 定位至第四段第二至五句。\n［命题解密］第四段首先点出报纸正变得更加平衡，接着指出美国报纸长期以来极度依赖广告（reliance on ads），2008 年高达 87% 的收入来自广告；而在日本这一比例仅为 35%，因此毫不意外日本报纸要稳定得多。可见日本报业更稳定的核心原因在于“对广告的依赖更少（less dependent on advertising）”，故［C］正确。\n［错项排除］［A］“have more sources of revenue”错误，首句明言报纸收入均来自“readers and advertisers”两大渠道，美日并无渠道数量差异；［B］“have more balanced newsrooms”将“more balanced businesses（商业模式更均衡）”偷换为“新闻编辑室”；［D］“are less affected by readership”与数据相反，日本广告占比仅 35%，说明来自读者的发行收入占比更高（65%），受读者群影响反而更大。' WHERE id = 'd8d01144-bc98-5983-8fc2-e9af101670e7'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'What can be inferred from the last paragraph about the current newspaper business?', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Distinctiveness is an essential feature of newspapers.", "content": "Distinctiveness is an essential feature of newspapers."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Completeness is to blame for the failure of newspapers.", "content": "Completeness is to blame for the failure of newspapers."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Foreign bureaus play a crucial role in the newspaper business.", "content": "Foreign bureaus play a crucial role in the newspaper business."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Readers have lost their interest in car and film reviews.", "content": "Readers have lost their interest in car and film reviews."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干关键词 the last paragraph 定位至第五段。\n［命题解密］末段指出，横扫编辑室的裁员潮虽波及所有人，但大部分裁撤集中在“报纸最缺乏特色的领域（where newspapers are least distinctive）”，如汽车和电影评论、大众商业及驻外机构，结果报纸不再求全，因为“完整性在报业已不再是美德（completeness is no longer a virtue）”。反向推知，当今报业生存的关键在于“独特性是不可或缺的特征（Distinctiveness is an essential feature）”，故［A］正确。\n［错项排除］［B］“Completeness is to blame for the failure of newspapers”强加因果，原文仅说求全不再是优势，未将其归咎为破产元凶；［C］“Foreign bureaus play a crucial role”与原文“驻外办事处遭到无情裁撤”相反；［D］“Readers have lost their interest in car and film reviews”无中生有，这些版块被裁是因为缺乏独特性而非读者失去兴趣。' WHERE id = '00640599-d76b-58c5-aa88-becf349af5ae'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The most appropriate title for this text would be', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "American Newspapers: Struggling for Survival", "content": "American Newspapers: Struggling for Survival"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "American Newspapers: Gone with the Wind", "content": "American Newspapers: Gone with the Wind"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "American Newspapers: A Thriving Business", "content": "American Newspapers: A Thriving Business"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "American Newspapers: A Hopeless Story", "content": "American Newspapers: A Hopeless Story"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［精准定位］本题为主旨标题题，统筹定位全文各段主旨。\n［命题解密］第一、二段指出曾被预言濒死的美国报业通过自救重获盈利；第三段详述裁员、涨价、停送偏远郊区等艰难求生手段；第四段说明收入结构日趋健康；末段点出舍弃求全、立足特色的生存之道。全篇紧扣美国报业在危机中“挣扎求生（Struggling for Survival）”的历程，故［A］正确。\n［错项排除］［B］“Gone with the Wind（随风而逝）”和［D］“A Hopeless Story（毫无希望的故事）”均停留在一年前悲观预言的基调上，与全文“死里逃生、重现盈利”的主基调矛盾；［C］“A Thriving Business（蓬勃兴旺的行业）”则过度拔高，原文第二、三段明确指出利润率远不如前且过程艰难（Not the 20% profit margins... It has not been much fun）。' WHERE id = '6ef4ae6c-bcc4-5fa2-a8f0-f100aabdb1d7'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The postwar American housing style largely reflected the Americans\'', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "prosperity and growth", "content": "prosperity and growth"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "efficiency and practicality", "content": "efficiency and practicality"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "restraint and confidence", "content": "restraint and confidence"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "pride and faithfulness", "content": "pride and faithfulness"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干关键词 postwar American housing style 定位至第二段。\n［命题解密］第二段明确指出，在住宅建筑上战后是一个崇尚“少即是多（less could truly be more）”的时期；在大萧条与战争期间，美国人学会了节俭生活，“而正是这种克制（restraint），加之战后对未来的信心（postwar confidence），使得小巧高效的住宅成为流行风尚”。由此直接对应［C］“restraint and confidence”，故［C］正确。\n［错项排除］［A］“prosperity and growth”是第一段对二战后总体社会背景的惯常印象，作者在第二段用 But 转折引出住宅风格的节俭取向；［B］“efficiency and practicality”中的高效是住宅本身的物理特点，而非美国人的精神心态；［D］“pride and faithfulness”将“confidence”过度曲解为对国家的自豪与忠诚，于文无据。' WHERE id = 'ca051bc1-3997-5b5a-9124-2a22df388ff6'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Which of the following can be inferred from Paragraph 3 about the Bauhaus?', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "It was founded by Ludwig Mies van der Rohe.", "content": "It was founded by Ludwig Mies van der Rohe."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Its designing concept was affected by World War II.", "content": "Its designing concept was affected by World War II."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Most American architects used to be associated with it.", "content": "Most American architects used to be associated with it."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "It had a great influence upon American architecture.", "content": "It had a great influence upon American architecture."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干关键词 Paragraph 3 及 the Bauhaus 定位至第三段第二、三句。\n［命题解密］第三段指出，“少即是多”由德国建筑师密斯推广，他和其他与包豪斯设计学院（the Bauhaus）有关的设计师在二战前移民美国并在美国建筑院校任教；紧接着第三句总结：“These designers came to exert enormous influence on the course of American architecture”（这些设计师对美国建筑业的发展进程产生了巨大影响）。由此可推知，包豪斯学院对美国建筑影响深远，故［D］正确。\n［错项排除］［A］“founded by Ludwig Mies van der Rohe”无中生有，原文仅说密斯“associated with the Bauhaus（与包豪斯有关）”，未提由他创立；［B］“designing concept was affected by World War II”偷换概念，二战只是这批设计师移民美国的时间节点；［C］“Most American architects used to be associated with it”张冠李戴，与包豪斯有关的是移民美国的德国设计师，而非多数美国建筑师。' WHERE id = '4f2cb9c8-917f-53c1-9162-966bff8cd9fd'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Mies held that elegance of architectural design', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "was related to large space", "content": "was related to large space"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "was identified with emptiness", "content": "was identified with emptiness"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "was not reliant on abundant decoration", "content": "was not reliant on abundant decoration"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "was not associated with efficiency", "content": "was not associated with efficiency"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干关键词 Mies 及 elegance of architectural design 定位至第四段第一、二句。\n［命题解密］第四段首句说明密斯的标志性名言意为“布局得当的精简装饰比繁复堆砌更具震撼力”，第二句紧接着点明其理念核心：“Elegance, he believed, did not derive from abundance”（他认为优雅并非来源于繁复冗余）。［C］“was not reliant on abundant decoration”是对“did not derive from abundance”的精准同义替换，故［C］正确。\n［错项排除］［A］“related to large space”与［B］“identified with emptiness”均误解了末句的“masked the fact that the spaces he designed were small and efficient, rather than big and often empty”，原文意为密斯的设计实为“小而精”而非“大而空”；［D］“not associated with efficiency”与文中强调的“small and efficient”正好相反。' WHERE id = '22bc4627-dcec-54a2-b281-9438eed05f42'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'What is true about the apartments Mies built on Chicago\'s Lake Shore Drive?', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "They ignored details and proportions.", "content": "They ignored details and proportions."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "They were built with materials popular at that time.", "content": "They were built with materials popular at that time."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "They were more spacious than neighboring buildings.", "content": "They were more spacious than neighboring buildings."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "They shared some characteristics of abstract art.", "content": "They shared some characteristics of abstract art."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干关键词 apartments Mies built on Chicago\'s Lake Shore Drive 定位至第五段。\n［命题解密］第五段首句将湖滨大道公寓与邻近老旧建筑对比，指出其面积更小；第二句解释其大受欢迎的原因，末尾将其建筑细节与比例的优雅直接称为“the architectural equivalent of the abstract art so popular at the time”（当时盛行的抽象艺术在建筑上的体现）。因此这些公寓具备抽象艺术的某些特征，故［D］正确。\n［错项排除］［A］“ignored details and proportions”与原文因“elegance of the buildings\' details and proportions”而受欢迎正相反；［B］“materials popular at that time”与第四段“materials...that in the 1940s symbolized the future（在当时尚属于超前象征而非流行普及）”相悖；［C］“more spacious than neighboring buildings”与第五段首句“smaller...than those in their older neighbors”直接冲突。' WHERE id = 'c5f48698-213b-5533-ba6f-907cd6c6fc7c'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'What can we learn about the design of the "Case Study Houses"?', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Mechanical devices were widely used.", "content": "Mechanical devices were widely used."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Natural scenes were taken into consideration.", "content": "Natural scenes were taken into consideration."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Details were sacrificed for the overall effect.", "content": "Details were sacrificed for the overall effect."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Eco-friendly materials were employed.", "content": "Eco-friendly materials were employed."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干关键词 design of the "Case Study Houses" 定位至第七段第一、二句。\n［命题解密］末段在介绍“案例研究住宅”时，第二句明确阐述其设计美学来源：“Aesthetic effect came from the landscape, new materials and forthright detailing”（审美效果源自自然景观、新材料和直观明了的细节处理）。［B］“Natural scenes were taken into consideration”中的 Natural scenes 恰是原文 landscape 的同义替换，故［B］正确。\n［错项排除］［A］“Mechanical devices were widely used”曲解了末句，拉尔夫·雷普森只是预言机械革命，但“很少有家庭购买直升机”；［C］“Details were sacrificed”与原文“forthright detailing（注重简洁明了的细节）”相反；［D］“Eco-friendly materials”将“landscape”和“new materials”强行嫁接，原文并未提及材料是否“环保”。' WHERE id = 'cbada250-5052-5e38-9a5d-908dae44186d'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The EU is faced with so many problems that', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "it has more or less lost faith in markets", "content": "it has more or less lost faith in markets"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "even its supporters begin to feel concerned", "content": "even its supporters begin to feel concerned"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "some of its member countries plan to abandon euro", "content": "some of its member countries plan to abandon euro"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "it intends to deny the possibility of devaluation", "content": "it intends to deny the possibility of devaluation"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干关键词 The EU is faced with so many problems 定位至第一段第三句。\n［命题解密］首段开篇先发问“欧盟还能挺过去吗？”，随后第三句用 Now 引出严峻现实：“even the project\'s greatest cheerleaders talk of a continent facing a \'Bermuda triangle\' of debt, population decline and lower growth”（就连欧盟项目最狂热的支持者也在谈论欧洲大陆正面临债务、人口下降和增长放缓的“百慕大三角”）。cheerleaders 对应选项中的 supporters，说明连支持者也开始感到担忧，故［B］正确。\n［错项排除］［A］“lost faith in markets”偷换主语，第二段第二句是“Markets have lost faith（市场失去信心）”，而非欧盟对市场失去信心；［C］“plan to abandon euro”无中生有，第二、三段讨论的是如何挽救单一货币而非计划放弃；［D］“intends to deny the possibility of devaluation”曲解了“denies uncompetitive members the quick fix of devaluation”，意为使用单一货币客观上使成员国无法靠本币贬值救急，并非欧盟有意“否定贬值可能性”。' WHERE id = 'a6b6b294-51d6-5529-b543-76f0579a646c'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The debate over the EU\'s single currency is stuck because the dominant powers', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "are competing for the leading position", "content": "are competing for the leading position"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "are busy handling their own crises", "content": "are busy handling their own crises"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "fail to reach an agreement on harmonisation", "content": "fail to reach an agreement on harmonisation"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "disagree on the steps towards disintegration", "content": "disagree on the steps towards disintegration"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干关键词 debate over the EU\'s single currency is stuck 定位至第三段第二句。\n［命题解密］第三段明确解释了僵局的原因：“It is stuck because the euro zone\'s dominant powers, France and Germany, agree on the need for greater harmonisation within the euro zone, but disagree about what to harmonise”（之所以陷入僵局，是因为欧元区两大主导国法国和德国虽然都同意需要加强协调统一，但在具体协调什么的问题上意见分歧）。［C］“fail to reach an agreement on harmonisation”精准概括此意，故［C］正确。\n［错项排除］［A］“competing for the leading position”无中生有，文中仅客观称法德为 dominant powers，未提争夺领导权；［B］“busy handling their own crises”未在文中提及；［D］“disagree on the steps towards disintegration”曲解文意，法德争论的是如何挽救单一货币免于解体（save...from disintegration），而非解体的步骤。' WHERE id = '287252a4-8105-56ba-aa77-9a93efdb1341'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'To solve the euro problem, Germany proposed that', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "EU funds for poor regions be increased", "content": "EU funds for poor regions be increased"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "stricter regulations be imposed", "content": "stricter regulations be imposed"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "only core members be involved in economic co-ordination", "content": "only core members be involved in economic co-ordination"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "voting rights of the EU members be guaranteed", "content": "voting rights of the EU members be guaranteed"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干关键词 solve the euro problem、Germany proposed 定位至第四段第一句。\n［命题解密］第四段首句清晰阐明德国的主张：“Germany thinks the euro must be saved by stricter rules on borrowing, spending and competitiveness, backed by quasi-automatic sanctions for governments that do not obey”（德国认为必须通过对借贷、支出和竞争力制定更严格的规则来拯救欧元，并辅以对违规政府的准自动制裁）。［B］“stricter regulations be imposed”与 stricter rules 完全对应，故［B］正确。\n［错项排除］［A］“EU funds for poor regions be increased”与原文“freeze EU funds for poorer regions（威胁冻结贫困地区资金）”正相反；［C］“only core members be involved”张冠李戴，德国坚持所有 27 个成员国都应参与经济协调，仅限核心国是法国的主张；［D］“voting rights...be guaranteed”与原文“suspension of a country\'s voting rights（暂停投票权）”完全相悖。' WHERE id = '2961a398-eb72-53df-baf2-52915c4483a5'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The French proposal of handling the crisis implies that', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "poor countries are more likely to get funds", "content": "poor countries are more likely to get funds"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "strict monetary policy will be applied to poor countries", "content": "strict monetary policy will be applied to poor countries"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "loans will be readily available to rich countries", "content": "loans will be readily available to rich countries"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "rich countries will basically control Eurobonds", "content": "rich countries will basically control Eurobonds"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干关键词 French proposal 定位至第五段第一、二句。\n［命题解密］第五段指出，以法国为首的“南部阵营”主张在欧元区核心国建立“欧洲经济政府”，第二句解释其含义：“politicians intervening in monetary policy and a system of redistribution from richer to poorer members, via cheaper borrowing for governments through common Eurobonds or complete fiscal transfers”（由政客干预货币政策，并通过共同欧元债券提供的低息贷款或全面财政转移支付，建立从富裕成员国向较贫困成员国的收入再分配体制）。由此推知，较贫困国家更有可能获得资金支持，故［A］正确。\n［错项排除］［B］“strict monetary policy”与第五段法国主张政客干预货币政策及德国第四段追求的“经济严纪”相悖；［C］“loans will be readily available to rich countries”与“from richer to poorer members”方向颠倒；［D］“rich countries will basically control Eurobonds”属于偷换概念，共同欧元债券是用来资助困难成员国低息借款的工具，文中并未提及由富国控制。' WHERE id = 'eecabdde-d188-5ab8-a26b-2dcc3fec1594'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Regarding the future of the EU, the author seems to feel', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "pessimistic", "content": "pessimistic"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "desperate", "content": "desperate"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "conceited", "content": "conceited"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "hopeful", "content": "hopeful"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干关键词 future of the EU 及 author seems to feel 定位至第六段（末段）。\n［命题解密］末段首句明确表态：“It is too soon to write off the EU”（现在断言欧盟彻底失败还为时过早），随后列举欧盟仍是世界最大贸易集团、内部市场高度自由开放、致力于缓和全球化冲击并使资本主义向善等重大优势。由此可见作者对欧盟的未来抱有信心，持乐观充满希望的态度（hopeful），故［D］正确。\n［错项排除］［A］“pessimistic（悲观的）”与［B］“desperate（绝望的）”均与末段“为时过早”及高度肯定欧盟前景的基调完全相反；［C］“conceited（自负的，骄傲自满的）”将作者客观肯定欧盟制度优势曲解为盲目自负，不符合行文态度。' WHERE id = 'f3273fe5-853d-5287-9bd1-5687b8da41b0'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to the text, Andrew Lansley held that ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "\\"fat taxes\\" should be imposed on fast-food producers such as McDonald\'s.", "content": "\\"fat taxes\\" should be imposed on fast-food producers such as McDonald\'s."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "the government should ban fast-food outlets in the neighborhood of schools.", "content": "the government should ban fast-food outlets in the neighborhood of schools."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "\\"lecturing\\" was an effective way to improve school lunches in England.", "content": "\\"lecturing\\" was an effective way to improve school lunches in England."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "cigarette-style warnings should be introduced to children about the dangers of a poor diet.", "content": "cigarette-style warnings should be introduced to children about the dangers of a poor diet."}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "the producers of crisps and candies could contribute significantly to the Change4Life campaign.", "content": "the producers of crisps and candies could contribute significantly to the Change4Life campaign."}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "parents should set good examples for their children by keeping a healthy diet at home.", "content": "parents should set good examples for their children by keeping a healthy diet at home."}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "the government should strengthen the sense of responsibility among businesses.", "content": "the government should strengthen the sense of responsibility among businesses."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'E', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干人物 Andrew Lansley 定位至第二段和第六段。\n［命题解密］第六段第一、二句指出，卫生大臣兰斯利主张让食品行业而非政府发挥主导作用，并明确表示“manufacturers of crisps and candies could play a central role in the Change4Life campaign”（薯片和糖果生产商可以在“为健康而改变”运动中发挥核心作用）。［E］“the producers of crisps and candies could contribute significantly to the Change4Life campaign”精准同义转述原文，故［E］正确。\n［错项排除］［C］项虽在第六段末句提及“lecturing”，但兰斯利认为“说教”并不是改变人们饮食行为的最佳方式（criticised...as an example of how \'lecturing\' people was not the best way），恰恰与［C］项观点相反。' WHERE id = 'cb03642f-2272-5d64-9241-20d342a3b2cc'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to the text, Terence Stephenson agreed that ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "\\"fat taxes\\" should be imposed on fast-food producers such as McDonald\'s.", "content": "\\"fat taxes\\" should be imposed on fast-food producers such as McDonald\'s."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "the government should ban fast-food outlets in the neighborhood of schools.", "content": "the government should ban fast-food outlets in the neighborhood of schools."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "\\"lecturing\\" was an effective way to improve school lunches in England.", "content": "\\"lecturing\\" was an effective way to improve school lunches in England."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "cigarette-style warnings should be introduced to children about the dangers of a poor diet.", "content": "cigarette-style warnings should be introduced to children about the dangers of a poor diet."}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "the producers of crisps and candies could contribute significantly to the Change4Life campaign.", "content": "the producers of crisps and candies could contribute significantly to the Change4Life campaign."}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "parents should set good examples for their children by keeping a healthy diet at home.", "content": "parents should set good examples for their children by keeping a healthy diet at home."}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "the government should strengthen the sense of responsibility among businesses.", "content": "the government should strengthen the sense of responsibility among businesses."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干人物 Terence Stephenson 定位至第四、五、七、八段。\n［命题解密］第四段末句指出斯蒂芬森认为食用不健康食品应被视作与吸烟同样有害；第七段第二句更直接引述其原话：“we might even begin to think of high-calorie fast food in the same way as cigarettes — by setting strict limits on...”（我们甚至应当像对待香烟一样对待高热量快餐）。综合第一段医生群体要求向儿童引入香烟式警示语（introduce cigarette-style warnings to children about the dangers of a poor diet）的呼吁，［D］项完整概括了斯蒂芬森的立场，故［D］正确。\n［错项排除］［A］项“fat taxes”虽在首段被广泛提及，但斯蒂芬森在第四、七、八段重点倡议的是参照控烟模式限制广告、植入、赞助和促销诱因，并未单独将脂肪税归为他的核心主张；［B］项“禁止校园周边开快餐店”在第八段未提及，该主张属于后文布格拉教授（Q44）。' WHERE id = '886e91d4-6c33-561c-97d5-0d2d6aaf8904'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to the text, Jamie Oliver seemed to believe that ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "\\"fat taxes\\" should be imposed on fast-food producers such as McDonald\'s.", "content": "\\"fat taxes\\" should be imposed on fast-food producers such as McDonald\'s."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "the government should ban fast-food outlets in the neighborhood of schools.", "content": "the government should ban fast-food outlets in the neighborhood of schools."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "\\"lecturing\\" was an effective way to improve school lunches in England.", "content": "\\"lecturing\\" was an effective way to improve school lunches in England."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "cigarette-style warnings should be introduced to children about the dangers of a poor diet.", "content": "cigarette-style warnings should be introduced to children about the dangers of a poor diet."}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "the producers of crisps and candies could contribute significantly to the Change4Life campaign.", "content": "the producers of crisps and candies could contribute significantly to the Change4Life campaign."}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "parents should set good examples for their children by keeping a healthy diet at home.", "content": "parents should set good examples for their children by keeping a healthy diet at home."}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "the government should strengthen the sense of responsibility among businesses.", "content": "the government should strengthen the sense of responsibility among businesses."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干人物 Jamie Oliver 定位至第六段第三句。\n［命题解密］该句指出兰斯利“criticised the celebrity chef Jamie Oliver\'s high-profile attempt to improve school lunches in England as an example of how \'lecturing\' people was not the best way to change their behaviour”（批评名厨杰米·奥利弗高调试图改善英国校园午餐的做法，称其证明了向人“说教”并非改变行为的最佳方式）。通过兰斯利对奥利弗的批评反向推知，奥利弗本人当时相信高调倡导与“说教”是改善校园午餐的有效方式，正好对应［C］项，故［C］正确。\n［错项排除］［E］项属于卫生大臣兰斯利而非名厨奥利弗的观点；其余选项均未在第六段涉及奥利弗。' WHERE id = '85518255-95d7-5ead-81e0-d17277f8dd5f'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to the text, Dinesh Bhugra suggested that ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "\\"fat taxes\\" should be imposed on fast-food producers such as McDonald\'s.", "content": "\\"fat taxes\\" should be imposed on fast-food producers such as McDonald\'s."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "the government should ban fast-food outlets in the neighborhood of schools.", "content": "the government should ban fast-food outlets in the neighborhood of schools."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "\\"lecturing\\" was an effective way to improve school lunches in England.", "content": "\\"lecturing\\" was an effective way to improve school lunches in England."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "cigarette-style warnings should be introduced to children about the dangers of a poor diet.", "content": "cigarette-style warnings should be introduced to children about the dangers of a poor diet."}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "the producers of crisps and candies could contribute significantly to the Change4Life campaign.", "content": "the producers of crisps and candies could contribute significantly to the Change4Life campaign."}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "parents should set good examples for their children by keeping a healthy diet at home.", "content": "parents should set good examples for their children by keeping a healthy diet at home."}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "the government should strengthen the sense of responsibility among businesses.", "content": "the government should strengthen the sense of responsibility among businesses."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干人物 Dinesh Bhugra 定位至第九、十段。\n［命题解密］第九段引述布格拉教授关于教育儿童认识食物危害的观点，第十段紧接着明确指出他的政策建议：“He also urged councils to impose \'fast-food-free zones\' around schools and hospitals — areas within which takeaways cannot open”（他还敦促地方议会在学校和医院周边设立“无快餐区”，即禁止外卖快餐店开张的区域）。［B］“the government should ban fast-food outlets in the neighborhood of schools”正是对“fast-food-free zones around schools”的精准同义改写，故［B］正确。\n［错项排除］［A］项“fat taxes”是首段医生们提及的总体要求，并未出现在第九、十段布格拉的个人建议中；［F］项在全文无据。' WHERE id = 'c9dffd81-e779-5a35-92ad-b3f6ea93dde2'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to the text, a Department of Health spokesperson proposed that ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "\\"fat taxes\\" should be imposed on fast-food producers such as McDonald\'s.", "content": "\\"fat taxes\\" should be imposed on fast-food producers such as McDonald\'s."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "the government should ban fast-food outlets in the neighborhood of schools.", "content": "the government should ban fast-food outlets in the neighborhood of schools."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "\\"lecturing\\" was an effective way to improve school lunches in England.", "content": "\\"lecturing\\" was an effective way to improve school lunches in England."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "cigarette-style warnings should be introduced to children about the dangers of a poor diet.", "content": "cigarette-style warnings should be introduced to children about the dangers of a poor diet."}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "the producers of crisps and candies could contribute significantly to the Change4Life campaign.", "content": "the producers of crisps and candies could contribute significantly to the Change4Life campaign."}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "parents should set good examples for their children by keeping a healthy diet at home.", "content": "parents should set good examples for their children by keeping a healthy diet at home."}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "the government should strengthen the sense of responsibility among businesses.", "content": "the government should strengthen the sense of responsibility among businesses."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'G', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干关键词 A Department of Health spokesperson 定位至第十一段。\n［命题解密］第十一段中，一位卫生部发言人指出应当构建全社会共同参与的公共卫生新愿景：“This includes creating a new \'responsibility deal\' with business, built on social responsibility, not state regulation”（这包括与企业达成一项基于社会责任而非国家强制监管的新“责任协议”）。［G］“the government should strengthen the sense of responsibility among businesses”精准概括了“built on social responsibility（with business）”，故［G］正确。\n［错项排除］［F］项将发言人首句“全社会共同努力（all of society works together）”过度引申为“父母在家保持健康饮食为孩子树立榜样”，而发言人全段重点明显落于企业社会责任而非家庭教育，故排除。' WHERE id = '14dfebe2-10d6-54de-9981-8d5e5e478161'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'Pretty in pink: adult women do not remember being so obsessed with the colour, yet it is pervasive in our young girls\' lives. It is not that pink is intrinsically bad, but it is such a tiny slice of the rainbow and, though it may celebrate girlhood in one way, it also repeatedly and firmly fuses girls\' identity to appearance. Then it presents that connection, even among two-year-olds, between girls as not only innocent but as evidence of innocence. Looking around, I despaired at the singular lack of imagination about girls\' lives and interests.\n\nGirls\' attraction to pink may seem unavoidable, somehow encoded in their DNA, but according to Jo Paoletti, an associate professor of American Studies, it is not. Children were not colour-coded at all until the early 20th century: in the era before domestic washing machines all babies wore white as a practical matter, since the only way of getting clothes clean was to boil them. What\'s more, both boys and girls wore what were thought of as gender-neutral dresses. When nursery colours were introduced, pink was actually considered the more masculine colour, a pastel version of red, which was associated with strength. Blue, with its intimations of the Virgin Mary, constancy and faithfulness, symbolised femininity. It was not until the mid-1980s, when amplifying age and sex differences became a dominant children\'s marketing strategy, that pink fully came into its own, when it began to seem inherently attractive to girls, part of what defined them as female, at least for the first few critical years.\n\nI had not realised how profoundly marketing trends dictated our perception of what is natural to kids, including our core beliefs about their psychological development. Take the toddler. I assumed that phase was something experts developed after years of research into children\'s behaviour: wrong. Turns out, according to Daniel Cook, a historian of childhood consumerism, it was popularised as a marketing trick by clothing manufacturers in the 1930s.\n\nTrade publications counselled department stores that, in order to increase sales, they should create a "third stepping stone" between infant wear and older kids\' clothes. It was only after "toddler" became a common shoppers\' term that it evolved into a broadly accepted developmental stage. Splitting kids, or adults, into ever-tinier categories has proved a sure-fire way to boost profits. And one of the easiest ways to segment a market is to magnify gender differences—or invent them where they did not previously exist.' WHERE id = '279ea384-fa7c-5f11-90cf-9d66120e1d65'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'In 2010, a federal judge shook America\'s biotech industry to its core. Companies had won patents for isolated DNA for decades—by 2005 some 20% of human genes were patented. But in March 2010 a judge ruled that genes were unpatentable. Executives were violently agitated. The Biotechnology Industry Organisation (BIO), a trade group, assured members that this was just a "preliminary step" in a longer battle.\n\nOn July 29th they were relieved, at least temporarily. A federal appeals court overturned the prior decision, ruling that Myriad Genetics could indeed hold patents to two genes that help forecast a woman\'s risk of breast cancer. The chief executive of Myriad, a company in Utah, said the ruling was a blessing to firms and patients alike.\n\nBut as companies continue their attempts at personalised medicine, the courts will remain rather busy. The Myriad case itself is probably not over. Critics make three main arguments against gene patents: a gene is a product of nature, so it may not be patented; gene patents suppress innovation rather than reward it; and patents\' monopolies restrict access to genetic tests such as Myriad\'s. A growing number seem to agree. Last year a federal task-force urged reform for patents related to genetic tests. In October the Department of Justice filed a brief in the Myriad case, arguing that an isolated DNA molecule "is no less a product of nature... than are cotton fibres that have been separated from cotton seeds."\n\nDespite the appeals court\'s decision, big questions remain unanswered. For example, it is unclear whether the sequencing of a whole genome violates the patents of individual genes within it. The case may yet reach the Supreme Court.\n\nAs the industry advances, however, other suits may have an even greater impact. Companies are unlikely to file many more patents for human DNA molecules—most are already patented or in the public domain. Firms are now studying how genes interact, looking for correlations that might be used to determine the causes of disease or predict a drug\'s efficacy. Companies are eager to win patents for "connecting the dots," explains Hans Sauer, a lawyer for the BIO.\n\nTheir success may be determined by a suit related to this issue, brought by the Mayo Clinic, which the Supreme Court will hear in its next term. The BIO recently held a convention which included sessions to coach lawyers on the shifting landscape for patents. Each meeting was packed.' WHERE id = 'cd317e47-751b-5d4e-84b0-a755e8ee9cb8'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'The great recession may be over, but this era of high joblessness is probably beginning. Before it ends, it will likely change the life course and character of a generation of young adults. And ultimately, it is likely to reshape our politics, our culture, and the character of our society for years.\n\nNo one tries harder than the jobless to find silver linings in this national economic disaster. Many said that unemployment, while extremely painful, had improved them in some ways: they had become less materialistic and more financially prudent; they were more aware of the struggles of others. In limited respects, perhaps the recession will leave society better off. At the very least, it has awoken us from our national fever dream of easy riches and bigger houses, and put a necessary end to an era of reckless personal spending.\n\nBut for the most part, these benefits seem thin, uncertain, and far off. In The Moral Consequences of Economic Growth, the economic historian Benjamin Friedman argues that both inside and outside the U.S., lengthy periods of economic stagnation or decline have almost always left society more mean-spirited and less inclusive, and have usually stopped or reversed the advance of rights and freedoms. Anti-immigrant sentiment typically increases, as does conflict between races and classes.\n\nIncome inequality usually falls during a recession, but it has not shrunk in this one. Indeed, this period of economic weakness may reinforce class divides, and decrease opportunities to cross them—especially for young people. The research of Till Von Wachter, the economist at Columbia University, suggests that not all people graduating into a recession see their life chances dimmed: those with degrees from elite universities catch up fairly quickly to where they otherwise would have been if they had graduated in better times; it is the masses beneath them that are left behind.\n\nIn the Internet age, it is particularly easy to see the resentment that has always been hidden within American society. More difficult, in the moment, is discerning precisely how these lean times are affecting society\'s character. In many respects, the U.S. was more socially tolerant entering this recession than at any time in its history, and a variety of national polls on social conflict since then have shown mixed results. We will have to wait and see exactly how these hard times will reshape our social fabric. But they certainly will reshape it, and all the more so the longer they extend.' WHERE id = 'cd048359-9eb2-5a7d-b14a-f5e01ca76930'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'"Universal history, the history of what man has accomplished in this world, is at bottom the History of the Great Men who have worked here," wrote the Victorian sage Thomas Carlyle. Well, not any more it is not.\n\nSuddenly, Britain looks to have fallen out with its favorite historical form. This could be no more than a passing literary craze, but it also points to a broader truth about how we now approach the past: less concerned with learning from our forefathers and more interested in feeling their pain. Today, we want empathy, not inspiration.\n\nFrom the earliest days of the Renaissance, the writing of history meant recounting the exemplary lives of great men. In 1337, Petrarch began work on his rambling writing De Viris Illustribus—On Famous Men, highlighting the virtus (or virtue) of classical heroes. Petrarch celebrated their greatness in conquering fortune and rising to the top. This was the biographical tradition which Niccolò Machiavelli turned on its head. In The Prince, he championed cunning, ruthlessness, and boldness, rather than virtue, mercy and justice, as the skills of successful leaders.\n\nOver time, the attributes of greatness shifted. The Romantics commemorated the leading painters and authors of their day, stressing the uniqueness of the artist\'s personal experience rather than public glory. By contrast, the Victorian author Samuel Smiles wrote Self-Help as a catalogue of the worthy lives of engineers, industrialists and explorers. "The valuable examples which they furnish of the power of self-help, of patient purpose, resolute working, and steadfast integrity, issuing in the formation of truly noble and manly character, exhibit," wrote Smiles, "what it is in the power of each to accomplish for himself." His biographies of James Watt, Richard Arkwright and Josiah Wedgwood were held up as beacons to guide the working man through his difficult life.\n\nThis was all a bit bourgeois for Thomas Carlyle, who focused his biographies on the truly heroic lives of Martin Luther, Oliver Cromwell and Napoleon Bonaparte. These epochal figures represented lives hard to imitate, but to be acknowledged as possessing higher authority than mere mortals.\n\nNot everyone was convinced by such bombast. "The history of all hitherto existing society is the history of class struggles," wrote Marx and Engels in The Communist Manifesto. For them, history did nothing, it possessed no immense wealth nor waged battles: "It is man, real, living man who does all that." And history should be the story of the masses and their record of struggle. As such, it needed to appreciate the economic realities, the social contexts and power relations in which each epoch stood. For: "Men make their own history, but they do not make it just as they please; they do not make it under circumstances chosen by themselves, but under circumstances directly found, given and transmitted from the past."\n\nThis was the tradition which revolutionised our appreciation of the past. In place of Thomas Carlyle, Britain nurtured Christopher Hill, EP Thompson and Eric Hobsbawm. History from below stood alongside biographies of great men. Whole new realms of understanding—from gender to race to cultural studies—were opened up as scholars unpicked the multiplicity of lost societies. And it transformed public history too: downstairs became just as fascinating as upstairs.' WHERE id = 'bd9bf6f1-7548-56a2-a34f-798ce97444a1'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [4] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "necessities", "content": "necessities"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "facilities", "content": "facilities"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "commodities", "content": "commodities"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "properties", "content": "properties"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［定位/考点］名词词义辨析与战地生活语境。\n［解题思路］空格前后指出士兵们在极端艰苦的条件下持续作战，“甚至常常缺少食物与庇护所等最基本的[4]（生活必需品）”。the necessities of food and shelter 为习惯表达，指维持基本生存所必需的物资，故选［A］necessities。\n［错项排除］［B］facilities（设施、设备，多指硬件场馆或公共装置）、［C］commodities（大宗日用商品，偏商业贸易属性）及［D］properties（财产、房地产）均无法精准传达战时匮乏基本生存保障之意。' WHERE id = '7812c015-2b43-5fa3-8eba-312906aaccf8'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [6] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "for", "content": "for"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "into", "content": "into"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "from", "content": "from"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "against", "content": "against"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［定位/考点］高频固定动词短语搭配与句内语义。\n［解题思路］空格所在定语成分修饰前线战士（an average guy），刻画其“正面[6]数百年来所见最训练有素、装备最精良也最凶残的敌人”。be up against 为固定习语搭配，意为“直面、面临（严峻困难或强敌劲旅）”，契合双方军力对比悬殊的战地语境，故选［D］against。\n［错项排除］［A］for、［B］into 与［C］from 均无法置于 be up... 之后构成“直面强敌竞争或挑战”的固定语义搭配。' WHERE id = '8e68b880-3b91-5e0f-bda4-3042ce8a6c0f'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [7] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "with", "content": "with"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "for", "content": "for"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "as", "content": "as"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "on", "content": "on"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'【命题解密】句内语义与介词辨析。\n【精准定位】句子指出“G.I. is just a military abbreviation [7] Government Issue”。\nabbreviation for sth是英语固有习惯用法，意为“……的缩写/简称”，如the abbreviation for kilograms is kg，故选[B] for。\n【错项排除】[A] with通常表示伴随或工具，不与abbreviation搭配表示简称；[C] as意为“作为”，语义不通；[D] on无“……的缩写”用法。' WHERE id = '2b18f1a5-2003-5072-a5e9-8719af8ef08a'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [15] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "traveled", "content": "traveled"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "walked", "content": "walked"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "marched", "content": "marched"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "covered", "content": "covered"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［定位/考点］动宾习惯搭配与路程表达语态。\n［解题思路］空格位于 how many miles were [15] 宾语从句中，主语为具体的英里距离（miles）。在英文地道表达中，cover miles 常用于表示“走过、行进、跨越（某段距离）”，且自然支持被动语态（miles were covered），指“行军到底走过了多少英里”，故选［D］。\n［错项排除］［A］traveled（虽可及物但多以人为主动旅行主语）、［B］walked（步行，常规不直接用路程作被动表达）及［C］marched（行军）皆不契合 miles were ~ed 的自然习惯用法。' WHERE id = '1ff254da-97db-5828-a835-9ab451c14b2f'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [16] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "paralleled", "content": "paralleled"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "counteracted", "content": "counteracted"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "duplicated", "content": "duplicated"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "contradicted", "content": "contradicted"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'【考点提炼】上下文语义+动词辨析。\n【解题思路】前文指出战地记者 Ernie Pyle 擅长报道战争中普通士兵的真实面貌（writing about the dirt-snow-and-mud soldiers），紧接着空格句说明“他的报道 [16] 著名漫画家 Bill Maulden 的《威利》系列漫画（His reports [16] the \'Willie\' cartoons...）”，而后一句进一步解释“两人都聚焦于战争的泥泞与疲惫（Both men... the dirt and exhaustion of war）”。可见 Pyle 的文字报道与 Maulden 的漫画在主题和情感基调上高度一致、相互呼应，[A] paralleled（与……相似/相呼应）最符合语境。\n【错项排除】[B] counteracted（抵消，对抗）和 [D] contradicted（反驳，与……相矛盾）均表达对立或相反关系，与下文 Both men 体现的“二者一致”完全相悖；[C] duplicated（复制，完全重复）程度过重，文字报道与漫画属于不同体裁，二者是主题契合与呼应，而非机械复制。' WHERE id = 'e4da1836-fd7c-55b0-ac7e-254892b746a6'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [17] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "endured", "content": "endured"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "shared", "content": "shared"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "reflected", "content": "reflected"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "understood", "content": "understood"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［定位/考点］上下文语义与动宾情感共鸣搭配。\n［解题思路］句中指出两名战地创作人员（记者与画家）与前线官兵一道，“共同体会了（[17]）战争的肮脏与疲惫（the dirt and exhaustion of war）”。share 意为“分担、共同经历体会”，准确突出随军人员与普通士兵同甘共苦的在场感，故选［B］。\n［错项排除］［A］endured（忍受折磨）多强调苦难亲历主体本身被动熬过痛楚，且较难体现随行两人与士兵共同分担之感；［C］reflected（反映）与［D］understood（理解）皆停留在外部旁观认知层面。' WHERE id = '9f4730e1-775f-5f39-806d-4a4693cf375b'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'By saying "it is...the rainbow" (Line 3, Para. 1), the author means pink ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "cannot explain girls\' lack of imagination", "content": "cannot explain girls\' lack of imagination"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "should not be associated with girls\' innocence", "content": "should not be associated with girls\' innocence"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "should not be the sole representation of girlhood", "content": "should not be the sole representation of girlhood"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "cannot influence girls\' lives and interests", "content": "cannot influence girls\' lives and interests"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'【命题解密】词句推断题。\n【精准定位】定位至首段②句“It is not that pink is intrinsically bad, but it is such a tiny slice of the rainbow and, though it may celebrate girlhood in one way, it also repeatedly and firmly fuses girls\' identity to appearance”。\n作者以“七色彩虹中极小的一抹色彩”比喻粉色只是缤纷色彩中的一种，年轻女孩的生活与童年本应丰富多彩，不应让粉色成为女孩身份的唯一代表。[C]项“should not be the sole representation of girlhood（粉色不应成为少女时代的唯一代表）”准确传达了作者意图，故选[C]。\n【错项排除】[A]项“不能解释女孩想象力的匮乏”对应末句人们对女孩生活与兴趣缺乏想象力，偏离彩虹比喻本体；[B]项针对③句粉色被视为纯真证明，非“彩虹一小片”的喻义；[D]项“不能影响女孩的生活和兴趣”与首句“粉色充斥着年轻女孩的生活”相悖。' WHERE id = 'e11c2827-4f65-55b6-9d43-02de42ebc444'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to Paragraph 2, which of the following is true of colours?', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Colours are encoded in girls\' DNA.", "content": "Colours are encoded in girls\' DNA."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Blue used to be regarded as the colour for girls.", "content": "Blue used to be regarded as the colour for girls."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "White is preferred by babies.", "content": "White is preferred by babies."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Pink used to be a neutral colour in symbolising genders.", "content": "Pink used to be a neutral colour in symbolising genders."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'【命题解密】事实细节题。\n【精准定位】定位至第二段④⑤句“When nursery colours were introduced, pink was actually considered the more masculine colour... Blue, with its intimations of the Virgin Mary, constancy and faithfulness, symbolised femininity”。\n文中明确指出，当婴儿房颜色刚引入时，粉色其实被视为更具男子气概的颜色，而蓝色象征女性气质，即过去蓝色曾被视作女孩的颜色。[B]项“Blue used to be regarded as the colour for girls”与原文完全契合，故选[B]。\n【错项排除】[A]项与首句明确否定的“encoded in their DNA, it is not”直接相悖；[C]项曲解②句，婴儿穿白色是因为水煮漂洗的实际需要，而非婴儿偏爱；[D]项错把dress（gender-neutral dresses）张冠李戴给pink，文中明确说明pink曾被视为更偏男性的颜色（masculine colour），而非中性色。' WHERE id = 'a3b42679-4f93-50c2-80a8-569d6028b3b0'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The author suggests that our perception of children\'s psychological development was much influenced by ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "text": "the observation of children\'s nature", "value": "A", "content": "the observation of children\'s nature"}, {"key": "B", "text": "the marketing of products for children", "value": "B", "content": "the marketing of products for children"}, {"key": "C", "text": "researches into children\'s behaviour", "value": "C", "content": "researches into children\'s behaviour"}, {"key": "D", "text": "studies of childhood consumption", "value": "D", "content": "studies of childhood consumption"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'【命题解密】事实细节题。\n【精准定位】定位至第三段①至③句“I had not realised how profoundly marketing trends dictated our perception of what is natural to kids, including our core beliefs about their psychological development. Take the toddler. I assumed that phase was something experts developed after years of research into children\'s behaviour: wrong. Turns out, according to Daniel Cook, a historian of childhood consumerism, it was popularised as a marketing trick by clothing manufacturers in the 1930s”。\n作者直白指出，商业营销趋势深刻支配了我们对儿童天性及心理发展的核心认知，甚至连“学步期（toddler）”也是1930年代服装制造商为促销发明的营销手段。[B]项“the marketing of products for children（针对儿童产品的市场营销）”精准对应，故选[B]。\n【错项排除】[A]项“对儿童天性的观察”只是受营销趋势支配的认知对象（what is natural to kids），并非原因；[C]项“对儿童行为的研究”在②句被作者以“wrong”明确否定；[D]项“儿童消费研究”偷换了童年消费主义历史学家Daniel Cook的身份背景。' WHERE id = '89e9ba07-9ec6-535e-a8f7-5aa64df6ce79'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'We may learn from Paragraph 4 that department stores were advised to ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "classify consumers into smaller groups", "content": "classify consumers into smaller groups"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "attach equal importance to different genders", "content": "attach equal importance to different genders"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "focus on infant wear and older kids\' clothes", "content": "focus on infant wear and older kids\' clothes"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "create some common shoppers\' terms", "content": "create some common shoppers\' terms"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'【命题解密】推理判断题。\n【精准定位】定位至第四段①至③句“Trade publications counselled department stores that, in order to increase sales, they should create a \'third stepping stone\' between infant wear and older kids\' clothes... Splitting kids, or adults, into ever-tinier categories has proved a sure-fire way to boost profits”。\n行业刊物建议百货商店在婴儿服与大童装之间增设“学步童装”这一中间层级，并将儿童乃至成人不断切分为更细小的类别来刺激利润。[A]项“classify consumers into smaller groups（将消费者划分为更小的群体）”精准概括了这一细分市场策略，故选[A]。\n【错项排除】[B]项与末句“放大甚至凭空捏造性别差异（magnify gender differences）”相悖；[C]项仅截取比较参照物infant wear和older kids\' clothes，建议实质是在二者之间开辟新分类；[D]项将结果当建议，common shoppers\' term是推行分类后的附带结果。' WHERE id = '781a2e31-b87a-5085-b7ac-bf7730aeb83d'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'It can be concluded that girls\' attraction to pink seems to be ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "fully understood by clothing manufacturers", "content": "fully understood by clothing manufacturers"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "clearly explained by their inborn tendency", "content": "clearly explained by their inborn tendency"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "mainly imposed by profit-driven businessmen", "content": "mainly imposed by profit-driven businessmen"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "well interpreted by psychological experts", "content": "well interpreted by psychological experts"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'【命题解密】推理概括题。\n【精准定位】综合全篇主旨，作者在第二段推翻了“粉色吸引力刻在女孩DNA里”的成见，并在第二至四段指出直到20世纪80年代中期商家将放大年龄与性别差异作为主导营销策略后，粉色才被塑造成定义女孩的特质；服装商为了利润甚至创造出“toddler”等细分类别。\n由此可知，女孩对粉色的迷恋主要由追逐利润的商人通过营销手段强加塑造而来，故选[C] mainly imposed by profit-driven businessmen。\n【错项排除】[A]项曲解了服装商的作用，商家利用营销技巧制造消费需求而非学术理解女孩天性；[B]项“由先天倾向清楚解释”与第二段“it is not（encoded in their DNA）”直接相悖；[D]项“得到心理学家很好阐释”与第三段明确否定的“experts developed after years of research: wrong”相反。' WHERE id = '2107caa7-5de4-517a-9abc-7e17fc628894'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'It can be learned from Paragraph 1 that the biotech companies would like ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "genes to be patentable", "content": "genes to be patentable"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "the BIO to issue a warning", "content": "the BIO to issue a warning"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "their executives to be active", "content": "their executives to be active"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "judges to rule out gene patenting", "content": "judges to rule out gene patenting"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'【命题解密】推理引申题。\n【精准定位】定位至首段②至⑤句“Companies had won patents for isolated DNA for decades... But in March 2010 a judge ruled that genes were unpatentable. Executives were violently agitated. The Biotechnology Industry Organisation (BIO), a trade group, assured members that this was just a \'preliminary step\' in a longer battle”。\n几十年来生物技术公司一直拥有分离DNA的专利权；2010年3月法官裁定基因不可申请专利后，高管们反应剧烈、极其愤怒，行业协会BIO也向成员保证这只是漫长抗争的“第一步”。由此反推，生物技术公司迫切希望基因能够申请专利。[A]项“genes to be patentable”准确概括其利益诉求，故选[A]。\n【错项排除】[B]项曲解了BIO的表态，BIO是向成员保证并安抚信心而非发出警告；[C]项将Executives were violently agitated（极其焦虑愤怒）曲解为希望高管活跃起来；[D]项与生物技术公司的诉求完全相反。' WHERE id = 'cfda7ac1-4d18-5303-bad8-b17a34fa8bd9'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Those who are against gene patents believe that ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "genetic tests are not reliable", "content": "genetic tests are not reliable"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "only man-made products are patentable", "content": "only man-made products are patentable"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "patents on genes depend much on innovation", "content": "patents on genes depend much on innovation"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "courts should restrict access to genetic tests", "content": "courts should restrict access to genetic tests"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'【命题解密】人物观点题。\n【精准定位】定位至第三段③句“Critics make three main arguments against gene patents: a gene is a product of nature, so it may not be patented; gene patents suppress innovation rather than reward it; and patents\' monopolies restrict access to genetic tests such as Myriad\'s”。\n反对者提出的三点理由之一是“基因是自然产物，因此不可申请专利”，亦即只有人工造物才具备专利资格。[B]项“only man-made products are patentable”正是这一观点的反向同义改写，故选[B]。\n【错项排除】[A]项文中并未质疑基因检测的可靠性；[C]项与反对者第二条理由“基因专利抑制（suppress）而非奖励创新”逻辑倒置；[D]项将反对者批评专利垄断限制（restrict access）基因检测使用，歪曲为法院应当限制。' WHERE id = 'b9202020-1c0c-5212-b444-100a4b67dd90'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to Hans Sauer, companies are eager to win patents for ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "discovering gene interactions", "content": "discovering gene interactions"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "establishing disease correlations", "content": "establishing disease correlations"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "drawing pictures of genes", "content": "drawing pictures of genes"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "identifying human DNA", "content": "identifying human DNA"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'【命题解密】人物观点题。\n【精准定位】定位至第五段③④句“Firms are now studying how genes interact, looking for correlations that might be used to determine the causes of disease or predict a drug\'s efficacy. Companies are eager to win patents for \'connecting the dots,\' explains Hans Sauer, a lawyer for the BIO”。\nHans Sauer所说的“connecting the dots（连点成线）”紧承上一句，其中dots指单个基因，即企业急于为发现基因间如何相互作用（how genes interact）从而建立关联申请专利。[A]项“discovering gene interactions”准确揭示了这一比喻，故选[A]。\n【错项排除】[B]项“establishing disease correlations”杂糅了disease与correlations，原文looking for correlations指向基因间关联，用于确定疾病成因而非疾病本身间的关联；[C]项“绘制基因图”对connecting the dots望文生义；[D]项“识别人类DNA”属于旧式分子专利，第②句明确指出公司已不太可能继续大量申请人类DNA分子专利。' WHERE id = '583afac4-1e31-5c8b-802e-4e0c0c9a316a'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'By saying "Each meeting was packed" (Line 4, Para. 6), the author means that ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "the supreme court was authoritative", "content": "the supreme court was authoritative"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "the BIO was a powerful organisation", "content": "the BIO was a powerful organisation"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "gene patenting was a great concern", "content": "gene patenting was a great concern"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "lawyers were keen to attend conventions", "content": "lawyers were keen to attend conventions"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'【命题解密】句意推断题。\n【精准定位】定位至第六段②③句“The BIO recently held a convention which included sessions to coach lawyers on the shifting landscape for patents. Each meeting was packed”。\nBIO举办大会并专门开设分场培训律师应对不断变化的专利形势，结果每场会议都座无虚席（Each meeting was packed）。结合前文最高法院将听审Mayo案及基因专利战旷日持久的语境，可见“每场座无虚席”旨在说明整个行业与法律界对基因专利归属问题的高度关注。[C]项“gene patenting was a great concern”揭示了深层含义，故选[C]。\n【错项排除】[A]项“最高法院极具权威”虽相关但并非培训会爆满的原因；[B]项“BIO组织强大”脱离文章基因专利战主旨；[D]项仅停留在律师热衷参会的表面现象。' WHERE id = 'e15b7bdc-2b6d-5dfb-9c5e-7538ddcb1516'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Generally speaking, the author\'s attitude toward gene patenting is ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "critical", "content": "critical"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "supportive", "content": "supportive"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "scornful", "content": "scornful"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "objective", "content": "objective"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'【命题解密】观点态度题。\n【精准定位】纵观全文，作者首先陈述2010年法官裁定基因不可获专利引发业内震动，随后第二段客观报道上诉法院推翻前判及Myriad公司称其为公司与患者的福音，第三至四段如实列出反对者的三大理由、司法部意见以及尚存争议，第五至六段进一步说明行业转向“连点”专利及最高法院即将审理的新讼案。\n全文既不偏袒生物技术公司，也不盲从反对者，而是平实严谨地报道双方交锋与案件走向，态度完全客观中立，故选[D] objective。\n【错项排除】[A] critical（批判的）与[C] scornful（鄙夷的）均带负面偏见，原文未流露否定；[B] supportive（支持的）忽略了作者大篇幅呈递反对声音及司法不确定性。' WHERE id = '497fc799-bb9f-5ae2-9e7f-36e6d1c94bdc'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to Paragraph 2, the recession has made people ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "struggle against each other", "content": "struggle against each other"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "realize the national dream", "content": "realize the national dream"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "challenge their prudence", "content": "challenge their prudence"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "reconsider their lifestyle", "content": "reconsider their lifestyle"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'【命题解密】事实细节题。\n【精准定位】定位至第二段②至④句“Many said that unemployment, while extremely painful, had improved them in some ways: they had become less materialistic and more financially prudent; they were more aware of the struggles of others... At the very least, it has awoken us from our national fever dream of easy riches and bigger houses, and put a necessary end to an era of reckless personal spending”。\n失业者变得不那么贪图物质、理财更为审慎，且大衰退把人们从轻轻松松发财买大房的狂热美梦中惊醒，结束了盲目挥霍的时代。可见大衰退促使人们反思并重新审视自己的生活方式与消费观，故选[D] reconsider their lifestyle。\n【错项排除】[A]项曲解more aware of the struggles of others（更加体谅他人的艰辛），并非彼此斗争；[B]项将awoken us from our national fever dream（从狂热美梦中醒来）反向曲解为实现梦想；[C]项将more financially prudent（在财务上更加审慎）歪曲为质疑自己的审慎。' WHERE id = '44bf494c-3dc9-5568-8c48-ca734a588ab4'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Benjamin Friedman believes that economic recessions may ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "impose a heavier burden on immigrants", "content": "impose a heavier burden on immigrants"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "bring out more evils of human nature", "content": "bring out more evils of human nature"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "promote the advance of rights and freedoms", "content": "promote the advance of rights and freedoms"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "ease conflicts between races and classes", "content": "ease conflicts between races and classes"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'【命题解密】事实细节题。\n【精准定位】定位至第三段②③句“Benjamin Friedman argues that both inside and outside the U.S., lengthy periods of economic stagnation or decline have almost always left society more mean-spirited and less inclusive, and have usually stopped or reversed the advance of rights and freedoms. Anti-immigrant sentiment typically increases, as does conflict between races and classes”。\n弗里德曼指出，长期的经济停滞或衰退几乎总是令社会变得更狭隘刻薄（mean-spirited）、包容性更差，权利与自由受阻甚至倒退，排外与种族阶级冲突加剧。这些均体现经济衰退会激发和暴露出人性中更多丑恶的一面，故选[B] bring out more evils of human nature。\n【错项排除】[A]项将排外情绪升高（Anti-immigrant sentiment increases）偷换为对移民施加更大负担；[C]项与原文stopped or reversed（受阻或倒退）彻底相反；[D]项与conflict... typically increases（冲突加剧）完全相悖。' WHERE id = '4f011eca-7c6d-522d-99c0-b03e9f497b72'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The research of Till Von Wachter suggests that in the recession graduates from elite universities tend to ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "lag behind the others due to decreased opportunities", "content": "lag behind the others due to decreased opportunities"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "catch up quickly with experienced employees", "content": "catch up quickly with experienced employees"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "see their life chances as dimmed as the others\'", "content": "see their life chances as dimmed as the others\'"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "recover more quickly than the others", "content": "recover more quickly than the others"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'【命题解密】事实细节题。\n【精准定位】定位至第四段③句“The research of Till Von Wachter... suggests that not all people graduating into a recession see their life chances dimmed: those with degrees from elite universities catch up fairly quickly to where they otherwise would have been if they had graduated in better times; it is the masses beneath them that are left behind”。\n研究证实名校毕业生能够相当迅速地追回在经济繁荣时期毕业本应达到的职业水平，而落后的是其下的普通大众。即名校毕业生比其他人恢复得更快，故选[D] recover more quickly than the others。\n【错项排除】[A]项把are left behind的主语由普通大众（the masses）张冠李戴为名校毕业生；[B]项把catch up to的对象由“繁荣期毕业本应达到的水平”篡改为“有经验的老员工”；[C]项忽略句首否定not all people，颠倒了名校生与其他人的差异。' WHERE id = '464a2678-2fae-521c-86f2-8ef7d1c02f51'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The author thinks that the influence of hard times on society is ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "text": "trivial", "value": "A", "content": "trivial"}, {"key": "B", "text": "positive", "value": "B", "content": "positive"}, {"key": "C", "text": "certain", "value": "C", "content": "certain"}, {"key": "D", "text": "destructive", "value": "D", "content": "destructive"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'【命题解密】观点态度题。\n【精准定位】定位至第五段④⑤句“We will have to wait and see exactly how these hard times will reshape our social fabric. But they certainly will reshape it, and all the more so the longer they extend”。\n作者指出，艰难时期究竟会如何重塑社会结构尚需观望，但可以确定的是，它一定会重塑社会结构，而且持续时间越长影响越深。因此作者认为艰难时期对社会的影响是确定无疑的（certain），故选[C]。\n【错项排除】[A]项trivial（微不足道的）与首段及末段强调深刻重塑社会相悖；[B]项positive（积极的）和[D]项destructive（毁灭性的）均以偏概全，文章第二段提到有限的积极面，三、四段分析负面效应，但末段明确表示具体形态尚未可知、唯独重塑本身确定无疑。' WHERE id = '6eb415d1-e658-5761-b509-04c6199512bf'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to the text, Niccolò Machiavelli ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "emphasized the virtue of classical heroes.", "content": "emphasized the virtue of classical heroes."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "highlighted the public glory of the leading artists.", "content": "highlighted the public glory of the leading artists."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "focused on epochal figures whose lives were hard to imitate.", "content": "focused on epochal figures whose lives were hard to imitate."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "opened up new realms of understanding the great men in history.", "content": "opened up new realms of understanding the great men in history."}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "held that history should be the story of the masses and their record of struggle.", "content": "held that history should be the story of the masses and their record of struggle."}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "dismissed virtue as unnecessary for successful leaders.", "content": "dismissed virtue as unnecessary for successful leaders."}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "depicted the worthy lives of engineers, industrialists and explorers.", "content": "depicted the worthy lives of engineers, industrialists and explorers."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'F', explanation = E'【命题解密】信息匹配题。定位至第四段“This was the biographical tradition which Niccolo Machiavelli turned on its head. In The Prince, he championed cunning, ruthlessness, and boldness, rather than virtue, mercy and justice, as the skills of successful leaders”。马基雅维利在《君主论》中主张狡诈、无情与果决，而不是仁慈、正义或道德美德，颠覆了传统的英雄传记传统。选项[F]“dismissed virtue as unnecessary for successful leaders（认为美德对成功的领导者是不必要的）”是对championed... rather than virtue的精准概括，故选[F]。' WHERE id = 'c043408b-8192-5d7e-bf6a-d457386a533c'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to the text, Thomas Carlyle ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "emphasized the virtue of classical heroes.", "content": "emphasized the virtue of classical heroes."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "highlighted the public glory of the leading artists.", "content": "highlighted the public glory of the leading artists."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "focused on epochal figures whose lives were hard to imitate.", "content": "focused on epochal figures whose lives were hard to imitate."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "opened up new realms of understanding the great men in history.", "content": "opened up new realms of understanding the great men in history."}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "held that history should be the story of the masses and their record of struggle.", "content": "held that history should be the story of the masses and their record of struggle."}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "dismissed virtue as unnecessary for successful leaders.", "content": "dismissed virtue as unnecessary for successful leaders."}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "depicted the worthy lives of engineers, industrialists and explorers.", "content": "depicted the worthy lives of engineers, industrialists and explorers."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'【命题解密】信息匹配题。\n【精准定位】定位至第五段（即原文倒数第三段）“This was all a bit bourgeois for Thomas Carlyle, who focused his biographies on the truly heroic lives of Martin Luther, Oliver Cromwell and Napoleon Bonaparte. These epochal figures represented lives hard to imitate, but to be acknowledged as possessing higher authority than mere mortals”。\n维多利亚时期思想家托马斯·卡莱尔认为斯迈尔斯的实用主义传记过于中产阶级化，他将笔墨专门聚焦于马丁·路德、奥利弗·克伦威尔和拿破仑等真正的英雄人物，认为这些划时代伟人的人生是难以效仿的。选项[C]“focused on epochal figures whose lives were hard to imitate”直接对应原文These epochal figures represented lives hard to imitate，故选[C]。\n【错项排除】[D]项“opened up new realms of understanding...”出自末段，那是批判卡莱尔英雄史观、转向“自下而上的民众史观”的当代英国史学家（替代卡莱尔者）所开启的新领域，且原文指理解历史的新领域而非伟人。' WHERE id = '62f00516-72ad-56be-b904-29c1fd6fd3c5'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to the text, Marx and Engels ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "emphasized the virtue of classical heroes.", "content": "emphasized the virtue of classical heroes."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "highlighted the public glory of the leading artists.", "content": "highlighted the public glory of the leading artists."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "focused on epochal figures whose lives were hard to imitate.", "content": "focused on epochal figures whose lives were hard to imitate."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "opened up new realms of understanding the great men in history.", "content": "opened up new realms of understanding the great men in history."}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "held that history should be the story of the masses and their record of struggle.", "content": "held that history should be the story of the masses and their record of struggle."}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "dismissed virtue as unnecessary for successful leaders.", "content": "dismissed virtue as unnecessary for successful leaders."}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "depicted the worthy lives of engineers, industrialists and explorers.", "content": "depicted the worthy lives of engineers, industrialists and explorers."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'E', explanation = E'【命题解密】信息匹配题。\n【精准定位】定位至第六段“Not everyone was convinced by such bombast. \'The history of all hitherto existing society is the history of class struggles,\' wrote Marx and Engels in The Communist Manifesto... And history should be the story of the masses and their record of struggle”。\n针对卡莱尔夸大伟人权威的言论，马克思和恩格斯在《共产党宣言》中明确提出历史是阶级斗争的历史，创造财富和进行斗争的是现实的、活生生的人，因此历史应当是人民大众及其斗争记录的故事。选项[E]“held that history should be the story of the masses and their record of struggle”在文中原句复现，故选[E]。\n【错项排除】[D]项属于后世英国大众史学家开辟的新研究领域，非马恩此处原话对应；[B]项“凸显杰出艺术家的公共荣耀”更是与第四段浪漫主义流派提及的“personal experience rather than public glory”双重相悖。' WHERE id = 'ec554780-bf63-5fe6-b157-380260a2aa34'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'In an essay entitled "Making It in America," the author Adam Davidson relates a joke from cotton country about just how much a modern textile mill has been automated: The average mill has only two employees today, "a man and a dog. The man is there to feed the dog, and the dog is there to keep the man away from the machines."\n\nDavidson\'s article is one of a number of pieces that have recently appeared making the point that the reason we have such stubbornly high unemployment and declining middle-class incomes today is largely because of the big drop in demand because of the Great Recession, but it is also because of the advances in both globalization and the information technology revolution, which are more rapidly than ever replacing labor with machines or foreign workers.\n\nIn the past, workers with average skills, doing an average job, could earn an average lifestyle. But, today, average is officially over. Being average just won\'t earn you what it used to. It can\'t when so many more employers have so much more access to so much more above average cheap foreign labor, cheap robotics, cheap software, cheap automation and cheap genius. Therefore, everyone needs to find their extra — their unique value contribution that makes them stand out in whatever is their field of employment.\n\nYes, new technology has been eating jobs forever, and always will. But there\'s been an acceleration. As Davidson notes, "In the 10 years ending in 2009, [U.S.] factories shed workers so fast that they erased almost all the gains of the previous 70 years; roughly one out of every three manufacturing jobs — about 6 million in total — disappeared."\n\nThere will always be change — new jobs, new products, new services. But the one thing we know for sure is that with each advance in globalization and the I.T. revolution, the best jobs will require workers to have more and better education to make themselves above average.\n\nIn a world where average is officially over, there are many things we need to do to support employment, but nothing would be more important than passing some kind of G.I. Bill for the 21st century that ensures that every American has access to post-high school education.' WHERE id = '33384f03-2864-5122-bc64-fb03a46b5193'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'A century ago, the immigrants from across the Atlantic included settlers and sojourners. Along with the many folks looking to make a permanent home in the United States came those who had no intention to stay, and who would make some money and then go home. Between 1908 and 1915, about 7 million people arrived while about 2 million departed. About a quarter of all Italian immigrants, for example, eventually returned to Italy for good. They even had an affectionate nickname, "uccelli di passaggio," birds of passage.\n\nToday, we are much more rigid about immigrants. We divide newcomers into two categories: legal or illegal, good or bad. We hail them as Americans in the making, or brand them as aliens to be kicked out. That framework has contributed mightily to our broken immigration system and the long political paralysis over how to fix it. We don\'t need more categories, but we need to change the way we think about categories. We need to look beyond strict definitions of legal and illegal. To start, we can recognize the new birds of passage, those living and thriving in the gray areas. We might then begin to solve our immigration challenges.\n\nCrop pickers, violinists, construction workers, entrepreneurs, engineers, home health-care aides and physicists are among today\'s birds of passage. They are energetic participants in a global economy driven by the flow of work, money and ideas. They prefer to come and go as opportunity calls them. They can manage to have a job in one place and a family in another.\n\nWith or without permission, they straddle laws, jurisdictions and identities with ease. We need them to imagine the United States as a place where they can be productive for a while without committing themselves to staying forever. We need them to feel that home can be both here and there and that they can belong to two nations honorably.\n\nAccommodating this new world of people in motion will require new attitudes on both sides of the immigration battle. Looking beyond the culture war logic of right or wrong means opening up the middle ground and understanding that managing immigration today requires multiple paths and multiple outcomes, including some that are not easy to accomplish legally in the existing system.' WHERE id = '4f5f933e-cdec-519e-a0eb-fd81bdbbb1bc'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'Europe is not a gender-equality heaven. In particular, the corporate workplace will never be completely family-friendly until women are part of senior management decisions, and Europe\'s top corporate-governance positions remain overwhelmingly male. Indeed, women hold only 14 per cent of positions on European corporate boards.\n\nThe European Union is now considering legislation to compel corporate boards to maintain a certain proportion of women — up to 60 per cent. This proposed mandate was born of frustration. Last year, European Commission Vice President Viviane Reding issued a call to voluntary action. Reding invited corporations to sign up for gender balance goals of 40 per cent female board membership. But her appeal was considered a failure: only 24 companies took it up.\n\nDo we need quotas to ensure that women can continue to climb the corporate ladder fairly as they balance work and family?\n\n"Personally, I don\'t like quotas," Reding said recently. "But I like what the quotas do." Quotas get action: they "open the way to equality and they break through the glass ceiling," according to Reding, a result seen in France and other countries with legally binding provisions on placing women in top business positions.\n\nI understand Reding\'s reluctance — and her frustration. I don\'t like quotas either; they run counter to my belief in meritocracy, governance by the capable. But, when one considers the obstacles to achieving the meritocratic ideal, it does look as if a fairer world must be temporarily ordered.\n\nAfter all, four decades of evidence has now shown that corporations in Europe as well as the US are evading the meritocratic hiring and promotion of women to top positions — no matter how much "soft pressure" is put upon them. When women do break through to the summit of corporate power — as, for example, Sheryl Sandberg recently did at Facebook — they attract massive attention precisely because they remain the exception to the rule.\n\nIf appropriate public policies were in place to help all women—whether CEOs or their children\'s caregivers—and all families, Sandberg would be no more newsworthy than any other highly capable person living in a more just society.' WHERE id = '379cc8f6-b46e-5027-a791-b9c7fe18bc3a'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'The hugely popular blog the Skint Foodie chronicles how Tony balances his love of good food with living on benefits. After bills, Tony has £60 a week to spend, £40 of which goes on food, but 10 years ago he was earning £130,000 a year working in corporate communications and eating at London\'s best restaurants at least twice a week. Then his marriage failed, his career burned out and his drinking became serious. "The community mental health team saved my life. And I felt like that again, to a certain degree, when people responded to the blog so well. It gave me the validation and confidence that I\'d lost. But it\'s still a day-by-day thing." Now he\'s living in a council flat and fielding offers from literary agents. He\'s feeling positive, but he\'ll carry on blogging—not about eating as cheaply as you can—"there are so many people in a much worse state, with barely any money to spend on food"—but eating well on a budget. Here\'s his advice for economical foodies.\n\n[41]\nImpulsive spending isn\'t an option, so plan your week\'s menu in advance, making shopping lists for your ingredients in their exact quantities. I have an Excel template for a week of breakfast, lunch and dinner. Stop laughing: it\'s not just cost effective but helps you balance your diet. It\'s also a good idea to shop daily instead of weekly, because, being human, you\'ll sometimes change your mind about what you fancy.\n\n[42]\nThis is where supermarkets and their anonymity come in handy. With them, there\'s not the same embarrassment as when buying one carrot in a little greengrocer. And if you plan properly, you\'ll know that you only need, say, 350g of shin of beef and six rashers of bacon, not whatever weight is pre-packed in the supermarket chiller.\n\n[43]\nYou may proudly claim to only have frozen peas in the freezer — that\'s not good enough. Mine is filled with leftovers, bread, stock, meat and fish. Planning ahead should eliminate wastage, but if you have surplus vegetables you\'ll do a vegetable soup, and all fruits threatening to "go off" will be cooked or juiced.\n\n[44]\nEveryone says this, but it really is a top tip for frugal eaters. Shop at butchers, delis and fish-sellers regularly, even for small things, and be super friendly. Soon you\'ll feel comfortable asking if they\'ve any knuckles of ham for soups and stews, or beef bones, chicken carcasses and fish heads for stock which, more often than not, they\'ll let you have for free.\n\n[45]\nYou won\'t be eating out a lot, but save your pennies and once every few months treat yourself to a set lunch at a good restaurant — £1.75 a week for three months gives you £21 — more than enough for a three-course lunch at Michelin-starred Arbutus. It\'s £16.95 there — or £12.99 for a large pizza from Domino\'s: I know which I\'d rather eat.' WHERE id = '41ab5bb2-e0e5-59a0-8a10-90ef85d959e7'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [10] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "give up", "content": "give up"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "take over", "content": "take over"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "bring back", "content": "bring back"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "pass down", "content": "pass down"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'【精准定位】空格位于第二段第三句末：...paper checks have the advantage that they provide receipts, something that many consumers are unwilling to [10]。\n【命题解密】考查动词短语辨析。上文提到纸质支票能提供收据凭据这一优势，而许多消费者不愿放弃这种切实的安全感与凭据保障。give up意为“放弃”，符合语境，故选[A]。\n【错项排除】[B] take over意为“接管、接替”；[C] bring back意为“带回、使恢复”；[D] pass down意为“传给后代、流传”，均与放弃纸质收据优势的文意不符。' WHERE id = 'af720887-e550-52e9-ba2e-98442dbbdaad'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [12] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "kept", "content": "kept"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "borrowed", "content": "borrowed"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "withdrawn", "content": "withdrawn"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "released", "content": "released"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'【精准定位】空格位于第二段第四句中：...it takes several days before a check is cashed and funds are [12] from the issuer\'s account...\n【命题解密】考查动词词义辨析。支票兑现流程中，资金需从开票人银行账户中被扣除或提取。withdraw funds from an account意为“从账户中提取/扣除资金”，为金融银行标准表达，故选[C]。\n【错项排除】[A] kept（保留、保存）与资金转出相反；[B] borrowed（借入）与兑付自有支票不符；[D] released（释放、解冻）虽与资金流动相关，但不与from an account搭配表示扣款提取。' WHERE id = 'e667bd2f-1624-568b-be19-c320f0c9b171'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the most suitable subheading from A-G for section [43]:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Shopkeepers are your friends", "content": "Shopkeepers are your friends"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Remember to treat yourself", "content": "Remember to treat yourself"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Stick to what you need", "content": "Stick to what you need"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Live like a peasant", "content": "Live like a peasant"}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "Balance your diet", "content": "Balance your diet"}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "Planning is everything", "content": "Planning is everything"}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "Waste not, want not", "content": "Waste not, want not"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'G', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至 [43] 段落：Planning ahead should eliminate wastage, but if you have surplus vegetables you\'ll do a vegetable soup, and all fruits threatening to "go off" will be cooked or juiced.\n【命题解密】段落核心围绕冷冻室储备与食材再利用展开：提前计划理应消除浪费（eliminate wastage），即便手头有富余蔬菜也用来煮蔬菜汤，快要变质的水果则拿去熬煮或榨汁。G项 Waste not, want not（不浪费则不匮乏）精准概括了杜绝浪费、物尽其用的中心思想。\n【错项排除】[F] Planning is everything 虽然前半句出现 Planning ahead，但随后以 but 转折聚焦于处理剩余食材以避免浪费，并非该段重心；其余选项亦脱离食材零浪费主题。' WHERE id = 'db1d4d8c-5eca-5d2d-88c1-e8e8cfe11078'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'Thinner isn\'t always better. A number of studies have [1] that normal-weight people are in fact at higher risk of some diseases compared to those who are overweight. And there are health conditions for which being overweight is actually [2]. For example, heavier women are less likely to develop calcium deficiency than thin women. [3], among the elderly, being somewhat overweight is often an [4] of good health.\n\nOf even greater [5] is the fact that obesity turns out to be very difficult to define. It is often defined [6] body mass index, or BMI. BMI [7] body mass divided by the square of height. An adult with a BMI of 18 to 25 is often considered to be normal weight. Between 25 and 30 is overweight. And over 30 is considered obese. Obesity, [8], can be divided into moderately obese, severely obese, and very severely obese.\n\nWhile such numerical standards seem [9], they are not. Obesity is probably less a matter of weight than body fat. Some people with a high BMI are in fact extremely fit, [10] others with a low BMI may be in poor [11]. For example, many collegiate and professional football players [12] as obese, though their percentage body fat is low. Conversely, someone with a small frame may have high body fat but a [13] BMI.\n\nToday we have a(n) [14] to label obesity as a disgrace. The overweight are sometimes [15] in the media with their faces covered. Stereotypes [16] with obesity include laziness, lack of will power, and lower prospects for success. Teachers, employers, and health professionals have been shown to harbor biases against the obese. [17] very young children tend to look down on the overweight, and teasing about body build has long been a problem in schools.\n\nNegative attitudes toward obesity, [18] in health concerns, have stimulated a number of anti-obesity [19]. My own hospital system has banned sugary drinks from its facilities. Many employers have instituted weight loss and fitness initiatives. Michelle Obama has launched a high-visibility campaign [20] childhood obesity, even claiming that it represents our greatest national security threat.' WHERE id = 'cbea03e5-b462-5138-8efc-98d151bacba1'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'Emerging in the late Sixties and reaching a peak in the Seventies, Land Art was one of a range of new forms, including Body Art, Performance Art, Action Art and Installation Art, which pushed art beyond the traditional confines of the studio and gallery. Rather than portraying landscape, land artists used the physical substance of the land itself as their medium.\n\nThe British land art, typified by Richard Long\'s piece, was not only more domestically scaled, but a lot quirkier than its American counterpart. Indeed, while you might assume that an exhibition of Land Art would consist only of records of works rather than the works themselves, Long\'s photograph of his work is the work. Since his "action" is in the past, the photograph is its sole embodiment.\n\nThat might seem rather an obscure point, but it sets the tone for an exhibition that contains a lot of black-and-white photographs and relatively few natural objects.\n\nLong is Britain\'s best-known Land Artist and his Stone Circle, a perfect ring of purplish rocks from Portishead beach laid out on the gallery floor, represents the elegant, rarefied side of the form. The Boyle Family, on the other hand, stand for its dirty, urban aspect. Comprising artists Mark Boyle and Joan Hills and their children, they recreated random sections of the British landscape on gallery walls. Their Olaf Street Study, a square of brick-strewn waste ground, is one of the few works here to embrace the commonplaceness that characterises most of our experience of the landscape most of the time.\n\nParks feature, particularly in the earlier works, such as John Hilliard\'s very funny Across the Park, in which a long-haired stroller is variously smiled at by a pretty girl and unwittingly assaulted in a sequence of images that turn out to be different parts of the same photograph.\n\nGenerally however British land artists preferred to get away from towns, gravitating towards landscapes that are traditionally considered beautiful such as the Lake District or the Wiltshire Downs. While it probably wasn\'t apparent at the time, much of this work is permeated by a spirit of romantic escapism that the likes of Wordsworth would have readily understood. Derek Jarman\'s yellow-tinted film Towards Avebury, a collection of long, mostly still shots of the Wiltshire landscape, evokes a tradition of English landscape painting stretching from Samuel Palmer to Paul Nash.\n\nIn the case of Hamish Fulton, you can\'t help feeling that the Scottish artist has simply found a way of making his love of walking pay. A typical work, such as Seven Days, consists of a single beautiful black-and-white photograph taken on an epic walk, with the mileage and number of days taken listed beneath. British Land Art as shown in this well selected, but relatively modestly scaled exhibition wasn\'t about imposing on the landscape, more a kind of landscape-orientated light conceptual art created passing through. It had its origins in the great outdoors, but the results were as gallery-bound as the paintings of Turner and Constable.' WHERE id = 'b4374d5b-74ec-5aaa-815f-3240b17bce48'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [1] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "denied", "content": "denied"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "concluded", "content": "concluded"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "doubted", "content": "doubted"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "ensured", "content": "ensured"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第一段第二句：A number of studies have [1] that normal-weight people are in fact at higher risk of some diseases compared to those who are overweight。\n【命题解密】考查动词语义辨析。首句指出“更瘦并不总是更健康”，第二句用科学研究结果加以印证：多项研究已得出结论（concluded），正常体重者实际上比超重者更容易患上某些疾病，故选[B]。\n【错项排除】[A] denied（否认）与顺承论证逻辑相悖；[C] doubted（怀疑）表否定态度，不合文意；[D] ensured（确保）通常不用于确保患病等负面结果的发生。' WHERE id = 'c47d071f-ee7c-5f48-8460-8da02c75877f'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [2] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "protective", "content": "protective"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "dangerous", "content": "dangerous"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "sufficient", "content": "sufficient"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "troublesome", "content": "troublesome"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第一段第三句：And there are health conditions for which being overweight is actually [2]。\n【命题解密】考查形容词词义辨析。本句与上句构成顺承关系，且下句举出较重女性更不易缺钙为例，说明在某些健康状况下超重其实起到保护性作用（protective），故选[A]。\n【错项排除】[B] dangerous（危险的）与下文不易缺钙的正向例证相反；[C] sufficient（足够的）与健康状况搭配不当且不符合上下文语义；[D] troublesome（麻烦的）带有负面色彩，与文意相悖。' WHERE id = 'fe060b00-501f-5f97-80c6-a7cb95891b32'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [3] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Instead", "content": "Instead"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "However", "content": "However"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Likewise", "content": "Likewise"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Therefore", "content": "Therefore"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第一段第五句句首：[3], among the elderly, being somewhat overweight is often an indicator of good health。\n【命题解密】考查逻辑副词辨析。前一句说明女性群体中体重较重的益处，本句紧接着指出老年人群体中稍微超重也对健康有益。两者属于并列类比关系，[C] Likewise（同样地）准确衔接前后两组相似例证，故选[C]。\n【错项排除】[A] Instead（相反）与[B] However（然而）均表转折对立，与并行例证不符；[D] Therefore（因此）表因果关系，女性与老年人的情况并无因果联系。' WHERE id = '45ece1c8-329c-5aaf-9b0c-cf201064b457'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [4] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "indicator", "content": "indicator"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "objective", "content": "objective"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "origin", "content": "origin"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "example", "content": "example"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第一段第五句：...among the elderly, being somewhat overweight is often an [4] of good health。\n【命题解密】考查名词辨析。本句旨在说明老年人稍微超重往往是身体健康的标志与表征。indicator意为“指示物，标志”，an indicator of good health准确传达出“健康良好的标志”，故选[A]。\n【错项排除】[B] objective（目标）指“超重是健康的目标”，不合逻辑；[C] origin（起源）夸大了体重对健康的决定性；[D] example（例子）中超重不能作为“身体健康”的同类实例。' WHERE id = '3afa9b52-315d-5e9c-97fc-33b72e165e97'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [5] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "impact", "content": "impact"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "relevance", "content": "relevance"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "assistance", "content": "assistance"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "concern", "content": "concern"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第二段首句：Of even greater [5] is the fact that obesity turns out to be very difficult to define。\n【命题解密】考查名词辨析与倒装结构。本句采用“of+抽象名词”作表语的倒装结构，指出“肥胖其实很难定义”这一事实甚至更令人担忧、更值得关注。of concern为固定搭配，意为“令人关切的、重要的”，故选[D]。\n【错项排除】[A] impact（影响）、[B] relevance（相关性/意义）与[C] assistance（帮助）均不如of even greater concern贴合下文对BMI标准误区的批判重心。' WHERE id = 'a9c7c611-990f-5989-b366-3e747864f164'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [6] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "in terms of", "content": "in terms of"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "in case of", "content": "in case of"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "in favor of", "content": "in favor of"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "in respects of", "content": "in respects of"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第二段第二句：It is often defined [6] body mass index, or BMI。\n【命题解密】考查介词短语辨析。此处说明肥胖在常规医学中往往是“根据/依照”身体质量指数（BMI）来界定的。in terms of意为“依据、从……角度/标准而言”，故选[A]。\n【错项排除】[B] in case of（万一，以防）；[C] in favor of（支持，赞成）；[D] in respects of并非地道英语搭配（常用in respect of），均与通过BMI标准进行定义无关。' WHERE id = '284b21dc-f190-5c50-bf77-ecaf43a2c720'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [7] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "measures", "content": "measures"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "determines", "content": "determines"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "equals", "content": "equals"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "modifies", "content": "modifies"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第二段第三句：BMI [7] body mass divided by the square of height。\n【命题解密】考查动词词义辨析。本句给出BMI指数的计算公式，即“BMI等于体重除以身高的平方”。equals意为“（数值、大小等）等于”，符合数学定义表达，故选[C]。\n【错项排除】[A] measures（测量）的宾语通常为长度、尺寸等物理量而非除法公式；[B] determines（决定）将公式与指标的因果关系颠倒；[D] modifies（修改）意为人为调整，不合公式运算语义。' WHERE id = '4e7548db-6ee3-578b-8129-317bf4268860'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [8] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "in essence", "content": "in essence"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "in contrast", "content": "in contrast"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "in turn", "content": "in turn"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "in part", "content": "in part"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第二段末句：Obesity, [8], can be divided into moderately obese, severely obese, and very severely obese。\n【命题解密】考查插入语逻辑辨析。前文按BMI数值划分出正常、超重与肥胖三大类别，此处进一步说明“肥胖”这一类别又可依次划分为中度、重度和极重度三个亚类。in turn意为“进而、反过来、转而”，体现层层递进的分类关系，故选[C]。\n【错项排除】[A] in essence（本质上）与分类列举无关；[B] in contrast（相比之下）错加对比关系；[D] in part（部分地）与全面划分为三类逻辑不符。' WHERE id = '7faeae94-1164-5fae-b224-69bdbcb002f1'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [9] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "complicated", "content": "complicated"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "conservative", "content": "conservative"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "variable", "content": "variable"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "straightforward", "content": "straightforward"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第三段首句：While such numerical standards seem [9], they are not。\n【命题解密】考查形容词辨析。上段列举了一系列清晰的BMI划分数值，本段首句借助While引导让步转折，指出这些数字标准“表面上看起来直接明了（straightforward），实则并非如此”，从而引出BMI测量的局限性，故选[D]。\n【错项排除】[A] complicated（复杂的）与下句“they are not”转折后的“肥胖难以界定”产生逻辑冲突；[B] conservative（保守的）；[C] variable（多变的）均非BMI固定区间数值给人的直观印象。' WHERE id = 'e4eeb8be-1f00-5d99-8019-11eed31626e3'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [10] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "so", "content": "so"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "while", "content": "while"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "since", "content": "since"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "unless", "content": "unless"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第三段第三句：Some people with a high BMI are in fact extremely fit, [10] others with a low BMI may be in poor [11]。\n【命题解密】考查并列连词语义逻辑。前半句说高BMI的人其实可能非常健壮，后半句说低BMI的人反而可能健康不佳。前后形成鲜明对比，while作并列连词可意为“然而、而”，精准衔接对比两分句，故选[B]。\n【错项排除】[A] so（因此）和[C] since（因为）均错置因果逻辑；[D] unless（除非）误设条件关系。' WHERE id = 'e3ad617d-8b01-5d08-a07e-8d374401a6d3'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [11] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "shape", "content": "shape"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "spirit", "content": "spirit"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "balance", "content": "balance"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "taste", "content": "taste"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第三段第三句后半句：...others with a low BMI may be in poor [11]。\n【命题解密】考查名词固定搭配。与前半句extremely fit（极其健壮）形成对照，此处表示BMI较低的人体格或健康状况可能很差。in poor shape意为“身体状况不佳、状态差”，为常见固定搭配，故选[A]。\n【错项排除】[B] spirit（情绪/精神，in poor spirit指士气低落）偏离身体健康话题；[C] balance（平衡）和[D] taste（品味）均不与in poor搭配表示体质好坏。' WHERE id = '086782b4-300e-55b9-9e5f-c5c8f99c96e7'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [12] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "start", "content": "start"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "qualify", "content": "qualify"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "retire", "content": "retire"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "stay", "content": "stay"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第三段第四句：For example, many collegiate and professional football players [12] as obese, though their percentage body fat is low。\n【命题解密】考查动词固定搭配。全句以体脂率极低的橄榄球运动员为例，说明他们在BMI标准下竟“算作/被归类为”肥胖人群。qualify as意为“符合标准、可算作是”，故选[B]。\n【错项排除】[A] start as（最初作为）、[C] retire as（退休时担任）、[D] stay as（保持作为）均无法表达按数值标准被界定归类的含义。' WHERE id = 'e92a1113-deeb-5952-a399-807817c59cba'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [13] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "strange", "content": "strange"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "changeable", "content": "changeable"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "normal", "content": "normal"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "constant", "content": "constant"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第三段末句：Conversely, someone with a small frame may have high body fat but a [13] BMI。\n【命题解密】考查形容词上下文对比。Conversely承接上文“高BMI却体脂低”的运动员案例，给出相反情形：骨架较小的人可能体脂率偏高，却拥有一个看似“正常的（normal）”BMI指数，从而再次证明BMI失准，故选[C]。\n【错项排除】[A] strange（奇怪的）；[B] changeable（易变的）；[D] constant（恒定的）均无法与上文形成“体脂高 vs BMI正常”的鲜明反差。' WHERE id = '348562b7-7507-5632-b0ed-928a1dc0db81'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [14] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "option", "content": "option"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "reason", "content": "reason"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "opportunity", "content": "opportunity"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "tendency", "content": "tendency"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第四段首句：Today we have a(n) [14] to label obesity as a disgrace。\n【命题解密】考查名词辨析与习惯搭配。下文提到媒体遮挡肥胖者面部、将肥胖与懒惰挂钩以及校园欺凌，可见当代社会普遍存在一种把肥胖视作耻辱的倾向。have a tendency to do sth意为“有做某事的倾向”，故选[D]。\n【错项排除】[A] option（选择，与a(n)搭配多指具体可选项）；[B] reason（理由）和[C] opportunity（机会）代入后意为“有理由/有机会羞辱肥胖者”，与作者批判社会偏见的立场不符。' WHERE id = '3132c05e-404a-5208-a6c8-04a62d4e93a4'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [15] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "employed", "content": "employed"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "pictured", "content": "pictured"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "imitated", "content": "imitated"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "monitored", "content": "monitored"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第四段第二句：The overweight are sometimes [15] in the media with their faces covered。\n【命题解密】考查动词语义与语境搭配。句中in the media与with their faces covered明确提示新闻媒体报道中的视觉画面处理——超重者在媒体影像中“被拍摄/被呈现（pictured）”时脸部常被遮挡，故选[B]。\n【错项排除】[A] employed（雇佣）；[C] imitated（模仿）；[D] monitored（监控）均与媒体配图遮面报道不符。' WHERE id = '24489621-4838-54eb-b452-201b41627c20'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [16] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "compared", "content": "compared"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "combined", "content": "combined"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "settled", "content": "settled"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "associated", "content": "associated"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第四段第三句：Stereotypes [16] with obesity include laziness, lack of will power, and lower prospects for success。\n【命题解密】考查动词分词短语搭配。句中列举的懒惰、缺乏意志力都是社会加诸于肥胖身上的固有偏见。associated with意为“与……相关联的”，Stereotypes associated with obesity意为“与肥胖相关的刻板印象”，故选[D]。\n【错项排除】[A] compared with（与……相比）、[B] combined with（与……结合）、[C] settled with（与……和解）均不与stereotypes搭配。' WHERE id = '7db94059-d5cd-5606-9c6b-23ab632fb38f'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [17] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Even", "content": "Even"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Still", "content": "Still"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Yet", "content": "Yet"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Only", "content": "Only"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第四段第五句句首：[17] very young children tend to look down on the overweight...\n【命题解密】考查上下文递进逻辑。前文提到成年人及教师、雇主、医护人员都对肥胖存有偏见，紧接着本句指出“甚至（Even）”连年幼的孩童也往往看不起超重者。Even在此表强烈递进与惊讶语气，故选[A]。\n【错项排除】[B] Still（仍然）与[C] Yet（然而）多表转折让步；[D] Only（仅仅）说只有小孩歧视肥胖者，与前文教师、雇主等歧视矛盾。' WHERE id = 'be304574-0e8f-5f8b-973d-fccc3123aa15'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [18] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "despised", "content": "despised"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "corrected", "content": "corrected"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "ignored", "content": "ignored"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "grounded", "content": "grounded"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第五段首句：Negative attitudes toward obesity, [18] in health concerns, have stimulated a number of anti-obesity [19]。\n【命题解密】考查动词固定搭配。对肥胖的负面态度“立足于/源于（grounded in）”健康顾虑，从而催生了诸多抗击肥胖的政策举措。be grounded in意为“建立在……基础上，基于”，过去分词短语作后置定语，故选[D]。\n【错项排除】[A] despised（鄙视）、[B] corrected（纠正）、[C] ignored（忽视）均无法与in health concerns构成合乎逻辑的原因状语定语。' WHERE id = '35582ce5-7c8b-576c-b736-4597c750ec83'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [19] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "discussions", "content": "discussions"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "businesses", "content": "businesses"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "policies", "content": "policies"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "studies", "content": "studies"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第五段首句末：...have stimulated a number of anti-obesity [19]。\n【命题解密】考查名词辨析与下文例证对应。紧随其后的句子列举了三项落地措施：医院禁止含糖饮料、雇主推出健身计划、米歇尔·奥巴马发起全国倡议。能够涵盖这些具体行政和机构举措的词是policies（政策，办法），故选[C]。\n【错项排除】[A] discussions（讨论）侧重口头层面；[B] businesses（商业业务）；[D] studies（研究）均无法概括禁售饮料和企业健身体制等行动举措。' WHERE id = '931f41ad-0226-5c50-9302-957fcb66c826'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [20] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "for", "content": "for"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "against", "content": "against"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "with", "content": "with"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "without", "content": "without"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第五段末句：Michelle Obama has launched a high-visibility campaign [20] childhood obesity...\n【命题解密】考查介词词义与语境搭配。米歇尔·奥巴马发起了一场高调的宣传运动，旨在“对抗/遏制”儿童肥胖问题。a campaign against sth意为“针对/反对……的运动”，完全契合下文将其视为国家安全威胁的打击立场，故选[B]。\n【错项排除】[A] for（支持，赞成）与遏制儿童肥胖的立场相反；[C] with和[D] without均不与campaign搭配表示“对抗某种问题”。' WHERE id = '435f2cec-4275-5a02-a27e-d3d280b2f077'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to Dunn and Norton, which of the following is the most rewarding purchase?', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "A big house.", "content": "A big house."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "A special tour.", "content": "A special tour."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "A stylish car.", "content": "A stylish car."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "A rich meal.", "content": "A rich meal."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第二段第四至五句：“It is far better to spend money on experiences, say Ms Dunn and Mr Norton, like interesting trips, unique meals or even going to the cinema.”\n【命题解密】考查事实细节。邓恩与诺顿明确建议与其购买汽车豪宅，不如把钱花在难忘的经历上，比如有趣的旅行（interesting trips）或独特的餐食。[B]项“A special tour（一次特别的旅行）”精准同义替换interesting trips，故选[B]。\n【错项排除】[A] A big house与[C] A stylish car属于上句明确批判满意度会快速消退的物质消费（fancy cars and extravagant homes）；[D] A rich meal偷换了unique meals（独特的餐饮体验），rich强调油腻丰盛/昂贵而非独特记忆。' WHERE id = '958e0232-96c7-5c40-979e-c595a7218e10'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The author\'s attitude toward Americans\' watching TV is', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "critical", "content": "critical"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "supportive", "content": "supportive"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "sympathetic", "content": "sympathetic"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "ambiguous", "content": "ambiguous"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第三段第二句：“It seems most people would be better off if they could shorten their commutes to work, spend more time with friends and family and less of it watching television (something the average American spends a whopping two months a year doing, and is hardly jollier for it).”\n【命题解密】考查观点态度。作者用a whopping（惊人的、高达）形容美国人每年耗在看电视上的时间长达两个月，并指出他们却并未因此更快乐（hardly jollier for it），建议少看电视以增加幸福感。字里行间体现作者对沉迷看电视的明确批评态度，故选[A] critical。\n【错项排除】[B] supportive（支持的）完全相反；[C] sympathetic（同情的）误解了hardly jollier的批评语气；[D] ambiguous（模棱两可的）忽略了作者明确的建议倾向。' WHERE id = 'b27dd00d-8f50-5876-96de-0828c089977c'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'McRib is mentioned in Paragraph 3 to show that', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "consumers are sometimes irrational", "content": "consumers are sometimes irrational"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "popularity usually comes after quality", "content": "popularity usually comes after quality"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "marketing tricks are often effective", "content": "marketing tricks are often effective"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "rarity generally increases pleasure", "content": "rarity generally increases pleasure"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第三段第三至四句：“...and luxuries are most enjoyable when they are consumed sparingly. This is apparently the reason McDonald\'s restricts the availability of its popular McRib — a marketing trick that has turned the pork sandwich into an object of obsession.”\n【命题解密】考查例证题。麦当劳刻意限制烤汁猪排堡供应期的案例紧承上句论点“适度节制消费奢侈品时才最令人愉悦”，旨在论证“稀缺性通常能增强愉悦体验”，故选[D] rarity generally increases pleasure。\n【错项排除】[A]项“消费者不理智”曲解顾客的痴迷；[B]项“流行源于品质”原文未谈及产品品质；[C]项“营销技巧常有效”过度泛化，且McRib案例重在揭示“限量稀缺提升快感”这一心理规律而非赞颂营销。' WHERE id = '37839295-9353-5e12-9f0f-016dcf69126c'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to the last paragraph, Happy Money', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "has left much room for readers\' criticism", "content": "has left much room for readers\' criticism"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "may prove to be a worthwhile purchase", "content": "may prove to be a worthwhile purchase"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "has predicted a wider income gap in the US", "content": "has predicted a wider income gap in the US"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "may give its readers a sense of achievement", "content": "may give its readers a sense of achievement"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第四段末两句：“Not everyone will agree with the authors\' policy ideas... But most people will come away from this book believing it was money well spent.”\n【命题解密】考查推理细节。末句借助But强烈转折指出，尽管并非人人都会赞同书中具体的政策建议，但绝大多数读者读完《快乐金钱》后都会认为“这钱花得很值”（money well spent），故选[B] may prove to be a worthwhile purchase。\n【错项排除】[A]项“为读者批评留下很大空间”将Not everyone will agree夸大；[C]项“预测美国收入差距扩大”无中生有，前文只对比了富国与穷国；[D]项“给读者带来成就感”张冠李戴了读者对书中如何花钱获得满足感的认知。' WHERE id = '560c686e-741e-5c45-827a-df55a7121773'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'This text mainly discusses how to', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "balance feeling good and spending money", "content": "balance feeling good and spending money"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "spend large sums of money won in lotteries", "content": "spend large sums of money won in lotteries"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "obtain lasting satisfaction from money spent", "content": "obtain lasting satisfaction from money spent"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "become more reasonable in spending on luxuries", "content": "become more reasonable in spending on luxuries"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'【精准定位】通读全文主旨，首段引出中奖能否带来“lasting feelings of fulfilment（持久的满足感）”，第二至四段介绍两位学者提出的科学花钱方法并高度评价该书值得买。\n【命题解密】考查主旨大意。全文自始至终探讨的核心议题是如何更明智地花钱以获得长期的幸福与满足感，故选[C] obtain lasting satisfaction from money spent。\n【错项排除】[A]项“平衡快乐感与花钱”曲解末段“快乐感与替别人花钱的关联”；[B]项“如何花掉彩票巨奖”仅是首段引子；[D]项“更理性购买奢侈品”属于第三段细节之一，无法概括全篇。' WHERE id = 'ca84105c-0599-54e4-a76a-153666e6c28c'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to the first paragraph, social psychologists have found that', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "our self-ratings are unrealistically high", "content": "our self-ratings are unrealistically high"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "illusory superiority is a baseless effect", "content": "illusory superiority is a baseless effect"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "our need for leadership is unnatural", "content": "our need for leadership is unnatural"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "self-enhancing strategies are ineffective", "content": "self-enhancing strategies are ineffective"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第一段第三句：“Social psychologists have amassed oceans of research into what they call the \'above average effect\', or \'illusory superiority\', and shown that, for example, 70% of us rate ourselves as above average in leadership, 93% in driving and 85% at getting on well with others — all obviously statistical impossibilities.”\n【命题解密】考查事实细节。高达70%、93%和85%的人自认为高于平均水平，这在统计学上是不可能的，证明人们普遍存在“虚幻的优越感”，自我评价高得脱离实际，故选[A] our self-ratings are unrealistically high。\n【错项排除】[B]项将“统计上不可能”歪曲为该心理学效应没有根据（baseless）；[C]项将70%自认为领导力超常曲解为对领导力的需求不正常；[D]项“自我美化策略无效”与文中人们借此维持自信的事实相悖。' WHERE id = 'c077feae-4c61-5ebd-aa26-cb9176208bab'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Visual recognition is believed to be people\'s', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "rapid matching", "content": "rapid matching"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "conscious choice", "content": "conscious choice"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "intuitive response", "content": "intuitive response"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "automatic self-defence", "content": "automatic self-defence"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第三段第二句：“Visual recognition, reads the study, is \'an automatic psychological process, occurring rapidly and intuitively with little or no apparent conscious deliberation\'.”\n【命题解密】考查事实细节。研究报告明文定义“视觉识别”是一种快速、凭借直觉、几乎没有有意识思考的自发心理过程。intuitive response（直觉反应）精准对应intuitively，故选[C]。\n【错项排除】[A]项rapid matching将心理反应偷换为机械配对；[B]项conscious choice与little or no apparent conscious deliberation彻底相反；[D]项automatic self-defence拼凑了automatic与第二段对批评作防卫反应（defensive）。' WHERE id = '562914d4-088b-50bb-adc5-01a0c2677ec5'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Epley found that people with higher self-esteem tended to', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "underestimate their insecurities", "content": "underestimate their insecurities"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "believe in their attractiveness", "content": "believe in their attractiveness"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "cover up their depressions", "content": "cover up their depressions"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "oversimplify their illusions", "content": "oversimplify their illusions"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第四段第二至三句：“In fact, those who thought that the images higher up the attractiveness scale were real directly corresponded with those who showed other markers for having higher self-esteem.”\n【命题解密】考查事实细节。Epley的实验结果显示，越是将被显著美化的照片当作真实自我的人，其自尊水平（higher self-esteem）的其他测量指标也越高，即自尊心较强的人往往深信自己极具魅力，故选[B] believe in their attractiveness。\n【错项排除】[A]项与原文否定“并非为了弥补不安全感（make up for profound insecurities）”相悖；[C]项曲解末句“抑郁的人不会自我美化”；[D]项将“不是个人妄想”篡改为过度简化幻觉。' WHERE id = '021f1bdc-b579-5be9-8c90-8160276bbf8f'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The word "viscerally" (Line 2, Para. 5) is closest in meaning to', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "instinctively", "content": "instinctively"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "occasionally", "content": "occasionally"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "particularly", "content": "particularly"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "aggressively", "content": "aggressively"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第五段第一句：“Knowing the results of Epley\'s study, it makes sense that many people hate photographs of themselves viscerally — on one level, they don\'t even recognise the person in the picture as themselves.”\n【命题解密】考查词义推断。前文指出视觉识图是瞬间自发且靠直觉的无意识心理过程，所以当人们看到未经美化的真实照片时，由于不认识那个不如想象中漂亮的人，会由衷、本能地排斥讨厌自己的照片。viscerally意为“发自内心/本能地”，与[A] instinctively完全同义，故选[A]。\n【错项排除】[B] occasionally（偶尔）；[C] particularly（尤其）；[D] aggressively（攻击性地/极力地）均不能与前文的无意识直觉反应呼应。' WHERE id = 'fe2e5928-ce45-53c6-b338-b4cd59f2443d'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'It can be inferred that Facebook is a self-enhancer\'s paradise because people can', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "present their dishonest profiles", "content": "present their dishonest profiles"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "define their traditional lifestyles", "content": "define their traditional lifestyles"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "share their intellectual pursuits", "content": "share their intellectual pursuits"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "withhold their unflattering sides", "content": "withhold their unflattering sides"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第五段第二至三句：“Facebook, therefore, is a self-enhancer\'s paradise, where people can share only the most flattering photos, the cream of their wit, style, beauty, intellect and lifestyles. It\'s not that people\'s profiles are dishonest... \'but they portray an idealised version of themselves.\'”\n【命题解密】考查细节推断。在Facebook上，人们可以只分享最奉承美化的照片以及机智、品位和生活方式中最精彩的部分，亦即可以筛选隐藏自己平庸、不讨喜的一面，从而构建理想化的个人形象，故选[D] withhold their unflattering sides。\n【错项排除】[A]项与下句明文否定“It\'s not that people\'s profiles are dishonest”直接矛盾；[B]项“定义传统生活方式”无中生有；[C]项把才智精华偷换为学术/知识追求且以偏概全。' WHERE id = 'b78f7600-b58a-5842-a18f-db7c5d3e8310'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to the first paragraph, economic downturns would', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "ease the competition of man vs. machine", "content": "ease the competition of man vs. machine"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "highlight machines\' threat to human jobs", "content": "highlight machines\' threat to human jobs"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "provoke a painful technological revolution", "content": "provoke a painful technological revolution"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "outmode our current economic structure", "content": "outmode our current economic structure"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第一段第一句：“The concept of man versus machine is at least as old as the industrial revolution, but this phenomenon tends to be most acutely felt during economic downturns and fragile recoveries.”\n【命题解密】考查事实细节。人机竞争虽历史悠久，但在经济下行与脆弱复苏期间这种感受最为剧烈尖锐，也就是说经济衰退会凸显机器取代人类工作的紧迫威胁，故选[B] highlight machines\' threat to human jobs。\n【错项排除】[A] ease（缓和）与most acutely felt相反；[C]项颠倒因果，是既有技术加剧失业而非衰退引发技术革命；[D]项将“被机器淘汰的岗位”与“重塑经济结构”混为一谈。' WHERE id = 'a51d825e-44ee-5ade-81df-d0b352b0ed0d'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The authors of Race Against the Machine argue that', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "technology is diminishing man\'s job opportunities", "content": "technology is diminishing man\'s job opportunities"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "automation is accelerating technological development", "content": "automation is accelerating technological development"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "certain jobs will remain intact after automation", "content": "certain jobs will remain intact after automation"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "man will finally win the race against machine", "content": "man will finally win the race against machine"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第二段第一至二句：“When there is rapid improvement in the price and performance of technology, jobs that were once thought to be immune from automation suddenly become threatened. This argument has attracted a lot of attention, via the success of the book Race Against the Machine...”\n【命题解密】考查人物观点。《与机器赛跑》的两位作者主张：随着技术价格下降和性能飞跃，连过去认为不受自动化影响的工作也突然岌岌可危，即技术正在不断蚕食减少人类的就业机会，故选[A] technology is diminishing man\'s job opportunities。\n【错项排除】[B]项颠倒了技术提升与自动化的关系；[C]项与“曾被认为不受影响的工作也受到威胁”相反；[D]项错将书名Race Against the Machine理解为人会赢得竞赛，而书作者重在警示就业缩水。' WHERE id = '53ba190a-e9f6-5ec0-8e77-a09feda0d31b'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Hagel argues that jobs in the U.S. are often', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "performed by innovative minds", "content": "performed by innovative minds"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "scripted with an individual style", "content": "scripted with an individual style"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "standardized without a clear target", "content": "standardized without a clear target"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "designed against human creativity", "content": "designed against human creativity"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第四段第一至二句：“Hagel says we have designed jobs in the U.S. that tend to be \'tightly scripted\' and \'highly standardized\' ones that leave no room for \'individual initiative or creativity\'.”\n【命题解密】考查人物观点。Hagel一针见血地指出美国工作岗位被设计得高度脚本化、高度标准化，完全没有留给个人主动性与创造力的空间，故选[D] designed against human creativity。\n【错项排除】[A]项与不留创造力空间相反；[B]项将scripted与individual杂糅，曲解了限制个性的严格脚本；[C]项把a giant target sign（令工人变成被机器替代的大靶子）偷换为工作缺乏清晰目标。' WHERE id = 'e7c8fbdd-05dc-57a7-b94d-ec983baee0ab'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to the last paragraph, Brynjolfsson and McAfee discussed', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "the predictability of machine behavior in practice", "content": "the predictability of machine behavior in practice"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "the formula for how work is conducted efficiently", "content": "the formula for how work is conducted efficiently"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "the ways machines replace human labor in modern times", "content": "the ways machines replace human labor in modern times"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "the necessity of human involvement in the workplace", "content": "the necessity of human involvement in the workplace"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第六段（末段）第一至三句：“As Hagel notes, Brynjolfsson and McAfee indeed touched on this point in their book. We need to reframe race against the machine as race with the machine. In other words, we need to look at the ways in which machines can augment human labor rather than replace it.”\n【命题解密】考查事实细节。末段首句“this point”虽承接前文，但随后两句直接阐述两位作者书中触及的观点：我们需要寻找机器“增强”而非替代人类劳动的方法，将人与机器的对抗重塑为人机协作，肯定了工作场所中人类参与的不可替代性，故选[D] the necessity of human involvement in the workplace。\n【错项排除】[A]与[B]项属于第五段Hagel本人论述内容，并非末段Brynjolfsson与McAfee书中观点；[C]项与原文“增强人类劳动而不是替代它（rather than replace it）”完全相反。' WHERE id = '2b56a8c1-55df-5a85-9ebf-db130a0cfc37'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Which of the following could be the most appropriate title for the text?', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "How to Innovate Our Work Practices?", "content": "How to Innovate Our Work Practices?"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Machines Will Replace Human Labor", "content": "Machines Will Replace Human Labor"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Can We Win the Race Against Machines?", "content": "Can We Win the Race Against Machines?"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Economic Downturns Stimulate Innovations", "content": "Economic Downturns Stimulate Innovations"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'【精准定位】综合全文脉络，第一、二段提出机器在衰退期吞噬就业岗位引出《与机器赛跑》的焦虑，第三至五段借Hagel指出问题根源在于僵化的工作设计而非技术本身，末段点明应当重塑工作制度与模式、与机器共舞。\n【命题解密】考查文章标题。全文围绕“人类能否在这场与机器的角逐中胜出”这一核心悬念层层剥茧并给出制度创新之道，故选[C] Can We Win the Race Against Machines?。\n【错项排除】[A]项仅指末段一句总结，无法涵盖前五段背景探讨；[B]项“机器将取代人类”只代表第二段担忧，违背末段人机协作主旨；[D]项偏离全文人机就业主题。' WHERE id = '65bdca81-b9e7-57a0-8536-ce63c9301ba1'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The author believes that the housing sector', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "has attracted much attention", "content": "has attracted much attention"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "has lost its real value in economy", "content": "has lost its real value in economy"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "shoulders too much responsibility", "content": "shoulders too much responsibility"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "involves certain political factors", "content": "involves certain political factors"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第二段末句：“But perhaps the most significant reason is that the issue has always been so politically charged.”\n【命题解密】考查事实细节。在探讨政府谈论基础设施时为何很少提及住房行业的原因时，作者最后强调最关键的症结在于该议题向来具有极强的政治敏感性（politically charged），即住房行业牵涉某些政治因素，故选[D] involves certain political factors。\n【错项排除】[A]项与首段seldom mentioned及第二段hard to shove for attention相反；[B]项曲解第二段第二句“未能有效传达自身对经济增长的真实价值”，不等于失去价值；[C]项将to some extent... must shoulder the blame（在某种程度上应负一定责任）过度引申为承担太多责任。' WHERE id = '0de3a9cb-cd30-5a8c-9cad-5d9d88cfb7f3'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'It can be learned that affordable housing has', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "suffered government biases", "content": "suffered government biases"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "increased its home supply", "content": "increased its home supply"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "offered spending opportunities", "content": "offered spending opportunities"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "disappointed the government", "content": "disappointed the government"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第四段第一至二句：“The comprehensive spending review offers an opportunity for the government to help rectify this. It needs to put historical prejudices to one side and take some steps to address our urgent housing need.”\n【命题解密】考查细节推断。作者呼吁政府利用综合开支审查的契机“把历史偏见（historical prejudices）放到一边”来纠正住房紧缺局面，由此可推知经济适用房长期以来遭受了政府的偏见，故选[A] suffered government biases。\n【错项排除】[B]项与第三段not building enough new homes相悖；[C]项把“综合开支审查提供契机”误套在经济适用房上；[D]项错将民众对严峻房市的绝望（desperate）当作令政府失望。' WHERE id = '3e6064a7-5f7d-59ba-b898-1ce2429ff9a4'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to Paragraph 5, George Osborne may', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "prepare to reduce housing stock debt", "content": "prepare to reduce housing stock debt"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "release a lifted GDP growth forecast", "content": "release a lifted GDP growth forecast"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "allow greater government debt for housing", "content": "allow greater government debt for housing"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "stop local authorities from building homes", "content": "stop local authorities from building homes"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第五段第二至三句：“The communities minister, Don Foster, has hinted that George Osborne, Chancellor of the Exchequer, may introduce more flexibility to the current cap on the amount that local authorities can borrow against their housing stock debt.”\n【命题解密】考查事实细节。财政大臣George Osborne可能会对地方政府以住房存量债务为抵押的借款上限采取更大的灵活性（即放宽借贷上限），从而允许为住房建设举借更多政府债务，故选[C] allow greater government debt for housing。\n【错项排除】[A]项把“提高地方政府举债上限”曲解为“减少住房存量债务”；[B]项把raising GDP by 0.6%的预测数据安在Osborne身上且偷换了前提；[D]项与抬高上限以建6万套新房（build extra new homes）截然相反。' WHERE id = 'a3f06882-ace5-5327-a651-bcb38884191d'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'It can be inferred that a stable rental environment would', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "lower the costs of registered providers", "content": "lower the costs of registered providers"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "relieve the ministers of responsibilities", "content": "relieve the ministers of responsibilities"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "contribute to funding new developments", "content": "contribute to funding new developments"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "lessen the impact of government interference", "content": "lessen the impact of government interference"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第六段：“Ministers should also look at creating greater certainty in the rental environment, which would have a significant impact on the ability of registered providers to fund new developments from revenues.”\n【命题解密】考查细节推断。若政府能为租房市场创造更大的确定性与稳定性，将对注册住房供应机构依靠营业收入为新建项目筹集资金（fund new developments）产生显著积极影响，故选[C] contribute to funding new developments。\n【错项排除】[A]项“降低成本”文中未提；[B]项“减轻大臣责任”与正文呼吁大臣积极作为（should also look at）相反；[D]项“减少政府干预影响”属于无中生有。' WHERE id = 'f19c6b9b-534b-5026-a0a0-e8cb735e12eb'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The author believes that after 2015, the government may', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "implement more policies to support housing", "content": "implement more policies to support housing"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "stop generous funding to the housing sector", "content": "stop generous funding to the housing sector"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "renew the affordable housing grants programme", "content": "renew the affordable housing grants programme"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "review the need for large-scale public grants", "content": "review the need for large-scale public grants"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第七段第二至四句：“...we must face up to the fact that the existing £4.5bn programme of grants to fund new affordable housing, set to expire in 2015, is unlikely to be extended beyond then... The housing sector needs to accept that we are very unlikely to ever return to the era of large-scale public grants.”\n【命题解密】考查作者观点。作者明言2015年到期的45亿英镑保障房拨款计划届时不太可能续期，工党亦表明会沿用缩减计划，今后很难回到大规模公共财政拨款年代，即2015年后政府可能停止向住房部门提供慷慨资金支持，故选[B] stop generous funding to the housing sector。\n【错项排除】[A]项“实施更多政策支持”违背整段指出的单靠政府拨款已不可持续的基调；[C]项“延续拨款项目”与unlikely to be extended直接相反；[D]项“重新审查大规模拨款需求”与文中不再回到大规模公共拨款时代的定论相悖。' WHERE id = '333aa60c-b2a0-557b-ac02-3a29e5d736ad'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Match the artwork \'Stone Circle\' with the statement that best reflects its artistic character (A-G):', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "originates from a long walk that the artist took.", "content": "originates from a long walk that the artist took."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "illustrates a kind of landscape-orientated light conceptual art.", "content": "illustrates a kind of landscape-orientated light conceptual art."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "reminds people of the English landscape painting tradition.", "content": "reminds people of the English landscape painting tradition."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "represents the elegance of the British land art.", "content": "represents the elegance of the British land art."}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "depicts the ordinary side of the British land art.", "content": "depicts the ordinary side of the British land art."}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "embodies a romantic escape into the Scottish outdoors.", "content": "embodies a romantic escape into the Scottish outdoors."}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "contains images from different parts of the same photograph.", "content": "contains images from different parts of the same photograph."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第四段首句：“Long is Britain\'s best-known Land Artist and his Stone Circle, a perfect ring of purplish rocks from Portishead beach laid out on the gallery floor, represents the elegant, rarefied side of the form.”\n【命题解密】考查多项对应。理查德·朗的作品《石环》（Stone Circle）在画廊地面用紫色卵石摆出完美圆环，明确代表着英国大地艺术优雅高洁的一面。选项[D]“represents the elegance of the British land art”精准对应原文elegant side of the form，故选[D]。\n【错项排除】[B]项指展览尾段对英国大地艺术总体特征的概括；[E]项对应博伊尔家族的《奥拉夫街研究》，与《石环》相反。' WHERE id = '143e03d1-ee7e-5188-bec3-f83f5ee4bda0'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Match the artwork \'Olaf Street Study\' with the statement that best reflects its artistic character (A-G):', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "originates from a long walk that the artist took.", "content": "originates from a long walk that the artist took."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "illustrates a kind of landscape-orientated light conceptual art.", "content": "illustrates a kind of landscape-orientated light conceptual art."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "reminds people of the English landscape painting tradition.", "content": "reminds people of the English landscape painting tradition."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "represents the elegance of the British land art.", "content": "represents the elegance of the British land art."}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "depicts the ordinary side of the British land art.", "content": "depicts the ordinary side of the British land art."}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "embodies a romantic escape into the Scottish outdoors.", "content": "embodies a romantic escape into the Scottish outdoors."}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "contains images from different parts of the same photograph.", "content": "contains images from different parts of the same photograph."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'E', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第四段第二至末句：“The Boyle Family, on the other hand, stand for its dirty, urban aspect... Their Olaf Street Study, a square of brick-strewn waste ground, is one of the few works here to embrace the commonplaceness that characterises most of our experience of the landscape most of the time.”\n【命题解密】考查多项对应。与朗的优雅风格相反，博伊尔家族代表脏乱世俗的城市风貌，其作品《奥拉夫街研究》（Olaf Street Study）以散落砖块的荒地拥抱日常生活中随处可见的平凡庸常（commonplaceness）。选项[E]“depicts the ordinary side of the British land art”精准对应原文，故选[E]。\n【错项排除】[D]项属于上句《石环》；[C]项和[F]项均属于后文对浪漫逃离或英国风景画传统的描述。' WHERE id = '22f4a07a-efab-5799-8e68-8e5c91c74210'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Match the artwork \'Across the Park\' with the statement that best reflects its artistic character (A-G):', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "originates from a long walk that the artist took.", "content": "originates from a long walk that the artist took."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "illustrates a kind of landscape-orientated light conceptual art.", "content": "illustrates a kind of landscape-orientated light conceptual art."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "reminds people of the English landscape painting tradition.", "content": "reminds people of the English landscape painting tradition."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "represents the elegance of the British land art.", "content": "represents the elegance of the British land art."}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "depicts the ordinary side of the British land art.", "content": "depicts the ordinary side of the British land art."}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "embodies a romantic escape into the Scottish outdoors.", "content": "embodies a romantic escape into the Scottish outdoors."}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "contains images from different parts of the same photograph.", "content": "contains images from different parts of the same photograph."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'G', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第五段：“Parks feature, particularly in the earlier works, such as John Hilliard\'s very funny Across the Park, in which a long-haired stroller is variously smiled at by a pretty girl and unwittingly assaulted in a sequence of images that turn out to be different parts of the same photograph.”\n【命题解密】考查多项对应。约翰·希利亚德的作品《穿越公园》（Across the Park）通过一组连续画面讲述一位长发散步者的遭遇，而这些图像实则切分自同一张完整照片的不同部位（different parts of the same photograph）。选项[G]与之原词复现，故选[G]。\n【错项排除】[A]项“源自一次长途步行”易因stroller（散步者）误导干扰，但作品核心在于同一张照片的局部剪裁拼贴，长途步行属于第45题的《七天》。' WHERE id = '8cd96e13-770d-58b4-8425-99e2be99c874'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Match the artwork \'Towards Avebury\' with the statement that best reflects its artistic character (A-G):', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "originates from a long walk that the artist took.", "content": "originates from a long walk that the artist took."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "illustrates a kind of landscape-orientated light conceptual art.", "content": "illustrates a kind of landscape-orientated light conceptual art."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "reminds people of the English landscape painting tradition.", "content": "reminds people of the English landscape painting tradition."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "represents the elegance of the British land art.", "content": "represents the elegance of the British land art."}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "depicts the ordinary side of the British land art.", "content": "depicts the ordinary side of the British land art."}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "embodies a romantic escape into the Scottish outdoors.", "content": "embodies a romantic escape into the Scottish outdoors."}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "contains images from different parts of the same photograph.", "content": "contains images from different parts of the same photograph."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第六段末句：“Derek Jarman\'s yellow-tinted film Towards Avebury, a collection of long, mostly still shots of the Wiltshire landscape, evokes a tradition of English landscape painting stretching from Samuel Palmer to Paul Nash.”\n【命题解密】考查多项对应。德里克·贾曼的黄色调影像作品《前往埃夫伯里》（Towards Avebury）捕捉威尔特郡风光，唤起了从塞缪尔·帕尔默延续至保罗·纳什的英国风景画传统（evokes a tradition of English landscape painting）。选项[C]“reminds people of the English landscape painting tradition”准确对应，故选[C]。\n【错项排除】[F]项“向苏格兰荒野的浪漫逃离”拼凑了第六段“romantic escapism”（指湖区/威尔特郡，非苏格兰）与第七段“Scottish artist”（Hamish Fulton），属于跨段拼凑干扰。' WHERE id = '0922751f-ab5c-5c7c-a103-97dcee1444cc'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Match the artwork \'Seven Days\' with the statement that best reflects its artistic character (A-G):', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "originates from a long walk that the artist took.", "content": "originates from a long walk that the artist took."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "illustrates a kind of landscape-orientated light conceptual art.", "content": "illustrates a kind of landscape-orientated light conceptual art."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "reminds people of the English landscape painting tradition.", "content": "reminds people of the English landscape painting tradition."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "represents the elegance of the British land art.", "content": "represents the elegance of the British land art."}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "depicts the ordinary side of the British land art.", "content": "depicts the ordinary side of the British land art."}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "embodies a romantic escape into the Scottish outdoors.", "content": "embodies a romantic escape into the Scottish outdoors."}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "contains images from different parts of the same photograph.", "content": "contains images from different parts of the same photograph."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'【精准定位】定位至第七段第一至二句：“In the case of Hamish Fulton, you can\'t help feeling that the Scottish artist has simply found a way of making his love of walking pay. A typical work, such as Seven Days, consists of a single beautiful black-and-white photograph taken on an epic walk, with the mileage and number of days taken listed beneath.”\n【命题解密】考查多项对应。苏格兰艺术家哈米什·富尔顿把对徒步的热爱融入创作，其代表作《七天》（Seven Days）正是将一次长途史诗般徒步中拍摄的黑白摄影配以里程与天数记录而成。选项[A]“originates from a long walk that the artist took”契合an epic walk，故选[A]。\n【错项排除】[B]项“说明以风景为导向的轻概念艺术”出自末句，评价的是整场英国大地艺术展的总体特质，而非《七天》单件作品，属于以偏概全干扰。' WHERE id = '2834ee96-b228-51a0-94a3-041d421066cb'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'In our contemporary culture, the prospect of communicating with — or even looking at — a stranger is virtually unbearable. Everyone around us seems to agree by the way they cling to their phones, even without a [1] on a subway.\n\nIt\'s a sad reality — our desire to avoid interacting with other human beings — because there\'s [2] to be gained from talking to the stranger standing by you. But you wouldn\'t know it, [3] into your phone. This universal protection sends the [4] "Please don\'t approach me."\n\nWhat is it that makes us feel we need to hide [5] our screens? One answer is fear, according to Jon Wortmann, an executive mental coach. We fear rejection, or that our innocent social advances will be [6] as "weird." We fear we\'ll be [7]. We fear we\'ll be disruptive. Strangers are inherently [8] to us, so we are more likely to feel [9] when communicating with them compared with our friends and acquaintances. To avoid this uneasiness, we [10] to our phones. "Phones become our security blanket," Wortmann says. "They are our happy glasses that protect us from what we perceive is going to be more [11]."\n\nBut once we rip off the band-aid, tuck our smartphones in our pockets and look up, it doesn\'t [12] so bad. In one 2011 experiment, behavioral scientists Nicholas Epley and Juliana Schroeder asked commuters to do the unthinkable: Start a [13]. They had Chicago train commuters talk to their fellow [14]. "When Dr. Epley and Ms. Schroeder asked other people in the same train station to [15] how they would feel after talking to a stranger, the commuters thought their [16] would be more pleasant if they sat on their own," The New York Times summarizes. Though the participants didn\'t expect a positive experience, after they [17] with the experiment, "not a single person reported having been embarrassed." [18], these commutes were reportedly more enjoyable compared with those without communication, which makes absolute sense, [19] human beings thrive off of social connections. It\'s that [20]: Talking to strangers can make you feel connected.' WHERE id = 'b6c718aa-1ace-58ff-8e8a-847e5ff6782c'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'A new study suggests that contrary to most surveys, people are actually more stressed at home than at work. Researchers measured people\'s cortisol, which is a stress marker, while they were at work and while they were at home and found it higher at what is supposed to be a place of refuge.\n\n"Further contradicting conventional wisdom, we found that women as well as men have lower levels of stress at work than at home," writes one of the researchers, Sarah Damaske. In fact women even say they feel better at work, she notes. "It is men, not women, who report being happier at home than at work." Another surprise is that the findings hold true for both those with children and without, but more so for nonparents. This is why people who work outside the home have better health.\n\nWhat the study doesn\'t measure is whether people are still doing work when they\'re at home, whether it is household work or work brought home from the office. For many men, the end of the workday is a time to kick back. For women who stay home, they never get to leave the office. And for women who work outside the home, they often are playing catch-up-with-household tasks. With the blurring of roles, and the fact that the home front lags well behind the workplace in making adjustments for working women, it\'s not surprising that women are more stressed at home.\n\nBut it\'s not just a gender thing. At work, people pretty much know what they\'re supposed to be doing: working, making money, doing the tasks they have to do in order to draw an income. The bargain is very pure: Employee puts in hours of physical or mental labor and employee draws out life-sustaining moola.\n\nOn the home front, however, people have no such clarity. Rare is the household in which the division of labor is so clinically and methodically laid out. There are a lot of tasks to be done, there are inadequate rewards for most of them. Your home colleagues — your family — have no clear rewards for their labor; they need to be talked into it, or if they\'re teenagers, threatened with complete removal of all electronic devices. Plus, they\'re your family. You cannot fire your family. You never really get to go home from home.\n\nSo it\'s not surprising that people are more stressed at home. Not only are the tasks apparently infinite, the co-workers are much harder to motivate.' WHERE id = '94033907-5cbc-5424-8256-4c5ea088d37d'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'Even in traditional offices, "the lingua franca of corporate America has gotten much more emotional and much more right-brained than it was 20 years ago," said Harvard Business School professor Nancy Koehn. She started spinning off examples. "If you and I parachuted back to Fortune 500 companies in 1990, we would see much less frequent use of terms like journey, mission, passion. There were goals, there were strategies, there were objectives, but we didn\'t talk about energy; we didn\'t talk about passion."\n\nKoehn pointed out that this new era of corporate vocabulary is very "team"-oriented — and not by coincidence. "Let\'s not forget sports - in male-dominated corporate America, it\'s still a big deal. It\'s not explicitly conscious; it\'s the idea that I\'m a coach, and you\'re my team, and we\'re in this together. There are lots and lots of CEOs in very different companies, but most think of themselves as coaches and this is their team and they want to win."\n\nThese terms are also intended to infuse work with meaning - and, as Rakesh Khurana, another professor, points out, increase allegiance to the firm. "You have the importation of terminology that historically used to be associated with non-profit organizations and religious organizations: terms like vision, values, passion, and purpose," said Khurana.\n\nThis new focus on personal fulfillment can help keep employees motivated amid increasingly loud debates over work-life balance. The "mommy wars" of the 1990s are still going on today, prompting arguments about why women still can\'t have it all and books like Sheryl Sandberg\'s Lean In, whose title has become a buzzword in its own right. Terms like unplug, offline, life-hack, bandwidth, and capacity are all about setting boundaries between the office and the home. But if your work is your "passion," you\'ll be more likely to devote yourself to it, even if that means going home for dinner and then working long after the kids are in bed.\n\nBut this seems to be the irony of office speak: Everyone makes fun of it, but managers love it, companies depend on it, and regular people willingly absorb it. As a linguist once said, "You can get people to think it\'s nonsense at the same time that you buy into it." In a workplace that\'s fundamentally indifferent to your life and its meaning, office speak can help you figure out how you relate to your work - and how your work defines who you are.' WHERE id = '34e06357-fd62-5f4d-a715-b0145eb48132'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'Many people talked of the 288,000 new jobs the Labor Department reported for June, along with the drop in the unemployment rate to 6.1 percent, as good news. And they were right. For now it appears the economy is creating jobs at a decent pace. We still have a long way to go to get back to full employment, but at least we are now finally moving forward at a faster pace.\n\nHowever, there is another important part of the jobs picture that was largely overlooked. There was a big jump in the number of people who report voluntarily working part-time. This figure is now 830,000 (4.4 percent) above its year ago level.\n\nBefore explaining the connection to the Obamacare, it is worth making an important distinction. Many people who work part-time jobs actually want full-time jobs. They take part-time work because this is all they can get. An increase in involuntary part-time work is evidence of weakness in the labor market and it means that many people will be having a very hard time making ends meet. There was an increase in involuntary part-time in June, but the general direction has been down. Involuntary part-time employment is still far higher than before the recession, but it is down by 640,000 (7.9 percent) from its year ago level.\n\nWe know the difference between voluntary and involuntary part-time employment because people tell us. The survey used by the Labor Department asks people if they worked less than 35 hours in the reference week. If the answer is "yes," they are classified as working part-time. The survey then asks whether they worked less than 35 hours in that week because they wanted to work less than full time or because they had no choice. They are only classified as voluntary part-time workers if they tell the survey taker they chose to work less than 35 hours a week.\n\nThe issue of voluntary part-time relates to Obamacare because one of the main purposes was to allow people to get insurance outside of employment. For many people, especially those with serious health conditions or family members with serious health conditions, before Obamacare the only way to get insurance was through a job that provided health insurance.\n\nHowever, Obamacare has allowed more than 12 million people to either get insurance through Medicaid or the exchanges. These are people who may previously have felt the need to get a full-time job that provided insurance in order to cover themselves and their families. With Obamacare there is no longer a link between employment and insurance.' WHERE id = '7e558466-7a01-5cc8-9f0d-41cd9bff9bbe'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [6] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "misapplied", "content": "misapplied"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "misinterpreted", "content": "misinterpreted"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "misadjusted", "content": "misadjusted"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "mismatched", "content": "mismatched"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］动词语义辨析与被动语态。\n［精准定位］第三段第三句：We fear rejection, or that our innocent social advances will be [6] as "weird."\n［命题解密］作者分析社交恐惧的根源：我们担心遭到拒绝，或者担心自己善意的社交举动会被对方“误解/曲解（misinterpreted）”为行为古怪（"weird"）。misinterpreted 准确传达了善意互动遭曲解的意思，故选[B]。\n［错项排除］[A] misapplied（被误用）、[C] misadjusted（被错误调整）与 [D] mismatched（不匹配）均无法表达社交意图被对方错误解读之意。' WHERE id = '5cb1e86d-e628-587c-874a-17f9a84309f4'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [9] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "comfortable", "content": "comfortable"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "confident", "content": "confident"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "anxious", "content": "anxious"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "angry", "content": "angry"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］形容词语义辨析与后文词汇照应。\n［精准定位］第三段第六至七句：so we are more likely to feel [9]... To avoid this uneasiness, we...\n［命题解密］第七句紧接着点出 To avoid this uneasiness（为了避免这种不安），this uneasiness 回指第[9]空，说明与陌生人交流比与熟人相处更容易感到焦虑不安，故 [C] anxious 正确。\n［错项排除］[A] comfortable（舒适的）与 [B] confident（自信的）情感极性相反；[D] angry（愤怒的）不符合面对陌生人时的紧张拘束心理。' WHERE id = '3f740472-eb95-515d-8558-6acc622dfe2d'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [10] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "attend", "content": "attend"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "turn", "content": "turn"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "take", "content": "take"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "point", "content": "point"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］动词短语搭配与语义逻辑。\n［精准定位］第三段第七句：To avoid this uneasiness, we [10] to our phones.\n［命题解密］turn to sb./sth. 为固定搭配，意为“转向、求助于”。为回避与陌生人互动的不安，人们转而拿起手机寻求掩护与心理依托，故 [B] turn 正确。\n［错项排除］[A] attend to（照料/专心处理）、[C] take to（喜欢上/养成……习惯）与 [D] point to（指向）均不能表达“为逃避焦虑而求助寄托”的语义。' WHERE id = '2c76eeb3-3a56-51b3-adc4-deb59790467c'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [12] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "bend", "content": "bend"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "resist", "content": "resist"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "hurt", "content": "hurt"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "decay", "content": "decay"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］动词语义辨析与习语用法。\n［精准定位］第四段第一句：But once we rip off the band-aid, tuck our smartphones in our pockets and look up, it doesn\'t [12] so bad.\n［命题解密］作者用“撕掉创可贴（rip off the band-aid）”作比喻：一旦收起手机抬头接触外界，其实“并没有那么痛/没那么糟（doesn\'t hurt so bad）”。hurt 此处体现克服社交障碍时的心理不适或疼痛感，故 [C] hurt 正确。\n［错项排除］[A] bend（弯曲）、[B] resist（抵抗）与 [D] decay（腐烂）均不与 so bad 搭配形容心理感受。' WHERE id = '6021ee3d-164c-5a45-bde5-bf0a9c19bf31'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [17] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "went through", "content": "went through"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "did away", "content": "did away"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "caught up", "content": "caught up"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "put up", "content": "put up"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］动词短语搭配与上下文语义。\n［精准定位］第四段第五句：after they [17] with the experiment, "not a single person reported having been embarrassed."\n［命题解密］go through with sth. 意为“坚持完成、把……做到底”。受试者顶住最初顾虑完成了搭讪实验，结果竟然“没有一个人表示感到尴尬（embarrassed）”，故 [A] went through 正确。\n［错项排除］[B] did away with（废除）、[C] caught up with（追赶上）与 [D] put up with（忍受）均不与完成实验（experiment）匹配。' WHERE id = 'baf6a010-2238-56f3-8081-361b430035d5'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The blurring of working women\'s roles refers to the fact that', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "their home is also a place for kicking back", "content": "their home is also a place for kicking back"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "they are both bread winners and housewives", "content": "they are both bread winners and housewives"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "there is often much housework left behind", "content": "there is often much housework left behind"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "it is difficult for them to leave their office", "content": "it is difficult for them to leave their office"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］细节理解题与因果语境整合。\n［精准定位］第三段第三至五句：For women who stay home, they never get to leave the office. And for women who work outside the home, they often are playing catch-up-with-household tasks. With the blurring of roles... it\'s not surprising that women are more stressed at home.\n［命题解密］文中指出在外工作的职业女性下班后还要匆忙赶做家务（playing catch-up-with-household tasks），兼顾“赚钱养家”和“家庭主妇”双重身份，这种角色界限模糊导致她们在家里压力更大。选项 [B] they are both bread winners and housewives 精准概括了“角色模糊”的内涵，故选 [B]。\n［错项排除］[A] 对应上句男性下班后在家放松（For many men, the end of the workday is a time to kick back）；[C] 仅体现繁重家务本身，遗漏了“外出工作”这重对比角色；[D] 对应全职主妇“never get to leave the office”，而非题干所问的“职业女性（working women）”。' WHERE id = 'b25a81f5-0b46-5880-9662-4cf12aea8b6b'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Many people work part-time because they', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "prefer part-time jobs to full-time jobs", "content": "prefer part-time jobs to full-time jobs"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "feel that is enough to make ends meet", "content": "feel that is enough to make ends meet"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "cannot get their hands on full-time jobs", "content": "cannot get their hands on full-time jobs"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "haven\'t seen the weakness of the market", "content": "haven\'t seen the weakness of the market"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］因果细节题与习语转换。\n［精准定位］第三段第一至三句：Many people who work part-time jobs actually want full-time jobs. They take part-time work because this is all they can get.\n［命题解密］很多人从事兼职并非自愿，而是因为他们真正想要全职工作却“只能找到兼职（this is all they can get）”，即无法获得全职岗位。选项 [C] cannot get their hands on full-time jobs 精准对应原文，故选 [C]。\n［错项排除］[A] 与 actually want full-time jobs 相反；[B] 与后文 having a very hard time making ends meet（艰难维持生计）相悖；[D] 曲解下句 weakness in the labor market，非自愿兼职者恰恰因劳动力市场疲软而找不到全职，并非未见识市场疲软。' WHERE id = '241b619c-3f75-546f-ac0a-b966b63854f5'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Involuntary part-time employment in the US', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "shows a general tendency of decline", "content": "shows a general tendency of decline"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "is harder to acquire than one year ago", "content": "is harder to acquire than one year ago"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "satisfies the real need of the jobless", "content": "satisfies the real need of the jobless"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "is lower than before the recession", "content": "is lower than before the recession"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］事实细节题与趋势归纳。\n［精准定位］第四段第一至二句：There was an increase in involuntary part-time in June, but the general direction has been down. Involuntary part-time employment is still far higher than before the recession, but it is down by 640,000 (7.9 percent) from its year ago level.\n［命题解密］尽管6月数据略升，但美国非自愿兼职就业的“总体趋势一直是下降的（the general direction has been down）”。[A]项 shows a general tendency of decline 精准复现这一结论，故选 [A]。\n［错项排除］[B] 错误归因；[C] 与被迫兼职者难以糊口相矛盾；[D] 与文中“still far higher than before the recession（仍远高于经济衰退前水平）”完全相反。' WHERE id = '6ff6118c-6272-50da-bc3e-2c1faea82977'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'It can be learned that with Obamacare,', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "it is no longer easy for part-timers to get insurance", "content": "it is no longer easy for part-timers to get insurance"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "full-time employment is still essential for insurance", "content": "full-time employment is still essential for insurance"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "it is still challenging to get insurance for family members", "content": "it is still challenging to get insurance for family members"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "employment is no longer a precondition to get insurance", "content": "employment is no longer a precondition to get insurance"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］细节推理题与因果核心破题。\n［精准定位］第六至七段：one of the main purposes was to allow people to get insurance outside of employment... With Obamacare there is no longer a link between employment and insurance.\n［命题解密］奥巴马医改让超过1200万人通过医疗补助或保险交易市场参保，彻底打破了工作与医保之间的绑定关系（no longer a link between employment and insurance），即就业不再是获取医保的前提条件，故选 [D]。\n［错项排除］[A] 曲解医改让人脱离工作也能轻松投保的本意；[B] 与打破绑定关系彻底相反；[C] 错将奥巴马医改“之前”必须靠全职工作为家人投保（in order to cover themselves and their families）的困境套用到医改“之后”。' WHERE id = '4ebd9995-67ca-559c-b652-d0fe74f24f54'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The text mainly discusses', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "employment in the US", "content": "employment in the US"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "part-timer classification", "content": "part-timer classification"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "insurance through Medicaid", "content": "insurance through Medicaid"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Obamacare\'s trouble", "content": "Obamacare\'s trouble"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］主旨大意题与全文脉络归纳。\n［精准定位］通读全文，第一至五段分析美国劳工部6月新增就业、失业率下降以及自愿/非自愿兼职的分类和走势，第六至七段说明奥巴马医改对自愿兼职与就业格局的影响。\n［命题解密］全文围绕美国的就业市场状况（employment, full-time jobs, voluntary/involuntary part-time jobs）展开，讨论其结构变化及影响因素。[A]项 employment in the US 高度涵盖全篇核心，故选 [A]。\n［错项排除］[B] 兼职分类仅见于第五段细节；[C] 通过Medicaid获得医保仅为第七段首句一笔带过的细节例证；[D] 奥巴马医改的麻烦属于无中生有，文中肯定了医改让千万民众脱离职场绑定获得医保。' WHERE id = '0e9740df-e51c-5eae-a326-e855670b38ca'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'It\'s true that high-school coding classes aren\'t essential for learning computer science in college. Students without experience can catch up after a few introductory courses, said Tom Cortina, the assistant dean at Carnegie Mellon\'s School of Computer Science.\n\nHowever, Cortina said, early exposure is beneficial. When younger kids learn computer science, they learn that it\'s not just a confusing, endless string of letters and numbers - but a tool to build apps, or create artwork, or test hypotheses. It\'s not as hard for them to transform their thought processes as it is for older students. Breaking down problems into bite-sized chunks and using code to solve them becomes normal. Giving more children this training could increase the number of people interested in the field and help fill the jobs gap, Cortina said.\n\nStudents also benefit from learning something about coding before they get to college, where introductory computer-science 101 classes are packed to the brim, which can drive the less-experienced or -determined students away.\n\nThe Flatiron School, where people pay to learn programming, started as one of the many coding bootcamps that\'s become popular for adults looking for a career change. The high-schoolers get the same curriculum, but “we try to gear lessons toward things they\'re interested in,” said Victoria Friedman, an instructor. For instance, one of the apps the students are developing suggests movies based on your mood.\n\nThe students in the Flatiron class probably won\'t drop out of high school and build the next Facebook. Programming languages have a quick turnover, so the "Ruby on Rails" language they learned may not even be relevant by the time they enter the job market. But the skills they learn - how to think logically through a problem and organize the results - apply to any coding language, said Deborah Seehorn, an education consultant for the state of North Carolina.\n\nIndeed, the Flatiron students might not go into IT at all. But creating a future army of coders is not the sole purpose of the classes. These kids are going to be surrounded by computers - in their pockets, in their offices, in their homes - for the rest of their lives. The younger they learn how computers think, how to coax the machine into producing what they want - the earlier they learn that they have the power to do that - the better.' WHERE id = 'db405343-12e6-5e24-8ab1-5c1932e7574f'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'Biologists estimate that as many as 2 million lesser prairie chickens - a kind of bird living on stretching grasslands - once lent red to the often grey landscape of the midwestern and southwestern United States. But just some 22,000 birds remain today, occupying about 16% of the species\' historic range.\n\nThe crash was a major reason the U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service (USFWS) decided to formally list the bird as threatened. “The lesser prairie chicken is in a desperate situation,” said USFWS Director Daniel Ashe. Some environmentalists, however, were disappointed. They had pushed the agency to designate the bird as “endangered,” a status that gives federal officials greater regulatory power to crack down on threats. But Ashe and others argued that the “threatened” tag gave the federal government flexibility to try out new, potentially less confrontational conservation approaches. In particular, they called for forging closer collaborations with western state governments, which are often uneasy with federal action, and with the private landowners who control an estimated 95% of the prairie chicken\'s habitat.\n\nUnder the plan, for example, the agency said it would not prosecute landowners or businesses that unintentionally kill, harm, or disturb the bird, as long as they had signed a range-wide management plan to restore prairie chicken habitat. Negotiated by USFWS and the states, the plan requires individuals and businesses that damage habitat as part of their operations to pay into a fund to replace every acre of destroyed habitat with 2 new acres of suitable habitat. The fund will also be used to compensate landowners who set aside habitat. USFWS also set an interim goal of restoring prairie chicken populations to an annual average of 67,000 birds over the next 10 years. And it gives the Western Association of Fish and Wildlife Agencies (WAFWA), a coalition of state agencies, the job of monitoring progress. Overall, the idea is to let “states remain in the driver\'s seat for managing the species,” Ashe said.\n\nNot everyone buys the win-win rhetoric. Some Congress members are trying to block the plan, and at least a dozen industry groups, four states, and three environmental groups are challenging it in federal court. Not surprisingly, industry groups and states generally argue it goes too far; environmentalists say it doesn\'t go far enough. “The federal government is giving responsibility for managing the bird to the same industries that are pushing it to extinction,” says biologist Jay Lininger.' WHERE id = '1af6dd5f-a12c-565a-98c9-0bb2a4bcd0f4'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'That everyone\'s too busy these days is a cliche. But one specific complaint is made especially mournfully: There\'s never any time to read.\n\nWhat makes the problem thornier is that the usual time-management techniques don\'t seem sufficient. The web\'s full of articles offering tips on making time to read: “Give up TV” or “Carry a book with you at all times.” But in my experience, using such methods to free up the odd 30 minutes doesn\'t work. Sit down to read and the flywheel of work-related thoughts keeps spinning - or else you\'re so exhausted that a challenging book\'s the last thing you need. The modern mind, Tim Parks, a novelist and critic, writes, “is overwhelmingly inclined toward communication... It is not simply that one is interrupted; it is that one is actually inclined to interruption.” Deep reading requires not just time, but a special kind of time which can\'t be obtained merely by becoming more efficient. In fact, "becoming more efficient" is part of the problem.\n\nThinking of time as a resource to be maximised means you approach it instrumentally, judging any given moment as well spent only in so far as it advances progress toward some goal. Immersive reading, by contrast, depends on being willing to risk inefficiency, goallessness, even time-wasting. Try to slot it in as a to-do list item and you\'ll manage only goal-focused reading - useful, sometimes, but not the most fulfilling kind. “The future comes at us like empty bottles along an unstoppable and nearly infinite conveyor belt,” writes Gary Eberle in his book Sacred Time, “and we feel a pressure to fill these different-sized bottles (days, hours, minutes) as they pass, for if they get by without being filled, we will have wasted them.” No mind-set could be worse for losing yourself in a book.\n\nSo what does work? Perhaps surprisingly, scheduling regular times for reading. You\'d think this might fuel the efficiency mind-set, but in fact, Eberle notes, such ritualistic behaviour helps us “step outside time\'s flow” into “soul time.” You could limit distractions by reading only physical books, or on single-purpose e-readers. “Carry a book with you at all times” can actually work, too - providing you dip in often enough, so that reading becomes the default state from which you temporarily surface to take care of business, before dropping back down. On a really good day, it no longer feels as if you\'re “making time to read,” but just reading, and making time for everything else.' WHERE id = 'eb685298-efa5-52b9-ae98-d84c4c04f5e3'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'Act Your Shoe Size, Not Your Age\n\nAs adults, it seems that we are constantly pursuing happiness, often with mixed results. Yet children appear to have it down to an art - and for the most part they don\'t need self-help books or therapy. Instead, they look after their wellbeing instinctively, and usually more effectively than we do as grownups. Perhaps it\'s time to learn a few lessons from them.\n\n[41] _________________________________\nWhat does a child do when he\'s sad? He cries. When he\'s angry? He shouts. Scared? Probably a bit of both. As we grow up, we learn to control our emotions so they are manageable and don\'t dictate our behaviours, which is in many ways a good thing. But too often we take this process too far and end up suppressing emotions, especially negative ones. That\'s about as effective as brushing dirt under a carpet and can even make us ill. What we need to do is find a way to acknowledge and express what we feel appropriately, and then—again, like children—move on.\n\n[42] _________________________________\nA couple of Christmases ago, my youngest stepdaughter, who was nine years old at the time, got a Superman T-shirt for Christmas. It cost less than a fiver but she was overjoyed, and couldn\'t stop talking about it. Too often we believe that a new job, bigger house or better car will be the magic silver bullet that will allow us to finally be content, but the reality is these things have very little lasting impact on our happiness levels. Instead, being grateful for small things every day is a much better way to improve wellbeing.\n\n[43] _________________________________\nHave you ever noticed how much children laugh? If we adults could indulge in a bit of silliness and giggling, we would reduce the stress hormones in our bodies, increase good hormones like endorphins, improve blood flow to our hearts and even have a greater chance of fighting off infection. All of which would, of course, have a positive effect on our happiness levels.\n\n[44] _________________________________\nThe problem with being a grownup is that there\'s an awful lot of serious stuff to deal with - work, mortgage payments, figuring out what to cook for dinner. But as adults we also have the luxury of being able to control our own diaries and it\'s important that we schedule in time to enjoy the things we love. Those things might be social, sporting, creative or completely random (dancing around the living room, anyone?) - it doesn\'t matter, so long as they\'re enjoyable, and not likely to have negative side effects, such as drinking too much alcohol or going on a wild spending spree if you\'re on a tight budget.\n\n[45] _________________________________\nHaving said all of the above, it\'s important to add that we shouldn\'t try too hard to be happy. Scientists tell us this can backfire and actually have a negative impact on our wellbeing. As the Chinese philosopher Chuang Tzu is reported to have said: “Happiness is the absence of striving for happiness.” And in that, once more, we need to look to the example of our children, to whom happiness is not a goal but a natural byproduct of the way they live.' WHERE id = 'a26e2be0-5e43-50e8-b0b3-283d139680c0'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [5] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "miss", "content": "miss"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "echo", "content": "echo"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "spoil", "content": "spoil"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "change", "content": "change"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］动词语义辨析与上下文照应。\n［精准定位］第三段第一句：The researchers wanted to know if the optimism and inclination for risk-taking that come with happiness would [5] the way companies invested.\n［命题解密］首段提出幸福感可能影响（influence）企业运作方式，本句研究人员意在探究伴随幸福感而来的乐观与冒险倾向是否会实际“改变（change）”公司的投资方式，与 influence 遥相呼应，故选 [D]。\n［错项排除］[A] miss 意为“错过、遗漏”；[B] echo 意为“回响、重复”；[C] spoil 意为“宠坏、糟蹋”，均无法表达影响并改变投资行为之意。' WHERE id = '5d04930e-c5f1-5af3-b33d-fdb6d6405d46'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [9] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "summarize", "content": "summarize"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "overstate", "content": "overstate"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "explain", "content": "explain"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "emphasize", "content": "emphasize"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］动词语义辨析与科研因果辨析。\n［精准定位］第四段第二句：But is it really happiness that\'s linked to investment, or could something else about happier cities [9] why firms there spend more on R&D?\n［命题解密］本句探讨因果归因的排他性检验：究竟是幸福感导致高研发投资，还是快乐城市中的其他混淆因素能够“解释（explain）”为何企业投入更多。explain why... 为标准科学归因句式，故选 [C]。\n［错项排除］[A] summarize 意为“总结”；[B] overstate 意为“夸大”；[D] emphasize 意为“强调”，均不能与 why 从句构成合理解释因果的搭配。' WHERE id = '8da78393-1fb6-51f0-94df-08ef97183b07'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [15] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "instead", "content": "instead"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "thus", "content": "thus"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "also", "content": "also"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "never", "content": "never"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］副词语义辨析与递进逻辑。\n［精准定位］第五段第二句：The relationship was [15] stronger in places where happiness was spread more equally.\n［命题解密］第一句已指出在年轻企业中幸福感与投资的关联尤为显著（particularly strong），第二句在此基础上进一步补充另一类强化关联的情况：在幸福感分布更均衡的地区，这种关联“也（also）”更强。also 准确衔接两处并列递增的情形，故选 [C]。\n［错项排除］[A] instead（相反）表对立取舍；[B] thus（因此）错加因果推论；[D] never（从不）与后句具体对比阐释相悖。' WHERE id = 'aa5d3238-628e-5546-823c-ec597944822b'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [19] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "share", "content": "share"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "rediscover", "content": "rediscover"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "simplify", "content": "simplify"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "shape", "content": "shape"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］动词语义辨析与文化影响语境。\n［精准定位］第六段第二句：It\'s not hard to imagine that local culture and sentiment would help [19] how executives think about the future.\n［命题解密］本句阐述地方氛围对企业决策者的心理影响路径：不难想象当地文化与情绪氛围有助于“塑造（shape）”高管看待未来的思维方式，使之更具前瞻性，故选 [D]。\n［错项排除］[A] share 意为“分享”；[B] rediscover 意为“重新发现”；[C] simplify 意为“简化”，均无法准确描述文化环境对高管长远思维的潜移默化塑造作用。' WHERE id = 'fb7ff721-3fca-564c-8a95-5bef10cdf4ad'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Deborah Seehorn believes that the skills learned at Flatiron will', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "help students learn other computer languages", "content": "help students learn other computer languages"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "have to be upgraded when new technologies come", "content": "have to be upgraded when new technologies come"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "need improving when students look for jobs", "content": "need improving when students look for jobs"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "enable students to make big quick money", "content": "enable students to make big quick money"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据人名 Deborah Seehorn 定位至第 5 段末尾。\n［解题思路］第 5 段指出：“Programming languages have a quick turnover, so the "Ruby on Rails" language they learned may not even be relevant by the time they enter the job market. But the skills they learn - how to think logically through a problem and organize the results - apply to any coding language, said Deborah Seehorn...”。编程语言迭代迅速，但学生在 Flatiron 学到的逻辑思考和结果组织能力适用于任何编程语言（apply to any coding language），即能帮助他们学习其他计算机语言。选项 [A] help students learn other computer languages 精准同义改写 apply to any coding language，故为正确答案。\n［错项排除］[B] have to be upgraded when new technologies come（新技术出现时必须升级），第 5 段指的是“编程语言”更替快，而学生学到的“核心思维技能”通用且无需随语言淘汰而失效；[C] need improving when students look for jobs（学生找工作时需要提升），原文强调核心技能直接迁移适用，并未提及求职时亟待提升；[D] enable students to make big quick money（使学生快速赚大钱），文中明确提到高中生不太可能辍学打造下一个 Facebook，属无中生有。' WHERE id = 'f0a4e986-0e49-530d-9336-fdc0a144d89f'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to the last paragraph, Flatiron students are expected to', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "bring forth innovative computer technologies", "content": "bring forth innovative computer technologies"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "stay longer in the information technology industry", "content": "stay longer in the information technology industry"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "become better prepared for the digitalized world", "content": "become better prepared for the digitalized world"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "compete with a future army of programmers", "content": "compete with a future army of programmers"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干中的 the last paragraph 定位至第 6 段（最后一段）。\n［解题思路］最后一段指出：“Indeed, the Flatiron students might not go into IT at all. But creating a future army of coders is not the sole purpose of the classes. These kids are going to be surrounded by computers - in their pockets, in their offices, in their homes - for the rest of their lives. The younger they learn how computers think, how to coax the machine into producing what they want... the better.” 孩子们未来生活将被计算机全面包围，尽早理解计算机的思维方式与操控规律，能让他们在数字化未来掌握主动权。选项 [C] become better prepared for the digitalized world（为数字化世界做好更充分准备）精准概括了培养数字化时代主动适应能力的育人宗旨，故选 [C]。\n［错项排除］[A] bring forth innovative computer technologies（创造革新的计算机技术），原文强调教学目的不是把学生都培养成技术开发者，而是普及数字素养；[B] stay longer in the information technology industry（在 IT 行业待得更久），首句直接否定“might not go into IT at all”；[D] compete with a future army of programmers（与未来程序员大军竞争），原文是说不仅为了培养程序员大军，而非与之竞争。' WHERE id = '75a5d4ad-7fe2-59e3-b304-30bbdec6ab45'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'It can be learned from Paragraph 3 that unintentional harm-doers will not be prosecuted if they ________.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "text": "agree to pay a sum for compensation", "value": "A", "content": "agree to pay a sum for compensation"}, {"key": "B", "text": "volunteer to set up an equally big habitat", "value": "B", "content": "volunteer to set up an equally big habitat"}, {"key": "C", "text": "offer to support the WAFWA monitoring job", "value": "C", "content": "offer to support the WAFWA monitoring job"}, {"key": "D", "text": "promise to raise funds for USFWS operations", "value": "D", "content": "promise to raise funds for USFWS operations"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［精准定位］定位至第三段第一至二句：“Under the plan, for example, the agency said it would not prosecute landowners or businesses that unintentionally kill, harm, or disturb the bird, as long as they had signed a range-wide management plan to restore prairie chicken habitat. Negotiated by USFWS and the states, the plan requires individuals and businesses that damage habitat... to pay into a fund to replace every acre destroyed with 2 new acres of suitable habitat.”\n［命题解密］根据第三段可知，只要签署栖息地恢复协议并向补偿基金出资，无意伤害小草原松鸡的土地所有者或企业便不会被起诉，故 [A] agree to pay a sum for compensation 正确。\n［错项排除］[B] 错在要求恢复“双倍”而非同等面积（replace every acre... with 2 new acres）；[C] WAFWA 负责监测进度，未要求加害方资助监测；[D] 资金用于赔偿地主及置换双倍栖息地，而非 USFWS 自身运营。' WHERE id = '90f62ba4-cdda-5cff-9313-a747c1c6bf04'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to Ashe, the leading role in managing the species is', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "the federal government", "content": "the federal government"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "the wildlife agencies", "content": "the wildlife agencies"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "the landowners", "content": "the landowners"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "the states", "content": "the states"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据人名 Ashe 定位至第 3 段最后一句。\n［解题思路］第 3 段末尾引用 Ashe 的原话明确指出：“Overall, the idea is to let \'states remain in the driver\'s seat for managing the species,\' Ashe said.”。in the driver\'s seat 是地道英语习语，意为“处于控制地位、居于主导/领先地位”。由此可知，Ashe 认为主导物种管理的是各个州（the states）。选项 [D] the states 是原文的直接对应，故为正确答案。\n［错项排除］[A] the federal government（联邦政府），Ashe 明确主张将控制权下放给州；[B] the wildlife agencies（野生动物机构），文中 WAFWA 负责的是 monitoring progress，并非主导治理的掌舵者；[C] the local landowners（当地土地拥有者），土地所有者是合作与补偿对象，并不掌控主导地位。' WHERE id = '42b58b3a-f1dc-5f90-b82e-6de589130f29'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Jay Lininger would most likely support', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "industry groups", "content": "industry groups"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "the win-win rhetoric", "content": "the win-win rhetoric"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "environmental groups", "content": "environmental groups"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "the plan under challenge", "content": "the plan under challenge"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据人名 Jay Lininger 定位至第 4 段末尾：“Not surprisingly, industry groups and states generally argue it goes too far; environmentalists say it doesn\'t go far enough. \'The federal government is giving responsibility for managing the bird to the same industries that are pushing it to extinction,\' says biologist Jay Lininger.”\n［解题思路］生物学家 Jay Lininger 尖锐抨击联邦政府将管理该鸟类的责任移交给将其推向灭绝的工业界，立场鲜明地站在环保主义者（environmentalists say it doesn\'t go far enough）一边，批判妥协方案保护力度不足。选项 [C] environmental groups（环保团体）代表其最可能支持的阵营，故选 [C]。\n［错项排除］[A] industry groups（行业组织），Lininger 明确指责正是相关行业将草原鸡推向灭绝，绝不会支持行业组织；[B] the win-win rhetoric（双赢说辞），第 4 段首句明确指出并非所有人都买账，Lininger 正是典型质疑者；[D] the plan under challenge（受到起诉质疑的计划），他强烈批评该妥协计划，与环保团体一起站到对立面。' WHERE id = 'a6e37580-37a1-507e-bdb8-afdc21ea75ac'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The "empty bottles" metaphor illustrates that people feel a pressure to', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "update their to-do lists", "content": "update their to-do lists"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "make passing time fulfilling", "content": "make passing time fulfilling"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "carry their plans through", "content": "carry their plans through"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "pursue carefree reading", "content": "pursue carefree reading"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干中的 "empty bottles" metaphor 定位至第 3 段后半部分。\n［解题思路］第 3 段引用 Gary Eberle 的话指出：“\'The future comes at us like empty bottles along an unstoppable and nearly infinite conveyor belt,\' writes Gary Eberle in his book Sacred Time, \'and we feel a pressure to fill these different-sized bottles (days, hours, minutes) as they pass, for if they get by without being filled, we will have wasted them.\'” 未来就像传送带上一排排等待灌满的空瓶子，人们感受到必须把每一小时、每一分钟都填满充实的焦虑压力，否则便视之为虚度光阴。选项 [B] make passing time fulfilling 准确对应 fill these different-sized bottles as they pass，故选 [B]。\n［错项排除］[A] update their to-do lists（更新待办事项清单），前文指出把阅读塞进 to-do list 会破坏沉浸式阅读，但空瓶子比喻针对的是把流逝时间塞满的压力，而非更新清单本身；[C] carry their plans through（贯彻计划）偏离对时间填满的隐喻；[D] pursue carefree reading（追求无忧阅读）与充满紧迫感的功利时间观完全相反。' WHERE id = 'f26d82a8-185d-5285-8a4e-83952980f708'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'"Carry a book with you at all times" can work if', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "reading becomes your primary business of the day", "content": "reading becomes your primary business of the day"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "all the daily business has been promptly dealt with", "content": "all the daily business has been promptly dealt with"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "you are able to drop back to business after reading", "content": "you are able to drop back to business after reading"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "time can be evenly split for reading and business", "content": "time can be evenly split for reading and business"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干中的 "Carry a book with you at all times" can work 定位至第 4 段倒数第 2 句。\n［解题思路］第 4 段指出：“\'Carry a book with you at all times\' can actually work, too — providing you dip in often enough, so that reading becomes the default state from which you temporarily surface to take care of business, before dropping back down.” 前提是足够频繁地翻看，从而让“阅读”成为日常默认状态，处理杂务只是暂时浮出水面，随后又回到阅读之中。也就是说阅读已成为每天最核心要务（primary business），故选 [A]。\n［错项排除］[B] all the daily business has been promptly dealt with（所有日常事务已被迅速处理完），原文是暂离阅读处理事务，而非先把事务处理完再读；[C] you are able to drop back to business after reading（阅读后能回到工作事务中），把原文句序与主次彻底颠倒，原文明确说明是处理事务之后“回到阅读之中（dropping back down [to reading]）”；[D] time can be evenly split for reading and business（时间可均分），文中强调以阅读为默认常态，并非平均分配。' WHERE id = 'e32a1401-e94a-51b1-b131-eaf043a9a1d3'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'It can be learned from Paragraph 3 that young people tend to', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "favor a slower life pace", "content": "favor a slower life pace"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "hold an occupation longer", "content": "hold an occupation longer"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "attach importance to pre-marital finance", "content": "attach importance to pre-marital finance"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "give priority to childcare outside the home", "content": "give priority to childcare outside the home"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［精准定位］定位至第三段：“Young people who are still getting started in life were more likely than older adults... to agree that couples should be financially secure before getting married or having children...”\n［命题解密］第三段对比代际差异时明确指出，刚步入社会的年轻人比老一辈更倾向于认同“伴侣在结婚或生子前应先具备稳固的经济保障（financially secure before getting married）”。[C]项 attach importance to pre-marital finance（重视婚前财务状况）正是原文的同义改写，故选 [C]。\n［错项排除］[A] favor a slower life pace 与原文更青睐“a faster pace of life（更快节奏的生活）”直接相反；[B] hold an occupation longer 与原文“regularly changing jobs（定期跳槽换工作）”完全相悖；[D] give priority to childcare outside the home 偷换原文“two parents working outside the home（父母双方外出工作）”，并非送往校外/家外托育。' WHERE id = '338c7252-a273-5f94-9ab4-54747b7754af'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The priorities and expectations defined by the young will', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "become increasingly clear", "content": "become increasingly clear"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "focus on materialistic issues", "content": "focus on materialistic issues"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "depend largely on political preferences", "content": "depend largely on political preferences"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "reach almost all aspects of American life", "content": "reach almost all aspects of American life"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干关键词 priorities and expectations defined by the young 定位至第 4 段。\n［解题思路］第 4 段指出：“these contrasts suggest that in the aftermath of the searing Great Recession, those just starting out in life are defining priorities and expectations that will increasingly spread through virtually all aspects of American life, from consumer preferences to housing patterns to politics.” 刚步入社会的年轻人所确立的优先事项与期望，将日益扩散并贯穿于美国社会生活的方方面面（virtually all aspects of American life）。[D]项 reach almost all aspects of American life 正是对此精准同义转述，故选 [D]。\n［错项排除］[A] become increasingly clear（变得越来越清晰）偷换了 increasingly spread through 的动作指向；[B] focus on materialistic issues（聚焦物质问题）忽略了社区、家庭和政治维度；[C] depend largely on political preferences（主要取决于政治偏好）颠倒因果，实为影响扩散至政治领域。' WHERE id = '72a0348f-27ba-58cf-8dbd-420f5de23be9'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Both young and old agree that', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "good-paying jobs are less available", "content": "good-paying jobs are less available"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "the old made more life achievements", "content": "the old made more life achievements"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "housing loans today are easy to obtain", "content": "housing loans today are easy to obtain"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "getting established is harder for the young", "content": "getting established is harder for the young"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干关键词 Both young and old agree 定位至第 5 段首句。\n［解题思路］第 5 段明确指出：“Young and old converge on one key point: Overwhelming majorities of both groups said they believe it is harder for young people today to get started in life than it was for earlier generations.” 无论老幼压倒性多数都同意当今年轻人立足起步（get started in life）比前几代人难得多，故选 [D]。\n［错项排除］[A] good-paying jobs are less available 仅为后文具体困难之一，未概括双方“总体起步更难”的核心共识；[B] the old made more life achievements 文中未作总成就量比较；[C] housing loans today are easy to obtain 与下句 finding affordable housing 面临艰难挑战（face a tougher climb）及下段 Schneider 独自负担不起月供（can\'t afford to pay my monthly mortgage payments）截然相反。' WHERE id = '696753cb-bed1-5bdc-a40e-49dad6375722'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'Every Saturday morning, at 9 am, more than 50,000 runners set off to run 5km around their local park. The Parkrun phenomenon began with a dozen friends and has inspired 400 events in the UK and more abroad. Events are free, staffed by thousands of volunteers. Runners range from four years old to grandparents; their times range from Andrew Baddeley\'s world record 13 minutes 48 seconds up to an hour.\n\nParkrun is succeeding where London\'s Olympic "legacy" is failing. Ten years ago on Monday, it was announced that the Games of the 30th Olympiad would be in London. Planning documents pledged that the great legacy of the Games would be to lever a nation of sport lovers away from their couches. The population would be fitter, healthier and produce more winners. It has not happened. The number of adults doing weekly sport did rise, by nearly 2 million in the run-up to 2012 — but the general population was growing faster. Worse, the numbers are now falling at an accelerating rate. The opposition claims primary school pupils doing at least two hours of sport a week have nearly halved. Obesity has risen among adults and children. Official retrospections continue as to why London 2012 failed to "inspire a generation." The success of Parkrun offers answers.\n\nParkrun is not a race but a time trial: Your only competitor is the clock. The ethos welcomes anybody. There is as much joy over a puffed-out first-timer being clapped over the line as there is about top talent shining. The Olympic bidders, by contrast, wanted to get more people doing sport and to produce more elite athletes. The dual aim was mixed up: The stress on success over taking part was intimidating for newcomers.\n\nIndeed, there is something a little absurd in the state getting involved in the planning of such a fundamentally "grassroots" concept as community sports associations. If there is a role for government, it should really be getting involved in providing common goods — making sure there is space for playing fields and the money to pave tennis and netball courts, and encouraging the provision of all these activities in schools. But successive governments have presided over selling green spaces, squeezing money from local authorities and declining attention on sport in education. Instead of wordy, worthy strategies, future governments need to do more to provide the conditions for sport to thrive. Or at least not make them worse.' WHERE id = '516d19f4-d2a3-5afa-85ac-c0c4f2421ce1'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'With so much focus on children\'s use of screens, it\'s easy for parents to forget about their own screen use. "Tech is designed to really suck you in," says Jenny Radesky in her study of digital play, "and digital products are there to promote maximal engagement. It makes it hard to disengage, and leads to a lot of bleed-over into the family routine."\n\nRadesky has studied the use of mobile phones and tablets at mealtimes by giving mother-child pairs a food-testing exercise. She found that mothers who used devices during the exercise started 20 per cent fewer verbal and 39 per cent fewer nonverbal interactions with their children. During a separate observation, she saw that phones became a source of tension in the family. Parents would be looking at their emails while the children would be making excited bids for their attention.\n\nInfants are wired to look at parents\' faces to try to understand their world, and if those faces are blank and unresponsive — as they often are when absorbed in a device — it can be extremely disconcerting for the children. Radesky cites the "still face experiment" devised by developmental psychologist Ed Tronick in the 1970s. In it, a mother is asked to interact with her child in a normal way before putting on a blank expression and not giving them any visual social feedback: The child becomes increasingly distressed as she tries to capture her mother\'s attention. "Parents don\'t have to be exquisitely present at all times, but there needs to be a balance and parents need to be responsive and sensitive to a child\'s verbal or nonverbal expressions of an emotional need," says Radesky.\n\nOn the other hand, Tronick himself is concerned that the worries about kids\' use of screens are born out of an "oppressive ideology that demands that parents should always be interacting" with their children: "It\'s based on a somewhat fantasised, very white, very upper-middle-class ideology that says if you\'re failing to expose your child to 30,000 words you are neglecting them." Tronick believes that just because a child isn\'t learning from the screen doesn\'t mean there\'s no value to it — particularly if it gives parents time to have a shower, do housework or simply have a break from their child. Parents, he says, can get a lot out of using their devices to speak to a friend or get some work out of the way. This can make them feel happier, which lets them be more available to their child the rest of the time.' WHERE id = 'd8609a07-d0bf-51b0-a4fa-5973dda0757b'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'Today, widespread social pressure to immediately go to college in conjunction with increasingly high expectations in a fast-moving world often causes students to completely overlook the possibility of taking a gap year. After all, if everyone you know is going to college in the fall, it seems silly to stay back a year, doesn\'t it? And after going to school for 12 years, it doesn\'t feel natural to spend a year doing something that isn\'t academic.\n\nBut while this may be true, it\'s not a good enough reason to condemn gap years. There\'s always a constant fear of falling behind everyone else on the socially perpetuated "race to the finish line," whether that be toward graduate school, medical school or a lucrative career. But despite common misconceptions, a gap year does not hinder the success of academic pursuits — in fact, it probably enhances it.\n\nStudies from the United States and Australia show that students who take a gap year are generally better prepared for and perform better in college than those who do not. Rather than pulling students back, a gap year pushes them ahead by preparing them for independence, new responsibilities and environmental changes — all things that first-year students often struggle with the most. Gap year experiences can lessen the blow when it comes to adjusting to college and being thrown into a brand new environment, making it easier to focus on academics and activities rather than acclimation blunders.\n\nIf you\'re not convinced of the inherent value in taking a year off to explore interests, then consider its financial impact on future academic choices. According to the National Center for Education Statistics, nearly 80 percent of college students end up changing their majors at least once. This isn\'t surprising, considering the basic mandatory high school curriculum leaves students with a poor understanding of the vast academic possibilities that await them in college. Many students find themselves listing one major on their college applications, but switching to another after taking college classes. It\'s not necessarily a bad thing, but depending on the school, it can be costly to make up credits after switching too late in the game. At Boston College, for example, you would have to complete an extra year were you to switch to the nursing school from another department. Taking a gap year to figure things out initially can help prevent stress and save money later on.' WHERE id = 'd9f62b4b-cb34-5a1b-b630-ead091abc8fd'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'Though often viewed as a problem for western states, the growing frequency of wildfires is a national concern because of its impact on federal tax dollars, says Professor Max Moritz, a specialist in fire ecology and management.\n\nIn 2015, the US Forest Service for the first time spent more than half of its $5.5 billion annual budget fighting fires — nearly double the percentage it spent on such efforts 20 years ago. In effect, fewer federal funds today are going towards the agency\'s other work — such as forest conservation, watershed and cultural resources management, and infrastructure upkeep — that affect the lives of all Americans.\n\nAnother nationwide concern is whether public funds from other agencies are going into construction in fire-prone districts. As Moritz puts it, how often are federal dollars building homes that are likely to be lost to a wildfire?\n\n"It\'s already a huge problem from a public expenditure perspective for the whole country," he says. "We need to take a magnifying glass to that. Like, \'Wait a minute, is this OK?\' Do we want instead to redirect those funds to concentrate on lower-hazard parts of the landscape?"\n\nSuch a view would require a corresponding shift in the way US society today views fire, researchers say.\n\nFor one thing, conversations about wildfires need to be more inclusive. Over the past decade, the focus has been on climate change — how the warming of the Earth from greenhouse gases is leading to conditions that worsen fires.\n\nWhile climate is a key element, Moritz says, it shouldn\'t come at the expense of the rest of the equation.\n\n"The human systems and the landscapes we live on are linked, and the interactions go both ways," he says. Failing to recognize that, he notes, leads to "an overly simplified view of what the solutions might be. Our perception of the problem and of what the solution is becomes very limited."\n\nAt the same time, people continue to treat fire as an event that needs to be wholly controlled and unleashed only out of necessity, says Professor Balch at the University of Colorado. But acknowledging fire\'s inevitable presence in human life is an attitude crucial to developing the laws, policies, and practices that make it as safe as possible, she says.\n\n"We\'ve disconnected ourselves from living with fire," Balch says. "It is really important to understand and try and tease out what is the human connection with fire today."' WHERE id = 'eca54e9d-3479-5641-bf79-3606e655ca4f'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'The decline in American manufacturing is a common refrain, particularly from Donald Trump. "We don\'t make anything anymore," he told Fox News, while defending his own made-in-Mexico clothing line.\n\nWithout question, manufacturing has taken a significant hit during recent decades, and further trade deals raise questions about whether new shocks could hit manufacturing. But there is also a different way to look at the data.\n\nAcross the country, factory owners are now grappling with a new challenge: Instead of having too many workers, they may end up with too few. Despite trade competition and outsourcing, American manufacturing still needs to replace tens of thousands of retiring boomers every year. Millennials may not be that interested in taking their place. Other industries are recruiting them with similar or better pay.\n\nFor factory owners, it all adds up to stiff competition for workers — and upward pressure on wages. "They\'re harder to find and they have job offers," says Jay Dunwell, president of Wolverine Coil Spring, a family-owned firm, "They may be coming [into the workforce], but they\'ve been plucked by other industries that are also doing as well as manufacturing." Mr. Dunwell has begun bringing high school juniors to the factory so they can get exposed to its culture.\n\nAt RoMan Manufacturing, a maker of electrical transformers and welding equipment that his father cofounded in 1980, Robert Roth keeps a close eye on the age of his nearly 200 workers. Five are retiring this year. Mr. Roth has three community-college students enrolled in a work-placement program, with a starting wage of $13 an hour that rises to $17 after two years.\n\nAt a worktable inside the transformer plant, young Jason Stenquist looks flustered by the copper coils he\'s trying to assemble and the arrival of two visitors. It\'s his first week on the job. Asked about his choice of career, he says at high school he considered medical school before switching to electrical engineering. "I love working with tools. I love creating," he says.\n\nBut to win over these young workers, manufacturers have to clear another major hurdle: parents, who lived through the worst US economic downturn since the Great Depression, telling them to avoid the factory. Millennials "remember their father and mother both were laid off. They blame it on the manufacturing recession," says Birgit Klohs, chief executive of The Right Place, a business development agency for western Michigan.\n\nThese concerns aren\'t misplaced: Employment in manufacturing has fallen from 17 million in 1970 to 12 million in 2015. When the recovery began, worker shortages first appeared in the high-skilled trades. Now shortages are appearing at the mid-skill levels.\n\n"The gap is between the jobs that take no skills and those that require a lot of skill," says Rob Spohr, a business professor at Montcalm Community College. "There\'re enough people to fill the jobs at McDonalds and other places where you don\'t need to have much skill. It\'s that gap in between, and that\'s where the problem is."\n\nJulie Parks of Grand Rapids Community College points to another key to luring Millennials into manufacturing: a work/life balance. While their parents were content to work long hours, young people value flexibility. "Overtime is not attractive to this generation. They really want to live their lives," she says.' WHERE id = 'ff3e00e5-4c95-5977-85b6-b0f6979d6428'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [1] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "boasting", "content": "boasting"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "denying", "content": "denying"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "warning", "content": "warning"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "ensuring", "content": "ensuring"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］动词词义辨析与上下文语义逻辑。\n［精准定位］定位至首段第二句：Today is no different, with academics, writers, and activists once again [1] that technology is replacing human workers.\n［解题思路］首句提出几个世纪以来人们一直在推测“没有工作的未来”，第二句借助“Today is no different”延续悲观警示，随后指出富人垄断资本、大众挣扎在贫困中。因此学者、作家等再次“警告（warning）”技术正在取代人类工人，符合语义，故选[C]。\n［错项排除］[A] boasting（自夸、吹嘘）、[B] denying（否认）与后文严峻危机描述相悖；[D] ensuring（确保、担保）与负面社会景象不搭。' WHERE id = 'f763dad3-0558-574d-8527-7f9c8f0737bc'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [2] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "inequality", "content": "inequality"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "instability", "content": "instability"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "unreliability", "content": "unreliability"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "uncertainty", "content": "uncertainty"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］名词辨析与冒号释义照应。\n［精准定位］定位至首段末句：Some imagine that the coming work-free world will be defined by [2]: A few wealthy people will own all the capital, and the masses will struggle in an impoverished wasteland.\n［解题思路］冒号后面具体阐释了空格词的内涵：少数富人占有全部资本，广大民众在贫穷荒原中苦苦挣扎。这正是极度贫富分化与社会“不平等（inequality）”的直观写照，故选[A]。\n［错项排除］[B] instability（不稳定）、[C] unreliability（不可靠）与[D] uncertainty（不确定性）均未切中“少数人掌握财富而多数人贫困”的对比核心。' WHERE id = '38e2c754-4044-5f58-b5db-0edbde7e4f53'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [3] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "policy", "content": "policy"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "guideline", "content": "guideline"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "resolution", "content": "resolution"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "prediction", "content": "prediction"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］名词辨析与上下文语义呼应。\n［精准定位］定位至第二段首句：A different and not mutually exclusive [3] holds that the future will be a wasteland of a different sort...\n［解题思路］第一段介绍了关于无工作未来的一种设想（Some imagine...），本段紧承其后引出另一种与前者并不互斥的对未来的“预测（prediction）”，即人们将陷入漫无目的的空虚生活，故选[D]。\n［错项排除］[A] policy（政策）、[B] guideline（准则）与[C] resolution（决议）均属于官方或机构文书范畴，脱离了社会发展趋势探讨语境。' WHERE id = '658c86d9-f0c8-50be-a6b8-07d8caed6340'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [4] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "characterized", "content": "characterized"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "divided", "content": "divided"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "balanced", "content": "balanced"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "measured", "content": "measured"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］过去分词固定搭配与后置定语。\n［精准定位］定位至第二段首句后半句：...one [4] by purposelessness: Without jobs to give their lives [5]...\n［解题思路］one 指代前文的 wasteland，此处需要动词被动形式构成“以无目的性为特征的荒原”。be characterized by... 为高频固定搭配，意为“具有……特征、以……为特点”，故选[A]。\n［错项排除］[B] divided（被划分）、[C] balanced（被平衡）与[D] measured（被衡量）均不能与 by purposelessness 搭配描述荒原的精神特征。' WHERE id = 'e2e39a39-04d4-5ec5-ab1d-c304b9a4b77b'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [5] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "wisdom", "content": "wisdom"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "meaning", "content": "meaning"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "glory", "content": "glory"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "freedom", "content": "freedom"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］名词搭配与上下文因果关系。\n［精准定位］定位至第二段首句冒号后：Without jobs to give their lives [5], people will simply become lazy and depressed.\n［解题思路］前文强调该荒原的特征是“purposelessness（漫无目的）”，紧接着具体阐明原因：没有工作来赋予生命“意义（meaning）”，人们就会变得懒散而沮丧。give one\'s life meaning 完美对应 purposelessness，故选[B]。\n［错项排除］[A] wisdom（智慧）、[C] glory（荣耀）与[D] freedom（自由）均不能精准回应前文的“漫无目的与精神空虚”。' WHERE id = '3af4870c-332e-5bfa-85b9-86f407f05ee5'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [6] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Instead", "content": "Instead"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Indeed", "content": "Indeed"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Thus", "content": "Thus"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Nevertheless", "content": "Nevertheless"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］逻辑副词与例证顺承。\n［精准定位］定位至第二段第二句句首：[6], today\'s unemployed don\'t seem to be having a great time.\n［解题思路］前一句论断失去工作会使人沮丧，本句接着以“当今失业人群过得并不愉快”及民调中失业者高抑郁率的事例加以佐证，属于语意递进与确认。Indeed（的确、事实上）承前作实证补充，故选[B]。\n［错项排除］[A] Instead（相反）和[D] Nevertheless（然而）表转折对比；[C] Thus（因此）表因果，前句预测与当下现实不构成因果关系。' WHERE id = '0418ce17-8bee-51fb-ab47-487699e4053a'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [7] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "rich", "content": "rich"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "urban", "content": "urban"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "working", "content": "working"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "educated", "content": "educated"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］形容词辨析与对照组对比。\n［精准定位］定位至第二段第三句：...20 percent of Americans who have been unemployed for at least a year report having depression, double the rate for [7] Americans.\n［解题思路］统计对比必然在“长期失业群体（unemployed）”与“在职群体（working）”之间展开：长期失业美国人的抑郁比例是在职美国人的两倍，对比鲜明合理，故选[C]。\n［错项排除］[A] rich（富有的）、[B] urban（城市的）与[D] educated（受过教育的）均未与“unemployed（失业的）”构成同一维度的精确对照组。' WHERE id = 'f0f7bea7-50a5-518a-b4d7-71c137f7949b'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [8] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "explanation", "content": "explanation"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "requirement", "content": "requirement"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "compensation", "content": "compensation"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "substitute", "content": "substitute"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］名词辨析与介词搭配。\n［精准定位］定位至第二段第四句：Also, some research suggests that the [8] for rising rates of mortality, mental-health problems, and addiction... is a shortage of well-paid jobs.\n［解题思路］句干为主系表结构“……的原因/解释是高薪工作短缺”。the explanation for... 意为“对……的解释、原因”，符合科学研究阐释社会现象因果的语境，故选[A]。\n［错项排除］[B] requirement（要求）、[C] compensation（补偿）与[D] substitute（替代品）代入后语义逻辑均荒谬不通。' WHERE id = '1408d81c-af08-58b2-acc7-d657d7858694'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [9] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "under", "content": "under"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "beyond", "content": "beyond"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "alongside", "content": "alongside"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "among", "content": "among"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］介词辨析与群体范围。\n［精准定位］定位至第二段第四句：...rising rates of mortality, mental-health problems, and addiction [9] poorly-educated, middle-aged people...\n［解题思路］此处表示死亡率、心理健康问题和成瘾比例上升发生在受教育程度较低的中年人这一群体之中。among（在……群体当中）精准引出统计适用范围，故选[D]。\n［错项排除］[A] under（在……下面）、[B] beyond（超出）与[C] alongside（在……旁边）均无法用于指代某类人口中的问题分布。' WHERE id = 'd9f9aebe-b7cc-577b-a081-24ec7f1f2eb3'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [10] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "leave behind", "content": "leave behind"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "make up", "content": "make up"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "worry about", "content": "worry about"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "set aside", "content": "set aside"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］动词短语搭配与句意总结。\n［精准定位］定位至第二段末句：Perhaps this is why many [10] the agonizing dullness of a jobless future.\n［解题思路］上文列举了当今失业者的高抑郁率和健康危机，本句总结指出：或许正是由于这些现实惨象，才使得许多人对无工作未来的煎熬乏味感到“担忧/焦虑（worry about）”，故选[C]。\n［错项排除］[A] leave behind（遗留、抛下）、[B] make up（弥补、编造）与[D] set aside（留出、搁置）均与面对悲观预期的心理感受不符。' WHERE id = '04a97c0b-fd91-5855-b288-863e00031cb6'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [11] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "statistically", "content": "statistically"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "occasionally", "content": "occasionally"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "necessarily", "content": "necessarily"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "economically", "content": "economically"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］副词辨析与逻辑推导批判。\n［解题思路］第三段首句以转折连词 But 开启对前文悲观预测的反驳：“但这并不[11]（必然）能从这类调查发现中推导出来（But it doesn\'t necessarily follow from findings like these...）”。not necessarily follow 为经典学术驳论句型，否定“前提数据”到“无工作必将充满焦虑”之间的必然因果推导，故选［C］。\n［错项排除］［A］statistically（在统计学上）、［B］occasionally（偶尔）与［D］economically（在经济层面）均偏离“对逻辑推演必然性提出质疑”的严谨语境。' WHERE id = 'b7ddd3df-acec-5e02-b9b3-ca7afe85c235'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [12] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "chances", "content": "chances"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "downsides", "content": "downsides"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "benefits", "content": "benefits"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "principles", "content": "principles"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］名词语义辨析与情感色彩。\n［精准定位］定位至第三段第二句：Such visions are based on the [12] of being unemployed in a society built on the concept of employment.\n［解题思路］前文将失去工作的未来描绘为抑郁、无意义的荒原，本句剖析这种悲观预言产生的根源：它是基于在“以雇佣为核心概念”的社会里失去工作的“弊端/负面影响（downsides）”，故选[B]。\n［错项排除］[A] chances（机会）、[C] benefits（益处）与[D] principles（原则）均无法匹配前文失业所带来的痛楚图景。' WHERE id = 'b3e90116-f227-5e7a-bd03-0a45fe4888f3'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [13] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "absence", "content": "absence"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "height", "content": "height"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "face", "content": "face"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "course", "content": "course"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］介词短语固定搭配。\n［精准定位］定位至第三段第三句句首：In the [13] of work, a society designed with other ends in mind could [14] strikingly different circumstances...\n［解题思路］本句设想如果在一个“没有工作（In the absence of work）”的社会里重新规划社会目标，劳动与闲暇的前景将会截然不同。in the absence of 意为“在缺乏……、没有……的情况下”，呼应全文主线 a future without work，故选[A]。\n［错项排除］[B] height（顶点）、[C] face（面对）与[D] course（过程）搭配此处均逻辑不通。' WHERE id = '3c6a6a18-2bd5-5acf-9c4d-5cd97eb3c143'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [14] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "disturb", "content": "disturb"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "restore", "content": "restore"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "exclude", "content": "exclude"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "yield", "content": "yield"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］动词辨析与上下文语义。\n［精准定位］定位至第三段第三句：...a society designed with other ends in mind could [14] strikingly different circumstances for the future of labor and leisure.\n［解题思路］主语为“以其他目标为基础设计的社会”，宾语为“截然不同的劳动与闲暇环境”。yield 意为“产生、带来、孕育（结果或环境）”，契合“全新制度设计催生全新面貌”的逻辑，故选[D]。\n［错项排除］[A] disturb（打扰）、[B] restore（恢复过去状态，与 different 冲突）与[C] exclude（排斥）均脱离语境。' WHERE id = '65fbeafe-9514-53fe-afd3-d9295cfafa7c'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [15] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "model", "content": "model"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "practice", "content": "practice"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "virtue", "content": "virtue"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "hardship", "content": "hardship"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］名词辨析与褒贬反转。\n［精准定位］定位至第三段第四至五句：Today, the [15] of work may be a bit overblown. "Many jobs are boring, degrading, unhealthy, and a waste of human potential," says John Danaher...\n［解题思路］紧接其后的引语指出许多工作枯燥乏味、贬低人格且浪费潜能，由此反推本句核心观点：当今社会对工作所谓“美德/正面价值（virtue）”的吹捧未免有些言过其实（overblown），故选[C]。\n［错项排除］[A] model（模式）、[B] practice（做法）与[D] hardship（艰苦）均不构成后文批判“把工作吹得太神圣”的对立靶点。' WHERE id = '0f127eab-104a-53f8-899c-3b393354d479'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [16] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "tricky", "content": "tricky"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "lengthy", "content": "lengthy"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "mysterious", "content": "mysterious"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "scarce", "content": "scarce"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］形容词辨析与转折常识。\n［精准定位］定位至第四段首句：These days, because leisure time is relatively [16] for most workers, people use their free time to counterbalance...\n［解题思路］对于当今大多数上班族而言，闲暇时间相对“稀缺（scarce）”，因此只能利用有限的空闲时间去抵消工作耗损。scarce 与后文假如不需要工作（in which I don\'t have to work）就有充裕精力形成对比，故选[D]。\n［错项排除］[A] tricky（棘手的）、[B] lengthy（冗长的）与[C] mysterious（神秘的）均违背当代工薪阶层闲暇有限的事实。' WHERE id = '253f5a6e-b123-59c5-b24d-74dc03b96aa7'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [17] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "demands", "content": "demands"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "standards", "content": "standards"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "qualities", "content": "qualities"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "threats", "content": "threats"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］名词辨析与上下文呼应。\n［精准定位］定位至第四段首句：...people use their free time to counterbalance the intellectual and emotional [17] of their jobs.\n［解题思路］下句提到下班后感到筋疲力尽，可知工作对人智力与情感产生了高强度消耗与负担，demands 意为“（对精力、能力等的）严苛要求、消耗”，精准搭配 counterbalance，故选[A]。\n［错项排除］[B] standards（标准）、[C] qualities（品质）与[D] threats（威胁）均不能与智力、情感上的日常耗竭形成对应。' WHERE id = '38dfb385-b854-5466-b598-af892f64df03'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [18] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "ignored", "content": "ignored"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "tired", "content": "tired"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "confused", "content": "confused"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "starved", "content": "starved"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］形容词词义辨析与日常工作状态语境。\n［精准定位］定位至第四段第二句："When I come home from a hard day\'s work, I often feel [18]," Danaher says...\n［解题思路］句中明确给出场景线索“from a hard day\'s work（辛苦工作一天回到家后）”，并与后半句“在不必工作的世界里，我的感受也许会大不相同”形成今昔对比。辛苦劳作一天后人最常感到的生理状态是“疲惫的、劳累的”，故选［B］tired。\n［错项排除］［A］ignored 意为“被忽视的”，与繁重工作后的体力消耗无直接联系；［C］confused 意为“困惑的，糊涂的”，不能呼应 a hard day\'s work 造成的身心疲劳；［D］starved 意为“饥饿的”，原文聚焦工作的脑力和情绪消耗，而非饮食饥饱。' WHERE id = '42846f10-9a38-5d36-bdde-3d86178e8a43'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [19] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "off", "content": "off"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "against", "content": "against"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "behind", "content": "behind"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "into", "content": "into"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］动词短语固定搭配。\n［精准定位］定位至第四段末句：...perhaps different enough to throw himself [19] a hobby or a passion project...\n［解题思路］throw oneself into sth. 是英语中极其地道的固定搭配，意为“全身心投入某项事业或爱好”。句意指在无需工作的世界里，人们会满腔热情地投身于兴趣爱好之中，故选[D]。\n［错项排除］[A] throw off（摆脱、脱掉）、[B] throw against（摔向）与[C] throw behind（支持、落后）均无“全神贯注投入爱好”的搭配用法。' WHERE id = '2fc7a793-5c81-5ebf-89f2-97023dcaa695'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [20] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "academic", "content": "academic"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "professional", "content": "professional"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "personal", "content": "personal"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "cultural", "content": "cultural"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］形容词对比与文章主旨收束。\n［精准定位］定位至第四段末句末尾：...with the intensity usually reserved for [20] matters.\n［解题思路］后文将业余爱好（a hobby or a passion project）与以往仅用于工作事务的专注强度进行对比，这里指通常留给“职业/工作（professional）”事务的心力强度，收束全文关于劳动与闲暇转换的讨论，故选[B]。\n［错项排除］[A] technological（技术的）、[C] educational（教育的）与[D] interpersonal（人际的）均脱离了“职业工作 vs 业余爱好”的对比框架。' WHERE id = '02d7be36-110a-5aab-a0ae-46fdc7acc221'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to Paragraph 1, Parkrun has', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "created many jobs", "content": "created many jobs"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "gained great popularity", "content": "gained great popularity"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "become an official festival", "content": "become an official festival"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "strengthened community ties", "content": "strengthened community ties"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］事实细节题（第一段）。\n［精准定位］定位至第一段第一至二句：“Every Saturday morning, at 9 am, more than 50,000 runners set off to run 5km around their local park. The Parkrun phenomenon began with a dozen friends and has inspired 400 events in the UK and more abroad.”\n［解题思路］首段开篇指出每逢周六早晨都有逾五万名跑者参加 Parkrun，该活动从十几个朋友发起，发展至在英国及海外催生出400多场赛事。这充分证明“公园跑”活动已获得广泛普及与极大欢迎，故选 [B] gained great popularity。\n［错项排除］[A] created many jobs（创造了许多就业岗位）与末句“staffed by thousands of volunteers（由数千名志愿者义务支持）”矛盾；[C] become an official festival（成为官方节日）属无中生有；[D] strengthened community ties（加强了社区纽带）并非首段数据直接陈述的事实。' WHERE id = 'c413129c-78ed-5902-9eb4-4c73ce2ede0d'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'With regard to mass sports, the author holds that governments should', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "increase funds for sports clubs", "content": "increase funds for sports clubs"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "invest in public sports facilities", "content": "invest in public sports facilities"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "organize \\"grassroots\\" sports events", "content": "organize \\"grassroots\\" sports events"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "supervise local sports associations", "content": "supervise local sports associations"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］作者观点题（第四段）。\n［精准定位］定位至第四段第二句：“If there is a role for government, it should really be getting involved in providing common goods — making sure there is space for playing fields and the money to pave tennis and netball courts, and encouraging the provision of all these activities in schools.”\n［解题思路］作者明确指出政府应当扮演提供公共产品（common goods）的角色——确保有场地建设运动场、拨款修筑网球和无板篮球场（playing fields / courts）。这实质上就是在呼吁政府投资公共体育设施，故选 [B] invest in public sports facilities。\n［错项排除］[A] increase funds for sports clubs（增加对体育俱乐部的资金）将公共场地偷换为私人或协会俱乐部；[C] organize "grassroots" sports events（组织草根赛事）与首句批评政府插手草根组织规划（something a little absurd in the state getting involved in the planning of... "grassroots" concept）相悖；[D] supervise local sports associations（监督地方体育协会）同首句背道而驰。' WHERE id = '750b56ea-a1b4-5a37-9425-12e9938a25ac'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The author\'s attitude to what UK governments have done for sports is', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "critical", "content": "critical"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "tolerant", "content": "tolerant"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "uncertain", "content": "uncertain"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "sympathetic", "content": "sympathetic"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］观点态度题（全文综合）。\n［精准定位］全文通过对比民间草根赛事 Parkrun 的兴盛与伦敦奥运会“遗产”在大众体育领域的落空，直指历届英国政府的问题（第四段：“Instead of wordy, worthy strategies, future governments need to do more to provide the conditions for sport to thrive. Or at least not make them worse.”）。\n［解题思路］作者一方面批判奥运重精英、轻参与的失策，另一方面批评历届政府出售绿地、削减地方财政且减少学校体育关注，直言政府与其空谈冠冕堂皇的战略，不如切实改善场地设施或至少别让情况更糟。全文对英国政府体育政策持明确批评态度（critical），故选 [A]。\n［错项排除］[B] tolerant（宽容的）、[C] uncertain（不确定的）与 [D] sympathetic（同情的）均未能体现作者对政府卖地裁撤预算、只做空洞战略的严厉指责。' WHERE id = '26b482b9-19ba-5d44-bb4d-6b2e75c535a1'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Radesky\'s food-testing exercise shows that mothers\' use of devices', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "takes away babies\' appetite", "content": "takes away babies\' appetite"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "distracts children\'s attention", "content": "distracts children\'s attention"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "slows down babies\' verbal development", "content": "slows down babies\' verbal development"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "reduces mother-child communication", "content": "reduces mother-child communication"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］事实细节题（第二段）。\n［精准定位］定位至第二段第一至二句：“Radesky has studied the use of mobile phones and tablets at mealtimes by giving mother-child pairs a food-testing exercise. She found that mothers who used devices during the exercise started 20 per cent fewer verbal and 39 per cent fewer nonverbal interactions with their children.”\n［解题思路］实验明确表明在食物测试期间使用电子设备的母亲，与子女之间发起的口头互动减少20%，非口头互动减少39%，直接证实母亲使用电子设备会显著减少母子间的沟通交流，故选 [D] reduces mother-child communication。\n［错项排除］[A] takes away babies\' appetite（夺走婴儿食欲）将食物测试（food-testing exercise）场景无中生有延伸为食欲问题；[B] distracts children\'s attention（分散儿童注意力）与第三句孩子正努力争夺母亲注意力（children would be making excited bids for their attention）方向相反；[C] slows down babies\' verbal development（延缓婴儿语言发育）把口头互动减少过度拔高为发育迟缓。' WHERE id = 'ff4843dc-b2f0-516c-b003-d1e9fb0e50b6'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Radesky cites the "still face experiment" to show that', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "it is easy for children to get used to blank expressions", "content": "it is easy for children to get used to blank expressions"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "verbal expressions are unnecessary for emotional exchange", "content": "verbal expressions are unnecessary for emotional exchange"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "parents need to respond to children\'s emotional needs", "content": "parents need to respond to children\'s emotional needs"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "children are insensitive to changes in their parents\' mood", "content": "children are insensitive to changes in their parents\' mood"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］例证目的题（第三段）。\n［精准定位］定位至第三段第二至四句：“Radesky cites the \'still face experiment\' devised by developmental psychologist Ed Tronick in the 1970s. In it, a mother is asked to interact with her child in a normal way before putting on a blank expression and not giving them any visual social feedback: The child becomes increasingly distressed as she tries to capture her mother\'s attention. \'Parents don\'t have to be exquisitely present at all times, but there needs to be a balance and parents need to be responsive and sensitive to a child\'s verbal or nonverbal expressions of an emotional need,\' says Radesky.”\n［解题思路］在“静止脸实验”中，母亲摆出毫无回应的表情，导致孩子在努力吸引母亲注意的过程中愈发焦虑痛苦（becomes increasingly distressed）；拉德斯基紧随其后得出结论：父母必须对孩子口头或非口头的情感需求保持敏感和回应，故选 [C] parents need to respond to children\'s emotional needs。\n［错项排除］[A] it is easy for children to get used to blank expressions 与孩子日益痛苦（increasingly distressed）直接相反；[B] verbal expressions are unnecessary for emotional exchange 曲解实验本身测试非言语视觉反馈的设计，也违背末句需兼顾 verbal or nonverbal expressions 的论述；[D] children are insensitive to changes in their parents\' mood 同样与孩子反应强烈相悖。' WHERE id = '04fa0c38-3b0d-508d-ba2a-bd1535d2b7be'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'A gap year may save money for students by helping them', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "switch to another college", "content": "switch to another college"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "decide on the right major", "content": "decide on the right major"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "avoid academic failures", "content": "avoid academic failures"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "establish long-term goals", "content": "establish long-term goals"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］因果细节题（第四段）。\n［精准定位］定位至第四段第二至六句：“According to the National Center for Education Statistics, nearly 80 percent of college students end up changing their majors at least once... Many students find themselves listing one major on their college applications, but switching to another after taking college classes... it can be costly to make up credits after switching too late in the game. At Boston College, for example, you would have to complete an extra year were you to switch to the nursing school from another department. Taking a gap year to figure things out initially can help prevent stress and save money later on.”\n［解题思路］末段指出近80%的大学生至少转过一次专业，如果在大学后期换专业可能需要花高昂代价补修学分（比如波士顿学院转至护理学院需多读一年）。间隔年让学生提前想清楚自己真正适合的学科方向，从而选定正确专业、省下后续巨额学费，故选 [B] decide on the right major。\n［错项排除］[A] switch to another college（转学到另一所大学）偷换原文 change their majors（更换专业）；[C] avoid academic failures（避免学业挂科失败）无中生有；[D] establish long-term goals（确立长远目标）过于宽泛，未落脚于第四段省钱的直接机制——避免转专业。' WHERE id = '269d7810-ce3e-5aeb-981c-d256153c4aad'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'More frequent wildfires have become a national concern because in 2015 they', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "consumed a record-high percentage of budget", "content": "consumed a record-high percentage of budget"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "exhausted unprecedented management efforts", "content": "exhausted unprecedented management efforts"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "severely damaged the ecology of western states", "content": "severely damaged the ecology of western states"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "caused a huge rise of infrastructure expenditure", "content": "caused a huge rise of infrastructure expenditure"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］因果细节题（第一、二段）。\n［精准定位］定位至第一段与第二段第一句：“...the growing frequency of wildfires is a national concern because of its impact on federal tax dollars, says Professor Max Moritz, a specialist in fire ecology and management. In 2015, the US Forest Service for the first time spent more than half of its $5.5 billion annual budget fighting fires — nearly double the percentage it spent on such efforts 20 years ago.”\n［解题思路］野火频发之所以成为全美关切，关键在于对联邦税收的挤压：2015年美国林务局首次将55亿美元年度预算的过半数额（几乎是20年前占比的两倍）用于扑救山火，耗费了创纪录高比例的财政预算，故选 [A] consumed a record-high percentage of budget。\n［错项排除］[B] exhausted unprecedented management efforts 偷换了文化与资源管理经费被挤压的表述；[C] severely damaged the ecology of western states 属于首句所说的传统局限于西部的狭隘认知，并非成为“全国性问题”的原因；[D] caused a huge rise of infrastructure expenditure 与第二段末句“fewer federal funds today are going towards... infrastructure upkeep”正好相反。' WHERE id = '2f22b13c-13f3-5965-9773-70355058acde'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The overly simplified view Moritz mentions is a result of failing to', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "discover the fundamental makeup of nature", "content": "discover the fundamental makeup of nature"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "explore the mechanism of the human systems", "content": "explore the mechanism of the human systems"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "understand the interrelations of man and nature", "content": "understand the interrelations of man and nature"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "maximize the role of landscape in human life", "content": "maximize the role of landscape in human life"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］因果细节题（第八段）。\n［精准定位］定位至第八段：“\'The human systems and the landscapes we live on are linked, and the interactions go both ways,\' he says. Failing to recognize that, he notes, leads to \'an overly simplified view of what the solutions might be.\'”\n［解题思路］莫里茨明确指出，人类社会系统与我们居住的自然景观之间紧密关联且存在双向互动（linked, and the interactions go both ways）；未能认识到这一点（that），正是导致解决方案过于片面简单化（an overly simplified view）的原因。选项 [C] understand the interrelations of man and nature 正是对人景双向关联的规范概括，故选 [C]。\n［错项排除］[A] discover the fundamental makeup of nature（发现自然的根本构成）、[B] explore the mechanism of the human systems（探索人类系统运作机制）与[D] maximize the role of landscape in human life（最大化自然景观的作用）均割裂了“人与自然双向互动（interrelations）”的核心关联。' WHERE id = 'eecc91d0-d9f1-54e9-a25b-de280d7d4ce2'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Professor Balch points out that fire is something man should', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "do away with", "content": "do away with"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "come to terms with", "content": "come to terms with"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "pay a price for", "content": "pay a price for"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "keep away from", "content": "keep away from"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］人物观点题（第九、十段）。\n［精准定位］定位至第九段末尾与第十段：“...says Professor Balch at the University of Colorado. But acknowledging fire\'s inevitable presence in human life is an attitude crucial to developing the laws, policies, and practices that make it as safe as possible, she says. \'We\'ve disconnected ourselves from living with fire,\' Balch says. \'It is really important to understand and try and tease out what is the human connection with fire today.\'”\n［解题思路］科罗拉多大学鲍尔奇教授指出，人类习惯把火看作必须彻底控制之物，从而割裂了“与火共存（living with fire）”的联系；实际上承认火在人类生活中不可避免的存在至关重要。come to terms with 意为“与……妥协/共存、学会面对并接受现实”，准确契合 Balch 倡导与火理性共存的观点，故选 [B]。\n［错项排除］[A] do away with（废除、彻底消灭）对应人们过去“wholly controlled”的错误态度；[C] pay a price for（为……付出代价）偏离题意；[D] keep away from（远离）与重新梳理人与火之联系（tease out what is the human connection with fire）相悖。' WHERE id = 'da1b1f33-5767-58d7-8dc9-7af2ec00219e'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Match Jay Dunwell with the statement that reflects his/her view (A-G):', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "says that he switched to electrical engineering because he loves working with tools.", "content": "says that he switched to electrical engineering because he loves working with tools."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "points out that there are enough people to fill the jobs that don\'t need much skill.", "content": "points out that there are enough people to fill the jobs that don\'t need much skill."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "points out that the US doesn\'t manufacture anything anymore.", "content": "points out that the US doesn\'t manufacture anything anymore."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "believes that it is important to keep a close eye on the age of his workers.", "content": "believes that it is important to keep a close eye on the age of his workers."}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "says that for factory owners, workers are harder to find because of stiff competition.", "content": "says that for factory owners, workers are harder to find because of stiff competition."}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "points out that a work/life balance can attract young people into manufacturing.", "content": "points out that a work/life balance can attract young people into manufacturing."}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "says that the manufacturing recession is to blame for the lay-off of the young people\'s parents.", "content": "says that the manufacturing recession is to blame for the lay-off of the young people\'s parents."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'E', explanation = E'［考点提炼］人物观点匹配题（第四段）。\n［精准定位］定位至第四段：“For factory owners, it all adds up to stiff competition for workers — and upward pressure on wages. \'They\'re harder to find and they have job offers,\' says Jay Dunwell, president of Wolverine Coil Spring, a family-owned firm, \'They may be coming [into the workforce], but they\'ve been plucked by other industries that are also doing as well as manufacturing.\'”\n［解题思路］Wolverine Coil Spring 总裁杰伊·邓韦尔谈及工厂主的用工处境时直言，其他发展同样良好的行业正把新生代劳动力招揽一空，由于对工人的激烈竞争（stiff competition for workers），工人更加难寻且工资水涨船高。选项 [E]“says that for factory owners, workers are harder to find because of stiff competition”精确复现原文，故选 [E]。\n［错项排除］段落同时提到其尝试邀请高中生参观工厂，但核心观点在于同行与跨行业抢人大战导致雇主招工难，与 [B] 无需技能岗位或 [D] 关注员工年龄无关（[D] 对应第五段 Robert Roth）。' WHERE id = 'e3a646cd-f356-58b6-a412-c857031e157a'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Match Jason Stenquist with the statement that reflects his/her view (A-G):', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "says that he switched to electrical engineering because he loves working with tools.", "content": "says that he switched to electrical engineering because he loves working with tools."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "points out that there are enough people to fill the jobs that don\'t need much skill.", "content": "points out that there are enough people to fill the jobs that don\'t need much skill."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "points out that the US doesn\'t manufacture anything anymore.", "content": "points out that the US doesn\'t manufacture anything anymore."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "believes that it is important to keep a close eye on the age of his workers.", "content": "believes that it is important to keep a close eye on the age of his workers."}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "says that for factory owners, workers are harder to find because of stiff competition.", "content": "says that for factory owners, workers are harder to find because of stiff competition."}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "points out that a work/life balance can attract young people into manufacturing.", "content": "points out that a work/life balance can attract young people into manufacturing."}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "says that the manufacturing recession is to blame for the lay-off of the young people\'s parents.", "content": "says that the manufacturing recession is to blame for the lay-off of the young people\'s parents."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］人物观点匹配题（第六段）。\n［精准定位］定位至第六段：“At a worktable inside the transformer plant, young Jason Stenquist looks flustered by the copper coils he\'s trying to assemble... Asked about his choice of career, he says at high school he considered medical school before switching to electrical engineering. \'I love working with tools. I love creating,\' he says.”\n［解题思路］变压器工厂的年轻工人杰森·斯滕奎斯特在组装铜线圈时接受采访，谈及自己的职业选择：他在高中时原本考虑过医学院，后来改学电气工程（switching to electrical engineering），因为他热爱用工具亲手创造（love working with tools）。选项 [A]“says that he switched to electrical engineering because he loves working with tools”精准对应原文，故选 [A]。\n［错项排除］[F] 提及工作生活平衡吸引年轻人，出自末段 Julie Parks；[C] 为首段 Donald Trump 言论，均与 Stenquist 无关。' WHERE id = '9de4e2ad-fb75-568e-8330-a1c2e53a20a4'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Match Birgit Klohs with the statement that reflects his/her view (A-G):', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "says that he switched to electrical engineering because he loves working with tools.", "content": "says that he switched to electrical engineering because he loves working with tools."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "points out that there are enough people to fill the jobs that don\'t need much skill.", "content": "points out that there are enough people to fill the jobs that don\'t need much skill."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "points out that the US doesn\'t manufacture anything anymore.", "content": "points out that the US doesn\'t manufacture anything anymore."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "believes that it is important to keep a close eye on the age of his workers.", "content": "believes that it is important to keep a close eye on the age of his workers."}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "says that for factory owners, workers are harder to find because of stiff competition.", "content": "says that for factory owners, workers are harder to find because of stiff competition."}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "points out that a work/life balance can attract young people into manufacturing.", "content": "points out that a work/life balance can attract young people into manufacturing."}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "says that the manufacturing recession is to blame for the lay-off of the young people\'s parents.", "content": "says that the manufacturing recession is to blame for the lay-off of the young people\'s parents."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'G', explanation = E'［考点提炼］人物观点匹配题（第七段）。\n［精准定位］定位至第七段：“But to win over these young workers, manufacturers have to clear another major hurdle: parents... telling them to avoid the factory. Millennials \'remember their father and mother both were laid off. They blame it on the manufacturing recession,\' says Birgit Klohs, chief executive of The Right Place, a business development agency for western Michigan.”\n［解题思路］经济发展机构负责人伯吉特·克洛斯指出，吸引年轻人的另一大障碍来自经历过大萧条以来最严重衰退的父母辈；千禧一代记得父母双双遭到解雇（father and mother both were laid off），并将此归咎于制造业衰退（blame it on the manufacturing recession）。选项 [G]“says that the manufacturing recession is to blame for the lay-off of the young people\'s parents”完整同义复现其核心论断，故选 [G]。\n［错项排除］[C] 提及美国不再制造任何东西系首段特朗普观点；[D] 关注员工年龄为 RoMan Manufacturing 负责人 Robert Roth 的做法。' WHERE id = 'ab788497-cfd1-5278-ab1f-d9759082904b'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Match Rob Spohr with the statement that reflects his/her view (A-G):', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "says that he switched to electrical engineering because he loves working with tools.", "content": "says that he switched to electrical engineering because he loves working with tools."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "points out that there are enough people to fill the jobs that don\'t need much skill.", "content": "points out that there are enough people to fill the jobs that don\'t need much skill."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "points out that the US doesn\'t manufacture anything anymore.", "content": "points out that the US doesn\'t manufacture anything anymore."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "believes that it is important to keep a close eye on the age of his workers.", "content": "believes that it is important to keep a close eye on the age of his workers."}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "says that for factory owners, workers are harder to find because of stiff competition.", "content": "says that for factory owners, workers are harder to find because of stiff competition."}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "points out that a work/life balance can attract young people into manufacturing.", "content": "points out that a work/life balance can attract young people into manufacturing."}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "says that the manufacturing recession is to blame for the lay-off of the young people\'s parents.", "content": "says that the manufacturing recession is to blame for the lay-off of the young people\'s parents."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］人物观点匹配题（第九段）。\n［精准定位］定位至第九段：“\'The gap is between the jobs that take no skills and those that require a lot of skill,\' says Rob Spohr, a business professor at Montcalm Community College. \'There\'re enough people to fill the jobs at McDonalds and other places where you don\'t need to have much skill. It\'s that gap in between, and that\'s where the problem is.\'”\n［解题思路］蒙特卡姆社区学院商学教授罗布·施波尔一针见血地指出，制造业真正短缺的是中等技能岗位：像麦当劳等不需要太多技能的工作（where you don\'t need to have much skill），有足够多的人手去填补（enough people to fill the jobs）。选项 [B]“points out that there are enough people to fill the jobs that don\'t need much skill”与原文几乎一字不差，故选 [B]。\n［错项排除］[D] believes that it is important to keep a close eye on the age of his workers 出自第五段 Robert Roth；[E] 讨论行业抢人竞争出自 Jay Dunwell。' WHERE id = 'c301ce3f-a194-59a3-9caf-b16dfc7da154'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Match Julie Parks with the statement that reflects his/her view (A-G):', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "says that he switched to electrical engineering because he loves working with tools.", "content": "says that he switched to electrical engineering because he loves working with tools."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "points out that there are enough people to fill the jobs that don\'t need much skill.", "content": "points out that there are enough people to fill the jobs that don\'t need much skill."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "points out that the US doesn\'t manufacture anything anymore.", "content": "points out that the US doesn\'t manufacture anything anymore."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "believes that it is important to keep a close eye on the age of his workers.", "content": "believes that it is important to keep a close eye on the age of his workers."}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "says that for factory owners, workers are harder to find because of stiff competition.", "content": "says that for factory owners, workers are harder to find because of stiff competition."}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "points out that a work/life balance can attract young people into manufacturing.", "content": "points out that a work/life balance can attract young people into manufacturing."}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "says that the manufacturing recession is to blame for the lay-off of the young people\'s parents.", "content": "says that the manufacturing recession is to blame for the lay-off of the young people\'s parents."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'F', explanation = E'［考点提炼］人物观点匹配题（第十段）。\n［精准定位］定位至第十段（末段）：“Julie Parks of Grand Rapids Community College points to another key to luring Millennials into manufacturing: a work/life balance. While their parents were content to work long hours, young people value flexibility. \'Overtime is not attractive to this generation. They really want to live their lives,\' she says.”\n［解题思路］大急流城社区学院的朱莉·帕克斯指出吸引千禧一代进入制造业的另一把钥匙在于工作与生活的平衡（a work/life balance）——与乐于加班的父辈不同，年轻一代重视工作灵活性、追求好好享受生活。选项 [F]“points out that a work/life balance can attract young people into manufacturing”精准对应原文，故选 [F]。\n［错项排除］文中未提及 Parks 讨论技能鸿沟（Rob Spohr）或跨界转行（Jason Stenquist），故精准匹配 [F]。' WHERE id = '3f53f515-d79f-5131-9ecd-ca6c508633b6'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'It is curious that Stephen Koziatek feels almost as though he has to justify his efforts to give his students a better future.\n\nMr. Koziatek is part of something pioneering. He is a teacher at a New Hampshire high school where learning is not something of books and tests and mechanical memorization, but practical. When did it become accepted wisdom that students should be able to name the 13th president of the United States but be utterly overwhelmed by a broken bike chain?\n\nAs Koziatek knows, there is learning in just about everything. Nothing is necessarily gained by forcing students to learn geometry at a graffitied desk stuck with generations of discarded chewing gum. They can also learn geometry by assembling a bicycle.\n\nBut he\'s also found a kind of insidious prejudice. Working with your hands is seen as almost a mark of inferiority. Schools in the family of vocational education "have that stereotype... that it\'s for kids who can\'t make it academically," he says.\n\nOn one hand, that viewpoint is a logical product of America\'s evolution. Manufacturing is not the economic engine that it once was. The job security that the US economy once offered to high school graduates has largely evaporated. More education is the new principle. We want more for our kids, and rightfully so.\n\nBut the headlong push into bachelor\'s degrees for all - and the subtle devaluing of anything less - misses an important point: That\'s not the only thing the American economy needs. Yes, a bachelor\'s degree opens more doors. But even now, 54 percent of the jobs in the country are middle-skill jobs, such as construction and high-skill manufacturing. But only 44 percent of workers are adequately trained.\n\nIn other words, at a time when the working class has turned the country on its political head, frustrated that the opportunity that once defined America is vanishing, one obvious solution is staring us in the face. There is a gap in working-class jobs, but the workers who need those jobs most aren\'t equipped to do them. Koziatek\'s Manchester School of Technology High School is trying to fill that gap.\n\nKoziatek\'s school is a wake-up call. When education becomes one-size-fits-all, it risks overlooking a nation\'s diversity of gifts.' WHERE id = 'bcdd6890-6fe5-5c3b-bb2f-1e13d154cc01'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'The power and ambition of the giants of the digital economy is astonishing - Amazon has just announced the purchase of the upmarket grocery chain Whole Foods for $13.5bn, but two years ago Facebook paid even more than that to acquire the WhatsApp messaging service, which doesn\'t have any physical product at all. What WhatsApp offered Facebook was an intricate and finely detailed web of its users\' friendships and social lives.\n\nFacebook promised the European commission then that it would not link phone numbers to Facebook identities, but it broke the promise almost as soon as the deal went through. Even without knowing what was in the messages, the knowledge of who sent them and to whom was enormously revealing and still could be. What political journalist, what party whip, would not want to know the makeup of the WhatsApp groups in which Theresa May\'s enemies are currently plotting? It may be that the value of Whole Foods to Amazon is not so much the 460 shops it owns, but the records of which customers have purchased what.\n\nCompetition law appears to be the only way to address these imbalances of power. But it is clumsy. For one thing, it is very slow compared to the pace of change within the digital economy. By the time a problem has been addressed and remedied it may have vanished in the marketplace, to be replaced by new abuses of power. But there is a deeper conceptual problem, too. Competition law as presently interpreted deals with financial disadvantage to consumers and this is not obvious when the users of these services don\'t pay for them. The users of their services are not their customers. That would be the people who buy advertising from them - and Facebook and Google, the two virtual giants, dominate digital advertising to the disadvantage of all other media and entertainment companies.\n\nThe product they\'re selling is data, and we, the users, convert our lives to data for the benefit of the digital giants. Just as some ants farm the bugs called aphids for the honeydew they produce when they feed, so Google farms us for the data that our digital lives yield. Ants keep predatory insects away from where their aphids feed; Gmail keeps the spammers out of our inboxes. It doesn\'t feel like a human or democratic relationship, even if both sides benefit.' WHERE id = '121063dd-a6af-5495-a971-3744ad962a0e'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'To combat the trap of putting a premium on being busy, Cal Newport, author of Deep Work: Rules for Focused Success in a Distracted World, recommends building a habit of "deep work" - the ability to focus without distraction.\n\nThere are a number of approaches to mastering the art of deep work - be it lengthy retreats dedicated to a specific task; developing a daily ritual; or taking a "journalistic" approach to seizing moments of deep work when you can throughout the day. Whichever approach, the key is to determine your length of focus time and stick to it.\n\nNewport also recommends "deep scheduling" to combat constant interruptions and get more done in less time. "At any given point, I should have deep work scheduled for roughly the next month. Once on the calendar, I protect this time like I would a doctor\'s appointment or important meeting," he writes.\n\nAnother approach to getting more done in less time is to rethink how you prioritise your day - in particular how we craft our to-do lists. Tim Harford, author of Messy: The Power of Disorder to Transform Our Lives, points to a study in the early 1980s that divided undergraduates into two groups: some were advised to set out monthly goals and study activities; others were told to plan activities and goals in much more detail, day by day.\n\nWhile the researchers assumed that the well-structured daily plans would be most effective when it came to the execution of tasks, they were wrong: the detailed daily plans demotivated students. Harford argues that inevitable distractions often render the daily to-do list ineffective, while leaving room for improvisation in such a list can reap the best results.\n\nIn order to make the most of our focus and energy, we also need to embrace downtime, or as Newport suggests, "be lazy". "Idleness is not just a vacation, an indulgence or a vice; it is as indispensable to the brain as vitamin D is to the body...[idleness] is, paradoxically, necessary to getting any work done," he argues.\n\nSrini Pillay, an assistant professor of psychiatry at Harvard Medical School, believes this counterintuitive link between downtime and productivity may be due to the way our brains operate. When our brains switch between being focused and unfocused on a task, they tend to be more efficient. "What people don\'t realise is that in order to complete these tasks they need to use both the focus and unfocus circuits in their brain," says Pillay.' WHERE id = '2c6e2fe1-9dd2-52a5-960d-5be0c5f625d3'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'Five Ways to Make Conversation with Anyone\n\nConversations are links, which means when you have a conversation with a new person a link gets formed and every conversation you have after that moment will strengthen the link.\n\nYou meet new people every day: the grocery worker, the cab driver, new people at work or the security guard at the door. Simply starting a conversation with them will form a link.\n\nHere are five simple ways that you can make the first move and start a conversation with strangers.\n\n[41] ____________________\nSuppose you are in a room with someone you don\'t know and something within you says "I want to talk with this person" - this is something that mostly happens with all of us. You wanted to say something, the first word, but it just won\'t come out - it feels like it is stuck somewhere. I know the feeling and here is my advice: just get it out.\nJust think: what is the worst that could happen? They won\'t talk with you? Well, they are not talking with you now!\nI truly believe that once you get that first word out everything else will just flow. So keep it simple: "Hi", "Hey" or "Hello" - do the best you can to gather all of the enthusiasm and energy you can, put on a big smile and just say "Hi".\n\n[42] ____________________\nIt\'s a problem all of us face: you have limited time with the person that you want to talk with and you want to make this talk memorable.\nHonestly, if we got stuck in the rut of "hi", "hello", "how are you?" and "what\'s going on?", you will fail to give the initial jolt to the conversation that can make it so memorable.\nSo don\'t be afraid to ask more personal questions. Trust me, you\'ll be surprised to see how much people are willing to share if you just ask.\n\n[43] ____________________\nWhen you meet a person for the first time, make an effort to find the things which you and that person have in common so that you can build the conversation from that point. When you start conversation from there and then move outwards, you\'ll find all of a sudden that the conversation becomes a lot easier.\n\n[44] ____________________\nImagine you are pouring your heart out to someone and they are just busy on their phone, and if you ask for their attention you get the response "I can multitask". It is not pleasant and it shows that you don\'t care about the person.\nSo when someone tries to communicate with you, just be in that communication wholeheartedly. Make eye contact. Trust me, eye contact is where all the magic happens. When you make eye contact, you can feel the conversation.\n\n[45] ____________________\nYou all came into a conversation where you first met the person, but after some time you may have met again and have forgotten their name. Isn\'t that awkward!\nSo, remember the little details of the people you met or you talked with; perhaps the places they have been to, the places they want to go, the things they like, the things they hate - whatever you talk about.\nWhen you remember such things you can automatically become investor in their wellbeing. So they feel a responsibility to you to keep that relationship going.\n\nThat\'s it. Five amazing ways that you can make conversation with almost anyone. Every person is a really good book to read, or to have a conversation with!' WHERE id = '8c62ec77-2d9c-5924-bcf3-94bf65f2c1df'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [11] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "food", "content": "food"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "pay", "content": "pay"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "marriage", "content": "marriage"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "schooling", "content": "schooling"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内并列关系＋同级生存需求类比。\n［解题思路］空格词与 shelter（住所）由并列连词 or 连接，共同作为 the basic drives for... 的宾语，修饰人类最底层的生理生存本能需求。food or shelter（食物与住所/衣食住行中的基本生存保障）为经典并列搭配，作者借此贴切类比人类求知欲与探索欲之深切，故选[A]。\n［错项排除］[B] pay（薪水报酬）、[C] marriage（婚姻）与[D] schooling（学校教育）均属于社会化衍生的次级需求，并不属于生物最底层的生存基本驱动力，无法与 shelter 并列。' WHERE id = '37e8defd-2771-5ef1-90aa-0d41833c2edc'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [19] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "where", "content": "where"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "why", "content": "why"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "whether", "content": "whether"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "how", "content": "how"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］宾语从句引导词＋权衡决策逻辑。\n［解题思路］空格所在句指出，事先设想顺从好奇心带来的最终结果有助于判断“这是否值得一试”（help determine [19] it is worth the endeavor）。whether 引导宾语从句表示“是否”，准确表达对盲目满足好奇心付出代价的审慎评估，故选[C]。\n［错项排除］[A] where（在哪里）询问地点、[B] why（为什么）询问缘由、[D] how（如何）询问方式，均无法与 is worth the endeavor 搭配构成“是否值得去做”的利弊权衡逻辑。' WHERE id = 'c168ad9c-0cf0-5bda-8ba2-5f929798f6dc'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The ants analogy is used to illustrate', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "a typical competition pattern among digital giants", "content": "a typical competition pattern among digital giants"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "a win-win business model between digital giants", "content": "a win-win business model between digital giants"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "the benefits provided for digital giants\' customers", "content": "the benefits provided for digital giants\' customers"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "the relationship between digital giants and their users", "content": "the relationship between digital giants and their users"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］写作手法题＋比喻类比说明。\n［解题思路］根据定位词 ants analogy 定位至第四段第二至四句：Just as some ants farm the bugs called aphids for the honeydew they produce when they feed, so Google farms us for the data that our digital lives yield. Ants keep predatory insects away from where their aphids feed; Gmail keeps the spammers out of our inboxes. It doesn\'t feel like a human or democratic relationship, even if both sides benefit。作者借蚂蚁饲养蚜虫汲取蜜露并为其驱赶天敌的关系，生动比喻数字巨头通过提供邮箱等服务圈养用户以获取个人数据的不平等控制关系。D项 the relationship between digital giants and their users 精确揭示了类比所阐明的核心对象，故选[D]。\n［错项排除］[A] a typical competition pattern among digital giants（数字巨头间的竞争模式）与[B] a win-win business model between digital giants（数字巨头间的双赢商业模式）均错将类比对象锁定为科技巨头彼此之间；[C] the benefits provided for digital giants\' customers（为数字巨头客户提供的利益）混淆了“免费服务使用者（users）”与“付费广告客户（customers）”的概念，偏离了巨头与普通数据用户关系不对等的批判本质。' WHERE id = 'f5d63b81-7702-5d86-9fe2-4ad756c987f0'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the most suitable subheading for section [43]:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Just say it", "content": "Just say it"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Be present", "content": "Be present"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Skip the small talk", "content": "Skip the small talk"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Ask for an opinion", "content": "Ask for an opinion"}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "Find the \\"me too\\"s", "content": "Find the \\"me too\\"s"}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "Name, places, things", "content": "Name, places, things"}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "Pay a unique compliment", "content": "Pay a unique compliment"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'E', explanation = E'［考点提炼］新题型小标题匹配（第[43]段）。\n［解题思路］[43]段明确指出初次见面时，应当主动寻找双方共同拥有的兴趣或经历（make an effort to find the things which you and that person have in common），并以此为基点向外延伸展开交谈，谈话会顿时轻松许多。E项 Find the "me too"s（寻找“我也是”的共同共鸣点）精准且地道地对应了“寻找共同点（have in common）”，故选[E]。\n［错项排除］[A] Just say it（勇于开口说出来）对应第[41]段；[C] Skip the small talk（跳过客套寒暄）对应第[42]段；[B] Be present 与 [F] Name, places, things 分别对应后两段，均不涉寻找共同话题。' WHERE id = '39c17eb6-6385-531b-8355-ffa57c5b90d2'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'Unlike so-called basic emotions such as sadness, fear, and anger, guilt emerges a little later, in conjunction with a child\'s growing grasp of social and moral norms. Children aren\'t born knowing how to say "I\'m sorry"; rather, they learn over time that such statements appease parents and friends — and their own consciences. This is why researchers generally regard so-called moral guilt, in the right amount, to be a good thing.\n\nIn the popular imagination, of course, guilt still gets a bad rap. It is deeply uncomfortable — it\'s the emotional equivalent of wearing a jacket weighted with stones. Yet this understanding is outdated. "There has been a kind of revival or a rethinking about what guilt is and what role guilt can serve," says Amrisha Vaish, a psychology researcher at the University of Virginia, adding that this revival is part of a larger recognition that emotions aren\'t binary — feelings that may be advantageous in one context may be harmful in another. Jealousy and anger, for example, may have evolved to alert us to important inequalities. Too much happiness can be destructive.\n\nAnd guilt, by prompting us to think more deeply about our goodness, can encourage humans to make up for errors and fix relationships. Guilt, in other words, can help hold a cooperative species together. It is a kind of social glue.\n\nViewed in this light, guilt is an opportunity. Work by Tina Malti, a psychology professor at the University of Toronto, suggests that guilt may compensate for an emotional deficiency. In a number of studies, Malti and others have shown that guilt and sympathy may represent different pathways to cooperation and sharing. Some kids who are low in sympathy may make up for that shortfall by experiencing more guilt, which can rein in their nastier impulses. And vice versa: High sympathy can substitute for low guilt.\n\nIn a 2014 study, for example, Malti looked at 244 children. Using caregiver assessments and the children\'s self-observations, she rated each child\'s overall sympathy level and his or her tendency to feel negative emotions after moral transgressions. Then the kids were handed chocolate coins, and given a chance to share them with an anonymous child. For the low-sympathy kids, how much they shared appeared to turn on how inclined they were to feel guilty. The guilt-prone ones shared more, even though they hadn\'t magically become more sympathetic to the other child\'s deprivation.\n\n"That\'s good news," Malti says. "We can be prosocial because we caused harm and we feel regret."' WHERE id = '6910ec7e-cbdb-5c67-b05b-6b62ac476320'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'Forests give us shade, quiet and one of the harder challenges in the fight against climate change. Even as we humans count on forests to soak up a good share of the carbon dioxide we produce, we are threatening their ability to do so. The climate change we are hastening could one day leave us with forests that emit more carbon than they absorb.\n\nThankfully, there is a way out of this trap — but it involves striking a subtle balance. Helping forests flourish as valuable "carbon sinks" long into the future may require reducing their capacity to absorb carbon now. California is leading the way, as it does on so many climate efforts, in figuring out the details.\n\nThe state\'s proposed Forest Carbon Plan aims to double efforts to thin out young trees and clear brush in parts of the forest. This temporarily lowers carbon-carrying capacity. But the remaining trees draw a greater share of the available moisture, so they grow and thrive, restoring the forest\'s capacity to pull carbon from the air. Healthy trees are also better able to fend off insects. The landscape is rendered less easily burnable. Even in the event of a fire, fewer trees are consumed.\n\nThe need for such planning is increasingly urgent. Already, since 2010, drought and insects have killed over 100 million trees in California, most of them in 2016 alone, and wildfires have burned hundreds of thousands of acres.\n\nCalifornia plans to treat 35,000 acres of forest a year by 2020, and 60,000 by 2030 — financed from the proceeds of the state\'s emissions-permit auctions. That\'s only a small share of the total acreage that could benefit, about half a million acres in all, so it will be vital to prioritize areas at greatest risk of fire or drought.\n\nThe strategy also aims to ensure that carbon in woody material removed from the forests is locked away in the form of solid lumber or burned as biofuel in vehicles that would otherwise run on fossil fuels. New research on transportation biofuels is already under way.\n\nState governments are well accustomed to managing forests, but traditionally they\'ve focused on wildlife, watersheds and opportunities for recreation. Only recently have they come to see the vital part forests will have to play in storing carbon. California\'s plan, which is expected to be finalized by the governor next year, should serve as a model.' WHERE id = '48bacb2d-0a69-5a18-a252-06e7527cf53a'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'American farmers have been complaining of labor shortages for several years. The complaints are unlikely to stop without an overhaul of immigration rules for farm workers.\n\nCongress has obstructed efforts to create a more straightforward visa for agricultural workers that would let foreign workers stay longer in the U.S. and change jobs within the industry. If this doesn\'t change, American businesses, communities, and consumers will be the losers.\n\nPerhaps half of U.S. farm laborers are undocumented immigrants. As fewer such workers enter the country, the characteristics of the agricultural workforce are changing. Today\'s farm laborers, while still predominantly born in Mexico, are more likely to be settled rather than migrating and more likely to be married than single. They\'re also aging. At the start of this century, about one-third of crop workers were over the age of 35. Now more than half are. And picking crops is hard on older bodies. One oft-debated cure for this labor shortage remains as implausible as it\'s been all along: Native U.S. workers won\'t be returning to the farm.\n\nMechanization isn\'t the answer, either — not yet, at least. Production of corn, cotton, rice, soybeans, and wheat has been largely mechanized, but many high-value, labor-intensive crops, such as strawberries, need labor. Even dairy farms, where robots do a small share of milking, have a long way to go before they\'re automated.\n\nAs a result, farms have grown increasingly reliant on temporary guest workers using the H-2A visa to fill the gaps in the workforce. Starting around 2012, requests for the visas rose sharply; from 2011 to 2016 the number of visas issued more than doubled. The H-2A visa has no numerical cap, unlike the H-2B visa for nonagricultural work, which is limited to 66,000 a year. Even so, employers complain they aren\'t given all the workers they need. The process is cumbersome, expensive, and unreliable. One survey found that bureaucratic delays led the average H-2A worker to arrive on the job 22 days late. The shortage is compounded by federal immigration raids, which remove some workers and drive others underground.\n\nIn a 2012 survey, 71 percent of tree-fruit growers and almost 80 percent of raisin and berry growers said they were short of labor. Some western farmers have responded by moving operations to Mexico. From 1998 to 2000, 14.5 percent of the fruit Americans consumed was imported. Little more than a decade later, the share of imports was 25.8 percent.\n\nIn effect, the U.S. can import food or it can import the workers who pick it.' WHERE id = '9e8f6aca-24cb-50be-8c96-bd05e46d2966'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'Arnold Schwarzenegger, Dia Mirza and Adrian Grenier have a message for you: It\'s easy to beat plastic. They\'re part of a bunch of celebrities starring in a new video for World Environment Day — encouraging you, the consumer, to swap out your single-use plastic staples like straws and cutlery to combat the plastics crisis.\n\nThe key messages that have been put together for World Environment Day do include a call for governments to enact legislation to curb single-use plastics. But the overarching message is directed at individuals.\n\nMy concern with leaving it up to the individual, however, is our limited sense of what needs to be achieved. On their own, taking our own bags to the grocery store or quitting plastic straws, for example, will accomplish little and require very little of us. They could even be detrimental, satisfying a need to have "done our bit" without ever progressing onto bigger, bolder, more effective actions — a kind of "moral licensing" that allays our concerns and stops us doing more and asking more of those in charge.\n\nWhile the conversation around our environment and our responsibility toward it remains centered on shopping bags and straws, we\'re ignoring the balance of power that implies that as "consumers" we must shop sustainably, rather than as "citizens" hold our governments and industries to account to push for real systemic change.\n\nIt\'s important to acknowledge that the environment isn\'t everyone\'s priority — or even most people\'s. We shouldn\'t expect it to be. In her latest book, Why Good People Do Bad Environmental Things, Wellesley College professor Elizabeth R. DeSombre argues that the best way to collectively change the behavior of large numbers of people is for the change to be structural.\n\nThis might mean implementing policy such as a plastic tax that adds a cost to environmentally problematic action, or banning single-use plastics altogether. India has just announced it will "eliminate all single-use plastic in the country by 2022." There are also incentive-based ways of making better environmental choices easier, such as ensuring recycling is at least as easy as trash disposal.\n\nDeSombre isn\'t saying people should stop caring about the environment. It\'s just that individual actions are too slow, she says, for that to be the only, or even primary, approach to changing widespread behavior.\n\nNone of this is about writing off the individual. It\'s just about putting things into perspective. We don\'t have time to wait. We need progressive policies that shape collective action (and rein in polluting businesses), alongside engaged citizens pushing for change.' WHERE id = '9a3faac8-4546-5da0-8093-ff85a1eee5ba'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'In choosing a new home, Camille McClain\'s kids have a single demand: a backyard.\n\nMcClain\'s little ones aren\'t the only kids who have an opinion when it comes to housing, and in many cases youngsters\' views weigh heavily on parents\' real estate decisions, according to a 2018 Harris Poll survey of more than 2,000 U.S. adults.\n\nWhile more families buck an older-generation proclivity to leave kids in the dark about real estate decisions, realty agents and psychologists have mixed views about the financial, personal and long-term effects kids\' opinions may have.\n\nThe idea of involving children in a big decision is a great idea because it can help them feel a sense of control and ownership in what can be an overwhelming process, said Ryan Hooper, a clinical psychologist in Chicago.\n\n"Children may face serious difficulties in coping with significant moves, especially if it removes them from their current school or support system," he said.\n\nGreg Jaroszewski, a real estate broker with Gagliardo Realty Associates, said he\'s not convinced that kids should be involved in selecting a home — but their opinions should be considered in regards to proximity to friends and social activities, if possible.\n\nYounger children should feel like they\'re choosing their home — without actually getting a choice in the matter, said Adam Bailey, a real estate attorney based in New York.\n\nAsking them questions about what they like about the backyard of a potential home will make them feel like they\'re being included in the decision-making process, Bailey said.\n\nMany of the aspects of homebuying aren\'t a consideration for children, said Tracey Hampson, a real estate agent based in Santa Clarita, Calif. And placing too much emphasis on their opinions can ruin a fantastic home purchase.\n\n"Speaking with your children before you make a real estate decision is wise, but I wouldn\'t base the purchasing decision solely on their opinions," Hampson said.\n\nThe other issue is that many children — especially older ones — may base their real estate knowledge on HGTV shows, said Aaron Norris of The Norris Group in Riverside, Calif.\n\n"They love Chip and Joanna Gaines just as much as the rest of us," he said. "HGTV has seriously changed how people view real estate. It\'s not shelter, it\'s a lifestyle. With that mindset change come some serious money consequences."\n\nKids tend to get stuck in the features and the immediate benefits to them personally, Norris said.\n\nParents need to remind their children that their needs and desires may change over time, said Julie Gurner, a real estate analyst with FitSmallBusiness.com.\n\n"Their opinions can change tomorrow," Gurner said. "Harsh as it may be to say, that decision should likely not be made contingent on a child\'s opinions, but rather made for them with great consideration into what home can meet their needs best — and give them an opportunity to customize it a bit and make it their own."\n\nThis advice is more relevant now than ever before, even as more parents want to embrace the ideas of their children, despite the current housing crunch.' WHERE id = 'af1ba86e-faf5-5f29-ab93-f83229176082'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [5] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "modify", "content": "modify"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "set", "content": "set"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "review", "content": "review"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "reach", "content": "reach"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］动宾搭配与目标达成。\n［解题思路］第二段末句指出，错误调整后的训练计划与自己为了“实现目标（reach my goals）”所需采用的训练方式产生了冲突。reach one\'s goals 为英语最地道高频搭配，意为“达成目标”，与上文 overall fitness goals 呼应，故选[D]。\n［错项排除］[A] modify（修改）与[B] set（设定）在前文均已完成目标设立背景下的行动阶段，此处强调训练目的是实现已定目标；[C] review（审视、回顾）同样不符通过训练兑现目标的语义。' WHERE id = 'd6bdaa21-5264-5e85-bc4c-cb6c68c0cf4f'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [9] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "claims", "content": "claims"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "judgments", "content": "judgments"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "reasons", "content": "reasons"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "methods", "content": "methods"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］固定搭配与段落因果过渡。\n［解题思路］第四段首句承接前两段剖析的每日称重弊端，作者总结道：出于以上这些原因（For these reasons），我停止每天称重。for these reasons 是英语中最经典的承前启后总结短语，指代前文只关注数字等一系列教训，故选[C]。\n［错项排除］[A] claims（主张、声称）、[B] judgments（判断）与[D] methods（方法）均不能与前面阐述的原因构成自然合理的因果总结搭配。' WHERE id = '5824642d-8fa9-5d5f-b775-a56e72509cd9'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [10] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "instead", "content": "instead"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "though", "content": "though"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "again", "content": "again"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "indeed", "content": "indeed"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］副词辨析与行为方式切换。\n［解题思路］第四段首句指出自己停止了每日称重，转而改用每两周一次的称重频率（switched to a bimonthly weighing schedule [10]）。副词 instead 置于句尾，意为“相反、作为替代”，精准凸显摒弃错误旧习、采取全新频率的转变，故选[A]。\n［错项排除］[B] though（虽然、然而，多表语气弱转折让步）；[C] again（再次）与改变频率的初次切换不符；[D] indeed（确实）表递进肯定，均不能准确刻画“舍甲取乙”的替代关系。' WHERE id = '4cba17e0-52c3-595d-80eb-ed420e103061'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [11] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "track", "content": "track"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "overlook", "content": "overlook"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "conceal", "content": "conceal"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "report", "content": "report"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］动词词义与健康监测固定搭配。\n［解题思路］第四段首句表明作者改为每两周称重一次，第二句紧接着指出：既然减重不是我的目标，那么每周去“记录、追踪（track）”体重就显得不那么重要了。track my weight 意为“持续追踪体重变化”，符合定期自我监测身体数据曲线的语境，并与下句 observe and record 呼应，故选［A］。\n［错项排除］［B］overlook（忽视、忽略）和［C］conceal（隐藏、隐瞒）语义方向与收集体重信息相反；［D］report（汇报、报告）常用于向他人呈报，个人日常健身记录无需每周汇报。' WHERE id = 'd192c493-b596-5faa-bc57-792052ca72fc'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [13] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "share", "content": "share"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "adjust", "content": "adjust"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "confirm", "content": "confirm"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "prepare", "content": "prepare"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］动宾搭配与语境连贯性。\n［解题思路］第四段末句指出：观察并弄清显著的体重变化，能够告诉我是否需要对训练计划进行调整（[13] my training program）。adjust 意为“调整、微调”，准确呼应第二段因误判而草率修改（altered）训练计划的正反对照，故选[B]。\n［错项排除］[A] share（分享）、[C] confirm（确认）与[D] prepare（准备）均不能体现依据身体反馈灵活改良已有计划的含义。' WHERE id = 'cd43a592-da92-5690-95a7-d407cb6789c1'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [14] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "results", "content": "results"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "features", "content": "features"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "rules", "content": "rules"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "tests", "content": "tests"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］名词词义辨析与称重信息采集。\n［解题思路］第五段首句指出：我还利用每半月一次的称重“结果、数据（results）”来获取有关营养状况的信息（to get information about my nutrition）。weigh-in results 指每次站上体重秤测得的客观数字结果，顺承下文根据体重下降来调整每日热量摄入的反馈机制，故选［A］。\n［错项排除］［B］features（特征、特点）和［C］rules（规则、条例）均无法直接量化产出营养摄入信息；［D］tests（测试）与前置定语 weigh-in（称重测试）在语义上重复，不构成动宾合理搭配。' WHERE id = '3451bd19-eb40-54a9-b6b4-63ed7ee9d8a9'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [16] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "principle", "content": "principle"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "secret", "content": "secret"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "belief", "content": "belief"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "sign", "content": "sign"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］名词辨析与生理预警信号表达。\n［解题思路］第五段第二句指出：如果我的训练强度保持不变，但我经常感到饥饿且体重持续下降，这就是一个明确的“迹象/信号（sign）”，表明我需要增加日常卡路里摄入量。a sign that... 为固定同位语结构，意为“显示……的征兆或信号”，契合身体发出的客观营养预警，故选［D］。\n［错项排除］［A］principle（原则、原理）、［B］secret（秘密）以及［C］belief（信念、看法）均带主观色彩或属抽象准则，无法指代饥饿和掉秤释放出的客观信号。' WHERE id = 'd9677bf4-1949-5965-969e-8ceda954c37f'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [17] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "request", "content": "request"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "necessity", "content": "necessity"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "decision", "content": "decision"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "wish", "content": "wish"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］名词辨析与自主行动抉择。\n［解题思路］第六段首句总结全篇核心举措：停止每日称重的这一“决定（decision）”对我的整体健康、体能水平和幸福感产生了极大益处（has done wonders）。the decision to stop weighing myself 紧扣第四段作者主动放弃每日称重、转向双周日程的关键选择，故选［C］。\n［错项排除］［A］request（请求）多指对他人提出要求；［B］necessity（必需品、必要性）未能体现个人主动取舍；［D］wish（愿望）仅停留在主观意愿层面，尚未转化为实际行动与成效。' WHERE id = '055d387c-16ec-54e1-b98b-86a6a532c53d'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [19] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "if", "content": "if"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "unless", "content": "unless"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "until", "content": "until"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "because", "content": "because"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］连词辨析与句间因果逻辑论证。\n［解题思路］第六段末句指出：我在实现具体健身目标方面也取得了更大成功，因为（because）我现在是依据那些切实的健身目标而非体重计上的冰冷数字来进行训练的。后半句直接揭示了前文“取得更大成功”的根本原因，构成前果后因的逻辑论证，故选［D］。\n［错项排除］［A］if（如果）和［B］unless（除非）均引导条件状语从句，表示假设前提；［C］until（直到……为止）引导时间状语从句，三者均无法解释已然实现的成功结果背后的原因。' WHERE id = '5a5f953d-0159-5c9e-9a14-0547a5df1674'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'By saying "one of the harder challenges", the author implies that', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "global climate change may get out of control", "content": "global climate change may get out of control"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "people may misunderstand global warming", "content": "people may misunderstand global warming"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "extreme weather conditions may arise", "content": "extreme weather conditions may arise"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "forests may become a potential threat", "content": "forests may become a potential threat"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］推理判断题（第一段）。\n［解题思路］第一段首句指出森林给了我们绿荫、宁静，也是抗击气候变化过程中最棘手的挑战之一（one of the harder challenges）。紧接着后两句解释：人类指望森林吸收大量二氧化碳，却正威胁其这一能力；加速中的气候变化有朝一日可能使森林排放的碳多于吸收的碳（emit more carbon than they absorb）。这暗示本该吸收碳的森林未来可能反过来成为气候问题的潜在威胁，故 [D] forests may become a potential threat 正确。\n［错项排除］[A] global climate change may get out of control 过度绝对化；[B] people may misunderstand global warming 与民众误解无关；[C] extreme weather conditions may arise 仅笼统泛指极端天气，未切中森林“角色逆转成威胁”的深层隐忧。' WHERE id = '04da79d1-80ab-5aab-8b8d-b82d8078062f'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'To maintain forests as valuable "carbon sinks", we may need to', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "preserve the diversity of species in them", "content": "preserve the diversity of species in them"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "accelerate the growth of young trees", "content": "accelerate the growth of young trees"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "strike a balance among different plants", "content": "strike a balance among different plants"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "lower their present carbon-absorbing capacity", "content": "lower their present carbon-absorbing capacity"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］事实细节题（第二段）。\n［解题思路］第二段明确指出：“Helping forests flourish as valuable \'carbon sinks\' long into the future may require reducing their capacity to absorb carbon now.”（要帮助森林在长远未来继续作为宝贵的“碳汇”茁壮成长，现在可能需要降低其吸碳能力。）选项 [D] lower their present carbon-absorbing capacity 是对 reducing their capacity to absorb carbon now 的精准同义改写，故选 [D]。\n［错项排除］[A] preserve the diversity of species in them（保护物种多样性）、[B] accelerate the growth of young trees（加速幼树生长——恰恰相反，下段倡导疏伐幼树 thin out young trees）与[C] strike a balance among different plants（在植物间取得平衡——偷换原文的“长期与短期平衡”）均偏离原意。' WHERE id = '39f990f8-bc30-5cb8-8e75-cf045e251f4a'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'California\'s Forest Carbon Plan endeavors to', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "cultivate more drought-resistant trees", "content": "cultivate more drought-resistant trees"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "reduce the density of some of its forests", "content": "reduce the density of some of its forests"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "find more effective ways to kill insects", "content": "find more effective ways to kill insects"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "restore its forests quickly after wildfires", "content": "restore its forests quickly after wildfires"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］事实细节题（第三段）。\n［解题思路］第三段首句指出：“The state\'s proposed Forest Carbon Plan aims to double efforts to thin out young trees and clear brush in parts of the forest.”（该州提议的森林碳计划旨在加倍努力对部分林区进行疏伐幼树和清理灌木丛。）疏伐多余幼树与灌木丛以让留存树木充分汲取水分并降低可燃性，本质上就是降低部分森林的树木密度，故选 [B] reduce the density of some of its forests。\n［错项排除］[A] cultivate more drought-resistant trees（培育抗旱树种）、[C] find more effective ways to kill insects（寻找更有效杀虫方法——健康大树自然能抵御虫害）与[D] restore its forests quickly after wildfires（火后快速恢复——计划旨在事先预防大火而非灾后补救）均属曲解。' WHERE id = '5981d5ad-909d-5d6e-81c3-c89d9f3d747e'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'What is essential to California\'s plan according to Paragraph 5?', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "To handle the areas in serious danger first.", "content": "To handle the areas in serious danger first."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "To carry it out before the year of 2020.", "content": "To carry it out before the year of 2020."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "To perfect the emissions-permit auctions.", "content": "To perfect the emissions-permit auctions."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "To obtain enough financial support.", "content": "To obtain enough financial support."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］事实细节题（第五段）。\n［解题思路］第五段（即加州计划具体落地段）指出：“That\'s only a small share of the total acreage that could benefit, about half a million acres in all, so it will be vital to prioritize areas at greatest risk of fire or drought.”（这只是可受益总面积的一小部分，因此优先处理火灾或干旱风险最大的区域将至关重要。）其中 prioritize areas at greatest risk 与 [A] To handle the areas in serious danger first 完美同义对应，故选 [A]。\n［错项排除］[B] To carry it out before the year of 2020 曲解了“by 2020 每年处理 3.5 万英亩”的阶段指标；[C] To perfect the emissions-permit auctions 将“从碳排放配额拍卖收益获得资金”偷换为完善拍卖制度本身；[D] To obtain enough financial support 偏离了本段强调空间优先级分配的核心重点（vital to prioritize）。' WHERE id = 'f8801a5e-9f8f-5747-864a-ad38ce7590ab'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The author\'s attitude to California\'s plan can best be described as', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "ambiguous", "content": "ambiguous"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "tolerant", "content": "tolerant"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "supportive", "content": "supportive"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "cautious", "content": "cautious"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］观点态度题（第二段及末段）。\n［解题思路］作者在第二段称赞加州在这方面走在前列（California is leading the way），并在末段末句给出明确正面评价：“California\'s plan, which is expected to be finalized by the governor next year, should serve as a model.”（加州的计划应当成为一个典范。）这充分表明作者对加州森林碳计划持明确的支持肯定态度，故选 [C] supportive。\n［错项排除］[A] ambiguous（含糊不清的）、[B] tolerant（容忍的，带有保留或勉强认可意味）与[D] cautious（谨慎的）均与称赞加州“领先并堪称典范”的鲜明赞许基调不符。' WHERE id = 'd2c83126-ce8a-59c6-8097-0411f7f74910'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'What problem should be addressed according to the first two paragraphs?', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Discrimination against foreign workers in the U.S.", "content": "Discrimination against foreign workers in the U.S."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Biased laws in favor of some American businesses.", "content": "Biased laws in favor of some American businesses."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Flaws in U.S. immigration rules for farm workers.", "content": "Flaws in U.S. immigration rules for farm workers."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Decline of job opportunities in U.S. agriculture.", "content": "Decline of job opportunities in U.S. agriculture."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］事实细节题（第一、二段）。\n［解题思路］第一段指出：“The complaints are unlikely to stop without an overhaul of immigration rules for farm workers.”（不对农工移民法规进行彻底改革，抱怨就不会停止。）第二段紧接着批评国会阻挠建立更简明高效的农业工人签证制度。由此可知亟待解决的问题在于美国农工移民法规存在的缺陷，故选 [C] Flaws in U.S. immigration rules for farm workers。\n［错项排除］[A] Discrimination against foreign workers in the U.S.（对外国工人的歧视）无中生有；[B] Biased laws in favor of some American businesses（偏袒部分美企的法律）曲解了立法阻碍导致美国企业成输家（will be the losers）；[D] Decline of job opportunities in U.S. agriculture（美国农业工作机会减少）与面临严重用工荒相反。' WHERE id = '11cc8ba7-343d-5a37-8f25-984d70fe5308'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'One trouble with U.S. agricultural workforce is', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "the rising number of illegal immigrants", "content": "the rising number of illegal immigrants"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "the high mobility of crop workers", "content": "the high mobility of crop workers"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "the lack of experienced laborers", "content": "the lack of experienced laborers"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "the aging of immigrant farm workers", "content": "the aging of immigrant farm workers"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］事实细节题（第三段）。\n［解题思路］第三段剖析了美国农业劳动力的结构性变化：“They\'re also aging. At the start of this century, about one-third of crop workers were over the age of 35. Now more than half are. And picking crops is hard on older bodies.” 目前过半农工超过35岁且劳力不断老化，难以胜任繁重的田间采摘工作，即面临移民农工老龄化困境，故选 [D] the aging of immigrant farm workers。\n［错项排除］[A] the rising number of illegal immigrants 与首句后半部分“As fewer such workers enter the country（进入的非法移民越来越少）”完全相反；[B] the high mobility of crop workers 与“more likely to be settled rather than migrating（更有可能定居而非四处迁徙）”相悖；[C] the lack of experienced laborers 混淆了年龄老化与缺乏经验。' WHERE id = '8fa6d8e9-2612-51cf-b0e8-b1f8cef699b1'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Agricultural employers complain about the H-2A visa for its', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "slow granting procedures", "content": "slow granting procedures"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "limit on duration of stay", "content": "limit on duration of stay"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "tightened requirements", "content": "tightened requirements"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "control of annual admissions", "content": "control of annual admissions"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］事实细节题（第五段）。\n［解题思路］第五段（即 H-2A 签证段）指出：“Even so, employers complain they aren\'t given all the workers they need. The process is cumbersome, expensive, and unreliable. One survey found that bureaucratic delays led the average H-2A worker to arrive on the job 22 days late.” 农业雇主抱怨 H-2A 流程繁琐、昂贵且不可靠，官僚延误导致工人平均迟到22天，核心痛点在于签证审批手续过于缓慢，故选 [A] slow granting procedures。\n［错项排除］[B] limit on duration of stay（逗留期限限制）来自第二段旧签证局限，非本段对 H-2A 抱怨；[C] tightened requirements（收紧申请条件）未提及；[D] control of annual admissions（年度配额控制）恰是 H-2B 签证的限制，原文明确指出“The H-2A visa has no numerical cap（H-2A 并无数量上限）”。' WHERE id = '8a00299b-6eb5-5515-b66f-85c86eb42851'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Which of the following could be the best title for this text?', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "U.S. Agriculture in Decline?", "content": "U.S. Agriculture in Decline?"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Import Food or Labor?", "content": "Import Food or Labor?"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "America Saved by Mexico?", "content": "America Saved by Mexico?"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Manpower vs. Automation?", "content": "Manpower vs. Automation?"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］主旨大意题（全文及末段）。\n［解题思路］文章从美国农场面临的用工荒和移民制度障碍切入，剖析了本土工人不愿回流、机械化尚未成熟、H-2A 签证官僚拖延等困境，随之指出不少西部农场迁往墨西哥导致美国进口水果占比攀升，并在末段点明核心抉择：“In effect, the U.S. can import food or it can import the workers who pick it.”（实际上，美国要么进口食物，要么进口采摘食物的工人。）[B] Import Food or Labor? 凝练抓住了全篇灵魂，故选 [B]。\n［错项排除］[A] U.S. Agriculture in Decline?（美国农业走向衰落？）过度拔高，问题在于劳动力短缺与供应链转移；[C] America Saved by Mexico?（美国被墨西哥拯救？）曲解农业迁往墨西哥与劳工来源；[D] Manpower vs. Automation?（人力与自动化之争？）仅涵盖第四段局部内容。' WHERE id = 'fb78c9a2-65a3-59e2-a125-d411046bab71'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The author is concerned that "moral licensing" may', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "mislead us into doing worthless things", "content": "mislead us into doing worthless things"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "prevent us from making further efforts", "content": "prevent us from making further efforts"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "weaken our sense of accomplishment", "content": "weaken our sense of accomplishment"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "suppress our desire for success", "content": "suppress our desire for success"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］细节理解题（第三段）。\n［解题思路］第三段指出，自带购物袋或停用塑料吸管之所以可能带来危害，是因为这会满足人们觉得自己已经“尽了本分（done our bit）”的心理需求，却止步于此而不再推进更大、更大胆、更有效的变革行动——即所谓的“道德许可（moral licensing）”，它抚慰了我们的担忧并阻碍我们做更多事情及向当权者追责（allays our concerns and stops us doing more and asking more of those in charge）。选项 [B] prevent us from making further efforts 精准对应 stops us doing more，故选 [B]。\n［错项排除］[A] mislead us into doing worthless things（误导做毫无价值的事）过度绝对化，作者指出这些举动收效微弱（accomplish little）而非完全无用；[C] weaken our sense of accomplishment 与原文“满足已尽力的感觉”相反；[D] suppress our desire for success 偷换了做更多环保行动与向政府问责的指向。' WHERE id = 'e88e3d21-30ae-59e6-a392-0774f937cf3d'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'By pointing out our identity "citizens", the author indicates that', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "our focus should be shifted to community welfare", "content": "our focus should be shifted to community welfare"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "our relationship with local industries is improving", "content": "our relationship with local industries is improving"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "we have been actively exercising our civil rights", "content": "we have been actively exercising our civil rights"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "we should press our government to lead the combat", "content": "we should press our government to lead the combat"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］推理判断题（第四段）。\n［解题思路］第四段指出，当环保讨论一直停留在购物袋和吸管上时，我们就忽视了权力平衡——那等于暗示我们作为“消费者（consumers）”只能靠可持续购物来承担责任，而不是作为“公民（citizens）”向政府和行业追责以推动真正的系统性变革（hold our governments and industries to account to push for real systemic change）。作者点出“公民”身份旨在呼吁公众敦促政府主导变革应对塑料危机，故选 [D] we should press our government to lead the combat。\n［错项排除］[A] our focus should be shifted to community welfare（重心应转向社区福利）偏离环保问责；[B] our relationship with local industries is improving（与地方产业关系改善）与追责问效相悖；[C] we have been actively exercising our civil rights（一直在积极行使公民权利）时态与事实均与当前“忽视了作为公民去追责”相反。' WHERE id = '9af31d69-0bc6-5834-8ee8-fbb3c0020f56'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The author concludes that individual efforts', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "can be too aggressive", "content": "can be too aggressive"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "can be too inconsistent", "content": "can be too inconsistent"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "are far from sufficient", "content": "are far from sufficient"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "are far from rational", "content": "are far from rational"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］观点结论题（第七、八段）。\n［解题思路］第七段与第八段明确收束观点：“It\'s just that individual actions are too slow, she says, for that to be the only, or even primary, approach to changing widespread behavior. None of this is about writing off the individual... We don\'t have time to wait. We need progressive policies that shape collective action...” 作者并非全盘否定个人作用，但强调个体行动过于缓慢，作为唯一或主要手段远远不够（far from sufficient），亟需系统性政策牵引集体行动，故选 [C] are far from sufficient。\n［错项排除］[A] can be too aggressive（可能过于激进）与温和微小的自带购物袋完全相反；[B] can be too inconsistent（可能太不一致）偏离时间紧迫、个体收效太慢的论据核心；[D] are far from rational（远非理性）并非作者对个人行动的定性。' WHERE id = '3d02466e-5343-563d-9019-b5301cf7514b'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Match Aaron Norris with the opinion that reflects his statement (A-G):', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "remarks that significant moves may pose challenges to children.", "content": "remarks that significant moves may pose challenges to children."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "says that it is wise to leave kids in the dark about real estate decisions.", "content": "says that it is wise to leave kids in the dark about real estate decisions."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "advises that home purchases should not be based only on children\'s opinions.", "content": "advises that home purchases should not be based only on children\'s opinions."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "thinks that children should be given a sense of involvement in homebuying decisions.", "content": "thinks that children should be given a sense of involvement in homebuying decisions."}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "notes that aspects like children\'s friends and social activities should be considered upon homebuying.", "content": "notes that aspects like children\'s friends and social activities should be considered upon homebuying."}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "believes that homebuying decisions should be based on children\'s needs rather than their opinions.", "content": "believes that homebuying decisions should be based on children\'s needs rather than their opinions."}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "assumes that many children\'s views on real estate are influenced by the media.", "content": "assumes that many children\'s views on real estate are influenced by the media."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'G', explanation = E'［考点提炼］人物观点匹配题（第十一至十三段）。\n［解题思路］加州 The Norris Group 的 Aaron Norris 指出：许多孩子尤其是年纪大一点的孩子，其房地产知识往往来源于 HGTV 家居装修电视节目（may base their real estate knowledge on HGTV shows）；这导致“房屋不再只是遮风挡雨的住所，而是一种生活方式”，孩子容易沉迷于特定功能与即时个人享乐而忽略高昂财务代价。HGTV 电视节目属于大众媒体，故与选项 [G] assumes that many children\'s views on real estate are influenced by the media 完美对应，故选 [G]。\n［错项排除］[A] 为 Ryan Hooper 观点；[C] 为 Tracey Hampson 观点；[F] 为 Julie Gurner 观点。' WHERE id = 'f3dc29a3-af7e-5e3f-b9c4-2ffd03ed5c19'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Match Julie Gurner with the opinion that reflects her statement (A-G):', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "remarks that significant moves may pose challenges to children.", "content": "remarks that significant moves may pose challenges to children."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "says that it is wise to leave kids in the dark about real estate decisions.", "content": "says that it is wise to leave kids in the dark about real estate decisions."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "advises that home purchases should not be based only on children\'s opinions.", "content": "advises that home purchases should not be based only on children\'s opinions."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "thinks that children should be given a sense of involvement in homebuying decisions.", "content": "thinks that children should be given a sense of involvement in homebuying decisions."}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "notes that aspects like children\'s friends and social activities should be considered upon homebuying.", "content": "notes that aspects like children\'s friends and social activities should be considered upon homebuying."}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "believes that homebuying decisions should be based on children\'s needs rather than their opinions.", "content": "believes that homebuying decisions should be based on children\'s needs rather than their opinions."}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "assumes that many children\'s views on real estate are influenced by the media.", "content": "assumes that many children\'s views on real estate are influenced by the media."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'F', explanation = E'［考点提炼］人物观点匹配题（第十四至十五段）。\n［解题思路］商业分析网站 FitSmallBusiness.com 的房产分析师 Julie Gurner 指出，父母应当提醒孩子需求与愿望会随时变化，“that decision should likely not be made contingent on a child\'s opinions, but rather made for them with great consideration into what home can meet their needs best”（买房决定不应取决于孩子的意见，而应立足于最能满足其长远需求的房屋来为他们做决定）。not contingent on opinions but meet needs 精确对应 [F] believes that homebuying decisions should be based on children\'s needs rather than their opinions，故选 [F]。\n［错项排除］[D] 强调让孩子有参与感出自 Adam Bailey；[C] 强调不单纯依据孩子意见由 Tracey Hampson 提出，而 Gurner 明确对比了“需求（needs）”与“意见（opinions）”。' WHERE id = 'f7a2022d-991d-5069-8dff-fa72e8816ea1'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'Rats and other animals need to be highly attuned to social signals from others so they can identify friends to cooperate with and enemies to avoid. To find out if this extends to non-living beings, Laleh Quinn at the University of California, San Diego, and her colleagues tested whether rats can detect social signals from robotic rats.\n\nThey housed eight adult rats with two types of robotic rat—one social and one asocial—for four days. The robot rats were quite minimalist, resembling a chunkier version of a computer mouse with wheels to move around and colourful markings.\n\nDuring the experiment, the social robot rat followed the living rats around, played with the same toys, and opened cage doors to let trapped rats escape. Meanwhile, the asocial robot simply moved forwards and backwards and side to side.\n\nNext, the researchers trapped the robots in cages and gave the rats the opportunity to release them by pressing a lever. Across 18 trials each, the living rats were 52 per cent more likely on average to set the social robot free than the asocial one. This suggests that the rats perceived the social robot as a genuine social being, says Quinn.\n\nThe rats may have bonded more with the social robot because it displayed behaviors like communal exploring and playing. This could lead to the rats better remembering having freed it earlier, and wanting the robot to return the favour when they get trapped, she says. "Rats have been shown to engage in multiple forms of reciprocal help and cooperation, including what is referred to as direct reciprocity where a rat will help another rat that has previously helped them," says Quinn.\n\nThe readiness of the rats to befriend the social robot was surprising given its minimal design. The robot was the same size as a regular rat but resembled a simple plastic box on wheels. "We\'d assumed we\'d have to give it a moving head and tail, facial features, and put a scent on it to make it smell like a real rat, but that wasn\'t necessary," says Janet Wiles at the University of Queensland in Australia, who helped with the research.\n\nThe finding shows how sensitive rats are to social cues, even when they come from basic robots, says Wiles. Similarly, children tend to treat robots as if they are fellow beings, even when they display only simple social signals. "We humans seem to be fascinated by robots, and it turns out other animals are too," says Wiles.' WHERE id = '33ba7d78-c44f-5fcc-b1f5-9974bea301de'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'It is true that CEO pay has gone up—top ones may make 300 times the pay of typical workers on average, and since the mid-1970s, CEO pay for large publicly traded American corporations has, by varying estimates, gone up by about 500%. The typical CEO of a top American corporation now makes about $18.9 million a year.\n\nThe best model for understanding the growth of CEO pay is that of limited CEO talent in a world where business opportunities for the top firms are growing rapidly. The efforts of America\'s highest-earning 1% have been one of the more dynamic elements of the global economy. It\'s not popular to say, but one reason their pay has gone up so much is that CEOs really have upped their game relative to many other workers in the U.S. economy.\n\nToday\'s CEO, at least for major American firms, must have many more skills than simply being able to "run the company." CEOs must have a good sense of financial markets and maybe even how the company should trade in them. They also need better public relations skills than their predecessors, as the costs of even a minor slipup can be significant. Then there\'s the fact that large American companies are much more globalized than ever before, with supply chains spread across a larger number of countries. To lead in that system requires knowledge that is fairly mind-boggling. Plus, virtually all major American companies are becoming tech companies, one way or another. Beyond this, major CEOs still have to do all the day-to-day work they have always done.\n\nThe common idea that high CEO pay is mainly about ripping people off doesn\'t explain history very well. By most measures, corporate governance has become a lot tighter and more rigorous since the 1970s. Yet it is principally during this period of stronger governance that CEO pay has been high and rising. That suggests it is in the broader corporate interest to recruit top candidates for increasingly tough jobs.\n\nFurthermore, the highest CEO salaries are paid to outside candidates, not to the cozy insider picks, another sign that high CEO pay is not some kind of depredation at the expense of the rest of the company. And the stock market reacts positively when companies tie CEO pay to, say, stock prices, a sign that those practices build up corporate value not just for the CEO.' WHERE id = 'c57be57c-1969-5e9b-8a4a-31250849e545'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'Five Ways to Win Over Everyone in the Office\n\n[A] Give compliments, just not too many\n[B] Put on a good face, always\n[C] Tailor your interactions\n[D] Spend time with everyone\n[E] Reveal, don\'t hide, information\n[F] Slow down and listen\n[G] Put yourselves in others\' shoes\n\nIs it possible to like everyone in your office? Think about how tough it is to get together 15 people, much less 50, who all get along perfectly. But unlike in friendships, you need coworkers. You work with them every day, and you depend on them just as they depend on you. Here are some ways that you can get the whole office on your side.\n\n[41] If you have a bone to pick with someone in your workplace, you may try to stay tight-lipped around them. But you won\'t be helping either one of you. A Harvard Business School study found that observers consistently rated those who were upfront about themselves more highly, while those who hid lost trustworthiness. The lesson is not that you should make your personal life an open book, but rather, when given the option to offer up details about yourself or studiously stash them away, you should just be honest.\n\n[42] Just as important as being honest about yourself is being receptive to others. We often feel the need to tell others how we feel, whether it\'s a concern about a project, a stray thought, or a compliment. Those are all valid, but you need to take time to hear out your coworkers, too. In fact, rushing to get your own ideas out there can cause colleagues to feel you don\'t value their opinions. Do your best to engage coworkers in a genuine, back-and-forth conversation, rather than prioritizing your own thoughts.\n\n[43] It\'s common to have a "cubicle mate" or special confidant in a work setting. But in addition to those trusted coworkers, you should expand your horizons and find out about all the people around you. Use your lunch and coffee breaks to meet up with colleagues you don\'t always see. Find out about their lives and interests beyond the job. It requires minimal effort and goes a long way. This will help to grow your internal network, in addition to being a nice break in the work day.\n\n[44] Positive feedback is important for anyone to hear. And you don\'t have to be someone\'s boss to tell them they did an exceptional job on a particular project. This will help engender good will in others. But don\'t overdo it or be fake about it. One study found that people responded best to comments that shifted from negative to positive, possibly because it suggested they had won somebody over.\n\n[45] This one may be a bit more difficult to pull off, but it can go a long way to achieving results. Remember in dealing with any coworker what they appreciate from an interaction. Watch out for how they verbalize with others. Some people like small talk in a meeting before digging into important matters, while others are more straightforward. Jokes that work on one person won\'t necessarily land with another. So, adapt your style accordingly to type. Consider the person that you\'re dealing with in advance and what will get you to your desired outcome.' WHERE id = '1eefd825-1417-5e7a-9ce7-355f2db261f1'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [2] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "in addition", "content": "in addition"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "for example", "content": "for example"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "at once", "content": "at once"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "by accident", "content": "by accident"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句间语义逻辑+副词短语辨析。\n［解题思路］空格词在句中作插入语，可先看句子主干信息A calm，rule-following child...better... than...a younger sibling，可知该句是针对上句宽泛结论children respond differently...（不同孩子对同种育儿风格反应不同）给出的具体实例一一性格、年龄不同，则反应不同（更稳重、守规和年长的孩子适应力更强），故空格词应表“举例说明”，[B]正确。\n［错项排除］[A]inaddition（=also，aswell）表并列，位于句中时，前后信息完整（其后常为省略形式），互为补充，如They study their instruments and，in addition，theory and music history.（他们研究其乐器，还研究其理论和音乐史。），文中空格前后皆不完整，需相连才能构成完整信息（better...than.. a younger sibling），故两者并非并列关系。注：副词短语Inaddition多见于句首，位于句中时常由and、but等连词引出。[C]atonce（=immediately；without delay或at the same time）表时间，用于强调动作在短时内或同时发生/实现，如Come here at once！（马上到这里来！），Don\'t all speak at once！（大家不要同时讲！）；[D]byaccident表方式，用于说明某事的发生是偶然、非刻意的，如Helen got into acting purely by accident.（海伦当演员完全出于偶然。）；文中③句谓语为respond better，为普遍状况，而非短时内或偶然之事，故排除两项。' WHERE id = 'f69d94e1-5233-57eb-90d8-ce14d93e700c'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [3] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Fortunately", "content": "Fortunately"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Occasionally", "content": "Occasionally"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Accordingly", "content": "Accordingly"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Eventually", "content": "Eventually"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义逻辑。\n［解题思路］上段提到“定义做好父母”很难（也即：人们即使想做好父母，也可能无所适从）”，本段\n①②句指出“还有一种稍容易的父母：耐心的父母。所有年龄段的孩子都能从有耐心的养育方式受益”。很明显，本段退而求其次，向人们介绍一种确定性的好父母特质“耐心”。[A]Fortunately既体现tricky VS easier间对比逻辑，又契合论述的情感色彩：虽难界定，但幸好还有某种标准可依。\n［错项排除］[B]Occasionally（= sometimes but not often）表频度，暗示“耐心的父母”只偶尔存在，与作者意图“介绍一种确定的好父母标准”不符。[C]Accordingly可表因果（=therefore），如Thetextwas too long and the editor accordingly cut it by20%.（文稿过长，因此编辑删减了五分之一。），还可表方式（=correspondingly），如Wehave to discover what his plans are andact accordingly.（我们必须弄清他有什么打算并采取相应行动。）；上文既非空格所在句的原因，也非其应该参照的情况，故排除。[D] Eventually用法有二：一为客观引出情况或过程的最终结局，二为影射某情况历经多时或万难总算达成，均表时间，而空格句并非最终结果。' WHERE id = '6e46515e-0516-551a-b3e2-d3798ae30a20'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [4] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "amuse", "content": "amuse"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "assist", "content": "assist"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "describe", "content": "describe"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "train", "content": "train"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义与句型逻辑。\n［解题思路］结合上题分析可知，空格句与上段②句形成转折对比（defining what it means to be a good parent is very tricky vs. another sort of parent that\'s easier to [4]），意在引出一种更容易界定且少有争议的好父母类型，故空格词应与首段 defining（下定义、界定）语义相近，［C］describe（意为 to say what sb/sth is like“描述、定性”）完全符合文意。\n［错项排除］干扰项试图利用惯常思维“耐心的父母会让孩子开心/协助孩子/进行培训”设障，但“be + 形容词 + to do”结构通常以不定式的主动形式表示被动意义（如 The apples are hard to reach.“苹果很难够到”），故主语 parent 与空格词的关系并非“主谓”，而是“动宾”，即“容易被描述/界定的父母”，据此可彻底排除［A］amuse、［B］assist 与［D］train。' WHERE id = 'ba3c3058-645e-5618-b694-73391c039d31'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [5] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "while", "content": "while"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "because", "content": "because"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "unless", "content": "unless"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "once", "content": "once"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义逻辑。\n［解题思路］空格词体现主句与从句间逻辑，需先明确两句大意。Still位于句首提示转折，表明本句与上文传递的积极情感“（虽难有明确的标准，但至少）可将耐心作为努力目标”方向相反，可能引出该方法的局限性或实现障碍，由此可见，主句this is no easy...（this回指to be patient）大意应为“耐心并不好达成”，明显与空格所在的分句“所有父母都想成为有耐心之人”为转折逻辑（理想虽好，但现实困难），故[A]while符合文意。\n［错项排除］[B]because、[D]once（=assoonas；when）利用“人人都向往的事情往往不易”这一常理\n干扰，但二者并非因果关系，也非条件关系：“都想有耐心”并非导致/触发“耐心不易”的因素/条件。三个选项均存在逻辑错误。' WHERE id = '9144d602-b688-5770-b67c-3c969a80f028'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [6] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "answer", "content": "answer"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "task", "content": "task"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "choice", "content": "choice"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "access", "content": "access"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义+名词辨析。\n［解题思路］结合上题分析可知，this is no easy大意为“耐心不易达成”，而空格词为表语，故应与主语this（代指to be patient，表示“目标"）属于同类且互相呼应，[B]task尤指艰巨或令人厌烦的任务、工作，与“目标”相吻合，同时符合上下文文意，即：变得耐心并非易事。\n[错项排除工A]暗指“耐心未必能真正解决问题”，与②句“所有孩子都能受益于耐心的养育”矛盾；\n[C]暗指“人们做出朝耐心努力这一选择”有一定困难，但文意实为“耐心本身不易达成”，而非“（外界因\n素等导致）选择难做”。[D]access表示“获得/使用/接近（某事/某地/某人）的能力、机会或权利”，常以介词to引出动作施加的对象，如have easy access to information（很容易获取信息）；故从结构上看，没有is this no easy access的说法，正确形式应为（thereis）noeasy access to sth；从语义上看，access的对象一般为资源、设施、场所、特定人物等，而“变耐心”为目标、任务，两者无法搭配。' WHERE id = '5f36eedb-a288-53b6-b2f0-70d97ae3bff4'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [8] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "move", "content": "move"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "drag", "content": "drag"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "push", "content": "push"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "send", "content": "send"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义+固定搭配。\n［解题思路］空格句指出，有时你的孩子会得你有些过头。结合上文“耐心不易”以及空格前半句“你只不过是凡人”可知，本句意在解释“父母为何难以做到耐心”，故文意应为“孩子让父母不得已失去耐心”，push有“迫使、促使”之意，push sb too far为固定搭配，意为“逼人太甚、逼得某人发脾气”，故[C]正确。\n［错项排除］本题考查固定短语，选项中只有[C]能与you...toofar搭配传达“逼迫某人”之意，且\n[A]“感动过头”与“失去耐心”的语义相；[B]drag也有“强迫”之意，但表示“生拉硬拽，劝人勉强来/去' WHERE id = '2dc8b38c-00bd-5302-b437-ee0ded64d012'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [9] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "mysterious", "content": "mysterious"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "illogical", "content": "illogical"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "suspicious", "content": "suspicious"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "inevitable", "content": "inevitable"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义+形容词辨析。\n［解题思路］“the + 形容词”表示“…的事情”，冒号提示其是对随后“父母失去耐心的具体表现”的概括性评价，而上句“你只是凡人，孩子有时会逼得人发脾气”传达作者态度：这些不耐心的表现是人在情急下的正常反应，在所难免，情有可原，故[D]inevitable符合文意。\n［错项排除］Andthen...happens表明①②句间为因果顺承关系，①句“孩子有时会把人逼得有些过头”这一情况为②句“父母失去耐心”提供了前提，且作者暗示两件事接连发生、在所难免。[A] mysterious、[B]illogical皆与文章所表达的“理所当然”之意相，故排除；the suspicious表示“可疑的人/事”，与犯罪或欺诈相关，脱离上下文语境，排除[C]。' WHERE id = 'c5b973f8-5cd5-5890-acdd-3372b098b045'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [12] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Overall", "content": "Overall"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Instead", "content": "Instead"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "However", "content": "However"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Otherwise", "content": "Otherwise"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义+副词辨析。\n［解题思路］空格句先让步承认（even though）“这种情况很常见”（it回指上文“父母失去耐心而发怒”），随后转折引出建议“父母应记住…….（it\'s important to keep in mind）”，下句阐述发怒行为的消极后果（dodamage）。可知本段主旨为“父母向孩子发怒造成危害”，段首逻辑词应在上下段之间起转折过渡作用，传达“这一行为虽情有可原、谁都难免经历，但仍需警醒其会造成危害”之意，[C]正确。\n［错项排除］[A]通常用于总结前文，其前后语义应保持一致，此处不符合原文逻辑。[B]、[D]均含转折意味，但instead侧重强调“后者替代前者（而发生）”，如：Geoffdidn\'tstudylaw. Instead，hedecided to become an actor.（杰夫没学法律，相反，他决定当演员。）；otherwise侧重强调“某人不照做某事、或某情况不发生/不同的后果”，两项均不符合文中“从探讨事物的正面转向探讨其负面（合理性→危害性）”，可排除。' WHERE id = '5d59f312-9eb0-5b97-99df-5f892823a4c8'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [13] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "like", "content": "like"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "miss", "content": "miss"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "believe", "content": "believe"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "regret", "content": "regret"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义。\n［解题思路］空格所在主句具体阐述作者建议（it\'s important to）：父母应记住，在疲惫的瞬间你会对孩子说一些你可能会良久的话。其中，moment of fatigue、say something to your child that...均复现第二、三段所述情形及后果“父母筋疲力尽、情绪失控→说出过于严厉、对双方都无益的话，以至想倒转时光，从头来过”。故①句实为过渡句，空格部分语义应为“说出让自己后悔许久的话”，以引出对具体负面影响的介绍，[D]regret正确。\n［错项排除］[A]like为正面语义，与文意相；[B]miss、[C]believe指向“错过/相信对孩子所说的话良久”，不合逻辑。' WHERE id = 'b432ae7d-b4d3-536e-9b58-9fc402ce8a34'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [15] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "time", "content": "time"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "bond", "content": "bond"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "race", "content": "race"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "cool", "content": "cool"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义+固定搭配。\n［解题思路］空格句内条件状语从句If...then提示“你给孩子树立缺乏情绪控制的范例”为“你不断对孩子失去”的结果（文中you均指“父母”），则空格词应与“情绪控制”语义相近。结合贯穿全文的话题“父母对孩子失去耐心”，可进一步明确空格词应表与“耐心”相近的特质，选项中只有[D]cool（平静、镇静）与之有交集，故正确，lose/keep your cool为习语，意为“火冒三丈/保持沉着”。\n［错项排除］[A]time指向“父母与孩子相处时间不足”，偏离文中要义“育儿难保持耐心”。[B]颠倒因果：bond虽与上段末句relationship同义，但“亲子关系遭破坏”是“父母对孩子发怒”的结果而非原' WHERE id = 'ce01fb7f-0f23-57a8-a057-57cb9cefcfe5'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [16] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "nature", "content": "nature"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "secret", "content": "secret"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "importance", "content": "importance"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "context", "content": "context"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义逻辑。\n［解题思路］空格句指出，我们都愈发认识到为年轻一代树立宽容、耐心典范的。结合前句“父母失去冷静会给孩子树立缺乏情绪控制的范例”、下两句“这（指代“情绪控制”）是一项可让孩子受益终身的技能（help...throughout life）”、“情绪调节/控制是最重要的生活技能（most important.. skills）”可推知本段逻辑链：①句暗示缺乏情绪控制力的后果→②句点明情绪控制力的重要性/价值/意义→③④句具体解释情绪控制力的意义，[C]符合文意。\n［错项排除］[A]指向“树立宽容、耐心典范”的“本质、属性（the basic qualities）”[B]指向其“方法、技巧”[D]指向其“外在条件、环境”，虽能使②句单独成为逻辑自洽的句子，但与上下文逻辑链条脱节。' WHERE id = '6485db02-5f90-5a73-a225-7e8853312537'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [19] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "trying", "content": "trying"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "changing", "content": "changing"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "exciting", "content": "exciting"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "surprising", "content": "surprising"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义+熟词僻义。\n［解题思路］空格句指出，一个更现实可行的目标是父母在面临涉及孩子的情况时尽可能地保持镇静。回溯上文多次复现的信息“成为耐心的父母并不容易，父母时常被孩子逼得情绪失控”可知，situations involving your children应为“令人烦恼或失去耐心的、难应付的育儿时刻”，[A] trying用于说明“某事/人惹人烦、难对付”，故正确。\n［错项排除］由上下文可知，空格词应体现处境对父母不利，首先排除含正向语义的[C]exciting。\n[B]changing、[D]surprising虽可传达负面语义，但前者表意过于宽泛，不能直接指向文中关注的焦点情\n况“育儿中失去耐心而暴怒”，而后者与文中I understand this、We\'\'ve all been there、it\'scommon所暗示的该情况“司空见惯，父母皆有体会”相矛盾。' WHERE id = 'b8798c5f-8a80-58f0-9eac-1fd1ee11a1ed'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [20] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "hide", "content": "hide"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "emerge", "content": "emerge"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "withdraw", "content": "withdraw"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "escape", "content": "escape"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义+动词辨析。\n［解题思路］空格句说明目标达成（goal与②句A more practical goal同指）的结果（promise you this、As a result... this goal)：父母和孩子都将从紧张的时刻中获益并，身心状态都得到提升。根据上下文以及and可知，from stressful moments应和“从中获益”一样，皆体现积极结果，emerge from sth意为“（从困境或苦难经历中）幸存下来，摆脱出来”，故[B]符合文意。\n［错项排除］[A]、[C]、[D]均可表示“与…分离，从…中出来”，但均含“因无法解决问题/被击溃而被动消极地逃避”之意，谈不上“最终结果积极、结局良好”。·词汇注释与难句分析·\n① incredibly [ɪnˈkredəbli] adv. 难以置信地；极其\n② practical [ˈpræktɪkl] adj. 实际的，务实的\n③ to the best 尽全力\n④ composed [kəmˈpəʊzd] adj. 镇静的；沉着的\n• be faced with 面对；面临\n• as a result of 由于；作为……的结果A more practical goal is to try, to the best of your ability, to be as tolerant and composed as you can when faced with trying situations involving your children.\n【结构切分】A more practical goal is [to try, to the best of your ability, to be as tolerant and composed as you can]（不定式作表语，含插入语 to the best of your ability） [when faced with trying situations involving your children]（时间状语从句分词省略结构）。' WHERE id = 'a5439ffd-d7e6-5d7c-8338-89e3e4883c40'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Quinn and her colleagues conducted a test to see if rats can ________.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "pick up social signals from non-living rats", "content": "pick up social signals from non-living rats"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "distinguish a friendly rat from a hostile one", "content": "distinguish a friendly rat from a hostile one"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "attain sociable traits through special training", "content": "attain sociable traits through special training"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "send out warning messages to their fellows", "content": "send out warning messages to their fellows"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［精准定位］首段末句介绍奎因等的研究目标（tested whether）：测试老鼠是否能察觉机器鼠发出的社交信号，[A]正确。\n［命题解密］“题干+[A]”同义改写首段末句，if...pickup...from non-living rats替换whether.. detect...from robotic rats/non-living beings。\n[B]、[C]均利用①句已知信息干扰，[B]改写identify friends...andenemies，但“接收社交信号以分\n辨敌友”是老鼠已被证实的能力，而非待证实的能力；[C]将need to be highly attuned to social signals断章取义为“老鼠对社交信号不够敏感”，并在此基础上臆断研究者想要观察是否可通过特殊训练提升其技能（attain...through special training）。[D]将研究目标“观察老鼠能否接收/识别（detect）机器鼠（其相似物）发出的社交信息”窜改为完全反向的“观察老鼠是否会向其发出（sendout）信息”。\n［技巧总结］本题就首段命制事实题，意在考查新研究的目的，要求考生辨别“研究背景/已知信息”与“研究目标/待验证信息”。可采用思路：先由②句To find out if this extends to...梳理首段逻辑“①句先介绍已知信息，②句引出研究者在已知信息基础之上的进一步研究”，从而明确“②句为正确项来源，且①句很可能被用于设置干扰”。随后重点分析②句，可进一步锁定正确项来源whether rats can detect social signals from robotic rats，并结合前半句得知robotic rats代表non-living beings，从而确定\n[A]正确。其余选项或利用①句背景信息干扰（[B]、[C]），或窜改研究目标（[D]）。\nThey housed eight adult rats with two types研究人员让8只成年鼠与2只不同类型ofrobotic rat—one social and one asocial—for four的机器鼠一一只爱社交，一只不合群days. The robot rats were quite minimalist,共处一室4天。这两只机器鼠外形相当简约resembling a chunkier version of a computer mouse抽象，就像矮胖版的电脑鼠标，靠轮子四处with wheels to move around and colourful markings移动，带有鲜艳的标记。Ⅲl During the experiment, the social robot rat在试验过程中，社交机器鼠跟随生物鼠followed the living rats around, played with the same们四处走动，玩同样的玩具，还会打开笼门toys, and opened cage doors to let trapped rats escape.让被困老鼠逃脱。在此期间，非社交机器鼠\n②Meanwhile, the asocial robot simply moved forwards则只是前后、左右移动。and backwards and side to sideide.' WHERE id = 'c1e6378a-6818-577c-a6ae-2116d521addd'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'What did the asocial robot do during the experiment?', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "It followed the social robot.", "content": "It followed the social robot."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "It played with some toys.", "content": "It played with some toys."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "It set the trapped rats free.", "content": "It set the trapped rats free."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "It moved around alone.", "content": "It moved around alone."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［精准定位］由the asocial robot、during the experiment定位至第三段末句。该句介绍试验过程中非社交机器鼠的表现：只是前后、左右移动。[D]正确。\n［命题解密］正确项[D]同义改写第三段末句，alone点明了句中simply一词暗含的对比之意：与社交机器鼠相反，非社交机器鼠不与老鼠们同游同玩儿，而是独自前后左右移动。\n[A]、[B]、[C]均张冠李戴，利用第三段首句社交机器鼠（thesocial robot）的表现捏造干扰，并非题\n目所问“非社交机器鼠（the asocial robot）行为”，[A]更是将“社交机器鼠跟随生物鼠走动”窜改为原文并未出现的信息“非社交机器鼠跟随社交机器鼠走动”。\n［技巧总结］本题考查试验过程中某一对象（非社交机器鼠）的表现，要求考生辨别不同对象的行为，避免张冠李戴。具体来说，可借助During the experiment，thesocial robotrat...Meanwhile，the asocial robot simply...以及关键词对social VS asocial明确“社交鼠”和“非社交鼠”的行为截然不同，锁定②句信息，并警惕①句陷阱。IVNext，the researchers trapped the robots in接下来，研究人员将机器鼠关进笼子，cages and gave the rats the opportunity to release them并给老鼠一个按下控制杆解救机器鼠的机by pressing a lever. Across 18 trials each, the living会。在对每只（生物鼠）各18次的试验中，\n\nrats were 52 per cent more likely on average toset the生物鼠解救社交机器鼠的几率比解救非社social robot free than the asocial one. This suggests交机器鼠的几率平均高出52%。奎因称，that the rats perceived the social robot as a genuine social这表明老鼠将社交机器鼠看作了真正的社being，says Quinn. The rats may have bonded more交生物。老鼠们可能因先前社交机器鼠表with the social robot because it displayed behaviours like现出集体探险及游戏等行为而与其建立了communal exploring and playing. This could lead to更强的情感纽带。她认为，这可能会使老the rats better remembering having freed it earlier, and鼠们更清楚记起自己之前曾经解救过机器wanting the robot to return thefavour when theyget鼠，并希望自己受困时能得到它相应的trapped, she says.回报。V“Rats have been shown to engage in multiple“已有研究表明，老鼠会进行多种形式forms of reciprocal help and cooperation，including的互助及合作，其中包括被称为‘直接互what isreferred to as direct reciprocity where aratwill惠”的行为，即老鼠会帮助之前曾帮助过自help another rat that has previously helped them，”己的另一只老鼠。”奎因说道。says Quinn.' WHERE id = 'b1d0d12c-8fa4-5b57-95f3-ac7bfd0206ae'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to Quinn, the rats released the social robot because they ________.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "tried to practice a means of escape", "content": "tried to practice a means of escape"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "expected it to do the same in return", "content": "expected it to do the same in return"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "wanted to display their intelligence", "content": "wanted to display their intelligence"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "considered that an interesting game", "content": "considered that an interesting game"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［精准定位］第四段①②句指出，老鼠更倾向于解救社交机器鼠；③④⑤句分析指出，老鼠可能与社交机器鼠建立起了情感联结，希望将来自己被困时也能得到相应的回报，所以愿意施救，［B］正确。\n［命题解密］正确项［B］同义改写第四段末句 wanting the robot to return the favour when they get trapped。\n［错项排除］［A］将第四段①句 release them by pressing a lever 断章取义为老鼠想实践一种新的逃跑方法，但“按下控制杆”是老鼠帮助机器鼠脱困的方式，不是施救的原因；［C］将④句 displayed behaviours...（社交机器鼠曾表现出集体探险及游戏行为）曲解为“老鼠想要展示自己的智力”；［D］将④句 exploring and playing（老鼠先前曾与机器鼠共同游戏）曲解为“老鼠如今之所以营救机器鼠是因为认为这是个有趣的游戏”。\n［技巧总结］本题针对“试验结果（老鼠解救社交机器鼠）的原因分析”命题。第四段③句 This suggests 开启分析，④⑤句以因果线索串联起施救逻辑：先前社交机器鼠参与老鼠的集体活动→老鼠与其建立更深情感联结→老鼠寄希望于机器鼠将来报答自己，因此更愿施救。' WHERE id = 'c4d607ff-98d2-5936-9acb-8f819fa8f6cb'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Janet Wiles notes that rats ________.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "can remember other rats\' facial features", "content": "can remember other rats\' facial features"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "differentiate smells better than sizes", "content": "differentiate smells better than sizes"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "respond more to actions than to looks", "content": "respond more to actions than to looks"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "can be scared by a plastic box on wheels", "content": "can be scared by a plastic box on wheels"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［精准定位］由题干人名关键词Janet Wiles定位至第六、七段。第六段③句指出，Wiles原以为要给机器鼠加上各种仿真的外形设计（可活动的头、尾等），老鼠才会愿意与其交朋友，但结果证明这些根本没有必要，即：尽管机器鼠样貌不够逼真，但老鼠仍然会因其行动而亲近它，[C]正确。\n\n［命题解密］正确项是对第六段③句We\'d assumed... but that wasn\'t necessary反映出的“对老鼠来说，机器鼠的样貌没那么重要（其行动更为重要）”的正确解读。\n[A]、[B]、[D]利用第六段②③句提及的facial features、scent、smell、size、a plastic box on wheels\n并不妨碍老鼠与机器鼠建立情感联结”（即：老鼠对这些特征并不在意/反应不大），选项与此相。从中并未提及老鼠对“味道”和“体型大小”的不同反应，[B]捏造比较；文中指出老鼠愿意与机器鼠（带轮子的塑料盒）做朋友，[D]违背文意。\n［技巧总结］本题考查某一研究人员对于研究对象的看法，要求考生正确理解人物观点。第六、七段均涉及Wiles观点，需整体理解。另外，理解过程中需结合其身份“研究者之一”，意识到正确项应顺应研究发现。第六段①②句指出研究发现尽管机器鼠外形简陋，老鼠仍然愿意与其交朋友，这令人惊讶；③句Wiles以虚拟语气指出“我们原以为必须给它加上…但（结果证明）没有必要”。第七段首句Wiles以让步结构强调“机器鼠对社交信号高度敏感，哪怕它来自外形设计简陋的机器鼠”。整体理解可知，Wiles意在说明“机器鼠外形不重要，其行动（回应第三段内容）已足以引起老鼠的交友意愿”，[C]正确。' WHERE id = '1faad9a8-e6cd-594a-a59a-ece75baeb574'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'It can be learned from the text that rats ________.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "appear to be adaptable to new surroundings", "content": "appear to be adaptable to new surroundings"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "are more socially active than other animals", "content": "are more socially active than other animals"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "behave differently from children in socializing", "content": "behave differently from children in socializing"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "are more sensitive to social cues than expected", "content": "are more sensitive to social cues than expected"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［精准定位］第六段①句指出，老鼠与设计简陋的机器鼠交朋友的行为出人意料；②③句解释：研究人员原以为要给机器鼠加上可活动的头和尾巴等，以使其更像老鼠，但事实证明这并不必要。第七段得出结论：老鼠对社交信号非常敏感，即使这些信号来自简单的机器鼠。可见，老鼠对社交信号的敏感超出研究者预期，[D]正确。\n［命题解密］[D]正确解读第六段The readiness of the rats..was surprising...及第七段how sensitive...are to social cues，evenwhen...传达的研究人员的“惊讶之情”。\n[A]夸大其词：文中只提及“老鼠愿意与机器鼠交朋友”，由此无法推知”老鼠擅长适应新环境”。\n[B]捏造比较：文中只提及老鼠对社交信号高度敏感，并未涉及与其他动物的比较。[C]与第七段②句\n相：“老鼠与儿童均可察觉到机器人发出的社交信号”表明“老鼠与儿童在社交方面表现相同”。\n［技巧总结］根据题目位置（最后一题）及各选项内容（关于“老鼠”的论断）可知本题很可能考查研究结论。解题时需先把握核心发现，再确认具体细节：首先从首尾段快速提取核心信息：老鼠对社交信号十分敏感，即便这些信号来自简单的机器鼠，大致确定[D]为正确项。随后确认细节：[D]涉及研究人员对研究的预期，可定位至第六段首句surprising，并确认选项正确。而“老鼠适应新环境的能力”、“老鼠社交能力与其他动物的比较”文中均未提及，可排除[A]、[B]；[C]与第七段②句相，也错误。' WHERE id = '5bd17948-2aa2-5235-871a-60c49cf03a83'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Which of the following has contributed to CEO pay rise?', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "The growth in the number of corporations.", "content": "The growth in the number of corporations."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "The general pay rise with a better economy.", "content": "The general pay rise with a better economy."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Increased business opportunities for top firms.", "content": "Increased business opportunities for top firms."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Close cooperation among leading economies.", "content": "Close cooperation among leading economies."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［精准定位］第二段解释 CEO 薪酬上涨的原因（①句 The best model 及③句 one reason...）：全球对 CEO 才能的旺盛需求带动薪酬上涨，故［C］正确。\n［命题解密］题干与正确项［C］是对第二段①句的合理推断，其中 Increased demand 对应原文 rising global demand / growing need for talent。\n［错项排除］［A］以偏概全，文中并未说高层管理职位的总体数量增加；［B］偷换因果，文中指出经济上行只是 CEO 付出努力的背景，并未将其当作带动全社会普遍涨薪的原因；［D］曲解第三段意思，文中指出 CEO 需具备多元复杂技能，并非要求高薪来弥补日常繁重工作。' WHERE id = '54323095-be2e-5176-90c9-b7c5c928c360'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Compared with their predecessors, today\'s CEOs are required to ________.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "foster a stronger sense of teamwork", "content": "foster a stronger sense of teamwork"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "finance more research and development", "content": "finance more research and development"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "establish closer ties with tech companies", "content": "establish closer ties with tech companies"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "operate more globalized companies", "content": "operate more globalized companies"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［精准定位］第三段首句总领整段：CEO必须拥有更多的技能。随后各句以CEOsmust...、They also...、Then...、Plus...、Beyondthis...分述CEO所需的技能。其中④句指出“美国大公司的全球化程度空前，胜任CEO需要异常广博的知识”，由此可知，CEO需要经营更加全球化的公司。[D]正确。\n［命题解密］[D]operate more globalized companies对应句CEO的职责之一Toleadinthat system（其中thatsystem指向④句信息“供应链遍布更多国家的全球化程度空前的大公司"）。\n[A]、[C]分别利用have a good sense of、tech companies设置干扰，[A]将原文“金融市场意识”曲解\n为“团队意识”，[C]将原文“大公司在向科技公司转变（暗示CEO需具备领导科技公司的技能）”曲解为“CEO与科技公司建立更紧密的联系”。[B]由文中financial（指向“金融市场”）捏造出动词finance（给……提供资金），且“研发”在文中无据可依。\n［技巧总结］由题干关键词不难定位到第三段，借表列举的逻辑词（also、Then、Plus、Beyondthis）以及相关近义表述（①句概述词many more skills引领后文agood sense of...、better...skills、requires knowledge、haveto do等具体技能/知识）可推知该段呈总分结构。可将各项与②至?句分述的各项技两类公司的逻辑关系，[D]“（CEO）经营全球化公司"近义对应句“（CEO）领导全球化公司”，故该项正司”相。' WHERE id = 'b0c2b5ba-7aff-5f89-9dfc-fea2d1d94719'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'CEO pay has been rising since the 1970s despite ________.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "continual internal opposition", "content": "continual internal opposition"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "strict corporate governance", "content": "strict corporate governance"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "conservative business strategies", "content": "conservative business strategies"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "repeated government warnings", "content": "repeated government warnings"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［精准定位］第四段②③句以让步转折逻辑指出：虽然上世纪70年代以来公司治理变得更为严格，但CEO高薪及上涨趋势恰恰出现于该强化治理时期，故[B]正确。\n［命题解密］[B]是对②③句让步转折逻辑中让步信息corporate governance has become a lot tighter and more rigorous的合理概括。\n[A]由①句普遍看法“CEO的高薪很大程度上是对员工的剥削”过度推断出原文未论及的信息“公司\n内部员工一直反对CEO拿高薪”。[C]源自商业常识“企业的商业战略往往影响薪酬水平：如果企业采取保守性战略，其薪酬水平通常也较保守”，但原文并未论及“商业战略”。[D]将②③句关键信息“公司治理力度不断强化（公司自我治理趋严）”曲解为“政府一再告诫公司强化治理（政府对公司的监管趋严）”。\n［技巧总结］本题考查让步转折逻辑中的让步信息（由despite体现），定位句②③句中，②句为让步信息，可初步定为答案来源，③句为转折信息（Yet），可用于验证答案来源。具体来看，③句用强调句式“it is + 特定时期 + that + 发生的事件”凸显CEO薪酬上涨情形的特定时期背景during this period of stronger governance，其中stronger governance是对②句主干corporate governance... tighter and more rigorous的高度概括，由此提炼两句逻辑“正是在70年代以来公司治理趋严的这段时期CEO薪酬却在不断上涨”，可确定答案[B]。本题还可借助段落主旨解题：首尾句提示段落主旨要义一驳斥惯常看法“CEO高薪伤害普通员工利益/不合理”，认定其“保障总体利益/合理”，故②③句为论据，表面上介绍CEO涨薪的发生背景，实则以子之矛攻子之盾：既然CEO高薪不合理，则治理严时应“修正”；而事实却正相反。选项“内部反对”“战略保守”和“政府警告”与题干“CEO薪酬上涨”虽能构成矛盾关系，但恰恰迎合了惯常看法，无益于佐证段落主旨。' WHERE id = '8352b1f6-fedd-52fb-9482-b36ed5d5bbdd'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'High CEO pay can be justified by the fact that it helps ________.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "confirm the status of CEOs", "content": "confirm the status of CEOs"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "motive inside candidates", "content": "motive inside candidates"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "boost the efficiency of CEOs", "content": "boost the efficiency of CEOs"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "increase corporate value", "content": "increase corporate value"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［精准定位］第四段表明“CEO 高薪是企业严格治理下的举措，不是对普通员工的剥削，而是符合公司整体利益；CEO 高薪制用于吸引外部顶尖人才而非内部安稳人士，故不会牺牲普通员工利益，反而有助于增加公司价值（具体逻辑链为：对 CEO 采取薪酬激励措施（如与股价挂钩）→促使 CEO 提升公司经营业绩→公司股价上涨，公司升值）”。综合可知 [D] 正确。\n［命题解密］[D] 直接对应第五段末句给 CEO 带来高薪的薪酬激励措施的作用 build up corporate value（增加公司价值）。\n[A] 蕴含逻辑为“薪酬与地位相匹配：高薪可巩固 CEO 的权威地位”，原文并未提及，且选项有意凸显“精英与平民地位有别”反而削减了 CEO 高薪的合理性。[B] 与第五段①句信息“最高薪酬是为了吸引外部候选人（即激励外部候选人）而非安逸的内部人选”相悖。[C] 结合第三段工作技能等信息将第五段①句“安逸的内部人选”曲解为“在任者安于现状，不思进取，效率低下”，进而臆断出“高薪可激励他们提高干劲”，而该句主旨实为“公司倾向于高薪外聘，而非内部提拔”。\n［技巧总结］本题难点一是解读题干信息：can be justified（justify 意为“证明……有道理；为……辩护”）提示考查“高薪的合理性/正当性”，it helps 进一步聚焦考查点“高薪的作用”，根据题文同序原则及末两段论述角度可锁定末两段。难点二是分析定位处长难句：[B]、[D] 分别源自第五段的两个长句，对两个长句进行句法语义分析可知，[B] 混淆了第五段首句的激励对象（外部候选人而非内部安稳人士），唯有 [D] 才是对第五段末句的正确解读。' WHERE id = 'd860303f-91c8-52cb-8c5a-95893ddf0328'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Which of the following is true about Madrid\'s clean air zone?', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Its effects are questionable.", "content": "Its effects are questionable."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "It has been opposed by a judge.", "content": "It has been opposed by a judge."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "It needs tougher enforcement.", "content": "It needs tougher enforcement."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Its fate is yet to be decided.", "content": "Its fate is yet to be decided."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［精准定位］第二段末句明确指出：马德里“清洁空气区”的未来看起来很不明朗。也即，它的命运尚未确定。故[D]正确。\n［命题解密］正确项[D]fate...yet to be decided同义改写第二段末句future looks uncertain。\n[A]根据第一段末句“市议会暂停实施”第二段首句“市长反对”捏造出其反对理由“（实施）效果不确\n定”，但很明显与第二段①句despite所引出的客观事实its success in improving air quality“清洁空气区’在改善空气质量方面取得良好效果”相；[C]则根据第一段②句“暂停实施”第二段①句客观事实“在改善空气质量方面取得良好效果”杂臆造出“清洁空气区”效果良好，市议会不应该暂停实施，理应得到更严厉的执行”，且由第二段②句“市政府中止实施VS法官责令恢复”可知“马德里清洁空气区”面临的问题并非“执行不力”，而是“能否继续实施”。[B] 将反对“清洁空气区”的主体由第二段①句中的“市长”偷换为②句中的“法官”，而②句明确指出“法官推翻市议会决定，并责令恢复收取罚金（也即，支持“清洁空气区”）。\n［技巧总结］Which型事实细节题的典型解题思路是“利用选项关键词回文对应一比对判别对错”。如本题，首先根据试题命制顺序按照文章由前至后原则以及题干关键词将范围限定至第一、二段，再根据选项关键词（核心名词/动词）将各选项回文定位：[A]effects对应第二段①句its success in improving、[B]ajudge对应第二段②句，[C]tougher enforcement对应第一段②句suspended enforcement，[D]Itsfate对应第二段③句thezone\'sfuture。随后一一比对发现，[D]为原文同义转述。Ⅲl Among other weaknesses, the measures除其他薄弱点以外，当污浊空气的治理落cities must employwhen left to tackle dirty air on到城市头上，他们所必须采取的措施会引发政their own are politically contentious，and therefore治争议，因此极易招致攻击。这是因为这些措vulnerable②That\'s because they inevitably put施不可避免地将清洁空气的成本加诸车主个the costs of cleaning the air on to individual drivers人一一车主必须为污染付费或者买更好的whomust payfees or buy better vehicles-rather than车一—而不是加诸汽车生产商，生产商的舞弊on to the car manufacturers whose cheating is the行为才是造成有毒污染的真正原因。real cause of our toxic pollution.' WHERE id = '90261b64-0cbf-5416-8616-78fe1f6fd83c'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Which is considered a weakness of the city-level measures to tackle dirty air?', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "They are biased against car manufacturers.", "content": "They are biased against car manufacturers."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "They prove impractical for city councils.", "content": "They prove impractical for city councils."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "They are deemed too mild for politicians.", "content": "They are deemed too mild for politicians."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "They put too much burden on individual motorists.", "content": "They put too much burden on individual motorists."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［精准定位］第三段①句指出市级污浊空气治理措施的一个薄弱之处：引发政治争议、易招致击；\n②句阐释原因：市级措施将空气清洁成本加诸车主个人而非引发有毒污染的真正“凶手”汽车生产商。可见，车主个人被迫承担了本不属于自己而应属于汽车生产商的责任，故[D]正确。\n［命题解密］题干+[D]put too much burden on individual motorists是对第三段段落主旨的Among other weaknesses，the measures...are...That\'s because they put the costs...on to individual drivers...rather than on to the car manufacturers...的高度概括。\n[A]将第三段②句取舍结构put the costs...onto A...rather than onto B中的A、B对调，将不公\n允对象由“车主个人”调换为“汽车生产商”（注：biased against...“对……有成见/不公允”与biasedfor/towards/iin favor of...“偏袒……”为反向关系）。[B]将第一段②句作者观点“马德里市议会（city council）中止实施‘清洁空气区”这一行为可能致使该措施走向失败（demise）”曲解为市议会观点“马德里清洁空气区可能失败、不切实际（impractical)”，并将其上升为各城市措施的薄弱之处。[C]源自第三段①句politically contentious...vulnerable，错误有二：一将“引发政治争议（即，各派政治家们观点对立）”曲解为“观点一致：政治家们认为处罚力度不够”；二将“易招致击、脆弱不堪（即，措施可能被否决/推翻）”曲解为“治理力度不够、太轻”。\n［技巧总结］常规思路：定位段围绕“市级措施的薄弱之处”展开论述，关键是理清其中论述逻辑、剥离次要信息、明确weaknesses所指。首先由①句从属结构Among other weaknesses，the measures.. are A确定A为所举市级措施的薄弱处：引发政治争议。再由回指词 + 因果标志词结构（That\'s because）可知②句解释①句，而取舍结构Bratherthan（而非）C提示争议来源：将空气净化成本错误施加于车主个人而非汽车生产商。最终敲定[D]。非常规思路：纵观选项发现各选项指向不同人物主体，其中B、C的city councils、politicians在段落中（由weakness可定位至第三段）并无明确提及，而A的car manufacturers、individual motorists则原词复现或同义复现段末原文，进而细读该句发现取舍结构put...onto A rather than onto B，最终锁定[D]为正确项。' WHERE id = 'f7205989-7a7a-55d8-ac84-ac612c79b4d5'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Who does the author think should have addressed the problem?', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Local residents.", "content": "Local residents."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Mayors.", "content": "Mayors."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Councilors.", "content": "Councilors."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "National governments.", "content": "National governments."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［精准定位］第六段②句指出：市长们、市议员们（They的指代内容）之所以在采取行动（各种市级治理措施）是因为国家政府未能采取行动（so指代内容）。可见，作者认为本该由国家政府解决问题，[D]正确。\n\n［命题解密］正确项+题干是对national governments... have failed to do so（failed意为“没有做，未做（应做的事情）”）的正确解读。\n[A]将第五段③句中所涉人物主体Local（officials）、residents语义杂为local residents，且将居民\n作为空气污染治理的受益对象偷换为问题解决者。[B]、[C]均截取第六段①句mayors and councilors，但两者均为当前正在采取措施解决问题的主体，与题干所问“谁应该去解决问题却又没去解决”不符。\n［技巧总结］常规思路：语义转折、取舍处与全文主旨息息相关，常作为命题焦点出现，所以必须重视but/however/yet等转折词后的内容，对于not...but.../ratherthan/insteadof等取舍结构，则须重点明辨“取”的内容（“舍”常为干扰来源之一）。第六段①句以But与前文形成转折，强调作者否定态度：问题涉及范围过大而市长与市议员能力有限（only...SOmuch），可推知真正主体应在能力上强大于市长、市议员，由此可初步选定[D]。②句主、从句A are acting because B... have failed to do so构成语义对比：“A=They=mayors and councils”正在采取行动VS“B=national governments”本该采取行动却没采取行动，确认[D]正确。非常规思路：四个选项指向不同主体，但全文尤其第六段首句中mayorsand councilors表示两个主体处于并列平行状态（两者行为态度大体一致），故可将与之相关的[B]、[C]两项同时排除，最后再在[A]、[D]中做执择，无论是借由第六段首句“空气污染问题并非局域性问题而是全局性问题”还是借由文意关注核心“污浊空气治理政策”可舍指向区域性基层人民的[A]而取指向全国性国家政府层面的[D]。' WHERE id = 'bcd0abf6-fa6c-56a1-8a2a-e4f23522581d'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'It can be inferred from the last paragraph that auto companies ________.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "will raise low-emission car production", "content": "will raise low-emission car production"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "should be forced to follow regulations", "content": "should be forced to follow regulations"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "will upgrade the design of their vehicles", "content": "will upgrade the design of their vehicles"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "should be put under public supervision", "content": "should be put under public supervision"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［精准定位］末段首句指出：目前缺乏更大规模的行动来确保现有管控措施的严格执行、来要求汽车公司生产合规机动车；末句又指出：我们虽在竭尽一切所能却独独没有坚持要求汽车生产商清洁其汽车。言外之意即为，汽车生产商/汽车公司应该被强制要求遵守相关规章制度，故[B]正确。\n［命题解密］正确项是末段首末句针对汽车公司所述内容的合理引申。\n[A]、[C]均只见①句require auto companies to bring their vehicles into compliance而臆测“汽车公\n司将积极转型、升级汽车”，而未见其前信息absence“缺乏此类要求”，与第三段末句“汽车公司舞以致毒害空气”所隐藏文意“汽车公司无视法律、生产高污染汽车”的消极态度相。[D]利用末句We\'re doing everything but insist that...望文生义出“我们（普通大众）正竭尽一切所能以坚持要求汽车公司…”，从而推断出“置于公众监督之下”，而句意实为“我们（政府官员们）正在做力所能及之事，却独独没有要求汽车公司”。\n［技巧总结］段落推理题通常可以按照“紧贴段落主旨”原则解题。可以先借助段落首末句、或者同义/近义复现所展示的相关语义场、或者特殊的句式等揣摩段落主旨，随后将选项与段落主旨比对，正确项通常不直接对应原文字句，而是段落主旨思想的转述或升华。如本题，末段首尾句分借theaabsence of a larger effort“缺乏更大规模的行动”、doing everything but insist“做了一切，却独独没有要求”两个隐\n锁定正确项[B]；再有，两句中effort“特别的行动”insist“坚决要求”指向“更为严格、更具针对性的要求或行动”，properly enforce、regulations、bring into compliance指向“严格遵守规章制度”，auto companies、manufacturers指向“汽车公司”，三者共同指向“需对汽车公司严加管控、强制遵守”，最终敲定[B]正确。' WHERE id = 'ba3ac9fc-1013-5606-95be-35253a71cd6a'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Generation Zs graduating college this spring ________.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "are recognized for their abilities", "content": "are recognized for their abilities"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "are optimistic about the labor market", "content": "are optimistic about the labor market"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "are in favor of office job offers", "content": "are in favor of office job offers"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "are drawing growing public attention", "content": "are drawing growing public attention"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［精准定位］第一段首句指出，由于 Z 世代今年春天就要从大学毕业，近几周来对他们的关注也在日益增长，可知［D］are drawing growing public attention 正确。\n［命题解密］正确项［D］是对第一段第一句 the attention has been rising steadily in recent weeks 的同义复现。\n［错项排除］［A］根据③句“雇主增加应届毕业生招聘人数”主观臆断出“Z 世代能力受到认可”，但由②句“劳动力市场人才紧缺”可知雇主做法是大环境使然，不涉及对其能力的单独认可；［B］将②句客观事实“今年的劳动力市场紧张”歪曲为主观看法“Z 世代对劳动力市场感到乐观”；［C］的干扰方式与［B］相似，将④句客观事实“Z 世代将步入办公室职场”歪曲为主观偏好“Z 世代偏爱办公室工作”。' WHERE id = '6f6bb7c3-624c-568d-880d-a70b052d6d20'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Generation Zs are keenly aware ________.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "what their parents expect of them", "content": "what their parents expect of them"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "how valuable a counselor\'s advice is", "content": "how valuable a counselor\'s advice is"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "what a tough economic situation is like", "content": "what a tough economic situation is like"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "how they differ from past generations", "content": "how they differ from past generations"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［精准定位］第二段③句首先指出，Z世代清楚经济火车失事的惨状。④句紧接着解释：Z世代在2008年经济危机到来之时正是易受影响的孩子，当时他们许多人的父母失去了工作或毕生积蓄。由此可知，Z世代非常明白“严酷的经济形势是什么样子”，[C]正确。\n［命题解密］正确项[C]中（keenly aware）what a tough economic situation is like是对③句（know）what an economic train wreck looks like的同义转换。\n[A]对④5句强加因果，认为Z世代“对冒险不感兴趣”是迎合经济危机中“丢掉工作或毕生积蓄”\n的父母之“期待”的结果，但文中并未提及他们父母的期待。[B]将②句内容“职业顾问和专家认为Z世代是头脑清醒的经济实用主义者”歪曲为“Z世代认同并珍惜职业顾问的建议”。[D]将①句事实“Z世代与千禧一代不同”歪曲为“Z世代知道自己与前几代人的区别”。\n［技巧总结］本题继续围绕Z世代进行考查，涉及Z世代的主观感受，解题关键是结合题干和选项中的关键词回文定位，然后比对信息确定答案。具体来看：题干中Generation Zs are keenly aware同义替换原文③句中Gen Zs know，因此正确答案应该是对原文what an economic train wreck looks like的同义改写，故可直接锁定[C]。其他三项均利用该段中涉及的其他对象进行干扰（[A]涉及“父母”、[B]涉及“顾问”[D]涉及“千禧一代”），均不是Z世代的认识对象。' WHERE id = '2cfa1cba-1f8c-5537-9e54-07e3ecc2aa39'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The word "assuage" (Line 9, Para. 2) is closest in meaning to ________.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "deepen", "content": "deepen"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "define", "content": "define"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "maintain", "content": "maintain"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "relieve", "content": "relieve"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［精准定位］所考单词 assuage 出现在第二段末，该句主语为 The booming economy（蓬勃发展的经济），宾语为 this underlying generational sense of anxious urgency（这一代人内心深处的忧患意识）。\n［解题思路］本段首句为主旨句，指出 Z 世代的总体特征是 practical and cautious（讲求实际、谨慎小心）。this underlying generational sense of anxious urgency 承接上文“经历 2008 年经济危机后不愿冒险”的保守焦虑心态，而主语 The booming economy 指向经济向好一面，全句意在说明“即便在半个世纪以来最好的经济形势下，蓬勃发展的经济似乎也未能减轻（done little to assuage）这一代人的焦虑感”。由此可知 assuage 意为“减轻、缓解”，［D］relieve 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］deepen（加深）与文意相反；［B］define（定义）虽看似涉及焦虑感的成因，但无法体现“经济向好也难以减弱其焦虑”的转折语义；［C］maintain（保持）不符合句中 seems to have done little to 所传达的“未能缓解/削弱”的逻辑关系。' WHERE id = '712a18e1-b5a0-5850-88f9-9abb57612bb5'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the most suitable subheading from [A]-[G] for paragraph [41].', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Give compliments, just not too many", "content": "Give compliments, just not too many"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Put on a good face, always", "content": "Put on a good face, always"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Tailor your interactions", "content": "Tailor your interactions"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Spend time with everyone", "content": "Spend time with everyone"}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "Reveal, don\'t hide, information", "content": "Reveal, don\'t hide, information"}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "Slow down and listen", "content": "Slow down and listen"}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "Put yourselves in others\' shoes", "content": "Put yourselves in others\' shoes"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'E', explanation = E'［定位/考点］段落主旨匹配（第二段）。\n［解题思路］第二段先借具体事例指出“在与同事相处时不要刻意隐瞒自己看法”，再说明理由：“刻意隐瞒的人会失去他人信任，坦承自我的人会受到好评（will be appreciated）”；最后给出明确行动建议：面对是“主动说出个人细节”还是“刻意将其隐瞒”之时，要选择坦诚（put it on the table）。［E］Reveal, don\'t hide, information（吐露信息，不要隐瞒）精准概括全段主旨。\n［错项排除］其余干扰项（如［C］Tailor your interactions 对应末段“根据对象调整交流方式”、［F］Slow down and listen 对应第三段“学会倾听”）均偏离本段“坦诚相待、切勿藏私”的核心。' WHERE id = '82e47a1a-dad7-57e2-8c88-3b7454dc7b0d'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the most suitable subheading from [A]-[G] for paragraph [42].', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Give compliments, just not too many", "content": "Give compliments, just not too many"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Put on a good face, always", "content": "Put on a good face, always"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Tailor your interactions", "content": "Tailor your interactions"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Spend time with everyone", "content": "Spend time with everyone"}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "Reveal, don\'t hide, information", "content": "Reveal, don\'t hide, information"}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "Slow down and listen", "content": "Slow down and listen"}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "Put yourselves in others\' shoes", "content": "Put yourselves in others\' shoes"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'F', explanation = E'［定位/考点］段落主旨匹配（第三段）。\n［解题思路］第三段先指出“乐于倾听他人”与坦诚同等重要，再说明理由：“不耐心倾听同事看法、急于表达自己观点会被认为不尊重他人”；最后重申耐心倾听的重要性，鼓励读者与同事开展平等互动的谈话，而非将个人想法置于优先位置。［F］Slow down and listen（慢下来倾听）与本段主旨一致。\n［错项排除］［A］Give compliments, just not too many 虽复现段中 compliment，但本段仅在列举想表达的感受时随笔提及“赞美”，并未就赞美的“度”给出建议；［E］Reveal, don\'t hide, information 虽与段首 being honest 近义，但作者转折（but you need to... too）后的重心在于“倾听他人想法”。' WHERE id = '800d49e0-5cac-5087-94c4-53eef02beaf5'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the most suitable subheading from [A]-[G] for paragraph [43].', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Give compliments, just not too many", "content": "Give compliments, just not too many"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Put on a good face, always", "content": "Put on a good face, always"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Tailor your interactions", "content": "Tailor your interactions"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Spend time with everyone", "content": "Spend time with everyone"}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "Reveal, don\'t hide, information", "content": "Reveal, don\'t hide, information"}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "Slow down and listen", "content": "Slow down and listen"}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "Put yourselves in others\' shoes", "content": "Put yourselves in others\' shoes"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［定位/考点］段落主旨匹配（第四段）。\n［解题思路］第四段先从职场常态“每天只与固定两三位同事往来（talk to only two or three people）”切入，提出改进建议“拓宽交友圈、去了解周围所有人（get to know everyone around you）”，随后介绍具体做法“利用休息时间走动并结识不同同事”，并阐明这样做的好处——不仅能丰富工间休息时间，还能拓展公司内部人脉。［D］Spend time with everyone（花时间与所有人相处）精准契合该段主旨。\n［错项排除］干扰项如［C］Tailor your interactions 强调的是沟通风格因人而异地调整（对应末段），而［G］Put yourselves in others\' shoes 侧重换位思考，均未体现本段“主动走出小圈子、与每位同事多接触相处”的重点。' WHERE id = '67639d59-e844-5ed0-9af8-bb8b8840b6fb'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the most suitable subheading from [A]-[G] for paragraph [44].', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Give compliments, just not too many", "content": "Give compliments, just not too many"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Put on a good face, always", "content": "Put on a good face, always"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Tailor your interactions", "content": "Tailor your interactions"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Spend time with everyone", "content": "Spend time with everyone"}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "Reveal, don\'t hide, information", "content": "Reveal, don\'t hide, information"}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "Slow down and listen", "content": "Slow down and listen"}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "Put yourselves in others\' shoes", "content": "Put yourselves in others\' shoes"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［定位/考点］段落主旨匹配（第五段）。\n［解题思路］第五段先给出核心建议“对同事的出色工作给予积极反馈（positive feedback）”，随后说明益处“有助于引发他人的善意（engender good will）”并提醒误区“适可而止、不要过度或虚伪（don\'t overdo it or be fake about it）”，最后补充人们最容易接受的评价方式——起初为客观甚至略带负面的评价、随后转为真诚赞赏。［A］Give compliments, just not too many（给予他人赞美，但莫过多）精准概括本段主旨。\n［错项排除］［E］Reveal, don\'t hide, information 与②句“不要因为你不是老板就不跟人说”及④句“不要作假”疑似吻合，但原文强调的是具体的“既不要吝啬你的夸赞、也不要虚伪地夸赞”，而非泛泛地不要隐瞒客观信息。' WHERE id = 'fd190c2d-d5e3-58e4-a8fc-0b6c65808b10'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the most suitable subheading from [A]-[G] for paragraph [45].', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Give compliments, just not too many", "content": "Give compliments, just not too many"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Put on a good face, always", "content": "Put on a good face, always"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Tailor your interactions", "content": "Tailor your interactions"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Spend time with everyone", "content": "Spend time with everyone"}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "Reveal, don\'t hide, information", "content": "Reveal, don\'t hide, information"}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "Slow down and listen", "content": "Slow down and listen"}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "Put yourselves in others\' shoes", "content": "Put yourselves in others\' shoes"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［定位/考点］段落主旨匹配（第六段）。\n［解题思路］第六段建议读者留心所有同事喜欢或惯用的沟通方式（communication style），并在与他们互动交流时相应地调整自己的说话风格，使自己的互动方式与对方的偏好相契合。［C］Tailor your interactions（调整你的互动方式）与该段主旨完全一致。\n［错项排除］［G］Put yourselves in others\' shoes（站在他人的角度看问题）的干扰源自末句 Consider the person you will be interacting with in advance（预先考虑互动对象），但设身处地重在“理解他人立场或苦衷”，而本段预先考虑对方的目的是为了调整自身交流方式以匹配对方风格。' WHERE id = '8947e2e6-e3a2-58dc-9e94-c5b384b72e1e'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [1] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "therefore", "content": "therefore"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "however", "content": "however"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "again", "content": "again"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "moreover", "content": "moreover"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义逻辑。\n［解题思路］首句指出，设定目标并不难；空格句指出，______ ，认识到这些目标的负面影响要难得多。可见，两句存在语义反差（It\'s not difficult vs It is much harder）,空格词作为插入语应体现两句间的转折对比逻辑，[B] however符合要求。\n［错项排除］[A] therefore用于引出结果，[D] moreover表示递进关系，用于引出补充或支撑前一论述的新信息，但“认识目标设定的负面影响较难”并非“目标设定不难”导致的结果，也非对其的进一步补充说明或论证。[C] again用于表示“某事在发生之后再次发生”或“某事又回到过去的状态或地方”，例:You\'ll soon feel well again.（你很快就会康复的。）但①②句间不存在再次发生的事件或两个相同的状态/地点，故“再一次，返回原处”无从谈起。' WHERE id = 'a26d5e7d-e8b6-5b90-bfdb-0c7f89e6133b'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [2] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Emphasize", "content": "Emphasize"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Identify", "content": "Identify"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Assess", "content": "Assess"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Explain", "content": "Explain"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义+动词辨析。\n［解题思路］③④句指出，与工作相关的行为含有多个要素，______其中一个，其他就会变得扭曲。此两句与①②句“目标设定会带来不良影响”之间不存在任何显性关联词，表明两者间存在顺承关系，③④句“______一个会扭曲其他”应意在解释说明①②句“目标设定的不良影响”，空格词应该与“目标设定（想要达到的标准）”相关，指向“关注，聚焦，以……为目标/重点”等意，[A] Emphasize表示to give special importance to sth“重视”，“重视一个要素”即“将之设立为目标”，故正确。\n［错项排除］总体而言，“确认/评估/解释某一个要素”与“其他要素被扭曲”不存在因果关联（and暗藏因果关联），且其语义内涵与“目标设定”关系较远。具体来看，[B] Identify可表示“找到，找出”，例：First of all we must identify the problem areas.（首先我们必须找出问题所在。）但由上句可知，各个要素是“已知的、显现的”。[C] Assess指的是对人/物的性质、质量而非构成成分进行评定。[D] Explain重“介绍事物的细节或原因以使他人理解”，其解释的对象应该是“某种复杂难解的事物或行为等”，而one已经是“被分解的、不难理解的一个要素”。' WHERE id = 'f1b87586-83c0-568b-9347-c7b182bfb9f3'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [3] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "nearly", "content": "nearly"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "curiously", "content": "curiously"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "eagerly", "content": "eagerly"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "quickly", "content": "quickly"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义+副词辨析。\n［解题思路］空格句指出，乘坐伦敦的公交车出行，你就会______ 明白这（this回指上段末句“目标设定的消极影响：扭曲目标以外的要素”）是如何发生在司机身上的；结合上文“要理解目标设定的负面影响很难”以及下文“公交司机频繁闯红灯”可知，空格句意在引岀公交车司机频繁闯红灯的例子来形象展示“设定目标的危害”，空格词应重点传递这一示例作用的有效性，[D] quickly与see结合表示“快速明白/理解”，故正确。\n［错项排除］[A] nearly表程度，暗示“不能完全理解/明白”，与事例“公交司机频繁闯灯（负面语义赫然纸上）”的服务目的“让大家理解目标设定的不良影响”不符。[B] curiously.CC] eagerly均利用人物心理“人们在车上好奇/热切地看”捏造干扰，但此处see表示思维上的“理解/明白”，而非行为上的“看/张望”，故与“好奇地”“热切地”无法形成合理搭配。\n［选项释义与词汇辨析］\n[A] nearly: 几乎；将近\n[B] curiously: 好奇地\n[C] eagerly: 热切地\n[D] quickly: 迅速地；很快地' WHERE id = '3ad2ea30-6be2-5a07-80de-eb1149460673'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [4] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "claim", "content": "claim"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "prove", "content": "prove"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "check", "content": "check"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "recall", "content": "recall"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义+动词辨析。\n［解题思路］空格句提出问题，有检票员_______人们已经付钱了吗？空格词的逻辑主语为inspectors,宾语为具体的情况that people have paid;故空格词应表示公交车上检票员的动作行为，结合常识不难判断空格词应表示"检查，核实，核查"等，[C] check可表示to find out if sth/sb is correct or true “查明，核实”,“核实人们是否购票”与检票员的职责对应，故正确。\n［错项排除］[A] claim可表示"索取；索要"，后应接费用、利益等，如claim unemployment benefit（申领失业救济金），而本句中空格词的宾语为“人们是否已经付款/买票”这一具体情况，语义上无法搭配。[B] prove表示“（用证据、论据）证明某事属实”，[D] recall后接宾语从句时表示“回想起某事”，但检票员的职责是“核实/确保”而非“证明/回想起”乘客已经付钱（应该是“乘客”而非“检票员”用证据证明自己已经付钱，也只有“乘客”自己才能想起自己已经付钱）。\n［选项释义与词汇辨析］\n[A] claim: 宣称；要求；索要\n[B] prove: 证明；证实\n[D] recall: 记起；使想起\n[C] check: 可表示to find out if sth/sb is correct or' WHERE id = '092e0dd4-0c63-5eec-b16c-574a15777889'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [5] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "threatened", "content": "threatened"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "ignored", "content": "ignored"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "mocked", "content": "mocked"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "blamed", "content": "blamed"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义+动词辨析。\n［解题思路］空格句前句提出问题：那些跑着追赶公交的人怎么样了？空格句作出回答：他们被______ 。结合空格上下文“公交车上无人查票，司机频繁闯红灯”可知本句应在讲述公交（司机）对待“追赶着想要赶上车的人”的态度，[B] ignored有“佯装未见，不予理睬”之意，契合上下文语境“对乘客是否购票无视，对路上车辆行人/车上乘客安全无视”，故正确。结合第四段③句“人们抱怨车辆晚点”亦可佐证“司机为赶时间会忽略那些还在跑着追赶公交的人”。\n［错项排除］[A]、[C]、[D]均利用常规思维“某些人（其他乘客、路人）会威胁/嘲笑/责怪那些跑着追赶公交车的人”设障，但都无法契合上下文“无人查票、频繁闯灯、人们抱怨晚点”所传递的“司机为争抢时间而无视收益、无视安全、无视乘客上车的需求”。\n［选项释义与词汇辨析］\n[A] threatened: 威胁；恐吓\n[B] ignored: 忽视；不予理睬\n[D] blamed: 责怪；指责' WHERE id = '12660896-40da-50b3-b953-2190fa29754b'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [6] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "punctuality", "content": "punctuality"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "hospitality", "content": "hospitality"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "competition", "content": "competition"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "innovation", "content": "innovation"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义+名词辨析。\n［解题思路］空格句指出原因：因为目标是______ 。结合空格上文所述伦敦公交的状况“不查车票、不顾追赶公交的人、频繁闯红灯”以及下文“人们抱怨公交车晚点”“司机们根据其行程所用时间……或受到惩罚"可知，此目标应与"时间"有关,[A] punctuality表示the fact or quality of being on time,符合上下文语义逻辑。\n［错项排除］[B] hospitality强调“对他人友好、热情的态度”，与上段公交车对跑着追赶公交之人的态度“视而不见”正好相悖。[C] competition强调的是“团队内部成员之间的争抢/争夺”，而上下文并未涉及到“司机之间的竞争”，故排除。[D] innovation由“增加公交车和公交车专用道”捏造而来，但由人们的抱怨及司机受罚的原因可知，这些措施的目的是“保证公交车的速度和班次”，与“创新”无关。\n［选项释义与词汇辨析］\n[A] punctuality: 准时；守时\n[B] hospitality: 殷勤好客；款待\n[C] competition: 竞争；比赛\n[D] innovation: 创新；新思想' WHERE id = '9b16c695-7606-55da-883b-cef9f69f600d'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [7] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Yet", "content": "Yet"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "So", "content": "So"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Besides", "content": "Besides"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Still", "content": "Still"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义逻辑。\n［解题思路］空格句前句介绍人们对公交车的抱怨“晚点、班次少”;空格句介绍与公交车有关的措施“增加公交车和公交车道的数量，依据司机的行程时间对其……或惩罚”，可见这些措施是为了解决公交车“晚点、班次少”的问题,人们的抱怨是“因”，相关措施是“果”，空格词应体现因果关系，[B] So 正确。\n［错项排除］[A] Yet、[D] Still置于句首时都有转折意味（despite what has just been said）,表示“不过，可是（用在先前说过的内容之后，引出令人惊讶的事实或情况）"，例：The weather was cold and wet. Still, we had a great time.（天气又冷又潮，不过我们仍旧玩得很开心。）但相应整改措施（增加公交车（道）的数量、依据行程时间惩罚）于公众抱怨（晚点、班次少）而言并没有令人惊讶/转折之处。[C] Besides 作副词时，可表示"此外"，常置于句尾，例：I\'m capable of doing the work, and a lot more besides.（我有能力做这工作，除此之外，还可以干更多的事。）besides还可表示“而且”，用于补充一个想法或解释，例：I don\'t really want to go. Besides, it\'s too late now.（我并不真的想去，而且现在太晚了。）上述两义项中besides呈递的是一种并列或递进关联，而“公交系统的应对措施”与“公众抱怨”并非并列/递进关系，而是因果关系。\n［选项释义与词汇辨析］\n[A] Yet: 然而；已经；还\n[B] So: 所以；因此\n[C] Besides: 此外；而且\n[D] Still: 还；仍然；不过' WHERE id = '5993a341-70b7-51d0-bcfb-1c3daf83d5be'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [8] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "hired", "content": "hired"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "trained", "content": "trained"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "rewarded", "content": "rewarded"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "grouped", "content": "grouped"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义+动词辨析。\n［解题思路］空格句指出，司机们根据其行程所用时间______ 或受到惩罚（_________or punished）。由上句分析可知，这一措施有助于解决“公交车晚点”的问题，即“根据其行程所用时间对司机进行______或惩罚”有利于提高准点率，空格词应与punished语义相对或类似，[C] rewarded表示“奖励，奖赏”，可有效激励司机提高准点率，故正确。\n［错项排除］[A]、[B]、[D]均无法与空格句中or“（用以引出另一种可能性）或，或者，还是”所呈递出的“并列语义（即与受罚相并列的另一种可能性）”契合，故排除。\n［选项释义与词汇辨析］\n[D] grouped: （使）成群，成组' WHERE id = '72642469-9506-5ee8-a2e7-f24c61b63e9a'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [9] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "only", "content": "only"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "rather", "content": "rather"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "once", "content": "once"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "also", "content": "also"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］ 上下文语义+副词辨析。\n［解题思路］ 前一句指出“司机们达到了（准时的）指标（And drivers hit these targets.）”，紧接着用 But 进行语意转折/补充：“但他们____撞到了骑行者（But they [9] hit cyclists.）”。此处呼应前文“只追求单一指标会产生负面后果”，且连用两个 hit（hit these targets / hit cyclists）形成强烈对比：司机们既完成了准点指标，同时也撞到了骑车人，因此填入 [D] also（也）最贴合句意与语境。\n［错项排除］ [A] only（仅仅）代入后意为“但他们只撞了骑行者”，违背常识与上下文（司机既达成了准点目标，又引发了撞人后果）；[B] rather（反而，相当）若表“反而”通常需与否定结构或 rather than 搭配，置于主谓之间不合此处递进/双关语义；[C] once（曾经，一旦）强调时间上的过去或条件，与全文一般过去时态下并列发生的客观后果不符。\n［选项释义与词汇辨析］\n[A] only: 仅仅；只有\n[B] rather: 相当；反而；宁愿\n[C] once: 曾经；一旦\n[D] also: 也；同样' WHERE id = '9132fb0c-485b-5046-8e9a-c0f9e97a3207'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [10] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "comfort", "content": "comfort"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "revenue", "content": "revenue"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "efficiency", "content": "efficiency"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "security", "content": "security"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］条件关系+句内语义。\n［解题思路］空格句指出，如果目标变成了______ ，就会有更多的检票员，定价也会更加灵活。“更多检票员”“更灵活的定价”均与公交收费有关，空格词应传递“票价、金钱、收益”等含义才可与之构成“条件一结果”关联，[B] revenue可表示“（公司、组织或政府的）收入”，正确。\n［错项排除］均利用常规思维“公共交通应舒适、高效、安全”设障，但均无法契合主句所示语境“公交费用”，无法与更多检票员、更灵活定价构成“条件一结果”关联。\n［选项释义与词汇辨析］\n[A] comfort: 舒适；安慰\n[B] revenue: 收益；收入\n[C] efficiency: 效率；功效\n[D] security: 安全工作；保护措施' WHERE id = '97e4cac3-1657-5a50-b5ff-a24cdbb81f5a'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [11] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "friendly", "content": "friendly"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "quiet", "content": "quiet"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "cautious", "content": "cautious"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "diligent", "content": "diligent"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］条件关系+句内语义。\n［解题思路］空格句指出，如果标准变成了安全，就会有更多______司机，他们会遵守交通法规。________ drivers 一方面是条件从句“标准变成了安全”带来的结果，另一方面应该与drivers的定语从句who obeyed traffic laws的语义指向一致，[C] cautious表示being careful about what you say or do, especially to avoid danger"小心谨慎的"，符合上述两项条件。\n［错项排除］均利用常规思维“公交车司机友好、稳重、勤奋”设障，但均无法契合条件句所传递的语境“安全”，不能与“将安全作为标准”构成“条件一结果”关联。' WHERE id = '5f1e3abf-eff1-5fef-a043-98d76cbf290c'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [12] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "purpose", "content": "purpose"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "problem", "content": "problem"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "prejudice", "content": "prejudice"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "policy", "content": "policy"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］段际逻辑+名词词义辨析。\n［解题思路］空格句指出，还存在另一个______。而上文伦敦公交示例“为了实现准时，对收益、对安全、对意欲乘车的顾客熟视无睹；而如若将目标设置为安全或收益，又无法做到准时”意在说明首段所提出的“设定目标的负面影响：使得目标以外的要素受到扭曲”，此处应接续介绍目标设定的另一负面影响（another________ ），且由本段末句“一个小时的航程现在号称需要两小时”所传递出的贬义色彩也能感知此空格应表“问题，负面影响”等，[B] problem正确。\n［错项排除］从总体语义导向看，[A]、[D]均为中性（偏正面）语义，与段间并列逻辑矛盾。具体而言，[A] purpose表示抽象的"意义"时指"人生或生活的意义/目的感"，例:Volunteer work gives her life（a sense of） purpose.（做志愿工作使她的生活有了意义。） [D] policy可指"宏观政治或经济上的政策、方针"，也可指"某种行事的原则",例：Honesty is the best policy.（诚实为上。）但空格后"人们（已经）变得极具创意”强调的是一种已然发生的事态变化，并非指向常态性的生活目标、行事原则，故均排除。[C] prejudice虽为负面语义，但着力强调的是一种负面态度/看法，也无法与空格后所述事实“事态变化”相契合。' WHERE id = '034097dd-7d68-595d-91b8-2e95a202613d'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [13] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "reported", "content": "reported"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "revealed", "content": "revealed"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "admitted", "content": "admitted"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "noticed", "content": "noticed"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义+动词辨析。\n［解题思路］空格句提出问题：你有没有______“你的航班延误一小时起飞，却仍能准时到达”？空格词应传递出主语“以你/读者为代表的普通大众”与反常事件“航班延误一小时起飞却仍按时着陆”之间的观察关联，表示“注意到、察觉到”，故选［D］noticed。\n［错项排除］［A］reported（报告、报道）通常指告知上级或公众；［B］revealed（透露、揭示）侧重使人得知原本不为人知的内幕，二者均涉及多个信息传递主体，而空格句前后是同一主体（you）的日常察觉；［C］admitted（承认）多指勉强承认自己不好或不快之事，但航班延误后仍准时到达的行为施动者是航空公司而非乘客。' WHERE id = '31641190-67ab-5b54-b822-ae98fff34967'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [14] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "break", "content": "break"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "trip", "content": "trip"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "departure", "content": "departure"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "transfer", "content": "transfer"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］ 上下文语义+名词辨析。\n［解题思路］ 空格句指出，航空公司只是修改了一下_______所需的时间。后一句具体介绍航空公司如何修改时间：一小时的航程被号称为两小时（one-hour flight -> two-hour flight）。可见，航空公司修改的是“一趟航行/航程（flight）”所需的时间，空格词应与flight近义，[B] trip表示“出行，旅行”，正确。\n［错项排除］ 分别利用航班的“经停/起飞/中转”时间捏造干扰，但由one-hour flight -> two-hour flight可知，航空公司修改的不是旅程中间某一阶段所花费的时间，而是整个旅程总共耗费的时间；另外，departure time指航班起飞的时间点，与is meant to take（时间段）无法搭配。' WHERE id = 'c6a77b93-0fb9-5d68-8286-670e3ea2e381'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [15] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "moral", "content": "moral"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "background", "content": "background"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "style", "content": "style"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "form", "content": "form"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］ 上下文语义+名词辨析。\n［解题思路］ 空格句指出：这个故事的______很简单（The [15] of the story is simple.）。空格句下文指出：大部分工作都有多个维度、多个标准，选择一个标准，很可能就要以其他标准为代价。两者之间为顺承阐释关系，可见“工作有多个维度、多个标准，顾此失彼”正是上文伦敦公交与航空公司事例所传递的深层道理与教训，[A] moral（寓意，教益）符合文意。\n［错项排除］ [B] background（背景）、[C] style（风格）、[D] form（形式）均利用常见搭配设障，但若说“故事的背景/风格/形式简单”，下文应围绕背景、风格或形式展开，无法引出“大多数工作是多维度的”这一规律性启示。' WHERE id = '965beb77-0bca-58e4-b4ad-b8be426a95b4'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [16] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "interpret", "content": "interpret"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "criticize", "content": "criticize"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "sacrifice", "content": "sacrifice"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "tolerate", "content": "tolerate"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义+动词辨析。\n［解题思路］空格句指出：选择一个工作标准，那么就很可能______ 其他标准。就空格句内部而言,and you may well...传递的是Choose one criterion的结果，根据常识"选择一个意味着舍弃其他"可锁定[C]。就上文语境而言，首段指出“与工作相关的行为含有多个要素，重视一个，其他要素就会扭曲”，第二、三段列举公交车示例“当目标设定为准时时，收益、安全等就会被忽略；当目标设为安全或收益时，准时就无法保证”，整体语境表明空格词应表“损害，放弃，扭曲”等贬义词，[C] sacrifice正确。\n［错项排除］总体而言，[A] interpret"领会”、［D］ tolerate“容忍”均不符合空格词的贬义语义指向。具体来看，[A] interpret表示"把 理解为 "或"以某种方式解读"，常用interpret sth as sth结构，[D] tolerate暗示宾语为“不同意、不喜欢或难以接受之事”，但是“解读其他标准”“容忍其他标准”均无法与空格前Choose one"选择一个标准"形成因果关联（and. . . may well表结果/因果）。[B] criticize虽为消极语义指向，但空格句中Choose. . . and you may well并不蕴藏"赞扬vs批评"的语意。\n［选项释义与词汇辨析］\n[A] interpret: 诠释；领会；口译\n[B] criticize: 批评；批判\n[C] sacrifice: 牺牲；舍弃\n[D] tolerate: 容许；忍受' WHERE id = '65044aa0-10ae-5bc5-8f34-9927ec3334cb'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [17] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "task", "content": "task"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "secret", "content": "secret"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "product", "content": "product"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "cost", "content": "cost"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］ 上下文语义+句内语义+名词辨析。\n［解题思路］ 空格句指出：所有事都能以更快的速度、更低的价格完成，但是有______（but there is a [17]）。空格句内部，but 标示语义转折，空格词应指向与 faster, cheaper 相反的负面代价，锁定具有负面语义的 [D]。结合上句“选择一个标准就会以其他标准为代价（at the expense of others）”及下句 negative consequences，[D] cost 表示“代价，损失”，完全符合这一语义逻辑。\n［错项排除］ [A] task（任务）、[B] secret（秘密）、[C] product（产物）均无法契合空格前后 but、negative consequences 所渲染的负面代价含义。' WHERE id = '71c28b7c-0ad1-5ebf-999c-f92de5dc3a4a'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [18] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "leading to", "content": "leading to"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "calling for", "content": "calling for"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "relating to", "content": "relating to"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "accounting for", "content": "accounting for"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］ 句内语义+动词词组辨析。\n［解题思路］ 空格句介绍好的目标的要求：应该要有多个标准______如时间、金钱、质量、顾客反馈等关键因素。根据上文公交车示例“以时间（标准）为目标时，金钱、顾客反馈、质量等（标准）会遭到忽视，以金钱、顾客反馈等（标准）为目标时，时间（标准）会受到忽略”可知空格词后“时间、金钱、质量、顾客反馈等关键因素”同空格词前“标准”语义指向一致，属上下义关联，[C] relating to符合文意。\n［错项排除］ [A] leading to可用于表示结果，强调的是因果关联；[B] calling for指向的是需求关联；[D] accounting for可用于表示原因，同样传递因果关联，均与句内“指向一致，上下义关联”不符。' WHERE id = '0f355053-7cba-5350-9435-a91c01657c03'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [19] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "specify", "content": "specify"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "predict", "content": "predict"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "restore", "content": "restore"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "create", "content": "create"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义+动词辨析。\n［解题思路］空格句介绍设立好的目标的窍门：不仅要______ 目标的一两个维度，还要了解如何帮助人们更好地……目标。结合上文“好的目标需要有多个标准集成”可知设定一个好的目标首先必须符合“多个标准集成/选择多个标准”这一先决条件，空格词应表“设定，指定，规定，选择，选取”等，[A] specify 表示 to state sth explicitly or in detail,符合语义逻辑。\n［错项排除］[B] predict"预测”暗示“目标维度目前尚未出现”,[C] restore恢复”暗示“目标维度已经遭到破坏”，［D］ create表示“创造”时强调“从无到有”，暗示“目标维度并不存在”，而上文已提及“大部分工作都有多个维度和标准”，且并未提及“目标维度遭受破坏”的相关信息，故此三项均不符合上下文语义逻辑。' WHERE id = '656deb9a-05d5-5a2d-8e13-8b0c0a5b06d5'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [20] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "modify", "content": "modify"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "review", "content": "review"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "present", "content": "present"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "achieve", "content": "achieve"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］ 句内语义+动词辨析。\n［解题思路］ 空格句以not only... but also呈现递进关系：不仅要指定目标的一两个维度，还要了解如何帮助人们更好地______目标。空格词应体现对“设立目标”的递进，[D] achieve表示“实现”，从“确立目标”到“实现目标”不仅体现了not only... but also...的递进关系，也充分表现了trick（a way of doing sth that works well）的内在含义。此外，结合本段首两句“探讨目标的后果”可知，本句应关注“目标的实现”。\n［错项排除］ [A] modify、[B] review均体现了对前述目标的“不赞同、不认可”，且动作发出者应该指向“目标设定者”，这与空格句中所示动作发出者people“目标执行者”不符（文首句明确指出“企业设定目标，员工去实现目标”）。[C] present表示to show or describe sth/sb in a particular way“展现，表现”，但“设立目标”与“展现目标”之间并没有明显的语义递进，也无法体现trick的“智慧方法”之意。' WHERE id = '92c11f06-06ae-5b26-b191-4284e38554ef'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Research by the World Economic Forum suggests ________.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "an increase in full-time employment", "content": "an increase in full-time employment"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "an urgent demand for new job skills", "content": "an urgent demand for new job skills"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "a steady growth of job opportunities", "content": "a steady growth of job opportunities"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "a controversy about the \\"core skills\\"", "content": "a controversy about the \\"core skills\\""}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干关键词Research by the World Economic Forum定位至首段③句，该句介绍世界经济论坛的研究发现：到2022年，各类职业中平均42%的“核心技能”将发生变化。这一研究发现支撑了②句“工作岗位的技能需求将迅速发生变化”这一时代趋势。结合末句“到2022年是非常短的时间”可知，未来的工作岗位迫切需要新的工作技能，［B］正确。\n［命题解密］正确项［B］中 demand for new job skills 是对③句 "core skills" within job roles will change 和②句 the jobs in demand will change rapidly 的同义转述，urgent 对应末句 a very short timeline。\n［A］利用首段①句a lot of would-be workers设置干扰，将我们对未来的期望“潜在劳动力不被大量抛弃”误解为“全职就业岗位将增多”，但原文并未涉及“全职工作”这一话题。［C］利用②句the jobs in demand will change rapidly设置干扰，但文中the jobs in demand实指“社会所需的工作（技能）”而非“社会提供的工作机会”，且“迅速变化”不意味着“稳步增长”。［D］由③句“平均42%的核心技能将发生变化”主观臆断出“核心技能存在争议”，但文中并未提及人们对核心技能的不同看法。\n［技巧总结］本题为事实细节题，解题关键在于准确锁定关键词。如本题，根据题干可定位至首段③句，其内容是“到2022年，各类职业中42%的核心技能将发生变化”，关键词是core skills和change。“工作的核心技能发生变化”也即“需要新的工作技能”，浏览四个选项可轻松锁定［B］。而并未涉及“工作技能”，［D］虽触及“工作（核心）技能”，但“争议”在文中并未提及。' WHERE id = '9de58b50-9efc-5fc5-aeaf-cc2db9a08723'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Some people argue that food self-sufficiency in the UK would ________.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "be hindered by its population growth", "content": "be hindered by its population growth"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "contribute to the nation\'s well-being", "content": "contribute to the nation\'s well-being"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "become a priority of the government", "content": "become a priority of the government"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "pose a challenge to its farming industry", "content": "pose a challenge to its farming industry"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干观点持有者 Some people 及关键词 food self-sufficiency in the UK 定位至第二段。该段①③句指出，一些人将脱欧视为扭转英国粮食大量依赖进口局面的契机，认为恢复自给自足将促进本国农业发展、加强政治主权，甚至提升国民健康水平（boost the nation\'s health），故［B］contribute to the nation\'s well-being 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］利用首段“全球人口预计逼近 100 亿加剧粮食危机”跨段捏造关联，原文未称人口增长阻碍英国粮食自给；［C］利用③句 political sovereignty 偷换概念，将自给自足带来的益处曲解为“已成为政府首要事项”；［D］利用③句 the farming industry 反向干扰，将“促进农业发展”曲解为“对农业构成挑战”。' WHERE id = '0715c893-3ad4-5307-9cb0-795e2d8879a1'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'What is true about Wunderlist and Sunrise after their acquisitions?', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Their engineers were retained.", "content": "Their engineers were retained."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Their market values declined.", "content": "Their market values declined."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Their tech features improved.", "content": "Their tech features improved."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Their products were re-priced.", "content": "Their products were re-priced."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［精准定位］由after their acquisitions定位至第二段首句中later。该段指出Wunderlist与Sunrise被收购后的情况：软件被下架（①句），工程师被留用（②句），故[A]正确。\n［命题解密］[A] Their engineers were retained 同义改写第二段②句 Their... engineers stayed on。[B]源于第六段①句their... market value，但此处谈论的是“五大科技巨头的市场价值巨大”而非“Wunderlist与Sunrise的市场价值下滑”。[C]张冠李戴：由第二段①句“微软将它们的最佳性能融入自身产品”，可知科技性能得到提升的对象为微软自家产品而非被收购的两款应用。[D]利用首段①句“微软收购两款软件”与常识“换东家后会重新定价”捏造，但“重新定价”所含的信息“仍在市场上销售”与第二段①句所含的信息“被下架”相悖。\n［技巧总结］四个选项的指向性很明确、辨识度也很高，对于此类事实细节题按照“回文定位法”最为合适。根据题干Wunderlist and Sunrise after their acquisitions直接定位至第二段，该段两句成段，第一句指向“软件的命运（下架）”，第二句指向“软件工程师的命运（留用）”，与之相匹配的唯有[A]，其余各选项要么捏造，要么偷换概念。' WHERE id = 'b1b41992-d881-5a0c-a552-8d64ad1da8a1'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Microsoft\'s critics believe that the big tech companies tend to ________.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "exaggerate their product quality", "content": "exaggerate their product quality"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "eliminate their potential competitors", "content": "eliminate their potential competitors"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "treat new tech talent unfairly", "content": "treat new tech talent unfairly"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "ignore public opinions", "content": "ignore public opinions"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［精准定位］由题干Microsoft\'s critics与big tech companies直接定位至第三段。该段①句点明批评者的总观点：科技巨头会蚕食挡道的创新公司。②句具体阐释①句：他们（科技巨头）将那些有朝一日可能会成长为竞争对手的企业扼杀于摇篮。可见［B］正确。\n［命题解密］［B］eliminate their potential competitors同义概述了第三段②句的putting an end to businesses that might one day turn into competitors，阐明了①句中chew up any innovative companies that lie in their path的内涵。\n［A］对第二段①句said... best features in its own products断章取义，将文意“表示自家产品借鉴了被购软件的最佳性能”曲解为“夸耀自家产品最佳，夸大产品质量”，且将微软个体的行为泛化为所有大型科技公司的行为。［C］歪曲第二段②句中大型科技公司对科技人才的态度：将原文的“求贤若渴（their great hunger for tech talent）”反向窜改为“不公正对待人才（treat... unfairly）”。［D］将第三段末句declined to comment所暗藏的“礼貌拒绝置评（decline：refuse politely to do sth）”窜改为“忽略（ignore: pay no attention to sth）”。此外，［A］［C］［D］均为作者陈述的事实，并非题干所问的“批评者的观点”。\n［技巧总结］本题考查人物观点，解答关键是锁定人物观点表达句。首先根据Microsoft\'s critics直接锁定第三段①句，该句中a remorseless drive by Big Tech to chew up any innovative companies that lie in their path明确表达科技巨头的倾向性行为（蚕食将阻碍其发展的任何创新公司），与之相匹配的唯有［B］。' WHERE id = '7e5b233b-770c-546d-8053-ad723aeca1b4'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Paul Arnold is concerned that small acquisitions might ________.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "weaken big tech companies", "content": "weaken big tech companies"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "worsen market competition", "content": "worsen market competition"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "harm the national economy", "content": "harm the national economy"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "discourage start-up investors", "content": "discourage start-up investors"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［精准定位］首先由题干中Paul Arnold定位至第三、四段，再由试题命制顺序（上题已针对第三段设题）可进一步定位至第四段。该段首先指出，对于“科技巨头收购初创企业”，阿诺德内心五味杂陈。随后点明其担忧的原因：这种小额收购可能会危害美国经济。可见，［C］正确。\n［命题解密］题干+［C］是对第四段③句疑问句式But are they good for the American economy?的正确解读，harm体现了阿诺德的质疑态度：这类收购可能不利于美国经济。\n［A］［B］均与第三段②句阿诺德的观点“科技巨头在初创企业发展为竞争者之前将其消灭”的言外之意相悖：这些小额收购不是削弱而是巩固大型科技公司现有的地位；不是加剧市场竞争，而是阻碍新竞争对手产生、保持市场竞争的现状。［D］与第四段②句阿诺德的观点“这些小额收购有利于我（阿诺德代表初创企业投资者）”所体现的积极意义相悖。\n［技巧总结］本题依然考查人物观点，但解答关键更在于利用人物站位排除部分干扰项，然后再借助其核心观点句锁定正确选项。首先，文中Paul Arnold作为微软批评者的代表人物出现，对微软所代表的做法“科技巨头在初创企业成长为竞争对手前将其收购（巩固科技巨头的垄断地位，杜绝新的市场竞争产生）”持反对态度，应首先排除［A］［B］。接着，根据题干中concerned所传递出的“疑虑，担忧”锁定到第四段中情感表达词mixed feelings以及疑问句式are they good for the American economy?所传递出的“对美国经济的担忧”，从而锁定正确答案为［C］。' WHERE id = '61dffdef-540d-519c-8a2f-955ca2259750'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The US Federal Trade Commission intends to ________.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "limit Big Tech\'s expansion", "content": "limit Big Tech\'s expansion"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "encourage research collaboration", "content": "encourage research collaboration"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "examine small acquisitions", "content": "examine small acquisitions"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "supervise start-ups\' operation", "content": "supervise start-ups\' operation"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干关键词Federal Trade Commission定位至第五段。该段①②句指出，FTC为了找到“科技巨头收购初创企业是否对美国经济不利”的答案，要求“五大科技公司提供其过去十年所进行的所有小额收购的相关信息”。可见，FTC意欲审查科技巨头小额收购行为，以防对美国经济不利，［C］正确。\n［命题解密］［C］是对②句中asked... for information about their many small acquisitions的同义转述。\n［A］由②③句中“要求提供”和“插手干预”等信息过度推导得来，文中无据可依。［B］对③句only a research project（只是一个研究项目）断章取义，但句中实际指向“FTC目前尚处研究调查阶段，尚未上升到政策措施等高度”，并未提及“政府要鼓励合作式研究”。［D］将③句“干预早期科技市场”错误理解为监管初创企业，句中实际指向“监督科技巨头对初创企业的收购”。\n［技巧总结］本题考查FTC的行为目的，可搜寻文内有关目的的表达词，找到答案信息，即根据第五段①句中wants to可锁定其后find the answer to that question，而追溯前文发现that question指向上段末句are they good for the American economy（they指向these things/selling start-ups to larger tech companies，进而可知small acquisitions），进而可知FTC意在调查“小额收购对美国经济的影响”，与之相匹配的唯有［C］，且由目标句（①句）后的解释说明句（②句）“FTC开始要求五大科技巨头提供其过去十年来的小额收购信息”可进一步佐证。' WHERE id = 'f87d3744-d72c-5734-b5ca-1c48275796dd'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'For the five biggest tech companies, their small acquisitions have ________.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "brought little financial pressure", "content": "brought little financial pressure"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "raised few management challenges", "content": "raised few management challenges"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "set an example for future deals", "content": "set an example for future deals"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "generated considerable profits", "content": "generated considerable profits"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题目关键词the five biggest tech companies可定位至第六段②句。该句表明，五大公司加起来每年用于小额收购的资金仅有34亿美元，同它们的金融储备相比，这笔钱无异于沧海一粟。再加上具体数字（3.4 billion vs 130 billion）的对比可知，五大公司财力雄厚，这些小额收购并未对公司财政造成多少压力，故［A］正确。\n［命题解密］［A］是对第六段②句中only $3.4 billion a year, a drop in the ocean compared with their massive financial reserves的合理推断。\n［B］由常识“公司并购之后带来的人员增长将会是一个管理问题”捏造，但文中并未提到任何“管理问题”。［C］由第三段②句中examples, in their path望文生义，但该句实质指向“微软收购Wunderlist/Sunrise是科技巨头收购初创企业的众多案例中的两例”而非“为这类收购树立了榜样”。［D］则将五大公司的巨额利润归功于他们所进行的小额收购，而文中并没有出现相应的因果联系。\n［技巧总结］本题考查“小型收购对科技巨头”的影响，实质于长难句处设题，意在考查学生明确复杂关系、了解特殊修辞、理解长难句的能力，解答关键在分解长难句主体，明确其语义要点。第六段②句主体信息实为the five biggest tech companies（主语）have spent an average of only $3.4 billion a year（谓语部分）— a drop in the ocean compared with their massive financial reserves...（同位语）。根据其中的情感表达词only、a drop in the ocean、massive不难锁定正确项为［A］。' WHERE id = '692404a8-e232-5be9-aa4d-99c14e37d0df'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Nalini Ambady\'s study deals with ________.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "the power of people\'s memory", "content": "the power of people\'s memory"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "the reliability of first impressions", "content": "the reliability of first impressions"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "instructor-student interaction", "content": "instructor-student interaction"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "people\'s ability to influence others", "content": "people\'s ability to influence others"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［精准定位］由题干中的Nalini Ambady\'s study定位至第一、二段安巴迪的“行为薄片撷取”能力研究。第一段①句指出人们擅长通过第一印象即thin slices of experience评判他人，②句顺而指出安巴迪就thin slicing这一能力进行了研究，说明安巴迪的研究与人们的第一印象有关。再结合第一段③⑤句、第二段②句所指出的“安巴迪将参与者和学生对教师的评分进行对比，评估参与者对教师的第一印象的准确性”，可知安巴迪的研究涉及“第一印象的可靠性”，故［B］正确。\n［命题解密］正确项［B］是对第一、二段中安巴迪的研究内容的正确概述，其中first impressions对应主题词first impressions、thin slices of experience，reliability是对correlated strongly、just as accurate、Accuracy dropped dramatically的高度概括。\n［A］将第一段④句中对参与者的干扰occupying their conscious working memory断章取义为安巴迪的研究涉及人们的记忆，但原文并未提及记忆的力量。［C］对第一段②③句中的关键信息professors, instructor, students强加关联，捏造出安巴迪的研究涉及“教师与学生的互动”。［D］将第二段①②句中“参与者被要求写下评分理由，导致他们的评分准确性大幅下降”这一研究发现错误解读为“研究人员影响了参与者的判断”，而原文的真实含义是“写出评分理由”这一思考行为降低了评分的准确性。\n［技巧总结］本题考察对细节信息进行整合概括的能力，解题时需要厘清段内、段际逻辑关系。1. 从段内逻辑来看，第一段①句指出第一印象即“经验薄片（thin slices of experience）”，②句直接说明安巴迪的研究关乎“行为薄片撷取（thin slicing）”，从两者的重合内容thin slice可推断安巴迪的研究关乎“第一印象”。另外，第一段②③句和④⑤句呈现相似的句间关系：先说明参与者在不同条件下根据第一印象对教师评分，后描述该评分的准确性。这也说明安巴迪的研究重点是“第一印象的准确性”，由此锁定答案［B］。2. 从段际逻辑来看，第一、二段都涉及安巴迪的研究，但两段之间构成对比关系：第一段的前两组参与者情况表明，当参与者根据第一印象评分时，评分结果往往非常准确；而第二段的第三组参与者（①②句）和另一项研究（④句）表明，过多思考反而会干扰我们判断的准确性。将两段逻辑串联可知，这两段的两项研究都在论证首段首句：我们很擅长运用第一印象来评判他人，此时深思不仅没有必要，而且会造成干扰。由此，进一步锁定答案［B］。［A］［C］［D］均运用各项研究对参与者的不同要求捏造干扰，可排除。' WHERE id = 'a4cecf1e-4483-52c2-9695-8c6f0dfef0d0'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'In Ambady\'s study, rating accuracy dropped when participants ________.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "focused on specific details", "content": "focused on specific details"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "gave the rating in limited time", "content": "gave the rating in limited time"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "watched shorter video clips", "content": "watched shorter video clips"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "discussed with one another", "content": "discussed with one another"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干关键词Ambady\'s study和rating accuracy dropped定位至第二段②句。梳理上下文逻辑可知，①句指出导致评分准确率下降的直接原因是“参与者需写下评分原因”，③句中安巴迪推测出现这一结果是因为“deliberation focused them on vivid but misleading cues（深思使他们将精力集中于那些生动但具有误导性的信号）”，其中focused them on vivid but misleading cues表明参与者将注意力放在了具体细节上，对应［A］选项中focused on specific details，因此［A］正确。\n［命题解密］正确项［A］是对第二段③句安巴迪对实验结果的解读deliberation focused them on vivid... cues的同义改写。\n［B］将第二段①句中的spend a minute writing down their reasons误当作对评分时间的限制，实际上这是对参与者写下评分理由的时间限制，且该限制也并非评分准确性下降的原因。［C］根据第一段②句中的10-second video clips和第二段④句中的15-second clips臆断出视频的时长影响了评分的准确性，实际上视频的时长并非研究重点。［D］由第一段④句的Another set和第二段①句的another group错误推断出one another，在此基础上捏造出“参与者需相互讨论，给出评分”，原文并未涉及相关描述。\n［技巧总结］因果细节题主要考查对上下文因果逻辑的把握，需要正确梳理句间逻辑。如本题，第二段①句描述评分条件：参与者需要写出评分理由；②句描述评分结果：此时评分准确性下降；③句介绍安巴迪分析的原因：参与者为写出理由而进行了深思（deliberation），深思时只关注生动的细节信息，忽略了整体印象。浏览选项后可锁定［A］选项为对评分下降原因的正确描述，其他三个选项均属主观臆断，可排除。' WHERE id = '0f748cfe-7908-5174-8921-5c33d76455d1'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Judith Hall mentions driving to show that ________.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "reflection can be distracting", "content": "reflection can be distracting"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "memory may be selective", "content": "memory may be selective"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "social skills must be cultivated", "content": "social skills must be cultivated"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "deception is difficult to detect", "content": "deception is difficult to detect"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［精准定位］由题干中的人名Judith Hall与关键词driving定位至第三段②③句。朱迪斯•霍尔称，若一个人开着手动挡车，如果他反复思考如何挂挡，就会导致他忘记本来是要做什么。如果他只是不假思索地按照习惯操作，就会开得很顺利。两种情形的对比表明，依靠直觉往往比较顺利，而深思熟虑可能反而会导致注意力分散，从而影响判断。另外，朱迪斯•霍尔的观点以It\'s as if...开始，表明该观点是为支撑上文观点服务的，因此我们也可以借助首句内容解题。首句指出，当我们依靠直觉而非深思时，更能从“行为薄片”中觉察到欺骗；言外之意即直觉比深思更可靠。［A］符合题意。\n［命题解密］正确项［A］是对朱迪斯•霍尔比较手动挡汽车驾驶员的两种心态之目的的正确解读。\n［B］对②句you can\'t remember what you\'re doing断章取义。该句意在说明“深入思考会将注意力导向其他事物，忘记原本所要做的事”，而非“记忆具有选择性”。［C］由末句碎片信息“社交生活”捏造而来，本文并未论及获得社交技能的途径。［D］由首句中we\'re better at detecting deception逆向推导而来，但该句意在指出依靠直觉作出的判断比依靠深思更准确。\n［技巧总结］人物观点+写作目的题。解答此类题时，除直接从人物观点本身推断出答案外，亦可借助论据（人物观点）与论点（作者观点）的关系进行判断：若论据是为支撑论点，此时两者意思相近；若提出论据的目的在于树靶驳斥，则两者意思相反。就本题而言，要判断作者引用朱迪斯•霍尔之观点的目的在于批驳还是引证，须先了解第三段与前两段的逻辑关系。首先，由于第三段首句中没有表转折的词，可初步推断本段与前两段为顺承关系。仔细分析也可得知，前两段作者通过引述研究的结果证明“处理社交类信息时依靠直觉做出的判断更准确，深思反而会对判断造成干扰（interference）”，而进入第三段，作者先在首句中通过引述其他研究发现再次证明“社会生活中直觉判断比深思更准确”，随后又在②③④句中引述朱迪斯•霍尔“驾驶手动挡汽车”的类比进一步阐释该观点。由此可知，朱迪斯•霍尔的言论是作为支撑性论据受到引用，其论点与首句作者观点相似。因此，朱迪斯•霍尔提及驾驶是为了表明（处理社交信息时）深思熟虑反会让人分心。' WHERE id = '97d5205b-e0b1-520e-a3c1-4c5d8c51d14b'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'When you are making complex decisions, it is advisable to ________.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "collect enough data", "content": "collect enough data"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "list your preferences", "content": "list your preferences"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "seek expert advice", "content": "seek expert advice"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "follow your feelings", "content": "follow your feelings"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干关键词complex decisions定位到第四段末句。该句指出，当人们被要求关注感觉而非细节时，他们做出的购车决定既合理又令自己满意，但只有在这一决定很复杂的情况下方才如此。由此可知，在做复杂决定时，明智的做法是“遵从你的感觉”，故［D］正确。同时排除［A］。\n［命题解密］题干+正确项［D］是对第四段末句的正确解读。\n［B］项由首句过度推断而来：如果说“考虑得太多会损害我们形成偏好的能力”，那么“（事先）列出偏好”就可以帮助我们做决定。但此种理解误解了首句的语义重心：作者想强调的并非偏好的形成，而是想得太多对形成偏好/做决定这一能力的损害。［C］由②句碎片信息experts\' opinions捏造而来。该句实指在不需要深思时，人们对事物的评估与专家意见更一致，也即“（在某些情况下）直觉判断更准确”。\n［技巧总结］事实细节题。解答此类题目的关键在于精准定位。对于那些关键词未落在定位句范围内的选项，多数情况下可被认定为干扰项。就本题而言，根据题目关键词complex decisions可定位至第四段末句。细察本句，可发现题干When you are making complex decisions同义改写only if the decision was complex，由此可知题干主句it is advisable to +正确项应复现if条件句的主句people made... details。而又因为［D］follow your feelings同义复现focus on their feelings，“明智的（advisable）”概括关注感觉的结果，即“人们做出的购车决定既合理又令自己满意（people made... satisfying）”，因此［D］正确。题干+［A］所反映之意为“关注细节是明智的”，与作者意思恰恰相反。而［B］项preferences、［C］项expert advice分别源自①②句，不在本题考查的信息范围内，因此排除。' WHERE id = '840fb83f-6139-54ac-afcb-5c1c1c6e3e30'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'What can we learn from the last paragraph?', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Generating new products takes time.", "content": "Generating new products takes time."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Intuition may affect reflective tasks.", "content": "Intuition may affect reflective tasks."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Vocabulary comprehension needs creativity.", "content": "Vocabulary comprehension needs creativity."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Objective thinking may boost intuitiveness.", "content": "Objective thinking may boost intuitiveness."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［精准定位］末段首句指出，直觉的特殊能力只有在特定情形下才能发挥出来。②③④句引用研究发现进一步说明：在一项研究中，参与者要完成四项运用深度思索能力、四项运用直觉与创造力的任务，并为其使用直觉的程度打分。结果发现，使用直觉损害了他们在前四项任务中的表现，而对后四项任务则有所帮助。由此可知，直觉会降低思考性工作的成效，故［B］正确。\n［命题解密］正确项［B］是对末段引述的研究发现（④句）的合理解读。\n［A］利用②句碎片信息generating new products捏造而来，文中并未涉及创造新产品所消耗时间的多少。［C］张冠李戴。②句明确指出，理解词汇需要运用的是深度思索能力，而创造新产品或修辞格需要的才是创造力。［D］利用第四段③句objectively捏造而来，文中并未论及提升直觉力的方法。\n［技巧总结］段落推理题。末段主体部分关注一项研究，结合各选项内容可知本题考查对研究结果的推理和引申。解题时需先确定引入该研究的语境，再在此基础上对研究结果进行解读。具体而言，由于首句指出“直觉的特殊能力只有在特定情形下才能发挥出来”，因此可确定下述研究应就论证“在何种情形下直觉的能力才能发挥出来”而展开。再细看研究本身可知，直觉在需要运用直觉与创造力的任务中发挥了积极作用，而对需要运用深度思索能力的任务的完成产生了负面影响。由此可知［B］正确。另外，本题的提问方式（根据某段可以得知什么？）也很有特点，这种问题实际上考查的是段落主旨或者在主旨基础上的合理推断。以本段为例，本段首句为段落主旨，指出直觉的特殊能力只有在特定情境下才会发挥出来。言外之意，直觉也不是“万能灵药”，有的情况并不适合运用直觉行事。［B］选项符合这一逻辑推理。' WHERE id = '51db2934-bb7b-5f3c-8358-2f12c6ac2da0'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best heading [A]-[G] for paragraph (41):', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Stay calm", "content": "Stay calm"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Stay humble", "content": "Stay humble"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Decide whether to wait", "content": "Decide whether to wait"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Be realistic about the risks", "content": "Be realistic about the risks"}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "Don\'t make judgements", "content": "Don\'t make judgements"}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "Identify a shared goal", "content": "Identify a shared goal"}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "Ask permission to disagree", "content": "Ask permission to disagree"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［定位/考点］段落主旨匹配（第2段）。\n［解题思路］第二段指出，如果还未充分考虑与上司产生争议的这一问题，或想要先了解同事的看法，或正身处会议室等公共场合，那么最好暂缓提反对意见，即要等待提异议的合适时机或场合，C项“决定是否再等等”与该段主旨相符，其中Decide原词复现首句（You may） decide, wait近义复现首句hold off on和⑤句delay。\n［错项排除］B项Stay humble虽能解释暂缓提异议的第二条原因（⑤⑥句）“避免让上司感觉受到威胁”，但由全段内容可知，之所以要暂缓异议，仅仅是因为客观时机或场合不对，而不是为了主观表现谦恭态度，且“保持谦卑”并未体现于第一条原因（②至④句），故可排除B。D项“务实对待风险”按常理来说很可能为“向上司进言”的第一步，且似乎也能说明暂缓异议的原因“有让上司感觉受威胁的风险”，但实际上第二段并未全面、务实地评估向上司表达不同意见的风险，而更侧重介绍具体做法，故D错误。F项shared goal虽能体现③④句“众人为共同目标（向上司传达异议）齐心协力、建言献策”之意，但段落其余各句均重在谈论“何时需暂缓表达异议及其原因”，选项无法概括全段，故排除。' WHERE id = '6873131a-3ac5-5aea-ba97-33116d1ce319'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best heading [A]-[G] for paragraph (42):', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Stay calm", "content": "Stay calm"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Stay humble", "content": "Stay humble"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Decide whether to wait", "content": "Decide whether to wait"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Be realistic about the risks", "content": "Be realistic about the risks"}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "Don\'t make judgements", "content": "Don\'t make judgements"}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "Identify a shared goal", "content": "Identify a shared goal"}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "Ask permission to disagree", "content": "Ask permission to disagree"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'F', explanation = E'［定位/考点］段落主旨匹配（第三段）。\n［解题思路］第三段针对向老板进言之前的准备工作与进言之时的谈吐措辞提出建议：首先要预先了解上司关注的核心目标（higher purpose / shared goal），随后将这一目标与个人异议相结合，并在进言时直白点明二者的关联，以向上司证明你是一个为实现双方共同利益而建言的同盟。［F］Identify a shared goal（确定共同目标）精准契合本段主旨。\n［错项排除］其余选项均未点中“先找准上司与自己的共同目标并将异议锚定其上”的核心策略：如［B］Stay humble 侧重末段保持谦逊态度，［G］Ask permission to disagree 侧重第四段进言前先征得对方许可，皆非本段重点。' WHERE id = 'c34324ca-3250-5e6b-b760-748c33f96fdb'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best heading [A]-[G] for paragraph (43):', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Stay calm", "content": "Stay calm"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Stay humble", "content": "Stay humble"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Decide whether to wait", "content": "Decide whether to wait"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Be realistic about the risks", "content": "Be realistic about the risks"}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "Don\'t make judgements", "content": "Don\'t make judgements"}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "Identify a shared goal", "content": "Identify a shared goal"}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "Ask permission to disagree", "content": "Ask permission to disagree"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'G', explanation = E'［定位/考点］段落主旨匹配（第4段）。\n［解题思路］第四段先评价“这一做法（This step）”：看似过于顺从，实则是卸下上司心理防卫的明智之举。后举例说明“这一做法”：向上司请求表达异议的许可。最后指出该做法的作用：让上司更可能听取反对意见。综合可见，G项“请求允许表达异议”与该段主旨一致，其中Ask permission与⑤句Would that be OK的请求之意相符。\n［错项排除］B项humble虽近义复现段首deferential,也与④⑤句would like to、Would that be OK体现的谦恭态度相符，但由②至⑤句可知，恭顺是为征得表达异议的许可这一目标服务，⑥⑦句也均围绕"上司许可与否（opt in says yes）"展开，【B】 Stay humble仅契合段落首句，无法概括余下内容，故排除。' WHERE id = 'bb42d1f8-2299-5833-8fdd-685384bbb560'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best heading [A]-[G] for paragraph (44):', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Stay calm", "content": "Stay calm"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Stay humble", "content": "Stay humble"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Decide whether to wait", "content": "Decide whether to wait"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Be realistic about the risks", "content": "Be realistic about the risks"}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "Don\'t make judgements", "content": "Don\'t make judgements"}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "Identify a shared goal", "content": "Identify a shared goal"}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "Ask permission to disagree", "content": "Ask permission to disagree"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［定位/考点］段落主旨匹配（第五段）。\n［解题思路］第五段先建议读者在向上司表达异议时尽力保持沉着、不动声色（keep your cool），随后说明紧张、焦虑等负面情绪对沟通说服力的破坏性影响，并给出两条具体平复情绪的可行做法：放慢前先深呼吸（deep breaths）以及更缓慢、更审慎地讲话（speak more slowly and deliberately）。可见本段重在建议避免负面情绪左右进言成败，［A］Stay calm（保持冷静）与本段主旨高度一致。\n［错项排除］［B］Stay humble 强调收敛自信、虚心纳谏（第六段），［D］Be realistic about the risks 为常识干扰项，二者均未涉及情绪调控与呼吸语速控制。' WHERE id = 'b593c251-b556-5caf-bc5d-6ed83ccc479c'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best heading [A]-[G] for paragraph (45):', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Stay calm", "content": "Stay calm"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Stay humble", "content": "Stay humble"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Decide whether to wait", "content": "Decide whether to wait"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Be realistic about the risks", "content": "Be realistic about the risks"}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "Don\'t make judgements", "content": "Don\'t make judgements"}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "Identify a shared goal", "content": "Identify a shared goal"}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "Ask permission to disagree", "content": "Ask permission to disagree"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［定位/考点］段落主旨匹配（第6段）。\n［解题思路］第六段先建议读者向上司强调自己仅是在提供“个人观点”而非“绝对真理”，后又提出要采用试探性的表达、收敛自信（talk tentatively and slightly understate your confidence），最后指出要保持好奇心并耐心倾听对方的意见甚至批评（invite critique / Be open to hearing other opinions）。[B] Stay humble（保持谦逊，不要自视甚高）是对这些建议的准确概括，其中 humble 近义复现句中的 understate your confidence。\n［错项排除］［E］Don\'t make judgements（不要下评判）虽然看似与“不要将自己的观点视作真理”相近，但段落并非反对提出判断（相反作者鼓励清晰陈述观点，只是将其作为个人立场而非绝对事实），而是强调陈述时要谦逊收敛、乐于倾听他人批评，故排除［E］。' WHERE id = '669e1daa-2cf1-58ef-bfcc-fd7e68420805'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [1] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "difficult", "content": "difficult"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "normal", "content": "normal"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "steady", "content": "steady"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "pleasant", "content": "pleasant"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义+上下文语义。\n［解题思路］首句说明哈兰•科本的观点：作家总能找到时间来写作；找不到写作时间的人不可称为作家。②句（空格句）指出，对哈兰•科本而言，写作是一份______ 工作—和其他任何工作一样。从②句句内来看，破折号后内容（a job like any other）解释说明a________ job,即空格词应说明写作的"普通/平常”。再联系①句可知，空格句意在说明写作只是一项普通工作，作家也应像其他行业的工作者一样花时间做好本职工作。综上，空格词应表示“平常的/普通的”，［B］normal正确。\n［错项排除］［A］、［C］、［D］均可描述写作的特点，且［A］、［D］看似符合①句暗含之意“人们往往很难找到时间来写作；但写作应是作家的优先项/爱做之事”，但三项都与破折号后的解释说明内容不符。' WHERE id = '81548c26-9d13-54f3-a594-3946fc6d1547'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [2] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "combined", "content": "combined"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "compared", "content": "compared"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "confused", "content": "confused"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "confronted", "content": "confronted"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］ 句内语义+上下文语义。\n［解题思路］ 空格句指出，哈兰•科本将写作（it = writing）与修管道（plumbing）________，指出管道工不会在早上醒来后说自己今天没法修理管道。联系上两句内容“如果你是一名作家，那你一定能找到时间来写作；写作和其他任何工作一样”可知，空格句是在将“写作”与最普通的工作“管道修理”相较，以此来直观说明“写作并没有什么特别之处，作家应该像管道工一样尽职尽责地完成工作”。空格词应表示“比较/对比”，compare A with B意为“将A与B比较”，［B］ compared正确。\n［错项排除］ 其他三项干扰性在于均能与with搭配，但［A］ combine A with B表示“使A和B结合”；［C］ confuse A with B表示“将A和B混淆；将A误认为B”；［D］ confront A with B表示“使A面对B（令人不快或难处的人、场合）”，均偏离文意。' WHERE id = 'ab8c6d20-06e9-53ce-b1d8-b62cbb8485f3'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [3] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "If", "content": "If"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Though", "content": "Though"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Once", "content": "Once"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Unless", "content": "Unless"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义逻辑+段际衔接。\n［解题思路］空格句从句部分指出，______ ，像现在的大多数作家一样，你干着一份糊口的工作。主句部分则指出，找到写作的时间不……。可见，从句是在引导读者想象自己是一位“边干其他工作养家边写作的作家”，来分析“这种情况下找到写作时间的难易等”，空格词应表示“如果/假设”等以引出假想情况，且这一“假定的具体情形”恰能顺接上段内容，[A] If正确。\n［错项排除］[B] Though表转折，利用空格句和随后句的转折关系（But）设障，但though位于句首时，体现的是"句内转折关系"或"对上句的让步"，且不与but成对出现。如Though she was tiny, she had a very loud voice.（虽然 她个头 很小，嗓门却 很大。）I like him. Though he makes me angry sometimes.（我喜欢他，尽管他有时惹我生气。）文中并非though的正确用法。[C] Once表条件，含一定的假设意味，有较强干扰。once与if的区别主要在于：if表示假设，其引出的情况可真可假（可以是真实条件句，也可以是假定情形）；而once（as soon as; when"   就；一旦；当 时候"）则表示实现某事的条件，其引出的情况一般都为真，如The water is fine once you\'re in!（你一旦下了水，就会觉得水里挺舒适！）。文中“你是一名作家”为假设情形而非真实条件，故[C]错误。[D] Unless表示某事不成立的唯一条件，如Unless it rains, the game will be played.（除非下雨，比赛将照常进行=只有下雨，比赛才会取消）,Unless填入文中表示“除非像大多数作家一样干着养家糊口的工作，否则找到写作时间将不是一件……的事”，若空格4表示“困难、不可能等”，则完全成立。这时需借助下句But it\'s not impossible先判断空4应大致表示“容易、可行等”，确定unless不符合逻辑。' WHERE id = '8eff9704-1239-579e-8670-0b56abaf4b16'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [4] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "enough", "content": "enough"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "strange", "content": "strange"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "wrong", "content": "wrong"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "easy", "content": "easy"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义+句间逻辑。\n［解题思路］空格句指出，如果你像大多数作家一样，干着一份养家糊口的工作，则找到写作时间不______ 。随后一句则转而指出，但这不是不可能（But it\'s not impossible. ） 。联系两句间逻辑以及常识常识可知句群意在说明作家在养家糊口的同时要找到时间写作“确有难处”，it\'s not _________指向“有难度”，空格词应表示“容易/简单”，[D] easy正确。\n［错项排除］[A] enough利用“作家需要养家糊口（ to pay the bills）”得出貌似合乎逻辑的语义“作家仅仅找时间写作是不够的（还要挣钱养家）”，但从句实则表示“分工并行”（一份工作来养家；同时进行写作），且后句转折指出"但这并非不可能"，故[A]偏离文意。[B] strange / [C] wrong 填入文中表示“找时间写作不奇怪/没有错”，均无法与前后文形成合乎逻辑的语义关系。' WHERE id = 'd60d57ae-e56c-5165-a87f-d2c66610ed2c'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [5] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Accept", "content": "Accept"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Explain", "content": "Explain"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Remember", "content": "Remember"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Suppose", "content": "Suppose"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义。\n［解题思路］空格句指出，______ 大多数畅销书作家当初开始写作的时候都在干着其他赖以谋生的工作。结合前三句大意“干着养家糊口工作的作家要找到写作时间不容易，但并非不可能，只是这需要决心和专注”可知，空格句是在以“畅销书作家大都经历的情形”来提醒/安慰/鼓励读者“开始写作的初期都是辛苦的（要想成为成功作家，必然要经历艰辛）”,[C] Remember正确。\n［错项排除］[A] Accept指向“接受/承认（某种对自己不利的情况）”，而空格后为“其他作家的成功经历”，不存在接受/不接受的问题。[B] Explain指向“解释说明某事发生的理由”，而下文中并未展开说明畅销书作家这样做的理由。[D] Suppose用于“假设某种情形”（其后从句常用一般现在时或现在/过去进行时），而空格后从句是在以一般过去时介绍大多数畅销书作家曾有的经历。' WHERE id = 'a78256f8-f6fd-5953-bf74-a310aa0e88dd'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [8] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "cause", "content": "cause"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "purpose", "content": "purpose"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "question", "content": "question"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "condition", "content": "condition"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义。\n［解题思路］空格句指出，正如哈兰•科本所说，这是一个优先项的______ 。“这(it)”指代II段所述问题“作家能否在从事其他工作的同时找到写作时间”，联系首段的科本观点“如果你找不到时间来写作，那写作就不是你的优先项，你也就不是一名作家”可知，空格句是在点明II段所述问题的实质“作家能否找到写作时间取决于写作是否被视为优先项”，空格词应体现“核心/关键问题”，a question of sth意为“……的问题”，表示问题的本质，[C] question正确。\n［错项排除］填入文中分别表示it(II段所述问题)为“优先项”的起因、目的和条件，但分析可知，it与“优先项”实指同一件事，两者为“表一里”关系，故三项均偏离文意。' WHERE id = 'fd9394cb-7f0b-56c3-be6e-0d8ff06cdc0e'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [9] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "highlight", "content": "highlight"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "sacrifice", "content": "sacrifice"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "continue", "content": "continue"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "explore", "content": "explore"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］词义分析+上下文语义。\n［解题思路］空格句指出，要想让写作成为优先项，你必须______ 一些日常活动和一些自己喜欢做的事。根据 priority 含义 sth that you think is more important than other things and should be dealt with first"优先事项；最重要的事"可知，"日常活动(day-to-day activities)”和"喜欢做的事(some things you really enjoy)"位于写作之后，居于次要地位，应做出让步/牺牲。根据下文spending less time、less socialising也可进一步推测，空格词应表加"减少/牺牲/舍弃"，[B] sacrifice 正确。\n［错项排除］[A] highlight 意为 to emphasize sth, especially so that people give it more attention“突出；强调；给予更多关注”，与“日常活动”等的次要地位相悖。虽能与activities搭配，但无法体现优先项和次要项间的取舍关系，三项均可排除。' WHERE id = '485e6eb5-8889-5a5d-ab9c-81476b02607f'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [10] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "relations", "content": "relations"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "interests", "content": "interests"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "memories", "content": "memories"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "skills", "content": "skills"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义+上下文语义。\n［解题思路］空格句指出，取决于你的“______ ”和“生活方式”，这可能意味着要减少花在“看电视”或"听音乐"上的时间。句内分析：your______ and your lifestyle 应能涵盖 watching television or listening to music 等活动 o 句间关联：空格句中 that 指代上句,watching television or listening to music 属于 day-to-day activities and some things you really enjoy,即 your and your lifestyle 应同样胄总体现 day-to-day activities and some things you really enjoy。综上，your and your lifestyle 应表示"兴趣爱好以及生活方式",[B] interests正确。\n［错项排除］[A]、[C]、[D]三项既无法涵盖“看电视”“听音乐”等活动，又无法体现上句的“日常活动和喜欢之事”，可排除。' WHERE id = 'f93e8a8d-a351-5994-918c-4e5bd814357d'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [11] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "until", "content": "until"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "because", "content": "because"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "while", "content": "while"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "before", "content": "before"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义+常识。\n[B] because 因为\n[D] before 在... 以前\n［解题思路］空格句指出，要让写作成为优先项，就要减少看电视或听音乐的时间，尽管有人可以写作______ 听音乐。though提示转折，即空格所在部分应指向“不必减少听音乐的时间”，结合常识可知，该部分表示“写作与听音乐可同时进行，两者并不冲突”，空格词应表示“与……同时”，[C]while正确。\n［错项排除］[A] until填入文中表示“直到听音乐前一直写作”意即“一开始听音乐就要停止写作”,表明写作需要让位于听音乐，不符合写作作为“优先项”的地位。[B] because填入文中表示“写作是因为听音乐”，显然不合逻辑，也无法和前半句形成转折。[D] before填入文中表示“在听音乐前写作”，同样表明两项活动无法同时进行，在时间上有冲突，无法与前半句形成转折。' WHERE id = 'fe3f51c4-c2b7-5590-a22f-4d041724e717'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [12] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "put up with", "content": "put up with"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "make up for", "content": "make up for"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "hang on to", "content": "hang on to"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "cut down on", "content": "cut down on"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义+固定短语。\n［解题思路］空格句指出，你可能不得不\n[B] make up for 补偿；弥补\n[D] cut down on 削减；减少\n锻炼或运动的量。其中，"锻炼（exercise）""运动（sport）”指向兴趣爱好/生活方式，可见空格句承上继续列举为了写作需要做出牺牲的活动，空格词应与上文 sacrifice‘spending less time 语义同向,表示"减少",[D] cut down on 正确。\n［错项排除］[A]、[C]指向“保持现有的运动的量”,[B]指向“以其他方式补上运动量”,三项均错误。' WHERE id = '909893e6-ae96-5d3a-a89d-e5059dd4cc31'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [13] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "intelligent", "content": "intelligent"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "occasional", "content": "occasional"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "intensive", "content": "intensive"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "emotional", "content": "emotional"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］形容词词义辨析与上下文对比逻辑。\n［解题思路］空格句指出，你将不得不让使用社交媒体成为一项______活动（an [13] activity）。联系上文“减少看电视、听音乐与运动时间”可知，“使用社交媒体”同样是需要为写作让路、作出时间妥协的活动，空格词应体现“偶尔为之的、非经常性的”含义，与后句“每日例行的、耗费时间的（daily, time-consuming）”形成反义照应，故选［B］occasional。\n［错项排除］［A］intelligent（明智的、智能的）与［D］emotional（情感的、情绪化的）均偏离“活动占用时间频率”这一核心语义场；［C］intensive（集中的、高强度的）意指加大投入精力与时间，与全文“削减社交娱乐时间以保证写作”的方向完全相反。' WHERE id = '727984e4-c7af-551c-bda7-a24edb08578d'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [14] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "habit", "content": "habit"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "test", "content": "test"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "decision", "content": "decision"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "plan", "content": "plan"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义。\n［解题思路］空格句指出，要让使用社交媒体成为一项偶尔为之的活动，而不是每日例行的、耗费时间的______。取舍结构 rather than 表明，a daily, time-consuming 应与"an occasional activity（偶尔为之的活动）"语义相对，再结合空格前修饰成分daily（每日例行的）,time-consuming（耗费时间的）"可知，空格词应表示“日常习惯/常规活动”，［A］ habit正确。\n［错项排除］三项均可与 daily, time-consuming 搭配，但无法与 occasional activity 形成对比，不符合rather than所体现的取舍逻辑。' WHERE id = 'a22a18d4-b1a9-57f8-9c48-922d7b26f4ad'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [15] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "tough", "content": "tough"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "gentle", "content": "gentle"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "rapid", "content": "rapid"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "funny", "content": "funny"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义+上下文语义。\n［解题思路］空格句指出，这是一条______ 学习曲线，而且并不一定能让你大受欢迎。结合上文可知，“这(It)”概括上文内容“为了找出写作时间，牺牲掉多种兴趣爱好及日常活动”。此处learning curve含义不明，应根据语义逻辑解题。首先进行句内分析：结合其字面义“学习曲线”和“并不一定能让你大受欢迎"，可推测learning curve指"学习过程"，a________ learning curve应指"一条艰难的/曲折的学习曲线”,体现“虽然过程艰难，但结果不一定如愿”之意，空格词应体现“艰难的/痛苦的/需要毅力的”等意。随后，结合上文用词 have to sacrifice, have to cut down on、have to make、have to be less 等隐含的"虽不情愿但不得不努力减少自己用于多种兴趣爱好的时间”，可进一步确认这一推测，［A］ tough正确。\n［错项排除］语义色彩均偏正面，不符合上文“不得不克服困难，努力为之”的语义色彩，另外，［B］填入文中，前后两个分句无法顺接—“学习过程平缓顺畅，且并不总能令你受欢迎”不合逻辑；［D］看似可以形成顺畅的语义“有趣并不一定能让你受欢迎”，实则偏离文意。' WHERE id = '48b6c45c-e75a-5e92-9faf-6035c497e360'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [16] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "in place of", "content": "in place of"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "in charge of", "content": "in charge of"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "in response to", "content": "in response to"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "in addition to", "content": "in addition to"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义。\n［解题思路］空格句指出，只有一件事你应该尽力留出一些时间去做，___写作—那就是阅读。上文提到，作家应将写作视为优先项，需为此牺牲一系列日常活动和兴趣爱好。联系可知，空格句是在转承上段，指出唯有“阅读”是唯一必须留时间去做的事，是重要性仅次于写作的事，故空格词应表示“除……之外/仅次于”，［D］ in addition to正确。\n［错项排除］［A］填入文中表示“阅读可代替写作”，这与本文主题“作家如何寻找写作时间”不符，且与随后一句信息“阅读是写作必不可少的支撑”不一致。［B］填入文中表示“阅读负责/主管写作”，貌似符合实际情形“阅读面很大程度上决定你的写作水平”，但实则不合英文逻辑。［C］利用“阅读是为了应对写作的需求"这一常识设置干扰，但 in response to(response 意为 a reaction to sth that has happened)意为“对……做出反应/响应”，实际上并不能表达这种需求关系。' WHERE id = '9cb7f685-8e34-5127-ba30-88f97f7c983e'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [17] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "indispensable", "content": "indispensable"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "innovative", "content": "innovative"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "invisible", "content": "invisible"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "instant", "content": "instant"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］形容词词义辨析与同义解释呼应。\n［解题思路］空格句指出，任何作家都需要尽可能多而广地阅读，因为阅读是______支撑——你没它不行（you can\'t do without）。前半句强调大量泛读的必要性，破折号后进一步直接点明“缺少它就无法写作”，故空格词应表达“不可或缺的、极其必要的”，［A］indispensable 精确契合。\n［错项排除］［B］innovative（革新的、创新的）、［C］invisible（看不见的、无形的）以及［D］instant（立即的、速成的）虽然有时能修饰抽象事物，但均无法与破折号后的解释成分“you can\'t do without（缺之不可）”构成同义呼应。' WHERE id = 'c7a94744-ea13-5f80-8b2a-4ebefb03ce6c'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [18] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "duller", "content": "duller"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "harder", "content": "harder"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "quieter", "content": "quieter"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "quicker", "content": "quicker"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义。\n［解题思路］末段①句指出，时间是有限的。②句（空格句）指出，年龄越大，时间似乎流逝得________。③句以We need to...顺而提出建议：确定活动的优先次序，将大部分时间花在我们真正要做的事情上。联系全文可知，末段进行升华，提醒读者时间有限、光阴飞逝，应将精力集中于优先事项。故空格词应表示"更快地"，[D] quicker正确。\n［错项排除］[A]、[B]、[C]三项均能在一定程度上体现年老（The older you get）的生活的特点，但无法与前后文内容顺接。' WHERE id = '925ed4e6-6a76-56ba-badc-b0b33c7bfc25'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [19] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "peacefully", "content": "peacefully"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "generously", "content": "generously"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "productively", "content": "productively"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "gratefully", "content": "gratefully"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义+上下文语义。\n［解题思路］空格句指出，我们要尽可能谨慎且______ 地利用时间，这意味着要确定活动的优先次序，以便将大多数时间花在我们真正要做的事情上。从句内来看，空格词应与其前的并列副词carefully（谨慎地）指向一致，“谨慎、______利用时间”应与其后的解释性从句“确定活动的优先次序，将时间花在真正要做的事上”语义一致，空格词应表示“合理地/有效地/明智地”等。此外，由上两句“时间有限、光阴飞逝"也可得出此结论，[C] productively正确。\n［错项排除］[A] peacefully虽与carefully搭配合理，但其强调"安静地、平和地"做某事，文中并未体现这一内容。[B] generously强调做某事时毫不吝啬、慷慨大方，与前后文意相悖。[D] gratefully能与其前顺接，形成“时间有限，且年龄越大流逝越快，因而我们应认真地、心存感激地利用自己所拥有的时间”这一合理逻辑，但与随后的解释性从句语义不一致，也偏离本文论述对象。' WHERE id = '8f1dff67-e854-516e-9fdc-a7ec20d74d83'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [20] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "at most", "content": "at most"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "in turn", "content": "in turn"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "on average", "content": "on average"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "above all", "content": "above all"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义。\n［解题思路］空格句指出，如果你是一名作家，那意味着一_____ 写作。“那（that）”指代上文的泛泛而谈“我们应确定活动的优先次序，将大多数时间花在真正要就両情上”。结合句间逻辑（从面向所有人到聚焦“作家”）、文章主旨（作家的优先项是写作）以及生活常识（作家的首要任务是写作）可知，故空格词应与prioritising, spend most time on语义指向一致，表示"优先/首要”,[D] above all正确。\n［错项排除］[A] at most表示"（数量、程度）等不超过某一数值"，如He faces at most 12 years in prison.（他面临最多12年的监禁。）该短语显然不符合文中语境。[B] in turn 利用中文表达“人们都应将时间花在优先事项上，轮到作家，优先事项则是写作”设置干扰。但in turn并不能用于表达这一情形。该词主要有两种用法：1.表示“多人依顺序做某事”，如We look after him in turn.（我们依次照顾他。）2.表示“继而;转而”，如Increased production will, in turn, lead to increased profits.（增加生产会继而增加利润。）这两种用法均不符合此处情形。[C] on average表示“一系列数值/情况的平均水平”，不符合此处语境。' WHERE id = 'e20c1f2e-7abd-54c0-bf74-b2efb8233a9b'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'It can be learned from the first two paragraphs that dark patterns', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "improve user experiences", "content": "improve user experiences"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "leak user information for profit", "content": "leak user information for profit"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "undermine users\' decision-making", "content": "undermine users\' decision-making"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "remind users of hidden costs", "content": "remind users of hidden costs"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［精准定位］题干已给出明确定位（前两段）。首段列举黑暗模式的例子，并指出它们损害消费者的选择权（impair consumer choice）；第二段①句进一步指出，黑暗模式实指操纵用户界面以影响用户决策能力的做法（manipulate user interfaces to influence the decision-making ability of users）。综合可知，黑暗模式损害用户的决策，［C］正确。\n［命题解密］［C］对应首段末句 impair consumer choice、第二段①句 influence the decision-making ability of users（influence 呼应 impair，实指“产生负面影响”）。\n［错项排除］［A］利用第二段②句 a user experience seems easy and intuitive 干扰，但忽略了该句的语义重点“当用户试图退出时，用户体验变得非常困难”；［B］由第五段 data privacy rights 过度推导而来，与前两段阐述的事实无关且超出定位范围；［D］利用第二段②句 hidden costs 干扰，“隐藏成本”实为黑暗模式欺诈用户的一种常见形式，并非“提醒用户注意”。\n［技巧总结］本题针对概念描述部分命制事实细节题，解题关键在于精准定位并区辨概念的语义色彩，同时注意正确项往往是对原文信息的同义改写。具体来看，可先基于前两段中 have encountered、felt tricked or frustrated、impair consumer choice、turns difficult... to get out 等消极语义场，排除正面表述［A］与［D］，再排除超范围的［B］，从而锁定［C］。' WHERE id = '1b388e93-8c9d-5543-9472-c79981ff1bf4'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The 2019 study on dark patterns is mentioned to show ________.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "their major flaws", "content": "their major flaws"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "their complex designs", "content": "their complex designs"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "their severe damage", "content": "their severe damage"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "their strong presence", "content": "their strong presence"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干关键词 The 2019 study 定位到第三段。该段①句引用 2019 年针对黑暗模式展开的一项涵盖 5.3 万个产品页面和 1.1 万个网站的研究，说明“大约有十分之一的页面或网站运用了黑暗设计手法”；②句紧接着明确问题“尽管黑暗模式广泛存在（widely prevalent），却仍未被充分了解”；③句针对该问题提议各大组织领导了解并避免运用黑暗模式。可见，文中借该项研究说明黑暗模式“大量运用/普遍存在”，进而引出相关建议，［D］正确。\n［命题解密］“题干 + ［D］”是对第三段①②句的正确推导，strong presence 不仅概括①句 53,000 product pages and 11,000 websites... one in 10 employs these design practices，而且契合②句 widely prevalent。\n［错项排除］［A］由第三段末 avoid the gray areas they engender 反推而来；［B］、［C］体现前两段中所提及的黑暗模式的特征，三项均非本文引用 2019 年研究所说明的核心事实，也与写作目的不符。\n［技巧总结］本题就引用论证处命制写作目的题，须注意引用的目的通常是引出主题或论证观点。解答本题时，可根据论据（2019 年关于黑暗模式的研究）本身的数据占比锁定［D］，再通过对比下文总结概括性内容（widely prevalent）确认［D］准确无误。' WHERE id = '450bd174-55c4-54ed-8c25-255d10b3b15b'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'To handle digital deception, businesses should', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "listen to customer feedback", "content": "listen to customer feedback"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "talk with relevant teams", "content": "talk with relevant teams"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "turn to independent agencies", "content": "turn to independent agencies"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "rely on professional training", "content": "rely on professional training"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［精准定位］根据题干关键词 digital deception 与 businesses 定位至第四段②③句。该段指出企业应当与 IT、合规、风控及法务团队展开对话（engage in conversations with IT, compliance, risk, and legal teams）以审查隐私政策，并将负责用户界面的设计师、程序员以及负责注册和促销的营销及广告团队纳入讨论，这些团队均在制造或避免“数字欺诈”中发挥作用。\n［命题解密］“题干 + ［B］”是对第四段②③句的正确概括，talk 同义复现 engage in conversations，relevant teams 概括 IT, compliance, risk, and legal teams 等多部门团队。\n［错项排除］［A］将第四段②句 include in the discussion the customer/user experience designers and coders 曲解为“听取客户反馈”；［C］、［D］均利用第四段②句提及的各专业团队干扰，［C］错将其概括为“独立机构”，［D］将“与专业团队对话”曲解为“展开专业培训”。\n［技巧总结］本题定位句为长难句且并列信息较多，解题时可先提炼句子主干（Businesses should engage in conversations with... and include in the discussion...），迅速抓住“与多个相关团队沟通协作”的核心动作，比对选项对象即可排除明显不符的［A］［C］［D］，锁定［B］。' WHERE id = 'ddecbd99-eac0-5b15-913a-4cf98d0ed52a'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The additional regulations under the CCPA are intended to', options = E'[{"key": "A", "text": "guide users through opt-out processes", "value": "A", "content": "guide users through opt-out processes"}, {"key": "B", "text": "protect consumers from being tricked", "value": "B", "content": "protect consumers from being tricked"}, {"key": "C", "text": "grant companies data privacy rights", "value": "C", "content": "grant companies data privacy rights"}, {"key": "D", "text": "restrict access to problematic content", "value": "D", "content": "restrict access to problematic content"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］细节事实题（法案条文目的定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 additional regulations under the CCPA 定位至第五段②③句。该段指出，《加州消费者隐私法案》（CCPA）补充规定旨在确保消费者在行使其数据隐私权时不会被迷惑或误导（will not be confused or misled），并明确禁止企业运用黑暗模式人为设置退出或选择障碍，即保护消费者免受欺骗，故［B］protect consumers from being tricked 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］guide users through opt-out processes（引导用户完成选择退出流程）仅是对禁令反面的过度引申，法案旨在阻止欺诈性界面而非提供操作指南；［C］grant companies data privacy rights（赋予公司数据隐私权）将“消费者（consumers）”的权益对象偷换为“公司（companies）”；［D］restrict access to problematic content（限制接触有问题的内容）属无中生有，黑暗模式涉及用户界面误导而非屏蔽网页内容。' WHERE id = 'd336eb7c-450e-5682-b476-31c67923a436'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to the last paragraph, a key to coping with dark patterns is', options = E'[{"key": "A", "text": "new legal requirements", "value": "A", "content": "new legal requirements"}, {"key": "B", "text": "businesses\' self-discipline", "value": "B", "content": "businesses\' self-discipline"}, {"key": "C", "text": "strict regulatory standards", "value": "C", "content": "strict regulatory standards"}, {"key": "D", "text": "consumers\' safety awareness", "value": "D", "content": "consumers\' safety awareness"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］段落主旨与细节推断题。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 the last paragraph 与 key to coping with dark patterns 定位至末段①②句。文章最后指出，整个商界必须承担起更多责任（greater accountability），暗黑模式问题可以在行业自律或企业自我监管（on a self-regulatory basis）的基础上得以解决，前提是各机构主动担当、严于律己。由此可知，企业的自我约束与行业自律是应对黑暗模式的关键所在，故［B］businesses\' self-discipline 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］new legal requirements（新的法律要求）与［C］strict regulatory standards（严格的监管标准）均与末段强调的非强制性“self-regulatory（自我监管/自律）”机制相悖；［D］consumers\' safety awareness（消费者的安全意识）将责任主体由“商界/企业（business community / organizations）”偷换为“消费者”。' WHERE id = '80bb9c86-3e99-5a9c-851b-147b1bfe8ae5'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best heading [A]-[G] for paragraph (41):', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Make It a Habit", "content": "Make It a Habit"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Don\'t Go It Alone", "content": "Don\'t Go It Alone"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Start Low, Go Slow", "content": "Start Low, Go Slow"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Talk With Your Doctor", "content": "Talk With Your Doctor"}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "Listen to Your Body", "content": "Listen to Your Body"}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "Go Through the Motions", "content": "Go Through the Motions"}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "Round Out Your Routine", "content": "Round Out Your Routine"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［定位/考点］段落主旨匹配（第二段）。\n［解题思路］第二段开篇即告诫恢复锻炼者“切勿试图直接回到中断前的运动量”，随后列举步行（从每天 3 英里减至隔天半英里）、高尔夫（18 洞减为 9 洞）以及举重（减至 5 磅哑铃 1 组）的具体减量方案，并总结指出应循序渐进地增加运动时长、距离与强度（Increase time, distance, and intensity gradually）。［C］Start Low, Go Slow（低起步，慢慢来）精准概括全段主旨。\n［错项排除］其中 Start Low 对应段首“先降低初始运动基线（reduce activity）”，Go Slow 对应段中“逐步递增强度（gradually）”，可排除侧重身体反馈监测的［E］Listen to Your Body 及聚焦坚持养成习惯的［A］Make It a Habit。' WHERE id = '8e19c856-54b0-5bdb-a47f-4e642c255fbb'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best heading [A]-[G] for paragraph (42):', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Make It a Habit", "content": "Make It a Habit"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Don\'t Go It Alone", "content": "Don\'t Go It Alone"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Start Low, Go Slow", "content": "Start Low, Go Slow"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Talk With Your Doctor", "content": "Talk With Your Doctor"}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "Listen to Your Body", "content": "Listen to Your Body"}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "Go Through the Motions", "content": "Go Through the Motions"}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "Round Out Your Routine", "content": "Round Out Your Routine"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'E', explanation = E'［定位/考点］段落主旨匹配（第3段）。\n［解题思路］第三段围绕运动者的身体反应提出建议：如果喘得太厉害，就停下来；如果\n\n没有不良反应，就可以多运动一会儿；并对一些严重的症状保持警惕，如果不适的症状过于明显，那么\n\n需要立即寻求治疗。可见，第三段建议运动者时刻关注自己的身体状况，运动时要根据身体的不同反\n\n应来调整运动量，E项“倾听身体的声音”准确概括该段主旨，其中Listen to与段中stay alert to近义，段\n\n中的 breathing feel / feeling symptoms 等是 your body 的具体体现。\n\n［错项排除］C项Go Slow虽与段中back off / Go easier所传达的"停下来"或"慢慢来"之意相符，\n\n但②句明确指出如果运动时感觉良好，可以增长运动时间或者提高运动的速度。可见，第三段并非一\n\n味强调“要从低基础开始慢慢加码”，而更侧重于强调“根据身体的反应来调整运动的强度和节奏”，故\n\n可排除C项。D项的Doctor虽与段中末句的medical attention语义相关，但本段末句仅针对严重的身\n\n体症状提议“立即寻求治疗"，并未明确指出要“与医生交谈”,D项无法正确概括段意，故排除。' WHERE id = '6ba926eb-48b3-5ad9-b358-083e0a9716d4'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best heading [A]-[G] for paragraph (43):', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Make It a Habit", "content": "Make It a Habit"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Don\'t Go It Alone", "content": "Don\'t Go It Alone"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Start Low, Go Slow", "content": "Start Low, Go Slow"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Talk With Your Doctor", "content": "Talk With Your Doctor"}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "Listen to Your Body", "content": "Listen to Your Body"}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "Go Through the Motions", "content": "Go Through the Motions"}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "Round Out Your Routine", "content": "Round Out Your Routine"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［定位/考点］段落主旨匹配（第4段）。\n［解题思路］第四段首先点明坚持不懈是增强体力、耐力和毅力的关键因素，随后提出具\n\n体可行的建议“每天步行十分钟”并说明原因。由此可见，第四段强调运动不在时长和强度，而在于每\n\n天的坚持，也就是说要将运动变成每天的习惯。A项契合本段段意，故正确。\n\n［错项排除］C项的Go Slow所体现的“慢慢来”看似是段中the easiest"最简单的”之意的体现，\n\n但本段重在强调将“每天十分钟运动”这一运动方式的简单易行、可坚持，而非强调“要慢慢增加运动强\n\n度"，故排除C项。G项的Round Out"完善"之意虽然与段中的a good starts a great first step所传递的\n\n“步行可以作为其他运动形式的补充和过渡”之意相近，但本段段末彰显“步行”的好处，是为了例证“每\n\n天运动十分钟”这一建议的可操作性，G项“完善你的常规锻炼”无法概括本段主旨，故排除。' WHERE id = 'ff6d0e7f-bcac-576c-a207-5765b884d0e7'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best heading [A]-[G] for paragraph (44):', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Make It a Habit", "content": "Make It a Habit"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Don\'t Go It Alone", "content": "Don\'t Go It Alone"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Start Low, Go Slow", "content": "Start Low, Go Slow"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Talk With Your Doctor", "content": "Talk With Your Doctor"}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "Listen to Your Body", "content": "Listen to Your Body"}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "Go Through the Motions", "content": "Go Through the Motions"}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "Round Out Your Routine", "content": "Round Out Your Routine"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'F', explanation = E'［定位/考点］段落主旨匹配（第5段）。\n［解题思路］第五段观点鲜明，呈“总一分”的论证模式，围绕“练习动作”这一中心话题展\n\n开。首句先引出中心话题“练习动作”，随后以击球、划船、游泳等运动为例，具体解释如何在不具备相\n\n关器械或条件的情况下练习动作，末句指出练习动作的益处。F项“练习动作”精确概括本段段意，其\n\n中,Go Through近义复现段中的practice, Motions近义复现段中的moves。\n\n［错项排除］G项的Round Out、Routine虽然与段中的prime、moves近义，但第五段侧重强调在\n\n不能去打球、划船或游泳的情况下，练习击球、划桨和游泳等动作，以调动运动状态，且prime强调“这些\n\n练习会使肌肉为恢复运动做好准备”，并非指完善锻炼组合，G项无法准确概括段落大意。' WHERE id = '1f2f80ab-95f7-5c2f-8295-419d6cf5be38'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best heading [A]-[G] for paragraph (45):', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Make It a Habit", "content": "Make It a Habit"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Don\'t Go It Alone", "content": "Don\'t Go It Alone"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Start Low, Go Slow", "content": "Start Low, Go Slow"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Talk With Your Doctor", "content": "Talk With Your Doctor"}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "Listen to Your Body", "content": "Listen to Your Body"}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "Go Through the Motions", "content": "Go Through the Motions"}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "Round Out Your Routine", "content": "Round Out Your Routine"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［定位/考点］段落主旨匹配（第六段）。\n［解题思路］第六段首句点明与他人共同锻炼的双重益处——既能形成相互监督与约束（keep you accountable），又能增添运动乐趣，从而提高长期坚持的概率；随后针对疫情期间的具体实践提出两类变通方案：选择高尔夫、网球、散步等可保持社交距离的结伴运动，或在居家锻炼时借助电话、FaceTime 及线上实时健身课程与亲友连线互动。［B］Don\'t Go It Alone（不要独自锻炼/不要单独行动）全面概括了上述所有建议。\n［错项排除］段中所提到的 online / livestream classes 只是实现“与他人互动锻炼”的技术手段，并不涉及医疗咨询（［D］Talk With Your Doctor）或多元化组合训练（［G］Round Out Your Routine）。' WHERE id = 'c09fee0f-40d2-57e0-a133-2c9236dca53c'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'In the quest for the perfect lawn, homeowners across the country are taking a shortcut—and it is the environment that is paying the price. About eight million square metres of plastic grass is sold each year but opposition has now spread to the highest gardening circles. The Chelsea Flower Show has banned fake grass from this year\'s event, declaring it to be not part of its ethos. The Royal Horticultural Society (RHS), which runs the annual show in west London, says it has introduced the ban because of the damage plastic grass does to the environment and biodiversity.\n\nEd Horne, of the RHS, said: "We launched our sustainability strategy last year and fake grass is just not in line with our ethos and views on plastic. We recommend using real grass because of its environmental benefits, which include supporting wildlife, alleviating flooding and cooling the environment."\n\nThe RHS\'s decision comes as campaigners try to raise awareness of the problems fake grass causes. A Twitter account, which claims to "cut through the greenwash" of artificial grass, already has more than 20,000 followers. It is trying to encourage people to sign two petitions, one calling for a ban on the sale of plastic grass and another calling for an "ecological damage" tax on such lawns. They have gathered 7,276 and 11,282 signatures.\n\nHowever, supporters of fake grass point out that there is also an environmental impact with natural lawns, which need mowing and therefore usually consume electricity or petrol. The industry also points out that real grass requires considerable amounts of water, weed killer or other treatments and that people who lay fake grass tend to use their garden more. The industry also claims that people who lay fake grass spend an average of £500 on trees or shrubs for their garden, which provides habitat for insects.\n\nIn response to another petition last year about banning fake lawns, which gathered 30,000 signatures, the government responded that it has "no plans to ban the use of artificial grass."\n\nIt added: "We prefer to help people and organizations make the right choice rather than legislating on such matters. However, the use of artificial grass must comply with the legal and policy safeguards in place to protect biodiversity and ensure sustainable drainage, while measures such as the strengthened biodiversity duty should serve to encourage public authorities to consider sustainable alternatives."' WHERE id = '7d25728e-7009-5ba8-8311-b2bb304a2a43'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'It\'s easy to dismiss as absurd the federal government\'s ideas for plugging the chronic funding gap of our national parks. Can anyone really think it\'s a good idea to allow Amazon deliveries to your tent in Yosemite or food trucks to line up under the redwood trees at Sequoia National Park?\n\nBut the government is right about one thing: U.S. national parks are in crisis. Collectively, they have a maintenance backlog of more than $12 billion. Roads, trails, restrooms, visitor centers and other infrastructure are crumbling.\n\nBut privatizing and commercializing the campgrounds would not be a cure-all. Campgrounds are a tiny portion of the overall infrastructure backlog, and businesses in the parks hand over, on average, only about 5% of their revenues to the National Park Service. Moreover, increased privatization would certainly undercut one of the major reasons why 300 million visitors come to the parks each year: to enjoy nature and get a break from the commercial drumbeat that overwhelms daily life.\n\nThe real problem is that the parks have been chronically starved of funding. We conducted a comprehensive survey examining how U.S. residents view their national parks, and we found that Americans place a very high value on them—whether or not they actually visit them. The peer-reviewed economic survey of 700 U.S. taxpayers, conducted by mail and internet, also found that people would be willing to pay a significant amount of money to make sure the parks and their programs are kept intact. Some 81% of respondents said they would be willing to pay additional taxes for the next 10 years to avoid any cuts to the national parks.\n\nThe national parks provide great value to U.S. residents both as places to escape and as symbols of nature. On top of this, they produce value from their extensive educational programs, their positive impact on the climate through carbon sequestration, their contribution to our cultural and artistic life, and of course through tourism. The parks also help keep America\'s past alive, working with thousands of local jurisdictions around the country to protect historical sites—including Ellis Island and Gettysburg—and to bring the stories of these places to life.\n\nThe parks do all this on a shoestring. Congress allocates only $3 billion a year to the national park system—an amount that has been flat since 2001 (in inflation-adjusted dollars) with the exception of a onetime boost in 2009 as part of the Obama stimulus package. Meanwhile, the number of annual visitors has increased by more than 50% since 1980, and now stands at 330 million visitors per year.' WHERE id = 'c595f087-f1cd-5ec1-a8f2-8287ae4c2458'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'The Internet may be changing merely what we remember, not our capacity to do so, suggests Columbia University psychology professor Betsy Sparrow. In 2011, Sparrow led a study in which participants were asked to record 40 factoids in a computer ("an ostrich\'s eye is bigger than its brain," for example). Half of the participants were told the information would be erased, while the other half were told it would be saved. Guess what? The latter group made no effort to recall the information when quizzed on it later, because they knew they could find it on their computers. In the same study, a group was asked to remember both the information and the folders it was stored in. They didn\'t remember the information, but they remembered how to find the folders. In other words, human memory is not deteriorating but "adapting to new communications technology," Sparrow says.\n\nIn a very practical way, the Internet is becoming an external hard drive for our memories, a process known as "cognitive offloading." Traditionally, this role was fulfilled by data banks, libraries, and other humans. Your father may never remember birthdays because your mother does, for instance. Some worry that this is having a destructive effect on society, but Sparrow sees an upside. Perhaps, she suggests, the trend will change our approach to learning from a focus on individual facts and memorization to an emphasis on more conceptual thinking—something that is not available on the Internet. "I personally have never seen all that much intellectual value in memorizing things," Sparrow says, adding that we haven\'t lost our ability to do it.\n\nStill other experts say it\'s too soon to understand how the Internet affects our brains. "There is no experimental evidence showing that it interferes with our ability to focus, for instance," wrote psychologists Christopher Chabris and Daniel J. Simons. And surfing the web exercised the brain more than reading did among computer-savvy older adults in a 2008 study involving 24 participants at the Semel Institute for Neuroscience and Human Behavior at the University of California, Los Angeles. "There may be costs associated with our increased reliance on the Internet, but I\'d have to imagine that overall the benefits are going to outweigh those costs," observes psychology professor Benjamin Storm. "It seems pretty clear that memory is changing, but is it changing for the better? At this point, we don\'t know."' WHERE id = 'ac3b8992-ddf1-5679-a19b-43e41c84a443'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'Teenagers are paradoxical. That\'s a mild and detached way of saying something that parents often express with considerably stronger language. But the paradox is scientific as well as personal. In adolescence, helpless and dependent children who have relied on grown-ups for just about everything become independent people who can take care of themselves and help each other. At the same time, once cheerful and compliant children become rebellious teenage risk-takers.\n\nA new study published in the journal Child Development, by Eveline Crone of the University of Leiden and colleagues, suggests that the positive and negative sides of teenagers go hand in hand. The study is part of a new wave of thinking about adolescence. For a long time, scientists and policy makers concentrated on the idea that teenagers were a problem that needed to be solved. The new work emphasizes that adolescence is a time of opportunity as well as risk.\n\nThe researchers studied "prosocial" and rebellious traits in more than 200 children and young adults, ranging from 11 to 28 years old. The participants filled out questionnaires about how often they did things that were altruistic and positive, like sacrificing their own interests to help a friend, or rebellious and negative, like getting drunk or staying out late.\n\nOther studies have shown that rebellious behavior increases as you become a teenager and then fades away as you grow older. But the new study shows that, interestingly, the same pattern holds for prosocial behavior. Teenagers were more likely than younger children or adults to report that they did things like unselfishly help a friend. Most significantly, there was a positive correlation between prosociality and rebelliousness. The teenagers who were more rebellious were also more likely to help others. The good and bad sides of adolescence seem to develop together.\n\nIs there some common factor that underlies these apparently contradictory developments? One idea is that teenage behavior is related to what researchers call "reward sensitivity." Decision-making always involves balancing rewards and risks, benefits and costs. "Reward sensitivity" measures how much reward it takes to outweigh risk.\n\nTeenagers are particularly sensitive to social rewards—winning the game, impressing a new friend, getting that boy to notice you. Reward sensitivity, like prosocial behavior and risk-taking, seems to go up in adolescence and then down again as we age. Somehow, when you hit 30, the chance that something exciting and new will happen at that party just doesn\'t seem to outweigh the effort of getting up off the couch.' WHERE id = '34109d29-7b4c-588c-b5f8-0e0c3603004c'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [1] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "purchase", "content": "purchase"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "profit", "content": "profit"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "connection", "content": "connection"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "bet", "content": "bet"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义与名词固定搭配。\n［解题思路］首句描摹了当今小企业主普遍面临的处境：虽然公司目前“盈利状况良好（making a nice [1]）”，但仍需寻找进一步提升营收的突破口。profit（利润、盈利）构成 make a profit 地道搭配，契合企业管理语境，故选［B］。\n［错项排除］［A］purchase（购买、采购）虽可构成 make a purchase，但动作发出者为小企业主而非普通消费者；［C］connection（联系、人脉）与［D］bet（打赌、押注）均偏离商业营收经营语境。' WHERE id = '6b01af66-a837-5487-bd73-27c363e2059e'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [2] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "define", "content": "define"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "predict", "content": "predict"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "prioritize", "content": "prioritize"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "appreciate", "content": "appreciate"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义衔接与动词辨析。\n［解题思路］空格句承接首句“提升公司收益”的诉求，指出解决之道在于通过组建增长团队来“优先考虑、重点推进（[2] growth）”业务增长，并与后句“集中力量专注寻找增长途径”构成手段与目的呼应，故选［C］prioritize。\n［错项排除］［A］define（下定义）宾语为 growth 而非增长团队，组建团队不能用来定义增长；［B］predict（预测）仅止步于预判数字，未体现主动推动业绩增长的实际行动；［D］appreciate（欣赏、感激）不合动宾逻辑。' WHERE id = '5a2b88db-54e7-5050-9345-4bc823bb2ad6'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [3] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "exclusively", "content": "exclusively"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "temporarily", "content": "temporarily"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "potentially", "content": "potentially"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "initially", "content": "initially"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义与副词词义辨析。\n［解题思路］增长团队汇聚跨部门成员并借用协作力量，目的就是为了“专心致志、专门地（[3]）专注于寻找增长方法”。exclusively（排他地、专门地）呼应上句 prioritize growth，体现整合全公司力量攻关核心目标，故选［A］。\n［错项排除］［B］temporarily（暂时地、临时地）与企业长期寻求业绩突破的战略定位矛盾；［C］potentially（潜在地）及［D］initially（最初、起初）均无法传达增长团队专注且单一的核心职能特征。' WHERE id = 'bc2a603d-c359-516e-9ff2-c1cd98a2414f'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [4] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "experiment", "content": "experiment"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "proposal", "content": "proposal"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "debate", "content": "debate"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "example", "content": "example"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］段际例证逻辑与名词辨析。\n［解题思路］第二段首句以 Let\'s look at a real-world [4]. 引出下文 BitTorrent 公司的真实运营历程，说明公司在成立增长团队前后由停滞转向增长的历程。example（例子、范例）自然承上启下引出具体企业案例，故选［D］。\n［错项排除］［A］experiment（科学实验、尝试）侧重主动设计的试验，而下文陈述的是 BitTorrent 公司客观经历的发展沿革；［B］proposal（提议）与［C］debate（辩论）均未在下文案例中有所体现。' WHERE id = '5e21fc41-cd8d-5dbc-acaa-c6ba14234c34'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [5] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "identical", "content": "identical"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "marginal", "content": "marginal"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "provisional", "content": "provisional"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "traditional", "content": "traditional"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义与形容词辨析。\n［解题思路］空格形容词修饰 departments，指出在组建跨学科增长团队前，50 名员工分别在工程、营销和产品研发等“传统的、常规职能分工下的（[5]）”部门各司其职。traditional 与上段创新的“增长团队”构成鲜明对比，故选［D］。\n［错项排除］［A］identical（完全相同的）违背常识，工程、营销与研发职能迥异；［B］marginal（边缘的、次要的）曲解部门地位，三大基础业务部门并非无足轻重；［C］provisional（临时的）意为临时拼凑部门，与“成立多年直至 2012 年才遭遇瓶颈”矛盾。' WHERE id = 'f1e61dde-904b-57d3-8ea2-872913629e30'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [6] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "rumor", "content": "rumor"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "secret", "content": "secret"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "myth", "content": "myth"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "problem", "content": "problem"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文因果衔接与名词辨析。\n［解题思路］前句指出旧模式一直运转良好，直到 2012 年增长陷入停滞；紧接着 The [6] was that... 点明导致停滞的症结所在——过多用户始终停留在免费基础版。problem（问题、症结）精准剖析瓶颈根源，故选［D］。\n［错项排除］［A］rumor（谣言）若成立则增长停滞并非事实，与下文团队着手解决认知问题相悖；［B］secret（秘诀）通常对应成功经验而非停滞原因；［C］myth（谬论、迷思）无法充当后文客观停滞原因的主语。' WHERE id = '7410f0ab-abd7-5761-8d7a-8ffe129252d8'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [7] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "despite", "content": "despite"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "unlike", "content": "unlike"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "through", "content": "through"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "besides", "content": "besides"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内让步转折逻辑与介词辨析。\n［解题思路］状语部分提及“对高级付费版进行了诸多改进（improvements to the premium, paid version）”，主句则指出“却依然鲜少有人升级付费”。前后构成强烈的让步转折反差，despite（尽管、虽然）接名词短语引出让步条件，故选［A］。\n［错项排除］［B］unlike（不像……）后接对比对象而非具体事实事件；［C］through（通过、凭借）表工具或手段，造成“改进反而导致无人升级”的逻辑谬误；［D］besides（除……之外）表补充递进，无法表现正反落差。' WHERE id = 'bf59e906-2fdd-52cd-a4cb-42795d5ed2c8'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [8] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "moreover", "content": "moreover"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "however", "content": "however"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "therefore", "content": "therefore"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "again", "content": "again"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］段际转折逻辑与逻辑副词辨析。\n［解题思路］第二段讲述 BitTorrent 公司自 2012 年起遭遇营收增长瓶颈与免费用户转化停滞，第三段开篇则引入一位富有革新精神的项目营销经理上任并彻底逆转局势。前后两段呈现明显的“困局→转机”强烈反差，however（然而、可是）作插入语置于主从结构间实现段落自然转折，故选［B］。\n［错项排除］［A］moreover（此外、而且）引导同向递进补充；［C］therefore（因此、从而）引导顺推因果关系；［D］again（再一次）仅表示重复发生，三者均无法表现“陷入停滞”到“局面彻底改观”的逆转态势。' WHERE id = '2b7193a8-0862-5469-a741-de7624cc12f9'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [9] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "inspected", "content": "inspected"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "created", "content": "created"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "expanded", "content": "expanded"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "reformed", "content": "reformed"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义呼应与动词辨析。\n［解题思路］革新营销经理上任后采取了关键行动：先是“[9] a growth team”，随后激发出全新视角。回溯前两段可知，此前公司并未设立过增长团队，因此此处应为“创建、组建（created）”该团队，并与“激发出全新视角”形成动作顺承，故选［B］。\n［错项排除］［A］inspected（视察、检查）前提是团队业已存在，与前文“组建增长团队之前（before a growth team existed）”直接冲突；［C］expanded（扩大）与［D］reformed（改革）同样预设该团队早已设立，不合文意。' WHERE id = 'e8885d62-abad-5260-9d07-055e5d3102fb'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [10] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "cultural", "content": "cultural"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "objective", "content": "objective"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "fresh", "content": "fresh"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "personal", "content": "personal"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义与形容词辨析。\n［解题思路］前文强调该经理“富有革新精神（innovative）”，随后团队“以营销视角审视原本属于工程范畴的困扰”。这正表明增长团队激发了公司急需的“崭新的、清新的（[10]）”视角，打破单一部门壁垒，故选［C］fresh。\n［错项排除］［A］cultural（文化的）在文中并无企业文化建设的相关佐证；［B］objective（客观的）虽无明显错误但未能呼应“从营销跨界审视工程难题”的新颖视角；［D］personal（个人的）与跨部门集体协作宗旨相悖。' WHERE id = '24700cfa-84ad-5f52-a70f-ccc413a240bb'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [11] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "end", "content": "end"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "burden", "content": "burden"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "lack", "content": "lack"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "decrease", "content": "decrease"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义衔接与名词辨析。\n［解题思路］从全新视角审视后发现，用户升级的“[11]（匮乏、不足）”并非源于产品质量缺陷，而是大部分客户根本不知道高级版的存在。lack 与前段 few people were making the upgrade 精准呼应，故选［C］。\n［错项排除］［A］end（终结）暗示升级已彻底停止，与下文转机及升级暴涨相悖；［B］burden（负担）与文意“无人升级”相反；［D］decrease（下降）若无基数对比易生歧义，原文强调长期以来鲜有人知、升级严重不足而非单纯速率下跌。' WHERE id = '1820853c-f291-5aa4-bd49-614da3b44afb'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [12] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "policy", "content": "policy"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "suggestion", "content": "suggestion"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "purpose", "content": "purpose"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "insight", "content": "insight"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］段际指代衔接与名词词义辨析。\n［解题思路］第四段首句 Armed with this [12] 中，this 回指第三段刚刚揭示的深层症结（客户压根不知晓付费版及其功能）。掌握这一“深刻认识、洞见（insight）”后，营销与工程团队联手精准破局，故选［D］。\n［错项排除］［A］policy（政策、方针）、［B］suggestion（建议）以及［C］purpose（目的）在第三段中均未提及；前段着力于视角的转换与问题根源的洞察，故只有 insight 严丝合缝。' WHERE id = '72f4a693-dc06-5d8c-8460-3836615841a0'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [13] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "contributing", "content": "contributing"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "allocating", "content": "allocating"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "promoting", "content": "promoting"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "transferring", "content": "transferring"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义与动宾搭配。\n［解题思路］针对“客户根本不知道高级付费版”的认知盲区，营销与工程团队联手向免费基础版用户突出地“[13]（推广、宣传）”高级版（prominently promoting the premium version to users of the free version），以提升市场知晓度，故选［C］。\n［错项排除］［A］contributing（捐赠）多指慈善或非营利性赠送，不适用商业软件推销；［B］allocating（分配、划拨）常用于分配资源份额；［D］transferring（转移）不能与推广认知语境匹配。' WHERE id = '2a7f6e8f-bd63-5962-8d19-b00c86866e1a'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [14] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "As a result", "content": "As a result"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "At any rate", "content": "At any rate"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "By the way", "content": "By the way"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "In a sense", "content": "In a sense"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句间因果逻辑与短语辨析。\n［解题思路］前句指出两部门联手大举向免费用户推广高级版、提高产品知名度，紧接空格句写明市场回报：“升级量呈爆炸式增长，营收跃升 92%”。前因后果逻辑链条明确，As a result（结果、因此）顺理成章，故选［A］。\n［错项排除］［B］At any rate（无论如何）常用于让步后强调重点；［C］By the way（顺便提一句）用于引出偏离主线的话题；［D］In a sense（在某种意义上）表限定程度，均不表因果。' WHERE id = '07dd3ca6-ee51-5518-adc7-0fd1a07a150b'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [15] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "unite", "content": "unite"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "finance", "content": "finance"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "follow", "content": "follow"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "choose", "content": "choose"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义与领导力语境。\n［解题思路］第五段探讨增长团队成功的核心保障：必须拥有一位强有力的领导者，能够“[15]（团结、凝聚）”来自不同部门的跨学科团队，并激励成员不断改进。unite 准确贴合 interdisciplinary（跨学科/跨部门）团队协作需求，故选［A］。\n［错项排除］［B］finance（为……提供资金）偏离领导者日常统筹职责；［C］follow（追随）主被动关系颠倒；［D］choose（挑选）在团队既已建成的语境下无法延续“领导团队持续进步”的动作连贯性。' WHERE id = '8aae2718-fba1-5093-b1a3-cfa686cb36fb'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [16] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "share", "content": "share"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "identify", "content": "identify"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "divide", "content": "divide"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "broaden", "content": "broaden"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内并列动作流与动词辨析。\n［解题思路］句内三个并列动宾结构描绘领导者的管理闭环：“[16] 目标领域 → 设定清晰目标（set clear goals）→ 制定实现时间表（establish a time frame）”。作为首要前置步骤，领导者应首先“识别、明确（identify）”核心发力领域，故选［B］。\n［错项排除］［A］share（分享、分担）削弱领导者明确方向的职责；［C］divide（划分、分割）容易导致跨部门重新割裂；［D］broaden（拓宽）与聚焦重点发力（target area）矛盾。' WHERE id = 'dfc7172a-6f82-5764-a72e-70b853f7738f'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [17] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "announcement", "content": "announcement"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "assessment", "content": "assessment"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "adjustment", "content": "adjustment"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "accomplishment", "content": "accomplishment"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义与形近抽象名词辨析。\n［解题思路］明确目标之后，团队需要设立这些目标得以“完成、达成（[17]）”的时间期限（a time frame for the accomplishment of these goals）。accomplishment 强调按期将目标转化为实际成果，符合目标管理闭环，故选［D］。\n［错项排除］［A］announcement（宣布）是一瞬间即可完成的公告动作，无需设置跨度时间框架；［B］assessment（评估）与［C］adjustment（调整）均非“设定清晰目标”后规划时间表的终极指向。' WHERE id = '60e3d1ac-8f98-5967-8639-26c925388864'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [18] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "famous", "content": "famous"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "responsible", "content": "responsible"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "available", "content": "available"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "respectable", "content": "respectable"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内固定搭配与形容词辨析。\n［解题思路］末段首句承接领导者职责继续说明：增长团队领导者也“[18]（负责、承担……职责）”保持团队专注前进，避开干扰因素（responsible for keeping the team moving forward）。be responsible for 精准表达岗位职责，故选［B］。\n［错项排除］［A］famous（以……闻名）仅描述外部声誉，文段重点阐述团队内部管理职能；［C］available（有空的、可用的）通常不接动名词作职责修饰；［D］respectable（值得尊敬的）语义与语境职能分工无关。' WHERE id = 'db4c3469-cc74-5a7c-92c1-a96cff37980b'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [19] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Before", "content": "Before"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Once", "content": "Once"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "While", "content": "While"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Unless", "content": "Unless"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内让步转折逻辑与从属连词辨析。\n［解题思路］从句意为“极具吸引力的新点子往往可能使团队分心（attractive new ideas can be distracting）”，主句则指出“但团队领导者必须能敏锐辨别何时这些点子无助于当前核心目标并果断将其暂缓搁置”。主从句呈现明显的让步对比关系，While（尽管、虽然）置于句首引导让步状语从句，故选［C］。\n［错项排除］［A］Before（在……之前）无端改变事件时序；［B］Once（一旦……就）表达触发的充分条件；［D］Unless（除非）逻辑反向，否定了“新点子客观上既诱人又容易令人分心”的两面事实。' WHERE id = '60d3fd7c-cd61-5165-b256-2ef05b499103'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [20] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "serve", "content": "serve"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "limit", "content": "limit"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "summarize", "content": "summarize"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "alter", "content": "alter"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义与熟词僻义搭配。\n［解题思路］领导者须敏锐识别那些看似诱人但实际上“无助于、不符合（don\'t [20]）”当前核心目标的新点子，并及时将其暂缓搁置（put on the back burner）。serve the current goal 意为“服务于/有助于当前目标”，故选［A］。\n［错项排除］［B］limit（限制）若带入 don\'t limit 则成为“当点子没有限制目标时将其搁置”，逻辑自相矛盾；［C］summarize（总结）与［D］alter（改变）均不能顺畅衔接“因分散注意力而必须暂时搁置”的决策理由。' WHERE id = 'b241ffbb-fd95-5b0d-aa4a-082227fbb263'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The RHS thinks that plastic grass', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "is harmful to the environment", "content": "is harmful to the environment"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "is a hot topic in gardening circles", "content": "is a hot topic in gardening circles"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "is overpraised in the annual show", "content": "is overpraised in the annual show"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "is ruining the view of west London", "content": "is ruining the view of west London"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］细节事实题（机构态度观点定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 RHS 及 plastic grass 定位至第一段末句及第二段。文中明确指出皇家园艺学会（RHS）禁止人造草坪参加切尔西花展，原因正是塑料草坪对环境与生物多样性造成破坏（the damage plastic grass does to the environment and biodiversity / Artificial grass... is just not in line with our ethos）。由此可知 RHS 认为塑料草坪对环境有害，故［A］is harmful to the environment 正确。\n［错项排除］［B］园艺界热点话题偏离禁令背后的实质批判；［C］在花展中被过度赞美与“已遭官方禁止参展”直接相反；［D］毁坏伦敦西部景观属于偷换概念，RHS 是从生态与生物多样性层面抵制，而非仅仅抱怨视觉景观。' WHERE id = 'd574466f-c1c0-5d3a-8540-07b3e4967597'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The petitions mentioned in Paragraph 3 reveal the campaigners\'', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "disappointment with the RHS", "content": "disappointment with the RHS"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "resistance to fake grass use", "content": "resistance to fake grass use"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "anger over the proposed tax", "content": "anger over the proposed tax"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "concern about real grass supply", "content": "concern about real grass supply"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］细节事实题（行为动机与态度定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 petitions 与 Paragraph 3 定位至第三段。该段指出，宣传反对人造草坪的活动者发起两份请愿书——分别呼吁“禁止出售塑料草坪”以及“对此类草坪征收生态破坏税”，且目前已征集大量签名。这种明确寻求禁售和征税的做法直接揭示了环保活动人士对使用人造草坪的抵制，故［B］resistance to fake grass use 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］对 RHS 感到失望与文意相反，请愿活动恰恰与 RHS 的禁展立场站在同一阵线；［C］对拟议征税感到愤怒正反颠倒，税收是请愿者主动呼吁出台的惩罚举措；［D］对天然草坪供应的担忧属无中生有。' WHERE id = 'dcf71bac-37e8-5096-90af-fd6953671a24'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'In Paragraph 4, supporters of fake grass point out', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "the necessity to lower the costs of fake grass", "content": "the necessity to lower the costs of fake grass"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "the disadvantages of growing real grass", "content": "the disadvantages of growing real grass"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "the way to take care of artificial lawns", "content": "the way to take care of artificial lawns"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "the challenges of insect habitat protection", "content": "the challenges of insect habitat protection"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］细节事实题（立场论据定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 Paragraph 4 与 supporters of fake grass 定位至第四段。该段开篇以 However 转折引出人造草坪支持者的反驳理由：天然草坪同样会带来环境影响（environmental impact with natural lawns），因为它们需要割草机修剪进而消耗电力或汽油，还需要耗费大量水资源、除草剂及其他化学护理（considerable amounts of water, weed killer or other treatments）。可见他们指出了种植天然草坪的缺点，故［B］the disadvantages of growing real grass 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］降低人造草坪成本在第四段未曾涉及；［C］护理人造草坪的方法属于偏离话题；［D］昆虫栖息地保护的挑战与第四段末句“铺人造草坪者平均花 500 英镑种树灌木，反而为昆虫提供了栖息地”矛盾。' WHERE id = 'd4276f57-a143-57de-a0fe-839d9cda9c10'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'What would the government do with regard to artificial grass?', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Urge legislation to restrict its use.", "content": "Urge legislation to restrict its use."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Take measures to guarantee its quality.", "content": "Take measures to guarantee its quality."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Remind its users to obey existing rules.", "content": "Remind its users to obey existing rules."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Replace it with sustainable alternatives.", "content": "Replace it with sustainable alternatives."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］细节理解题（官方回应与政策导向）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 government 与 artificial grass 定位至最后两段。第五段首先明确政府回应称“目前无计划立法禁止人造草坪”；第六段进一步补充：政府更倾向于引导民众自主作出正确选择而非强制立法，“不过人造草坪的使用必须遵守现行旨在保护生物多样性及确保可持续排水的法律与政策保障条款（must comply with the legal and policy safeguards in place）”。可见政府虽不禁售，但会提醒并要求使用者遵守现行规定，故［C］Remind its users to obey existing rules 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］推动立法限制与第五段“no plans to ban”和“rather than legislating”相悖；［B］确保人造草坪质量未在文中出现；［D］强行以替代品取代与“不强制立法、仅鼓励公共机构考虑”的温和政策不符。' WHERE id = 'd7f1bdc3-aaa5-585d-a946-758bd816de56'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'It can be learned from the text that fake grass', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "is being improved continuously", "content": "is being improved continuously"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "has seen a market share decline", "content": "has seen a market share decline"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "is becoming increasingly affordable", "content": "is becoming increasingly affordable"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "has been a controversial product", "content": "has been a controversial product"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］主旨推断题（全文争议脉络梳理）。\n［精准定位］纵览全文，首段与第二段介绍切尔西花展和 RHS 严厉抨击并封杀塑料草坪；第三段描述网络活动者征集万人签名要求禁售征税；第四段则展示行业与支持者辩称真草坪耗水耗电且人造草坪业主也栽树护虫；第五、六段呈现政府不加禁止但重申合规的折中回应。由此可见，人造草坪在业内与社会层面引发剧烈分歧，是一种颇具争议的产品，故［D］has been a controversial product 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］产品不断改进未在原文着墨；［B］市场份额下滑与首段每年仍卖出约 800 万平方米的表述不符；［C］变得愈发便宜未有提及。' WHERE id = 'ef17a714-ee83-5d96-8746-2d6643be283f'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'What problem are U.S. national parks faced with?', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Decline of business profits.", "content": "Decline of business profits."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Inadequate commercialization.", "content": "Inadequate commercialization."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Lack of transportation services.", "content": "Lack of transportation services."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Poorly maintained infrastructure.", "content": "Poorly maintained infrastructure."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］细节事实题（困境梳理定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干提问美国国家公园面临的问题，定位至第二段。该段明确指出美国国家公园正陷入危机，累积了高达逾 120 亿美元的维护积压账目（a maintenance backlog of more than $12 billion），道路、步道、洗手间、游客中心及其他各类基础设施正在坍塌毁坏（crumbling）。可见核心困境在于基础设施维护严重不足、破败不堪，故［D］Poorly maintained infrastructure 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］商业利润下滑在第三段仅提及公园内商业企业上交约 5% 收入，并非企业利润下降；［B］商业化程度不够恰恰是作者批判的政府错误思路，而非实际根源；［C］缺少交通服务偷换了“道路（Roads）破损”的概念。' WHERE id = '8a009fe7-c112-5a5f-967b-d811e21aedb1'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Increased privatization of the campgrounds may', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "spoil visitor experience", "content": "spoil visitor experience"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "help preserve nature", "content": "help preserve nature"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "bring operational pressure", "content": "bring operational pressure"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "boost visits to parks", "content": "boost visits to parks"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］观点细节与因果推断题。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 privatization of the campgrounds 定位至第三段末句。文中明确反驳营地商业化与私有化提议，指出扩大私有化必将破坏每年吸引 3 亿游客前来的主要初衷之一（undercut one of the major reasons...）——即让人们亲近自然并暂时远离充斥日常生活的喧嚣商业气息（get a break from the commercial drumbeat）。这说明过度商业私有化将败坏并破坏游客的自然体验，故［A］spoil visitor experience 正确。\n［错项排除］［B］有助于保护自然违背公园去商业化初衷；［C］带来运营压力及［D］大幅推高入园人数在第三段均未提及。' WHERE id = 'e8fbe148-fb83-54f1-8345-cead875ce715'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to Paragraph 5, most respondents in the survey would', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "go to the national parks on a regular basis", "content": "go to the national parks on a regular basis"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "advocate a bigger budget for the national parks", "content": "advocate a bigger budget for the national parks"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "agree to pay extra for the national parks", "content": "agree to pay extra for the national parks"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "support the national parks\' recent reforms", "content": "support the national parks\' recent reforms"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］细节事实题（民意调查数据定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 Paragraph 5（注意对应原文第四段核心调查部分及结构）与 respondents in the survey 定位至经同行评审的 700 名美国纳税人调查。调查显示，绝大多数民众高度重视国家公园，且愿意拿出可观资金确保公园体系完好保留；具体而言，约 81% 的受访者表示未来 10 年愿意额外缴纳附加税（willing to pay additional taxes），以避免对国家公园削减预算。这直接印证大多数受访者同意为国家公园多掏费用，故［C］agree to pay extra for the national parks 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］定期游览国家公园与文中强调“无论本人是否实际去参观（whether or not they actually visit them）都珍视其价值”相悖；［B］呼吁扩大财政预算虽接近态度但不如直接“自愿多缴税款”贴合受访者具体表态；［D］支持近期商业改革恰恰是全文极力批评的对象。' WHERE id = 'ea785cdd-0e4c-537b-8ee5-d637fcd24cdd'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The national parks are valuable in that they', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "lead the way in tourism", "content": "lead the way in tourism"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "have historical significance", "content": "have historical significance"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "sponsor research on climate", "content": "sponsor research on climate"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "provide an income for the locals", "content": "provide an income for the locals"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］细节事实题（公园多重价值梳理）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 national parks are valuable 定位至倒数第二段。该段在说明公园既是精神避风港与自然象征外，着重指出它们还携手全美成千上万地方管辖区保护历史遗迹（protect historical sites—including Ellis Island and Gettysburg），让美国的历史故事鲜活留存（keep America\'s past alive）。可见国家公园具备极其重要的历史保存价值，故［B］have historical significance 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］引领旅游业发展过度拔高（原文仅客观列举旅游创收与多种公益产出并行）；［C］资助气候研究将原文“公园通过碳汇对气候产生积极影响（positive impact on the climate through carbon sequestration）”篡改为“资助科研”；［D］为当地人创造收入偷换了“与各地协作保护古迹”的语意。' WHERE id = '7fcc348f-df57-5e97-8a4c-cc19d3dcfdfb'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'It can be concluded from the text that the national park system', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "is able to cope with staff shortages", "content": "is able to cope with staff shortages"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "is able to meet visitors\' demands", "content": "is able to meet visitors\' demands"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "is in need of a new pricing policy", "content": "is in need of a new pricing policy"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "is in need of a funding increase", "content": "is in need of a funding increase"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］主旨推断题（根源揭示与政策呼吁）。\n［精准定位］结合全文主线及第四段 The real problem is that the parks have been chronically starved of funding 与末段 The parks do all this on a shoestring 可知：国家公园长期经费拮据，国会每年仅拨款 30 亿美元（且自 2001 年起计入通胀后基本停滞，仅 2009 年有一笔一次性刺激拨款），与此同时年均游客人次却较 1980 年猛增超 50% 至 3.3 亿。由此可明确得出结论，国家公园体系亟需增加财政拨款，故［D］is in need of a funding increase 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］应对人手短缺与［B］满足游客需求均与资源见肘现状不符；［C］需要制定新定价政策偏离主题，全文批判靠商业开发变现，主张解决公共拨款长期不足问题。' WHERE id = 'aefd0e74-939f-5ae6-a570-abc604fc6e63'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Sparrow\'s study shows that with the Internet, the human brain will ________.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "analyze information in detail", "content": "analyze information in detail"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "collect information efficiently", "content": "collect information efficiently"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "switch its focus of memory", "content": "switch its focus of memory"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "extend its memory duration", "content": "extend its memory duration"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］细节事实题（实验结论定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 Sparrow\'s study 与 human brain 定位至第一段。实验中，以为电脑会保存 40 条冷知识的那组受试者事后回忆不起信息内容，却能清楚记住文件存放路径与文件夹名称（They didn\'t remember the information, but they remembered how to find the folders）。Sparrow 据此得出结论：人类记忆并未退化，而是转而记忆寻找信息的渠道。这表明在互联网时代，人脑正在切换记忆关注的重点，故［C］switch its focus of memory 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］详尽分析信息（将 factoids 偷换为深入分析）与［B］高效搜集信息均非该实验观察到的记忆存储偏移结论；［D］延长记忆时长与受试者记不住具体知识点正好相反。' WHERE id = 'ac5badd6-5b37-5218-9661-e32e46a3c373'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The process of "cognitive offloading" ________.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "helps us identify false information", "content": "helps us identify false information"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "keeps our memory from failing", "content": "keeps our memory from failing"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "enables us to classify trivial facts", "content": "enables us to classify trivial facts"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "lessens our memory burdens", "content": "lessens our memory burdens"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］细节事实题（核心概念释义定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 cognitive offloading 定位至第二段首二句。文中指出，在非常实际的意义上，互联网正在成为人类记忆的“外接硬盘（an external hard drive for our memories）”，即所谓的“认知卸载（cognitive offloading）”；过去这一外包分担角色通常由数据库、图书馆以及配偶等他人替我们记琐事（如妻子帮丈夫记生日）来承担。可见“认知卸载”把死记硬背的存储任务外包出去，从而切实减轻了人脑的记忆负担，故［D］lessens our memory burdens 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］帮助甄别虚假信息未在文中体现；［B］防止记忆力衰退曲解了“并非记忆坏掉，而是外包存储”的客观说明；［C］使我们能对琐碎事实归类将“文件夹存储位置记忆”混同为对零散知识本身加以分类。' WHERE id = '454d83ec-a71b-5c33-af70-7c22d9a8ef69'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Which of the following would Sparrow support about the Internet?', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "It may reform our learning approach.", "content": "It may reform our learning approach."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "It may impact our society negatively.", "content": "It may impact our society negatively."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "It may enhance our adaptability to technology.", "content": "It may enhance our adaptability to technology."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "It may interfere with our conceptual thinking.", "content": "It may interfere with our conceptual thinking."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］人物观点题（积极前景推论）。\n［精准定位］根据题干询问 Sparrow 对互联网积极一面的看法，定位至第二段中间部分（but Sparrow sees an upside）。Sparrow 提出，借助认知卸载这一趋势，人类的学习方式或许将迎来变革：从过去聚焦零散事实与死记硬背（from a focus on individual facts and memorization），转向更加注重培养概念性思维能力（to an emphasis on more conceptual thinking）。这直接支持互联网将改革我们的学习方式，故［A］It may reform our learning approach 正确。\n［错项排除］［B］对社会产生负面影响实为担心者的观点（Some worry that...），Sparrow 对此持积极态度；［C］提升人类对技术的适应力把“记忆本身正在适应新传播技术（adapting to new communications technology）”篡改为对技术普遍适应能力的提高；［D］干扰概念性思维正好与 Sparrow 主张“更重视概念思维”完全反向。' WHERE id = '6db047af-4a1d-556b-9843-18b9170f9fa4'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'It is indicated in Paragraph 3 that how the Internet affects our brains ________.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "requires further academic research", "content": "requires further academic research"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "is most studied in older adults", "content": "is most studied in older adults"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "is reflected in our reading speed", "content": "is reflected in our reading speed"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "depends on our web-surfing habits", "content": "depends on our web-surfing habits"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］段落主旨与态度推断题。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 Paragraph 3（与第三段对齐）及 how the Internet affects our brains 定位至末段。该段开篇明确点出“还有其他专家认为，现在要弄清互联网如何影响我们的大脑还为时过早（it\'s too soon to understand how the Internet affects our brains）”；末句亦作总结：“似乎很明显记忆正在发生改变，但究竟是在变好还是变坏？在现阶段，我们还不得而知（At this point, we don\'t know）”。这清晰表明该问题仍需进一步的学术研究，故［A］requires further academic research 正确。\n［错项排除］［B］在老年人中最常被研究以偏概全（2008 年那项研究只是受试群体之一）；［C］体现在阅读速度中及［D］取决于上网习惯均属无中生有。' WHERE id = '0946f686-e2e5-5593-8f07-8f4c09bae484'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Neither Sparrow nor Storm would agree that', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "our reliance on the Internet will be costly", "content": "our reliance on the Internet will be costly"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "the Internet is weakening our memory", "content": "the Internet is weakening our memory"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "memory exercise is a must for our brains", "content": "memory exercise is a must for our brains"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "our ability to focus declines with age", "content": "our ability to focus declines with age"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］观点态度与排除法推理（两位学者共同否认的立场）。\n［精准定位］综合评估 Sparrow 与 Storm 的全部论述：第一段结尾 Sparrow 明确指出“human memory is not deteriorating（人类记忆力并未衰退）”，第二段末补充说明人类“haven\'t lost our ability to do it（并未丧失记忆能力）”；末段 Storm 则乐观认为“overall the benefits are going to outweigh those costs（总体上利大于弊）”，且记忆只是在改变形式而非确定变差。由此可见，两位学者都绝不认同“互联网正在削弱我们的记忆力”，故［B］the Internet is weakening our memory 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］依赖互联网会有代价是 Storm 亲自承认的前提（There may be costs）；［C］大脑必须锻炼记忆与［D］专注力随年龄下滑均非二人探讨与否定的核心分歧。' WHERE id = 'ef8e4191-67a1-5aca-b7f9-60cb4e73c643'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to Paragraph 1, children growing into adolescence tend to', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "develop opposite personality traits", "content": "develop opposite personality traits"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "see the world in an unreasonable way", "content": "see the world in an unreasonable way"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "have fond memories of their past", "content": "have fond memories of their past"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "show affection for their parents", "content": "show affection for their parents"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］细节事实题（首段核心矛盾特征）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 Paragraph 1 与 growing into adolescence 定位至第一段。文章开篇点明“Teenagers are paradoxical（青少年充满矛盾）”，随后具体阐释这一双重反差：一方面原本无助且事事依赖成人的孩子变得更加独立、能够自理并互助（independent people）；但与此同时，昔日开朗顺从的孩子却又摇身一变成叛逆爱冒险的少年（rebellious teenage risk-takers）。正负特质并存表明步入青春期的孩子趋于发展出截然相反的性格特征，故［A］develop opposite personality traits 正确。\n［错项排除］［B］以不合理方式看世界属于无依据的主观贬低；［C］怀念美好过去及［D］向父母表达爱意均偏离首段对“依赖向独立兼叛逆转型”的剖析。' WHERE id = 'eaf4e867-acd4-54cf-8617-409130b3e417'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'It can be learned from Paragraph 2 that Crone\'s study', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "explores teenagers\' social responsibilities", "content": "explores teenagers\' social responsibilities"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "examines teenagers\' emotional problems", "content": "examines teenagers\' emotional problems"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "provides a new insight into adolescence", "content": "provides a new insight into adolescence"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "highlights negative adolescent behavior", "content": "highlights negative adolescent behavior"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］细节理解题（研究视角突破定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 Paragraph 2 与 Crone\'s study 定位至第二段。该段首先指明该研究属于看待青春期新思潮的一部分（a new wave of thinking）；接着与长期以来的传统认知做对比：过去科学家与决策者总把青少年视作“需要解决的麻烦”，而 Crone 的新研究强调青春期“既是充满风险也是蕴含机遇的时期（a time of opportunity as well as risk）”。显然该研究打破成见，提供了认识青春期的全新视角，故［C］provides a new insight into adolescence 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］探索青少年社会责任以偏概全，下文调查涵盖助人与叛逆两方面；［B］审视青少年情绪问题及［D］突出消极叛逆行为恰是传统旧观念的局限所在，并非克罗恩研究的突破点。' WHERE id = '9f39aa89-1fd7-5aff-bf7d-b13444bce87e'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'What does Crone\'s study find about prosocial behavior?', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "It results from the wish to cooperate.", "content": "It results from the wish to cooperate."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "It is cultivated through education.", "content": "It is cultivated through education."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "It is subject to family influence.", "content": "It is subject to family influence."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "It tends to peak in adolescence.", "content": "It tends to peak in adolescence."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］细节事实题（实验主要发现定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 Crone\'s study 与 prosocial behavior 定位至第四段。文中提到既有研究表明叛逆行为随青春期升高并在成年后消退；紧接着 Crone 的新研究显示，令人惊讶的是，亲社会行为遵循完全相同的变化模式（the same pattern holds for prosocial behavior）——青少年比幼童或成年人更倾向于报告自己做过无私助友之举。这表明亲社会行为往往在青春期达到峰值，故［D］It tends to peak in adolescence 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］源于合作愿望、［B］通过教育培养及［C］受家庭影响在第四段对正相关性与变化曲线的论述中均未曾提及。' WHERE id = '07b01303-3a27-55db-a4ef-e8d22b922bf2'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'It can be learned from the last two paragraphs that teenagers', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "overstress their influence on others", "content": "overstress their influence on others"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "care a lot about social recognition", "content": "care a lot about social recognition"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "become anxious about their future", "content": "become anxious about their future"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "endeavor to live a joyful life", "content": "endeavor to live a joyful life"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］细节推断题（行为动机深度剖析）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 last two paragraphs 与 teenagers 定位至最后两段。倒数第二段归因于“回报敏感性（reward sensitivity）”，末段首句更是直言青少年“对社会性回报尤为敏感（particularly sensitive to social rewards）”，如赢得比赛、给新朋友留下好印象、吸引心仪异性注意等。这鲜明说明青少年非常看重来自同伴和周围人的社会认可，故［B］care a lot about social recognition 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］过度强调自己对他人的影响混淆因果，青少年是在意他人评价与认可而非高估自身影响力；［C］对未来感到焦虑及［D］努力过快乐生活均偏离“对社交赞赏敏感度峰值”的主题。' WHERE id = 'c01fb7d7-5c7f-5565-8e54-0b01a0541e6c'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'What is the text mainly about?', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Why teenagers are self-contradictory.", "content": "Why teenagers are self-contradictory."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Why teenagers are risk-sensitive.", "content": "Why teenagers are risk-sensitive."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "How teenagers develop prosociality.", "content": "How teenagers develop prosociality."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "How teenagers become independent.", "content": "How teenagers become independent."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］主旨大意题（全篇行文脉络总结）。\n［精准定位］文章首段即开门见山提出“Teenagers are paradoxical”的核心谜题：青少年同时展现无私独立与叛逆冒险的两面；第二至四段引用 Crone 团队对 200 多名青少年的调查，实证亲社会行为与叛逆行径竟呈正相关；最后两段从心理学机制“社交回报敏感度”揭示二者共存并随年龄回落的内在原因。全文始终围绕“青少年为何自我矛盾”层层解密，故［A］Why teenagers are self-contradictory 正确。\n［错项排除］［B］为何青少年对风险敏感仅涉及最后两段的解释概念，且文中重在说明他们看重社交回报压倒风险而非单纯怕风险；［C］如何培养亲社会性及［D］如何变得独立均以偏概全。' WHERE id = 'fffa6286-825d-5895-b23c-db20f73a5d01'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Match the person [Brian Berry] with the corresponding opinion:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "The rise of home prices is a temporary matter.", "content": "The rise of home prices is a temporary matter."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Builders possibly need to submit new estimates of their projects.", "content": "Builders possibly need to submit new estimates of their projects."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "There will be specific limits on home extensions to prevent heat loss.", "content": "There will be specific limits on home extensions to prevent heat loss."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "The new rules will take home prices to an even higher level.", "content": "The new rules will take home prices to an even higher level."}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "Many people feel that home prices are already beyond what they can afford.", "content": "Many people feel that home prices are already beyond what they can afford."}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "The new rules will affect people whose home extensions include new windows or doors.", "content": "The new rules will affect people whose home extensions include new windows or doors."}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "The rule changes will benefit homeowners eventually.", "content": "The rule changes will benefit homeowners eventually."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［定位/考点］人名观点匹配（Brian Berry）。\n［解题思路］根据题干人名 Brian Berry 定位至原文第四段。身为建筑商联合会（Federation of Master Builders）首席执行官，Brian Berry 明确指出节能新规将要求安装新材料、新检测方法、新产品与新系统，而此时本就面临物价居高不下的局面（prices are already sky high），由此必然导致消费者不得不支付更高费用（consumers will have to pay more）。选项［D］The new rules will take home prices to an even higher level（新规将把房价推升至更高水平）精准概括其观点。\n［错项排除］注意区分第十段 Jonathan Rolande 认为很多人感觉房价本就超出负担能力（对应［E］），而 Berry 着重阐述新规在原本高物价基础上“进一步加价（increased cost / pay more）”，故选［D］。' WHERE id = '461cc50c-2e84-5a7e-acd2-3942e5e1ad7d'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Match the person [Gareth Belsham] with the corresponding opinion:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "The rise of home prices is a temporary matter.", "content": "The rise of home prices is a temporary matter."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Builders possibly need to submit new estimates of their projects.", "content": "Builders possibly need to submit new estimates of their projects."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "There will be specific limits on home extensions to prevent heat loss.", "content": "There will be specific limits on home extensions to prevent heat loss."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "The new rules will take home prices to an even higher level.", "content": "The new rules will take home prices to an even higher level."}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "Many people feel that home prices are already beyond what they can afford.", "content": "Many people feel that home prices are already beyond what they can afford."}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "The new rules will affect people whose home extensions include new windows or doors.", "content": "The new rules will affect people whose home extensions include new windows or doors."}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "The rule changes will benefit homeowners eventually.", "content": "The rule changes will benefit homeowners eventually."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'F', explanation = E'［定位/考点］人名观点匹配（Gareth Belsham）。\n［解题思路］根据题干人名 Gareth Belsham 定位至原文第五段。作为测量师事务所 Naismiths 的代表，Belsham 指出正在翻新或扩建住宅的业主（upgrading, or extending their home）将直接受到冲击：新规最大变动涉及供暖与隔热，针对扩建中的玻璃用量做出新规定，且所有新装门窗必须达到高度隔热标准（any new windows or doors must be highly insulated）。选项［F］The new rules will affect people whose home extensions include new windows or doors 严丝合缝。\n［错项排除］第七段 Thomas Goodman 同样讨论扩建限制，但他明确规定玻璃覆盖地面面积不得超 25% 以防热量流失（对应［C］），不可与专论新装门窗隔热要求的 Belsham 混淆。' WHERE id = 'bad16475-78b9-5935-9d2b-c0ba975f45e7'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Match the person [Marcus Jefford] with the corresponding opinion:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "The rise of home prices is a temporary matter.", "content": "The rise of home prices is a temporary matter."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Builders possibly need to submit new estimates of their projects.", "content": "Builders possibly need to submit new estimates of their projects."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "There will be specific limits on home extensions to prevent heat loss.", "content": "There will be specific limits on home extensions to prevent heat loss."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "The new rules will take home prices to an even higher level.", "content": "The new rules will take home prices to an even higher level."}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "Many people feel that home prices are already beyond what they can afford.", "content": "Many people feel that home prices are already beyond what they can afford."}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "The new rules will affect people whose home extensions include new windows or doors.", "content": "The new rules will affect people whose home extensions include new windows or doors."}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "The rule changes will benefit homeowners eventually.", "content": "The rule changes will benefit homeowners eventually."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［定位/考点］人名观点匹配（Marcus Jefford）。\n［解题思路］根据题干人名 Marcus Jefford 定位至原文第九段。供职于 Build Aviator 的 Jefford 指出，那些此前已经完成了项目造价核算但尚未赶在截止日期前提交备案手续的建筑商（Builders which have costed projects, but have not filed the paperwork），受新规生效影响，或许不得不回过头去重新计算并递交最新的造价估算（go back and submit fresh estimates）。选项［B］Builders possibly need to submit new estimates of their projects 精准对应。\n［错项排除］第八段虽提及开发商赶在新规前递交规划方案，但针对未备案建筑商需“重提交新预算”的具体论述专属于第九段 Marcus Jefford。' WHERE id = 'b0caf21a-8dfc-5056-a61c-e87cca9a1ab5'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Match the person [John Kelly] with the corresponding opinion:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "The rise of home prices is a temporary matter.", "content": "The rise of home prices is a temporary matter."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Builders possibly need to submit new estimates of their projects.", "content": "Builders possibly need to submit new estimates of their projects."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "There will be specific limits on home extensions to prevent heat loss.", "content": "There will be specific limits on home extensions to prevent heat loss."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "The new rules will take home prices to an even higher level.", "content": "The new rules will take home prices to an even higher level."}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "Many people feel that home prices are already beyond what they can afford.", "content": "Many people feel that home prices are already beyond what they can afford."}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "The new rules will affect people whose home extensions include new windows or doors.", "content": "The new rules will affect people whose home extensions include new windows or doors."}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "The rule changes will benefit homeowners eventually.", "content": "The rule changes will benefit homeowners eventually."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［定位/考点］人名观点匹配（John Kelly）。\n［解题思路］根据题干人名 John Kelly 定位至原文第十一段。建筑法律师 John Kelly 明确表示，房价最终一定会降下来（prices will eventually come down），只是短期内不会立竿见影；因为随着市场不断适应新规要求及配套支持技术实现规模化普及（scaling up of these technologies），长期来看建筑成本终将回落，眼下涨价只是必然经历的过渡阶段（short term... necessary transition）。选项［A］The rise of home prices is a temporary matter 精确契合。\n［错项排除］切勿与末段 Andrew Mellor 的“房主最终能从节能省电中回本受益”（对应［G］）混淆：Kelly 谈的是“技术规模化令房价/成本回落”，Mellor 谈的是“房主从长远电费节省中获益”。' WHERE id = 'e4ac3b7b-2ba3-5ee1-9574-8d9a19129aaf'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Match the person [Andrew Mellor] with the corresponding opinion:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "The rise of home prices is a temporary matter.", "content": "The rise of home prices is a temporary matter."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Builders possibly need to submit new estimates of their projects.", "content": "Builders possibly need to submit new estimates of their projects."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "There will be specific limits on home extensions to prevent heat loss.", "content": "There will be specific limits on home extensions to prevent heat loss."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "The new rules will take home prices to an even higher level.", "content": "The new rules will take home prices to an even higher level."}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "Many people feel that home prices are already beyond what they can afford.", "content": "Many people feel that home prices are already beyond what they can afford."}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "The new rules will affect people whose home extensions include new windows or doors.", "content": "The new rules will affect people whose home extensions include new windows or doors."}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "The rule changes will benefit homeowners eventually.", "content": "The rule changes will benefit homeowners eventually."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'G', explanation = E'［定位/考点］人名观点匹配（Andrew Mellor）。\n［解题思路］根据题干人名 Andrew Mellor 定位至原文最后一段（第十二段）。PRP 建筑事务所的 Mellor 指出，建筑新规的长远效应将是打造更加舒适且节能环保的住宅，虽然当下建造成本存在剧烈波动，但随着时间推移，房主极可能通过省下的能源账单收回改造成本并收获长远益处（recoup that cost over time in energy bill savings... have that benefit over time）。选项［G］The rule changes will benefit homeowners eventually 高度概括其立场。\n［错项排除］前段 John Kelly 聚焦房价成本自身的“短期上扬→长期下降”（对应［A］），而 Mellor 聚焦新规最终给“房主群体（homeowners）”带来的居住体验与电费实惠。' WHERE id = 'ff6681b8-5356-5093-9758-9e3f848fa695'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'If you look at the apps on your phone, chances are you have at least one related to your health—and probably several. Whether it is a mental health app, a fitness tracker, a connected health device or something else, many of us are taking advantage of this technology to keep better track of our health in some shape or form. Recent research from the Organization for the Review of Care and Health Applications found that 350,000 health apps were available on the market, 90,000 of which launched in 2020 alone.\n\nWhile these apps have a great deal to offer, it is not always clear how the personal information we input is collected, safeguarded and shared online. Existing health privacy law, such as the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act, is primarily focused on the way hospitals, doctors’ offices, clinics and insurance companies store health records online. The health information these apps and health data tracking wearables are collecting typically does not receive the same legal protections.\n\nWithout additional protections in place, companies may share (and potentially monetize) personal health information in a way consumers may not have authorized or anticipated. In 2021, Flo Health faced a Federal Trade Commission (FTC) investigation. The FTC alleged in a complaint that “despite express privacy claims, the company took control of users’ sensitive fertility data and shared it with third parties.” Flo Health and the FTC settled the matter with a Consent Order requiring the company to get app users’ express affirmative consent before sharing their health information as well as to instruct the third parties to delete the data they had obtained.\n\nSection 5 of the FTC Act empowers the FTC to initiate enforcement action against unfair or deceptive acts, meaning the FTC can only act after the fact if a company’s privacy practices are misleading or cause unjustified consumer harm. While the FTC is doing what it can to ensure apps are keeping their promises to consumers around the handling of their sensitive health information, the rate at which these health apps are hitting the market demonstrates just how immense of a challenge this is.\n\nAs to the prospects for federal legislation, commentators suggest that comprehensive federal privacy legislation seems unlikely in the short term. States have begun implementing their own solutions to shore up protections for consumer-generated health data. California has been at the forefront of state privacy efforts with the California Consumer Privacy Act of 2018. Virginia, Colorado and Utah have also recently passed state consumer data privacy legislation.' WHERE id = '28ff6ad9-13d7-42d6-abfa-066d999f0d66'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [1] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "because", "content": "because"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "unless", "content": "unless"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "whereas", "content": "whereas"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "until", "content": "until"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义与句内对比逻辑。\n［解题思路］前分句指出“一些人会因与他人共度大量时光而精力充沛（feel energised）”，后分句转而表明“另一些人即便是在做自己喜爱之事时，也可能感到精疲力竭（feel drained）”。两者主系表结构平行且情绪截然相反，故需选用表达对比转折关系的连词 whereas（而、却），故选［C］。\n［错项排除］［A］because（因为）强加因果；［B］unless（除非）表示否定条件；［D］until（直到……为止）表时间终点，误将两类对立人群当作同一群人的先后状态转变。' WHERE id = 'a60d2f57-4554-4bd7-8c98-889514733c2c'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [2] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "contrast", "content": "contrast"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "balance", "content": "balance"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "link", "content": "link"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "gap", "content": "gap"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义与全篇核心主旨。\n［解题思路］首段指明同一种社交体验于不同人利弊各异；下文紧接着分别剖析“独处过多（社交过少）造成孤独”与“社交过度引发倦怠疲劳”。可见全篇主旨围绕如何在两端之间寻求合理均衡展开，空格句作为中心主旨句，意为“在社交生活中找到平衡（[2] balance）至关重要”，故选［B］。\n［错项排除］［A］contrast（差异、对比）干扰来自前段人群对比，但寻找差异不合全篇“调和适度”的建议主旨；［C］link（联系、纽带）常与 between 搭配；［D］gap（缺口、分歧）均背离均衡主线。' WHERE id = '06dca805-276e-441d-85d6-0e2a60c67921'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [3] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "seeing", "content": "seeing"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "pleasing", "content": "pleasing"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "judging", "content": "judging"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "teaching", "content": "teaching"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内取舍结构与常见动词熟词僻义。\n［解题思路］主语部分为否定对照结构：花太多时间独处（Spending too much time on your own），即“不与他人会面交往（not [3] others）”。see 后接人时意为“会面、来往、与……相处”，精确对应“缺少人际往来”的孤立状态，故选［A］seeing。\n［错项排除］［B］pleasing（取悦他人）带有迎合色彩，偏离客观陈述日常交往；［C］judging（评判他人）与［D］teaching（教导他人）均无法与前文的“花过多时间独处”构成直接的语义反面对应。' WHERE id = 'fdf36ada-b6a1-4c4e-b667-d58f27f08b36'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [4] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "misguided", "content": "misguided"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "surprised", "content": "surprised"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "spoiled", "content": "spoiled"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "disconnected", "content": "disconnected"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内并列结构与情感形容词辨析。\n［解题思路］句中 feel lonely and [4] 由并列连词 and 连接两个充当表语的消极心理形容词，共同描摹过度独处给人带来的负面体会。disconnected 意为“与外界脱离联系的、孤立无援的、脱节的”，精准贴合社交缺失带来的孤独隔绝感，故选［D］。\n［错项排除］［A］misguided（被误导的、糊涂的）、［B］surprised（惊讶的）及［C］spoiled（被宠坏的/破坏的）均无法与 lonely 构成同向语义并列。' WHERE id = '895ee14c-650e-4840-a8a9-3b0600634913'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [5] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "contribute to", "content": "contribute to"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "rely on", "content": "rely on"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "interfere with", "content": "interfere with"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "go against", "content": "go against"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内因果并列逻辑与动词短语辨析。\n［解题思路］主语为 Loneliness（孤独感），and 连接两个并列不定式成分作补足语：“已知孤独不仅会损害你的心理健康（impact on your mental health），还会促成、导致低落情绪（[5] a low mood）”。contribute to 表示“引起、促成、导致”，与前面负面影响顺理成章构成并列，故选［A］。\n［错项排除］［B］rely on（依赖、依靠）受前面介词 on 结构干扰，但逻辑主被动完全错位；［C］interfere with（妨碍、干扰）带入后意为“孤独妨碍好心情”尚可，但与负面名词 a low mood 搭配变为“阻碍低落情绪”，反向违背文意；［D］go against（违背、与……作对）同样与“加重负面情绪”相反。' WHERE id = '95ea980b-faab-4a38-9d20-c2f543fe349e'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [6] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "in fact", "content": "in fact"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "of course", "content": "of course"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "for example", "content": "for example"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "on average", "content": "on average"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句间例证关系与高频插入短语辨析。\n［解题思路］前句泛指“任何人在任何时候都可能感到孤独”，空格句以 This（这种情况）回指前文，并具体描绘“当你居家办公从而错失办公室社交”这一典型场景。因此逗号隔开的插入语用于引出具体实例，for example（例如）最合句意，故选［C］。\n［错项排除］［A］in fact（事实上）多用于修正或反驳前文预期；［B］of course（当然）表理所当然的让步；［D］on average（平均而言）用于量化统计语境，三者均无法承担由泛指到具体个例的例证衔接功能。' WHERE id = '32caf196-24ae-4f4e-84c0-3be4260c5250'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [7] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "cutting back", "content": "cutting back"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "missing out", "content": "missing out"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "breaking in", "content": "breaking in"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "looking down", "content": "looking down"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义逻辑与动词短语搭配。\n［解题思路］条件从句通过并列结构描绘居家办公状态：“你在家办公（working from home）并且你正在[7]办公室里习惯发生的日常社交互动（the usual social conversations that happen in an office）”。物理隔离导致无法参与公司茶水间或走廊闲聊，miss out on 表示“错失、错过（良机或益事）”，恰如其分，故选［B］missing out。\n［错项排除］［A］cutting back on（削减经费或用量）暗示主动减量，而居家办公令办公室现场寒暄直接无法发生；［C］breaking in on（强行闯入打断对话）及［D］looking down on（轻视、蔑视）语义与场景严重冲突。' WHERE id = 'bb847543-0672-42c6-a96b-f87ce9c7fac3'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [8] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "shorten", "content": "shorten"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "trigger", "content": "trigger"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "follow", "content": "follow"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "interrupt", "content": "interrupt"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句际并列逻辑与动词辨析。\n［解题思路］空格句紧接“居家办公极易诱发孤独”一例，以句尾 too（也）表示并列补充：“其他生活变故——例如退休、换工作或初为人父母——同样可能[8]一阵阵孤独期（periods of loneliness）”。trigger（触发、引发）形象传达重大人生节点诱发阶段性孤独的因果链条，故选［B］。\n［错项排除］［A］shorten（缩短）和［D］interrupt（打断、中止）均与前句引出孤独成因的方向截然相反；［C］follow（跟随在……之后）逻辑颠倒，是生活变故引发孤独而非单纯时序尾随。' WHERE id = '2c3762ec-c372-4c9b-bbaa-d8cdc4d516ba'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [9] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "assess", "content": "assess"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "interpret", "content": "interpret"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "provide", "content": "provide"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "regain", "content": "regain"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文呼应与动宾搭配。\n［解题思路］第三段转入“面对孤独如何破局”的实用建议。在强调“意识到这些孤独感很重要”后，作者指出“存在多种办法能帮助你重拾、恢复（[9]）社交生活（a social life）”，并随后依次展开从兴趣爱好切入的具体方案，故选［D］regain（重新获得、重拾）。\n［错项排除］［A］assess（评估）与［B］interpret（诠释、理解）对象重在评价或解读已有事物；［C］provide（提供）通常无法与个人自身“重新过上社交生活”直接构成自反语义（provide a social life 多指组织为他人提供社交场合）。' WHERE id = 'a4db5ad9-bb81-4af0-9178-6c7461d6a082'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [10] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "at first", "content": "at first"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "in turn", "content": "in turn"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "on time", "content": "on time"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "by chance", "content": "by chance"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句际“问题—策略”顺承与介词短语。\n［解题思路］句内指出重拾社交生活的方法虽然很多，“但这在[10]（一开始、起初）或许让人感到不知所措”；紧接着下句给出破冰第一招：“从思考你喜欢的兴趣爱好开始（start by...）是个好主意”。at first 与下句 start 构成天然呼应，描绘万事开头难但有法可循的逻辑，故选［A］。\n［错项排除］［B］in turn（依次、继而）、［C］on time（准时地）和［D］by chance（偶然地）均无法回应下句专门针对“最初起步（start by）”的循序指导。' WHERE id = '7f5dbb47-cfa3-4cae-9a26-2a723cbcef95'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [11] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "far-sighted", "content": "far-sighted"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "strong-willed", "content": "strong-willed"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "kind-hearted", "content": "kind-hearted"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "like-minded", "content": "like-minded"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文顺承与复合形容词辨析。\n［解题思路］承接“思考个人兴趣爱好”的起步建议，作者指出接着去参加相关的兴趣社团或活动，在那里你就能结识“志趣相投的（[11]）”朋友。like-minded（志同道合的、有相同兴趣爱好的）严密贴合“因共同爱好相聚”的社团属性，故选［D］。\n［错项排除］［A］far-sighted（有远见的）、［B］strong-willed（意志坚定的）和［C］kind-hearted（心地善良的）虽然均属褒义品质形容词，但皆非依托特定共同爱好拓展交际圈所聚焦的筛选纽带。' WHERE id = 'c8e298a0-1d67-4732-897e-ad5c83af4cc2'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [12] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "try", "content": "try"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "promote", "content": "promote"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "watch", "content": "watch"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "describe", "content": "describe"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语义与并列对照。\n［解题思路］本句与前面的 aimed at new parents（针对新手父母）并列，共同列举初次开启新体验的社群类别：“针对那些想要生平第一次[12]一项新运动的人（[12] a new sport for the first time）”。try 意为“尝试、试一试”，贴合新手初次体验的动作特征，故选［A］。\n［错项排除］［B］promote（推广、促销）多为资深参与者或组织方职责；［C］watch（观看体育比赛）属旁观而非亲身融入社团练习；［D］describe（描述）脱离参与式运动社团语境。' WHERE id = 'be5b8c08-a922-44bb-aa46-33603e7780ff'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [13] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "test", "content": "test"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "share", "content": "share"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "accept", "content": "accept"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "revise", "content": "revise"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内并列搭配与社交语境。\n［解题思路］末分句举例面向同行举办的行业交流活动（networking events），目的是让业内人士聚在一起并“[13]观点、分享想法（meet up and [13] ideas）”。share ideas 为极其地道的并列高频搭配，凸显同行线下交流互通有无的价值，故选［B］。\n［错项排除］［A］test（测试想法）偏重严谨实验或调研；［C］accept（接受）侧重单方被动认可；［D］revise（修改观点）均不符轻松互通信息的职场交流场合。' WHERE id = '25cc8f51-84bd-45d9-9ce4-4fc076100e71'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [14] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "already", "content": "already"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "thus", "content": "thus"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "also", "content": "also"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "only", "content": "only"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］段际转折并列逻辑与副词辨析。\n［解题思路］第二、三段剖析“社交过少”的孤独困扰及应对，第四段开篇以 On the other hand（另一方面）切换视角，指出社交过度同样是客观风险——“另一方面，过度社交[14]是可能的（it\'s [14] possible to have too much of a social life）”。also（也、同样）承前启后引出另一端失衡状况，故选［C］。\n［错项排除］［A］already（已经）与探讨普遍客观可能性不符；［B］thus（因此）错误构建了因果推论；［D］only（仅仅）排除了前两段刚刚讨论过的“社交匮乏”这一半边问题。' WHERE id = 'bdcbce6b-68d1-4adb-bb69-06c2a92f355b'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [15] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "list", "content": "list"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "order", "content": "order"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "space", "content": "space"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "boundary", "content": "boundary"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内并列与名词语法词义辨析。\n［解题思路］条件从句指出：若你觉得自己仿佛永远都在连轴转，并且在日程表（calendar）里从未给休整闲暇时间留出过任何“[15]（空隙、空白时段）”。space 作为不可数名词恰可紧跟否定句中的 any，表示日程表中可供喘息的“余地/空白时段”，故选［C］。\n［错项排除］［A］list（清单）作“清单”解通常为可数单数，不可直接置于 never any 后，且“没列闲暇清单”不等同“日程排满无空”；［B］order（顺序、条理）及［D］boundary（边界）亦无法在日程格（calendar）内形象表达预留可支配空闲区域之意。' WHERE id = 'bf9de3b7-e34e-497b-b8f9-3d97f0489ed2'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [16] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "fatigue", "content": "fatigue"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "criticism", "content": "criticism"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "injustice", "content": "injustice"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "dilemma", "content": "dilemma"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内并列逻辑与名词词义辨析。\n［解题思路］句内 or 连接两个意义相近的负面状态：如果你日程毫无空档，就可能遭受“社交耗竭（social burnout）”或者“社交[16]（疲劳、倦怠）”。fatigue（极度疲惫、劳累）与 burnout 构成精准近义呼应，指出过量社交对精力的消耗，故选［A］。\n［错项排除］［B］criticism（批评、指责）、［C］injustice（不公正）与［D］dilemma（进退两难的困境）皆侧重外部人际摩擦或道德冲突，而非连续赶场社交导致的个人身心倦怠。' WHERE id = '62fb75d1-50a8-482a-8507-b5cb15d45570'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [17] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "sources", "content": "sources"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "standards", "content": "standards"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "signs", "content": "signs"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "scores", "content": "scores"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文顺承与名词语义辨析。\n［解题思路］前句刚刚呼吁“要能察觉自己何时快到承受极限”，紧接着本句列举四个典型临床表现——“情绪低落、精力枯竭、烦躁易怒以及失眠”都可能是社交健康亮红灯的“[17]（迹象、征兆）”。signs of poor social health 贴切承担由表象诊断状态的作用，故选［C］。\n［错项排除］［A］sources（根源、来源）颠倒因果——失眠等是过度社交导致的结果症状而非病因；［B］standards（标准）与［D］scores（分数）均不用于指代身体不适表现。' WHERE id = '62193d7e-87aa-4a06-b3ab-fa16adc4e8b8'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [18] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "take over", "content": "take over"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "wipe off", "content": "wipe off"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "add up", "content": "add up"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "mark out", "content": "mark out"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文对应与动词短语搭配。\n［解题思路］针对前文“日程表中毫无空隙”引发的社交耗竭，作者在本段末给出可操作性建议：务必在日程本（in your diary）上专门“[18]（划出、标记出）”留给自己休整的一段专属时光。mark out 意为“划定界线、特别标出（时间段）”，精准呼应“在日程表留白”，故选［D］。\n［错项排除］［A］take over（接管、占满日程）反而挤压空白；［B］wipe off（擦掉涂抹表面）多指清除污渍，或完全消灭；［C］add up（累加计算）不构成从忙碌日程中“划分预留独处时段”的操作含义。' WHERE id = 'cd8da46f-8410-4c9f-ad78-a35446eb4aeb'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [19] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "ungrateful", "content": "ungrateful"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "unavailable", "content": "unavailable"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "responsible", "content": "responsible"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "regretful", "content": "regretful"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义与形容词搭配。\n［解题思路］既然这段划出的独处时光旨在“用来放松和恢复”，那就意味着在这段时间里，你对于一切社交邀约处于“[19]（谢绝参与的、无暇应酬的）”状态（when you\'re unavailable for socialising）。unavailable 正是指对外界发出“此刻不予安排社交”的谢客信号，故选［B］。\n［错项排除］［A］ungrateful（忘恩负义的）与社交休息毫无干系；［C］responsible（负责任的）与［D］regretful（遗憾懊悔的）皆无法准确界定这段“对外关闭社交通道”的物理状态。' WHERE id = '1e92553f-9dbc-41e5-b973-146a02666002'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [20] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "react", "content": "react"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "repeat", "content": "repeat"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "return", "content": "return"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "rest", "content": "rest"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内并列结构与动作收尾。\n［解题思路］最后一句以三个并列不定式说明预留独处空档的用途：“用这段时间来放松（relax）、[20]以及休养恢复（recover）”。rest（休息、歇息）与前后两个动词词性、声韵及语义方向完全一致，共绘闭环调节图景，故选［D］。\n［错项排除］［A］react（作出反应，常需接 to）、［B］repeat（重复）以及［C］return（返回、归还）均无法与 relax、recover 并肩表示从过度社交疲劳中抽身休整。' WHERE id = '03194249-470e-477d-870a-1e144ea6e8cd'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Coyle argues in her new book that economic growth should', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "give rise to innovations.", "content": "give rise to innovations."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "diversify career choices.", "content": "diversify career choices."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "benefit people equally.", "content": "benefit people equally."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "be promoted forcefully.", "content": "be promoted forcefully."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］细节事实题（著作主旨与分配正义定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 Coyle argues in her new book 与 economic growth 定位至第一段。作者援引剑桥经济学家 Diane Coyle 的新书观点指出：若想避免政治秩序分崩离析，经济增长的成果必须比近年来更公平地分享给大众（the gains will have to be more evenly shared than in the recent past）。选项［C］benefit people equally 精准同义改写 more evenly shared，故正确。\n［错项排除］［A］催生创新、［B］使职业选择多元化及［D］强力推动经济增速均将“成果分配更加均衡”的政治经济警告偷换为创新手段或单纯总量扩张，偏离首段关切。' WHERE id = 'e913e19f-b0a4-4b8a-8069-0ca663061d54'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to Paragraph 2, digital technologies should be used to', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "bring about instant prosperity.", "content": "bring about instant prosperity."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "reduce people’s workload.", "content": "reduce people’s workload."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "raise overall work efficiency.", "content": "raise overall work efficiency."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "enhance cross-sector cooperation.", "content": "enhance cross-sector cooperation."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］细节理解题（Paragraph 2 措施定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 Paragraph 2 与 digital technologies 定位至第二段。首句指出：Coyle 认为提升大众生活水平与富足度需要更广泛地运用数字技术，以提高各经济领域的生产效率（to boost productivity in various sectors），从而遏制不平等扩大。选项［C］raise overall work efficiency 是对 boost productivity in various sectors 的标准同义转述，故正确。\n［错项排除］［A］带来瞬间繁荣过度夸大（原文用 improving 并强调需长期配套变革）；［B］减轻工作量将“提高生产率”误读为让人少干活；［D］加强跨行业协作在第二段未有论述。' WHERE id = 'ac02e0dc-a4bc-4152-a0ff-7a20caf65d51'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'What does Coyle fear about transformative technologies?', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "They may affect work-life balance.", "content": "They may affect work-life balance."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "They may be impractical to deploy.", "content": "They may be impractical to deploy."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "They may incur huge expenditure.", "content": "They may incur huge expenditure."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "They may be unwelcome to the public.", "content": "They may be unwelcome to the public."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］人物态度与担忧定位题。\n［精准定位］根据题干询问 Coyle 对变革性技术的担忧，定位至第三、四段。第三段指出若想让人们接受颠覆性变化，社会认同（social buy-in）至关重要，但许多人心头怨气正在暗涌（resentment is simmering among many）；第四段进一步补充指出人们担忧好工作被摧毁、自己反而受害。这些均说明她担心变革性技术得不到公众欢迎甚至遭遇抵制，故［D］They may be unwelcome to the public 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］影响工作生活平衡与［C］产生巨额财政开支在两段均未涉及；［B］部署不切实际偷换了民众情感排斥与技术落地可行性的概念。' WHERE id = 'abcc3be5-af70-488a-bd36-85bc95f974d6'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Several American cities are mentioned to show', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "the uneven distribution of AI technologies in the US.", "content": "the uneven distribution of AI technologies in the US."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "the disappointing prospect of tech jobs in the US.", "content": "the disappointing prospect of tech jobs in the US."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "the fast progress of US regional economies.", "content": "the fast progress of US regional economies."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "the increasing significance of US AI assets.", "content": "the increasing significance of US AI assets."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］例证目的题（例证结构前后关联定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 Several American cities 定位至第五、六段。第五段列举旧金山、圣何塞、波士顿等寥寥数座城市便吸纳了全美约三分之二的人工智能相关资产（two-thirds of the nation\'s AI assets）；第六段首句立即点破该例证的核心论证意图：少数城市的垄断主导地位意味着财富的地域失衡（geographical disparities in wealth）将继续加剧。可见举例意在凸显 AI 技术在美国地理分布上的高度不均，故［A］the uneven distribution of AI technologies in the US 正确。\n［错项排除］［B］对美国科技就业前景感到失望与文本呼吁重塑应用方向相悖；［C］区域经济快速发展及［D］AI 资产日益重要均把少数城市的极端集中误当作全美普遍态势或重点偏离。' WHERE id = 'be966a0a-864b-476d-bbcb-e7bc14ab5be6'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'With regard to Coyle’s concern, the author suggests', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "raising funds to start new AI projects.", "content": "raising funds to start new AI projects."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "encouraging collaboration in AI research.", "content": "encouraging collaboration in AI research."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "guarding against the side effects of AI.", "content": "guarding against the side effects of AI."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "redefining the role of AI technologies.", "content": "redefining the role of AI technologies."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］作者观点与建议定位题（末段收束定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 Coyle\'s concern 与 author suggests 定位至文章最后一段。作者借对“只关心替代人工而漠视分配公平”的反思指出：我们需要拓宽数字想象力（broaden our digital imaginations），重新构想那些不只是淘汰岗位的 AI 技术，让它们在人类与机械各自擅长的领域里扩展新机遇（expand opportunities）。这实质是主张重新界定人工智能技术的社会功能定位，故［D］redefining the role of AI technologies 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］筹资开启新项目与［B］鼓励 AI 科研合作在末段均无着落；［C］防范 AI 副作用泛泛而谈，未能切中作者提倡“赋能扩展机会而非单一替代人工”的建设性转折主旨。' WHERE id = 'c793ae56-01db-4395-9fe6-bd0bf582fdb5'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'It can be learned from Paragraph 1 that the UK needs to', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "increase its domestic wood supply.", "content": "increase its domestic wood supply."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "reduce its demand for timber.", "content": "reduce its demand for timber."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "lower its wood production costs.", "content": "lower its wood production costs."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "lift its control on timber imports.", "content": "lift its control on timber imports."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］细节事实题（首段核心问题定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 Paragraph 1 与 UK needs to 定位至第一段。英国木材行业协会 Confor 呼吁采取紧急行动减少对进口木材的依赖（reduce the country\'s reliance on timber imports）并提供稳定供应，因目前建筑用材仅 20% 为本国自产（home-grown），英国沦为全球第二大木材净进口国。由此清晰可知英国急需增加国内木材供应，故［A］increase its domestic wood supply 正确。\n［错项排除］［B］削减木材需求与建筑环保减碳急需大批用材的现实相反；［C］降低生产成本及［D］解除进口管制在首段均无提及（文中反而是担忧过度依赖进口）。' WHERE id = '2d33cb5f-44ad-49c8-adbd-0415bf5e7533'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to Confor, the UK government’s fresh incentives', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "can hardly address a construction crisis.", "content": "can hardly address a construction crisis."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "are believed to come at a wrong time.", "content": "are believed to come at a wrong time."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "seem to be misleading for landowners.", "content": "seem to be misleading for landowners."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "will be too costly to put into practice.", "content": "will be too costly to put into practice."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］观点细节题（行业机构对现行政策的评估）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 Confor 与 fresh incentives 定位至第二段首句。在提及政府于气候减排计划下最新宣布的鼓励植树政策（fresh incentives for tree planting）后，Confor 负责人直言“但这些举措远远不够（don\'t go far enough），未能有效倡导植树造林提升木材供给的益处”，而前段首句已警示英国正因缺林少木面临未来建筑危机（a future construction crisis）。可见这些新激励远远不足以化解建筑危机，故［A］can hardly address a construction crisis 正确。\n［错项排除］［B］时机不当将政策力度不足错改成了时间节点错误；［C］误导土地所有者在第二段并未指明；［D］推行成本高昂在后文未曾讨论。' WHERE id = '792efb26-f6fa-47fd-8e69-0cf872b187d4'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The UK’s exposure to fluctuating wood prices is a result of', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "the government’s inaction on timber imports.", "content": "the government’s inaction on timber imports."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "inadequate investment in growing wood.", "content": "inadequate investment in growing wood."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "the competition among timber traders at home.", "content": "the competition among timber traders at home."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "wood producers’ motive to maximise profits.", "content": "wood producers’ motive to maximise profits."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］因果细节题（历史成因追踪定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 exposure to fluctuating wood prices 定位至第二段末句。Confor 负责人指出：几十年来我们始终未担负起投资本土木材供应的责任（have not taken responsibility for investing in our domestic wood supply），致使国家轻易暴露在动荡的国际市场价格与供应链断裂风险之下。Options 中［B］inadequate investment in growing wood（对林木种植投资不足）精准对应原文未投资本土供材的历史短板，故正确。\n［错项排除］［A］对木材进口的无所作为将缺口根源“本土缺投资”偷换为“政府不管进口”；［C］国内木材贸易商竞争及［D］逐利动机均属无中生有。' WHERE id = 'd3869fce-aed1-45da-ae3c-cbdd04ca57dc'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Which of the following causes the shortage of wood supply in the UK?', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Excessive timber consumption in construction.", "content": "Excessive timber consumption in construction."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Unfavourable conditions for growing wood.", "content": "Unfavourable conditions for growing wood."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Outdated technologies of the wood industry.", "content": "Outdated technologies of the wood industry."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Farmers’ unwillingness to plant trees.", "content": "Farmers’ unwillingness to plant trees."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］细节理解题（行业供应链障碍定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干询问英国木材短缺的成因，定位至第三段末句。该段分析缺木的多重原因，其中不仅涉及审批制度与技术培训滞后，最后还特别指出农民及其他土地所有者对投资长期植树项目顾虑重重、犹豫不决（significant hesitation on behalf of farmers and other landowners to invest in longer-term planting projects）。选项［D］Farmers\' unwillingness to plant trees 准确提炼这一主观畏难障碍，故正确。\n［错项排除］［A］建筑业木材消耗过量与第一段提倡木结构减排环保趋势冲突；［B］自然种植条件不利与英国气候宜林（第二段仅说人为投资失责）不符；［C］木材行业技术过时曲解了原文“培训技术工人以助植树（training people to help plant them）”的表述。' WHERE id = 'e06ca123-fecb-49dc-8ccd-b09af39bd4d1'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'What does Goodall think the UK government should do?', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Subsidise the building of low-carbon homes.", "content": "Subsidise the building of low-carbon homes."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Pay greater attention to boosting rural economies.", "content": "Pay greater attention to boosting rural economies."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Provide more support for productive tree planting.", "content": "Provide more support for productive tree planting."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Give priority to pursuing its net-zero strategy.", "content": "Give priority to pursuing its net-zero strategy."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］人物观点题（对策诉求总结定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干人名 Goodall 定位至第四、五段。Goodall 在第四段批判政府现行扶持只聚焦于粮食生产和专为生物多样性服务的野生原始林，而忽略了具有生产力的商业林业（productive forestry）；第五段他紧接着强调必须借助合理政策推动更多生产性树木的栽种（greater impetus to the vision of planting more productive trees），为建筑与制造业提供稳固资源。可见他认为英国政府应加大对生产性植树的扶持，故［C］Provide more support for productive tree planting 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］直接补贴低碳建房及［B］重在促进乡村经济虽有附带词根联系（如 rural economies），但并非 Goodall 向政府提出的核心林政呼吁；［D］将净零排放置于最优先偏离其强调具体产木政策的重心。' WHERE id = '8a505c51-ded2-4ec8-b4f3-36dbdb649100'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to Paragraph 1, keeping unsafe aging drivers off the road', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "is a new safety measure.", "content": "is a new safety measure."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "has become a disputed issue.", "content": "has become a disputed issue."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "can be a tough task to complete.", "content": "can be a tough task to complete."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "will be beneficial to their health.", "content": "will be beneficial to their health."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］细节事实题（首段核心难点定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 Paragraph 1 与 unsafe aging drivers off the road 定位至第一段首句。文中开篇明义：让高龄不安全驾驶者停止开车（keeping unsafe aging drivers off the road）面临的最大挑战之一（One of the biggest challenges），就是说服他们接受是时候交出车钥匙了——而对许多人来说这形同丧失独立生活能力。biggest challenges 直接对应选项［C］can be a tough task to complete（是一项难以完成的棘手任务），故正确。\n［错项排除］［A］称其为新安全举措与“长期以来都是棘手挑战”及后文多年争议不符；［B］成为争议话题在首段未强调（首段聚焦说服老人本身的心理困难而非政策争论）；［D］有益健康同样未在首段阐述。' WHERE id = '03ad2225-8fd9-4a38-8916-5200e6f08ee3'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The American Medical Association’s advice', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "has won support from drivers.", "content": "has won support from drivers."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "is generally considered unrealistic.", "content": "is generally considered unrealistic."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "is widely dismissed as unnecessary.", "content": "is widely dismissed as unnecessary."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "has met with different responses.", "content": "has met with different responses."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］细节事实题（各州对行业建议的态度对比）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 American Medical Association\'s advice 定位至第二段。文中指出美国医学会虽建议医生一旦认为某患者不再适宜驾车即应予以报告（physicians report when they think a patient is no longer fit to drive），但各州立法却五花八门：有的州强制规定医生汇报，有的允许但不强求，少数州甚至视之为违反医患保密原则的侵权行为。显然该建议在各地遭遇截然不同的反应，故［D］has met with different responses 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］赢得驾驶员普遍支持在文中无据（连医生和州立法都意见不一）；［B］普遍被视为不现实及［C］被广泛斥为多余皆过度概括（实际上不少州已采用并强行要求上报）。' WHERE id = 'd3fe41b0-90aa-4d54-8025-447b4ec9c27b'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to Dugan, efforts to keep older drivers safe', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "have brought about big changes.", "content": "have brought about big changes."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "need to be well coordinated.", "content": "need to be well coordinated."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "have gained public recognition.", "content": "have gained public recognition."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "call for relevant legal support.", "content": "call for relevant legal support."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］观点推断题（问题症结概括定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干人名 Dugan 与关键词 older drivers safe 定位至第三段。专家 Elizabeth Dugan 抱怨道，当下老年人行车安全难题只是由各个专注点不同的行业分支“零敲碎打（addressed piecemeal）”地各自应付——“我们甚至没有一个全国老年驾驶研究机构”；她指出我们需要从全局顶层加以统筹改进。由此推断有关安全措施亟待良好协调与整合，故［B］need to be well coordinated 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］带来了巨大变化与现状停滞破碎相反；［C］已获得公众认可及［D］急需专门法律支持均脱离她批评“各行其是、缺乏顶层研究统筹机构”的核心论点。' WHERE id = 'fc3fbf0e-6117-4aee-8cbb-092d0d88025a'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Some older drivers have trouble driving because they tend to', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "stick with bad driving habits.", "content": "stick with bad driving habits."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "have a weakened memory.", "content": "have a weakened memory."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "suffer from chronic pains.", "content": "suffer from chronic pains."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "neglect car maintenance.", "content": "neglect car maintenance."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］因果细节题（驾驶困难生理原因定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干提问部分老人驾车困难的原因，定位至第五段。该段第二句直接道出常见诱因：一些老年人在驾车时感到吃力，是因为他们无法灵活转头，或是不记得自己正要开往哪里（can\'t turn their heads or remember where they are going），或是反应速度变慢而无法躲避危险。其中“记不起目的地”正体现记忆力衰退，故［B］have a weakened memory 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］固守坏驾驶习惯、［C］忍受慢性疼痛以及［D］忽视汽车日常保养在原文第五段生理与认知退化说明中均无根据。' WHERE id = 'c315adab-23fe-468c-bab0-ed1beb286dfe'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Dugan thinks that the solution to the problems of crashes may lie in', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "upgrading self-driving vehicles.", "content": "upgrading self-driving vehicles."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "developing senior-friendly cars.", "content": "developing senior-friendly cars."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "renovating transport facilities.", "content": "renovating transport facilities."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "adjusting the age limit for drivers.", "content": "adjusting the age limit for drivers."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］人物观点题（末段未来汽车设计方案定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干人名 Dugan 与 solution to the problems of crashes 定位至文章最后一段。谈及如何减少涉及老龄司机的恶性碰撞事故，Dugan 直言：我们必须着眼于设计制造适应寿命延长时代的交通工具——“既然人能活到百岁，我们就需要打造出 90 岁老人都能自如舒适驾驶的汽车（cars that a 90-year-old can drive comfortably）”。选项［B］developing senior-friendly cars 准确转述，故正确。\n［错项排除］［A］单纯升级完全自动驾驶车偏离原文“让 90 岁老人亲手舒适安全驾车”的设计理念；［C］翻新交通基础设施及［D］调整司机法定驾龄上限在末段均未主张。' WHERE id = 'b397b333-c481-4dac-92eb-1bca747664c8'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The research findings are cited in Paragraph 1 to show', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "the prevalence of health apps", "content": "the prevalence of health apps"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "the public concern over health", "content": "the public concern over health"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "the popularity of smartphones", "content": "the popularity of smartphones"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "the advancement of technology", "content": "the advancement of technology"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］例证目的题（数据支撑现象定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 research findings 与 Paragraph 1 定位至第一段。文章首句即指出手机里往往装着不止一款健康类 APP，随即通过调研机构数据（2021 年市面上有逾 35 万款健康应用，仅 2020 年就上线 9 万款）予以量化夯实。引用庞大增长数据意在生动展示如今健康类 APP 的极度普及与盛行，故［A］the prevalence of health apps 正确。\n［错项排除］［B］公众对健康的高度担忧及［C］智能手机本身的普及率均偏离例证主体“健康应用程序的数量爆炸与普及”；［D］泛言科技进步同样不如［A］紧扣全篇聚焦的健康应用监管主题。' WHERE id = '95927e72-8402-401b-a421-742ace2834e7'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'What does the author imply about existing health privacy law?', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Its coverage needs to be extended.", "content": "Its coverage needs to be extended."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Its enforcement needs strengthening.", "content": "Its enforcement needs strengthening."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "It has discouraged medical misconduct.", "content": "It has discouraged medical misconduct."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "It has disappointed insurance companies.", "content": "It has disappointed insurance companies."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］推理判断题（现行医疗隐私法规漏洞定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干询问作者对现有健康隐私法律的暗示，定位至第二段。该段指出如 HIPAA 等现行法律严格规范传统医院、诊所、药房及医保商，但这些新兴健康 APP 与科技公司所采集的海量个人健康数据却通常无法享受到同等的法律保护（typically does not receive the same legal protections）。由此合理推出，现有健康隐私法案覆盖面过窄，亟待扩展完善以涵盖新应用，故［A］Its coverage needs to be extended 正确。\n［错项排除］［B］执法力度需加强将“法律压根没覆盖管辖新应用”曲解为原有条文执行不力；［C］遏制了医疗不当行为及［D］令保险公司失望均无正文依据。' WHERE id = '343ab23e-8c1b-4c16-86b7-9f0779f89a07'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Before sharing its users’ health information, Flo Health is required to', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "seek the approval of the FTC", "content": "seek the approval of the FTC"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "find qualified third parties", "content": "find qualified third parties"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "remove irrelevant personal data", "content": "remove irrelevant personal data"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "obtain their explicit permission", "content": "obtain their explicit permission"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］细节事实题（典型判例监管要求定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 Flo Health 与 sharing its users\' health information 定位至第三段末句。在联邦贸易委员会（FTC）对生殖健康经期跟踪应用 Flo Health 违约向脸书等第三方泄露用户私密数据的执法和解中，FTC 强制要求该公司在今后分享任何用户健康信息前，必须事先取得用户的“明示肯定同意（get app users\' express affirmative consent）”。选项［D］obtain their explicit permission（获取明确许可）精准对应，故正确。\n［错项排除］［A］须先获得 FTC 逐案审批将原本“须征得用户本人明确同意”的主体错换成监管机构；［B］寻找合资格第三方及［C］清除无关个人资料均违背法律强调的授权前置原则。' WHERE id = 'f5a84c6d-eee2-49fc-b758-a44b88c415a6'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'What challenge is the FTC currently faced with?', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "The complexity of health information.", "content": "The complexity of health information."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "The rapid increase in new health apps.", "content": "The rapid increase in new health apps."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "The subtle deceptiveness of health apps.", "content": "The subtle deceptiveness of health apps."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "The difficulty in assessing consumer harm.", "content": "The difficulty in assessing consumer harm."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］细节理解题（监管机构现实困境定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干询问 FTC 当前面临的挑战，定位至第四段末句。文中首先说明 FTC 的职责涵盖防止行业普遍存在的欺骗与不公平行为，随后紧接着强调：但这些健康 APP 铺天盖地涌向市场的惊人速度本身，便足见这一监管挑战是何等巨大（the rate at which these health apps are hitting the market demonstrates just how immense of a challenge this is）。选项［B］The rapid increase in new health apps 直接照应前句新应用飙升速度，故正确。\n［错项排除］［A］健康信息本身的复杂性、［C］应用的隐蔽欺诈性与［D］难以量化消费者损害虽可能属实务难点，但本段末句指出的具体巨量挑战明确定格于“高速涌入市场的新应用浪潮”。' WHERE id = '00f70977-5d9b-463f-859e-0951733a72aa'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'It can be learned from the last paragraph that health data protection', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "has been embraced by health app developers", "content": "has been embraced by health app developers"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "has been a focus of federal policy-making", "content": "has been a focus of federal policy-making"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "has encountered opposition in California", "content": "has encountered opposition in California"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "has gained legislative support in some states", "content": "has gained legislative support in some states"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］段落推断题（地方立法推进概括）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 last paragraph 与 health data protection 定位至末段。文中指出加州率先通过消费者隐私法案等立法保障本州居民信息安全，而弗吉尼亚、科罗拉多和犹他等州也已接连效仿跟进出台隐私法律。这说明个人健康信息与数据隐私保护已率先在多州赢得明确立法支持，故［D］has gained legislative support in some states 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］已受到 APP 开发者普遍拥护违背文中开发者常暗自违约牟利的现象；［B］已成为联邦层面的立法核心恰与前文缺乏联邦层面涵盖 APP 的法律现实矛盾；［C］在加州遭遇强烈阻力与“加州领衔出台隐私保护法”正好相反。' WHERE id = '7ae2c79d-927d-4ca5-816e-0d09b7c46037'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Match the person [Sue Rexford] with the corresponding opinion:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Students who stand out in a specific extracurricular activity will be favored by top-tier institutions.", "content": "Students who stand out in a specific extracurricular activity will be favored by top-tier institutions."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Students whose extracurricular activity has benefited their community are likely to win a scholarship.", "content": "Students whose extracurricular activity has benefited their community are likely to win a scholarship."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Undertaking too many extracurricular activities will hardly be seen as a plus by colleges.", "content": "Undertaking too many extracurricular activities will hardly be seen as a plus by colleges."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "A student who exhibits abilities in doing business can impress colleges.", "content": "A student who exhibits abilities in doing business can impress colleges."}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "High school students participating in a popular activity should excel in it.", "content": "High school students participating in a popular activity should excel in it."}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "Engaging in uncommon activities can demonstrate students’ determination and dedication.", "content": "Engaging in uncommon activities can demonstrate students’ determination and dedication."}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "It is advisable for students to choose an extracurricular activity that is related to their future study at college.", "content": "It is advisable for students to choose an extracurricular activity that is related to their future study at college."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［定位/考点］人名观点匹配（Sue Rexford）。\n［解题思路］定位至原文第三、四段。查尔斯·E·史密斯犹太走读中学的大学升学指导主任 Sue Rexford 明确指出，学生在填写通用申请（Common Application）时完全不必凑齐一长串 10 项课外活动；没有任何一所大学会期待看到学生列出一份冗长而泛泛的课外活动清单（No college will expect that a student has a huge laundry list of extracurriculars），质量远胜于堆积数量。选项［C］Undertaking too many extracurricular activities will hardly be seen as a plus by colleges 精准匹配，故正确。\n［错项排除］不可误选只提“聚焦深耕单一领域助申名校”的［A］（属 Katie Kelley 观点）或提倡围绕未来专业选题的［G］（属 Mayghin Levine 观点）。' WHERE id = 'b66143eb-0b9c-459f-9ecc-4a52bbebc68a'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Match the person [Sara Harberson] with the corresponding opinion:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Students who stand out in a specific extracurricular activity will be favored by top-tier institutions.", "content": "Students who stand out in a specific extracurricular activity will be favored by top-tier institutions."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Students whose extracurricular activity has benefited their community are likely to win a scholarship.", "content": "Students whose extracurricular activity has benefited their community are likely to win a scholarship."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Undertaking too many extracurricular activities will hardly be seen as a plus by colleges.", "content": "Undertaking too many extracurricular activities will hardly be seen as a plus by colleges."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "A student who exhibits abilities in doing business can impress colleges.", "content": "A student who exhibits abilities in doing business can impress colleges."}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "High school students participating in a popular activity should excel in it.", "content": "High school students participating in a popular activity should excel in it."}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "Engaging in uncommon activities can demonstrate students’ determination and dedication.", "content": "Engaging in uncommon activities can demonstrate students’ determination and dedication."}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "It is advisable for students to choose an extracurricular activity that is related to their future study at college.", "content": "It is advisable for students to choose an extracurricular activity that is related to their future study at college."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'E', explanation = E'［定位/考点］人名观点匹配（Sara Harberson）。\n［解题思路］定位至原文第六段。大学升学顾问 Sara Harberson 分析热门课外活动与冷门活动之别：大众常见活动竞争极其惨烈、要想在其中产生影响力难度大得多，“因此如果学生执意要做一项大众热门活动，我建议他们务必做到出类拔萃、名列前茅（be the best at it）”。选项［E］High school students participating in a popular activity should excel in it（参加热门活动的高中生应当力争出类拔萃）严丝合缝，故正确。\n［错项排除］注意区分第八段提及创立小企业的 Olivia Valdes（对应［D］）及第九段专讲冷门活动体现决心的 Joseph Adegboyega-Edun（对应［F］），均非 Harberson 针对“热门活动”的策略。' WHERE id = '64876c61-512e-4bb7-8af0-404d7b491693'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Match the person [Katie Kelley] with the corresponding opinion:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Students who stand out in a specific extracurricular activity will be favored by top-tier institutions.", "content": "Students who stand out in a specific extracurricular activity will be favored by top-tier institutions."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Students whose extracurricular activity has benefited their community are likely to win a scholarship.", "content": "Students whose extracurricular activity has benefited their community are likely to win a scholarship."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Undertaking too many extracurricular activities will hardly be seen as a plus by colleges.", "content": "Undertaking too many extracurricular activities will hardly be seen as a plus by colleges."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "A student who exhibits abilities in doing business can impress colleges.", "content": "A student who exhibits abilities in doing business can impress colleges."}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "High school students participating in a popular activity should excel in it.", "content": "High school students participating in a popular activity should excel in it."}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "Engaging in uncommon activities can demonstrate students’ determination and dedication.", "content": "Engaging in uncommon activities can demonstrate students’ determination and dedication."}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "It is advisable for students to choose an extracurricular activity that is related to their future study at college.", "content": "It is advisable for students to choose an extracurricular activity that is related to their future study at college."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［定位/考点］人名观点匹配（Katie Kelley）。\n［解题思路］定位至原文第十、十一段。招生咨询机构 IvyWise 的咨询师 Katie Kelley 强调，在某一种高度聚焦的特定课外活动中脱颖而出（Distinguishing yourself in one focused type of extracurricular activity）对于大学申请——尤其是竞争白热化的顶尖名校（highly selective institutions）而言——是极为显著的加分项，因为单凭满分成绩与标化考分已远远不够。选项［A］Students who stand out in a specific extracurricular activity will be favored by top-tier institutions 完美匹配，故正确。\n［错项排除］［A］强调“高选拔度顶尖高校青睐专注某一领域的突出表现”，区别于［E］单就“大众常见项目本身做到最好”的表述。' WHERE id = '25804586-0772-4936-bf3a-5236e5a6f888'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Match the person [Mayghin Levine] with the corresponding opinion:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Students who stand out in a specific extracurricular activity will be favored by top-tier institutions.", "content": "Students who stand out in a specific extracurricular activity will be favored by top-tier institutions."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Students whose extracurricular activity has benefited their community are likely to win a scholarship.", "content": "Students whose extracurricular activity has benefited their community are likely to win a scholarship."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Undertaking too many extracurricular activities will hardly be seen as a plus by colleges.", "content": "Undertaking too many extracurricular activities will hardly be seen as a plus by colleges."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "A student who exhibits abilities in doing business can impress colleges.", "content": "A student who exhibits abilities in doing business can impress colleges."}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "High school students participating in a popular activity should excel in it.", "content": "High school students participating in a popular activity should excel in it."}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "Engaging in uncommon activities can demonstrate students’ determination and dedication.", "content": "Engaging in uncommon activities can demonstrate students’ determination and dedication."}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "It is advisable for students to choose an extracurricular activity that is related to their future study at college.", "content": "It is advisable for students to choose an extracurricular activity that is related to their future study at college."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'G', explanation = E'［定位/考点］人名观点匹配（Mayghin Levine）。\n［解题思路］定位至原文第十二段。肯塔基州路易斯维尔非营利社区中心主管 Mayghin Levine 建议道，那些与申请表上所填报大学专业方向契合的课外活动尤为加分——“如果心里已经有了明确的未来专业，拥有一段与该专业紧密贴合的课外活动经历将会是一大优势（having an extracurricular that fits into that major can be a big plus）”。选项［G］It is advisable for students to choose an extracurricular activity that is related to their future study at college 准确转述，故正确。\n［错项排除］注意区分 Levine 谈“与大学拟修专业匹配（major / future study at college）”和下文 Gwyn 谈“回馈当地社区赢取奖学金”。' WHERE id = 'f4cce0d4-970c-4cc8-9d44-ee352985fe96'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Match the person [Erica Gwyn] with the corresponding opinion:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Students who stand out in a specific extracurricular activity will be favored by top-tier institutions.", "content": "Students who stand out in a specific extracurricular activity will be favored by top-tier institutions."}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Students whose extracurricular activity has benefited their community are likely to win a scholarship.", "content": "Students whose extracurricular activity has benefited their community are likely to win a scholarship."}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Undertaking too many extracurricular activities will hardly be seen as a plus by colleges.", "content": "Undertaking too many extracurricular activities will hardly be seen as a plus by colleges."}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "A student who exhibits abilities in doing business can impress colleges.", "content": "A student who exhibits abilities in doing business can impress colleges."}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "High school students participating in a popular activity should excel in it.", "content": "High school students participating in a popular activity should excel in it."}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "Engaging in uncommon activities can demonstrate students’ determination and dedication.", "content": "Engaging in uncommon activities can demonstrate students’ determination and dedication."}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "It is advisable for students to choose an extracurricular activity that is related to their future study at college.", "content": "It is advisable for students to choose an extracurricular activity that is related to their future study at college."}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［定位/考点］人名观点匹配（Erica Gwyn）。\n［解题思路］定位至原文末段（第十三段）。亚特兰大非营利机构执行主任 Erica Gwyn 指出，通过课外活动对自身所在社区产生显著正面影响的高中生（had a strong positive influence on their community），极易打动高校招生官并进而赢得奖学金（impress a college and win a scholarship）。选项［B］Students whose extracurricular activity has benefited their community are likely to win a scholarship 直接对应句意，故正确。\n［错项排除］原文共有两位来自非营利组织的发言人，切记区分第十二段侧重“专业吻合”的 Levine 与末段紧扣“造福社区+奖学金”的 Gwyn。' WHERE id = '427db2a0-5821-4cac-8443-9eef48d1177b'::uuid;
UPDATE public.passages SET content = E'Five Steps to Suggesting a Change at Work That\'ll Actually Get Taken Seriously\n\n[A] Stay positive\n[B] Respect the past\n[C] Use channels\n[D] Give it time\n[E] Invite resistance\n[F] Be a salesman\n[G] Be humble\n\nEveryone wants to be that person—the one who looks at the same information as everyone else, but who sees a fresh, innovative solution. However, it takes more than simply having a good idea. How you share it is as important as the suggestion itself. Why? Because writing a new script—literally or figuratively—means that other team members will have to adapt to something new. So whether you\'re suggesting a (seemingly) benign change like streamlining outdated protocol, or a bigger change like adding an hour to each workday so people can leave early on Fridays, you\'re asking others to reimagine their workflow or schedule. Not to mention, if the process you\'re scrapping is one someone else suggested, there\'s the possibility of hurt feelings. To gain buy-in on an innovative, new idea, follow these steps:\n\n[41] Great ideas don\'t stand alone. In other words, you can\'t mention your suggestion once and expect it to be adopted. To see a change, you\'ll need to champion your plan and sell its merits. In addition, you need to be willing to stand up to scrutiny and criticism and be prepared to explain your innovation in different ways for various audiences.\n\n[42] Sometimes it makes sense to go to your boss first. But other times, it\'s useful to build a coalition among your co-workers or other stakeholders. When it works, it works great—because you\'re ready for your stubborn supervisor\'s pushback with answers like, "Actually, I connected with a few people in our tech department to discuss how much time these kinds of website updates would take, and they suggested they have the bandwidth."\n\n[43] One of the biggest barriers to gaining buy-in occurs when the owner of an idea is viewed as argumentative, defensive, or close-minded. Because, let\'s be honest: No one likes a know-it-all. So, if people disagree with you, don\'t be indignant. Instead, listen to their concerns fully, try to understand their perspective, and include their concerns (and possible remedies) in future discussions. So, instead of saying, "Martha, our current slogan is confusing and should be updated," you could try, "Martha raises a great point that our current slogan has a long history for our stakeholders, but I wonder if we might be able to brainstorm a tagline that could build on that—and be clearer for new customers."\n\n[44] New ideas are the grandchildren of old ones. In other words, don\'t throw old solutions under the bus to make your improvement stand out. Remember that in light of whatever the problem the old system solved—or, maybe, has failed to solve in recent memory—it was a great idea at the time. Appreciating the older contributions as you suggest future innovations helps bolster the credibility of your idea.\n\n[45] When pitching a new idea, it\'s important to use the language of abundance instead of the language of deficit. Instead of saying what is wrong, broken, or suboptimal, talk about what is right, fixable, or ideal. For example, try, "I can see lots of applications for this new approach" rather than, "This innovation is the only way." Be optimistic but realistic, and you will stand out.' WHERE id = '954b533e-edbd-5eaa-b0ae-2818e838c4db'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [1] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "illusion", "content": "illusion"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "discussion", "content": "discussion"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "tradition", "content": "tradition"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "question", "content": "question"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文指代与名词词义辨析。\n［解题思路］首句指出“当你需要帮助时，有许多情有可原的理由会令你觉得难以开口”；空格句以 this [1] 回指上文所述心理现象，说明“心理学家几十年来一直对这个[1]（问题、议题）很感兴趣”。question 在此指供探讨研究的社会心理“课题/问题”，与句首“为何难求助”呼应，故选［D］。\n［错项排除］［A］illusion（错觉、幻觉）指虚幻不实的错认，而“难以开口求助”是客观普遍心理事实；［B］discussion（讨论）指讨论行为本身，与句中 interested in this... 搭配不够自然；［C］tradition（传统、惯例）偏离科学研究对象语境。' WHERE id = '6bb69ca3-a7cf-54b9-9ec0-e5110d3e7059'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [2] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "reluctance", "content": "reluctance"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "ambition", "content": "ambition"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "tendency", "content": "tendency"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "enthusiasm", "content": "enthusiasm"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内因果逻辑与上下文态度照应。\n［解题思路］逗号前后存在明确的“原因→结果”关联：“尤其因为人们普遍[2]求助（people\'s widespread [2] to ask for help）导致了一些备受瞩目的失败案例”。结合全文主题“不愿或不敢开口求助”，reluctance（不情愿、抗拒、勉强）与前句 difficult to ask for help 及负面失败后果严丝合缝，故选［A］。\n［错项排除］［B］ambition（志向、野心）属积极进取愿望，不合求助心理阻力及“导致失败”语境；［C］tendency（倾向、趋势）中性偏平，缺乏抗拒阻力色彩（且通常倾向于正面或习惯动作）；［D］enthusiasm（热情）则与文意完全相反。' WHERE id = '0a953aca-102a-58a0-9fc5-c0d33c5aca0a'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [3] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "attention", "content": "attention"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "talent", "content": "talent"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "courage", "content": "courage"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "patience", "content": "patience"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义与段落核心观点。\n［解题思路］本段围绕“求助面临重重心理顾虑”展开，紧接句指出“求助需要承认自己做不到、暴露弱点并承担控制权丧失等风险”。可见提出求助本身需要跨越心理关口，需要“[3]（勇气、胆量）”，故选［C］courage。\n［错项排除］［A］attention（注意力）关注细节而非克服心理怯懦；［B］talent（天赋、才能）暗示求助需依赖天生禀赋，与下文剖析众人共有的心理障碍无关；［D］patience（耐心）偏重等待耐久力，不能呼应克服怯懦胆怯之意。' WHERE id = '6da38c44-8efc-564d-895c-992ff05ec68a'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [4] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "At any time", "content": "At any time"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "In other words", "content": "In other words"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "By all means", "content": "By all means"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "On the contrary", "content": "On the contrary"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句间同义释义逻辑与短语辨析。\n［解题思路］前句指出“求助需要表达自己的需要，也就是有些事情你做不到（there is something you can\'t do）”；紧接空格句从本质上重新解读这一行为：“你是在向外界宣扬自己的弱点（broadcasting your own weaknesses）”。两句语义等价、表层与深层互相诠释，故需填入表“换言之、也就是说”的［B］In other words。\n［错项排除］［A］At any time（随时随地）抹杀了“仅在开口求助特定情形下”的条件限制；［C］By all means（无论如何、务必）与［D］On the contrary（恰恰相反）分别表示强烈允许或直接语义对立，均不符合前后同义换言逻辑。' WHERE id = '47bc461f-6211-5a1d-ada4-7d357310ac91'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [5] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "unrealistic", "content": "unrealistic"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "deceptive", "content": "deceptive"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "tiresome", "content": "tiresome"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "uncomfortable", "content": "uncomfortable"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内情感语境与形容词辨析。\n［解题思路］非限制性定语从句中的 which 指代前文“将自己的弱点公之于众（broadcasting your own weaknesses）”，这自然是一种令人“[5]（不自在的、局促不安的）”体验（can be [5]）。uncomfortable 精准刻画暴露短板时的尴尬抵触情绪，与下文一连串忧虑并列，故选［D］。\n［错项排除］［A］unrealistic（不切实际的）多修饰想法或计划，不修饰正在经历的心理体验；［B］deceptive（欺骗性的）暗示假装不能以博取同情，偏离真诚求助困境；［C］tiresome（令人厌烦的、繁琐的）侧重枯燥耗神，未能抓住尴尬不安的痛点。' WHERE id = '0a583fa3-fa4d-555e-90e0-41d3bce9686a'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [6] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "doubts", "content": "doubts"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "concerns", "content": "concerns"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "suggestions", "content": "suggestions"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "secrets", "content": "secrets"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义与名词搭配辨析。\n［解题思路］句内指出：“无论你寻求帮助的是什么事，你都可能对失去对它的控制权存在[6]（顾虑、担忧）。”紧接下句“一旦别人介入，也许会接管并抢功”正是对这种忧虑的解释，have concerns about 为表达“对……心存顾虑”的地道固定搭配，故选［B］。\n［错项排除］［A］doubts（怀疑）带入后表示“你怀疑自己会失去控制权”（意即不相信会失控），与下句直接担心他人抢功接管相矛盾；［C］suggestions（建议）与［D］secrets（秘密）皆无法接 about losing control 表心理顾忌。' WHERE id = 'e1bd6b73-fd66-5aa4-8ac9-8baf5ba4f44f'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [7] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Once", "content": "Once"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Unless", "content": "Unless"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Although", "content": "Although"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Before", "content": "Before"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内条件逻辑与连词辨析。\n［解题思路］本句细化“怕失控”的具体担忧：“[7]有人开始帮忙，说不定他们就会接手甚至把你的辛勤功劳占为己有。”这里以一般现在时引导假设触发条件，主句指出由此引发的担忧结果，Once（一旦……就）精准连接假设与后果，故选［A］。\n［错项排除］［B］Unless（除非）导致主从逻辑反向悖谬（变成“除非没人帮忙，否则就会抢功”）；［C］Although（尽管）表示让步转折；［D］Before（在……之前）表示“在对方还没帮忙前就已经接管”，不合时序与事理。' WHERE id = 'c9bd088d-7d43-5844-807f-7d4b1170101b'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [8] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "theory", "content": "theory"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "choice", "content": "choice"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "factor", "content": "factor"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "context", "content": "context"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文并列脉络与名词辨析。\n［解题思路］句首 Yet another [8] 承接上段已剖析的“怕暴露弱点”“怕失控被抢功”两点心理阻力，进一步引出求助者还可能担心的另一个重要“[8]（因素、层面）”，即害怕成为别人负担（being a nuisance）。factor（因素、要素）恰当地并列归纳各项阻因，故选［C］。\n［错项排除］［A］theory（理论、未证实猜想）过高估了普通求助者的顾虑属性；［B］choice（选择）与下文畏惧被动成为累赘冲突；［D］context（语境、背景）通常不用于被担忧的心理障碍本身（be worried about context 不自然）。' WHERE id = '43c741c2-21f5-54f4-9e97-e9ef3a719634'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [9] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "overpraising", "content": "overpraising"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "outperforming", "content": "outperforming"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "reassessing", "content": "reassessing"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "inconveniencing", "content": "inconveniencing"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内并列语义与动名词搭配。\n［解题思路］句尾由 or 连接两个并列表语“给求助对象[9]或者成为一个累赘（being a nuisance）”。因此空格动词短语必须表达给他人带来的“打扰、烦扰或不便”，inconveniencing（给……添麻烦）与“变成累赘”语义完全同向呼应，故选［D］。\n［错项排除］［A］overpraising（过分奉承夸赞）虽可能伴随求助，但属个人可控行为而非惧怕沦为负担的消极后果；［B］outperforming（胜过、表现优于）与求助语境反向；［C］reassessing（重新评估）与“成为麻烦”无关。' WHERE id = '3172b82d-283f-51a7-ba12-17022daf7dc1'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [10] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "reach out", "content": "reach out"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "settle down", "content": "settle down"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "turn over", "content": "turn over"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "look back", "content": "look back"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文语义与固定动词短语。\n［解题思路］句内指出：“如果你深受自卑感困扰，你可能会觉得特别难以[10]寻求帮助（[10] for help）。”reach out for sth 意为“主动伸出援手获取/向他人主动寻求（帮助）”，既地道又精准呼应开篇 ask for help，故选［A］。\n［错项排除］［B］settle down（安定下来、静下心）；［C］turn over（翻转、移交）；［D］look back（回顾、回头看），三者均不与 for help 构成“主动向人求助”的动介搭配。' WHERE id = '81dc9ac3-8c2e-5f45-901b-4b621e4c4295'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [11] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "declining", "content": "declining"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "considering", "content": "considering"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "criticizing", "content": "criticizing"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "evaluating", "content": "evaluating"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文同义复现与动词熟词僻义。\n［解题思路］紧随空格后的次句出现关键词 such refusals（这样的拒绝），由此即可倒推出空格部分“你还额外担心对方会[11]你的请求”指的必是“回绝、婉拒”。decline 的熟词僻义即为“谢绝、婉拒（请求/邀请）”，与下句 refusals 构成原义复现，故选［A］declining。\n［错项排除］［B］considering（考虑）、［C］criticizing（批评）及［D］evaluating（评估）虽各有动作语义，但均不能直接对应下句的 such refusals（拒绝）。' WHERE id = '57811214-c99f-51b5-8c18-9477ecedacd9'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [12] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "unnecessary", "content": "unnecessary"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "negative", "content": "negative"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "strange", "content": "strange"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "impractical", "content": "impractical"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内语境与情感形容词辨析。\n［解题思路］高自卑敏感者最怕请求被拒，因为他们容易把对方拒绝看作是在暗示双方人际关系中出现了某些“[12]（负面的、糟糕的）”苗头（something [12] about the status of your relationship）。negative 准确传递“对关系状况作出悲观负面解读”的忧惧心理，故选［B］。\n［错项排除］［A］unnecessary（不必要的）通常评价措施或物品，不用于形容担忧关系出了负向裂痕；［C］strange（奇怪的）语义模糊且缺乏自卑者害怕关系恶化的痛感；［D］impractical（不切实际的）不修饰人际关系状态。' WHERE id = '66974787-a9b7-53fe-8d9e-faa48a2dc91c'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [13] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "explain", "content": "explain"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "identify", "content": "identify"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "predict", "content": "predict"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "overcome", "content": "overcome"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］段际脉络转折与动词搭配。\n［解题思路］第三段正式从前两段的“求助为何难”过渡至“如何破局打消顾虑”。首句以目的状语开篇：“为了[13]（克服、战胜）这些困难（To [13] these difficulties），请试着提醒自己每个人都需要帮助。”overcome difficulties 为高频搭配，且顺理成章引出破解方法，故选［D］。\n［错项排除］［A］explain（解释）属于前两段已完成的内容而非本段启下的破局策略；［B］identify（识别）同样已在上文列举完毕；［C］predict（预测）偏离解决当下阻碍的祈使句方向。' WHERE id = '65bcc494-59f7-554d-842b-bd3a60ee9c20'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [14] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "deny", "content": "deny"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "forget", "content": "forget"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "miss", "content": "miss"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "fear", "content": "fear"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内让步逻辑与动词辨析。\n［解题思路］句内由 while 引导让步状语从句，呈现“主观担忧”与“客观研究结论”的鲜明反转：“尽管你也许[14]（害怕、担心）给别人留下无能的印象（while you might [14] coming across as incompetent），但研究表明求助者其实会被看作更有能力而非相反。”fear 呼应全文“求助顾虑”基调，故选［D］。\n［错项排除］［A］deny（否认）暗示求助者并不觉得自己无能，抹平了句内转折反差；［B］forget（忘记）与［C］miss（错过）均无法衔接“害怕显得无能”与后文打消顾虑的反转逻辑。' WHERE id = 'a94b3bb7-c1aa-5bf2-a404-641569224536'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [15] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "disguised", "content": "disguised"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "perceived", "content": "perceived"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "followed", "content": "followed"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "introduced", "content": "introduced"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内对比逻辑与动词被动搭配。\n［解题思路］接续前句“你担心在他人眼里显得（coming across as）无能”，研究反驳指出：事实上求助者会被他人“[15]（看待、视为）更有能力（are [15] as more competent, not less）”。perceive... as... 意为“把……视作/看作……”，精准回击主观臆测，故选［B］perceived。\n［错项排除］［A］disguised（伪装成）反指求助者其实无能、只是被包装成有能；［C］followed（跟随）与［D］introduced（介绍）皆不能构成 be ~ed as 表达主观认知评价之义。' WHERE id = '55983fc0-1d1f-5b03-9a87-808e09eba341'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [16] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "recall", "content": "recall"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "classify", "content": "classify"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "analyse", "content": "analyse"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "compare", "content": "compare"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］学术研究设计与动词语义辨析。\n［解题思路］斯坦福大学 2022 年发表的论文采用了双轨研究方式：既包含实验设计的求助互动（manufactured help-seeking interactions），也包括让受试者“[16]（回忆、回溯）”自己过往真实的求助经历（[16] past experiences）。recall（回忆）与前项“人工模拟实验”形成“回忆真实过往 vs 现场模拟交互”的经典研究对照，故选［A］。\n［错项排除］［B］classify（分类）、［C］analyse（分析）及［D］compare（比较）多为研究人员自身处理数据的方法，而非要求普通受试者报告个人经历的常见诱导步骤。' WHERE id = '6bf6a90c-875b-5773-b6e3-a164f85694cc'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [17] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "brave", "content": "brave"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "disapproving", "content": "disapproving"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "willing", "content": "willing"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "hesitant", "content": "hesitant"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内并列阳性情感与形容词辨析。\n［解题思路］研究结果显示：求助者通常会双双低估两件事——既低估别人有多么“[17]（乐意、愿意）提供帮助（how [17] other people will be to help）”，又低估助人能让对方有多开心（how good it makes the helper feel）。be willing to do sth 与助人收获愉悦构成强烈因果呼应，故选［C］。\n［错项排除］［A］brave（勇敢的）主体错置，文段说缺乏勇气的是求助者而非施助者；［B］disapproving（不赞成的）与［D］hesitant（犹豫迟疑的）均与下文“对方乐在其中”的乐观研究结论彻底相反。' WHERE id = '4e6b144e-3f2e-5d5f-8f53-35f88adc76aa'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [18] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "relaxing", "content": "relaxing"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "surprising", "content": "surprising"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "rewarding", "content": "rewarding"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "demanding", "content": "demanding"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句内解释呼应与形容词词义辨析。\n［解题思路］括弧内句子解释前文“让助人者感觉良好（how good it makes the helper feel）”，指出对大多数人而言，有机会帮别人本身是一件“极有成就感、极为有益令人满足的（highly [18]）”事情。rewarding（令人收获满满的、有成就感的）完美解释为何助人令人心情愉悦，故选［C］。\n［错项排除］［A］relaxing（轻松惬意的）指不费力的休闲放松，而助人往往需主动付出时间心力；［B］surprising（令人惊讶的）重点在出乎意料，并非正效价收益感；［D］demanding（费力苛求的）强调负担繁重，与“feel good”正相反。' WHERE id = 'b02d96ef-e8db-5982-9cc8-92f2e44cb666'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [19] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Thus", "content": "Thus"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Also", "content": "Also"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Finally", "content": "Finally"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Instead", "content": "Instead"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］句际并行建议与逻辑副词。\n［解题思路］末段连续以祈使句给出行动锦囊：首句呼吁下次求助时记住上述鼓舞人心的结论，次句则补充另一条实用提醒：“[19]（此外、同时），要慎选向谁求助以及何时开口。”两句同属收尾实操建议，呈并列补充关系，Also 顺接自然，故选［B］。\n［错项排除］［A］Thus（因此）强加因果（记结论并不推导出必须慎选对象时机）；［C］Finally（最后）虽可列举但下文尚有第三条别往心里去；［D］Instead（反而、取而代之）无中生有地否定前句建议。' WHERE id = '6c664a7f-dede-50e4-8b7c-513028e114df'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the best option for blank [20] in the passage:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "polite", "content": "polite"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "proud", "content": "proud"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "busy", "content": "busy"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "lazy", "content": "lazy"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］上下文合理解释与形容词辨析。\n［解题思路］末两句安慰遭拒的求助者：若有人无法立刻搭手，切莫觉得是针对你个人；因为他们也许只是太过“[20]（忙碌、脱不开身）”，又或者对自身能否帮上忙信心不足。too busy 与后分句并列提供善意客观的解释，故选［C］。\n［错项排除］［A］polite（礼貌的）、［B］proud（骄傲自大的）及［D］lazy（懒惰的）要么反而显得是人品问题引发误会（如傲慢或懒惰，恰好会让人觉得被轻慢），要么与“没能立刻帮忙”逻辑矛盾（礼貌更可能尽量搭把手）。' WHERE id = '75d934cb-4276-55a0-a094-9a5f2dc70de3'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to Paragraph 1, the practice of tipping in the U.S. ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "was regarded as a sign of generosity", "content": "was regarded as a sign of generosity"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "was considered essential for waiters", "content": "was considered essential for waiters"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "was a way of rewarding diligence", "content": "was a way of rewarding diligence"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "was optional in most businesses", "content": "was optional in most businesses"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］细节事实题（首段历史渊源定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 Paragraph 1 与 tipping in the U.S. 定位至第一段首句。该句指出，从历史上看，美国顾客习惯向那些“人们假定主要靠小费维生”的从业者支付小费，典型例子便是“基本时薪低于法定最低工资标准的餐馆服务员（such as restaurant servers earning less than the minimum wage）”。由于基本底薪不足，小费对餐厅服务员而言自然是至关重要的基本生计支撑，故［B］was considered essential for waiters 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］被视为慷慨的象征、［C］作为奖励勤奋的方式及［D］在大多数行业属自愿之举虽在全文其余语境偶有似是而非表述，但首段第一句对传统美国小费合法性与普遍前提的界定明确落在“弥补低底薪员工主要收入”。' WHERE id = 'e8e6dad8-863b-5a89-af0a-22ab6a329d21'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Compared with tips in the past, today\'s tips ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "are paid much less frequently", "content": "are paid much less frequently"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "are less often requested in advance", "content": "are less often requested in advance"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "have less to do with service quality", "content": "have less to do with service quality"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "contribute less to workers\' income", "content": "contribute less to workers\' income"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］对比推断题（今昔小费属性对比）。\n［精准定位］根据题干比较对象 tips in the past 与 today\'s tips 定位至第二段及文章末尾总结句。第二段指出过去小费几乎总是在体验完毕后才付，以此“奖赏优质服务（in recognition of a good job）”；而末段末句直接点出当今现状的蜕变——小费如今“显得更具强迫性、缺少慷慨感，且常常与服务质量完全脱钩（often completely disassociated from service quality）”。由此可见如今小费与服务优劣的关系大为削弱，故［C］have less to do with service quality 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］支付频率大幅降低与第三、四段“小费索要渗透至各行各业”事实相反；［B］更少预先索要与末句前文“预先要求小费（asked for... before receiving service）”相反；［D］占工人收入比例更低缺乏正文对应。' WHERE id = 'f2dd9d61-9069-522a-baf5-9033e0b98e2f'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Tip requests are creeping into new kinds of services as a result of ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "the advancement of technology", "content": "the advancement of technology"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "the desire for income increase", "content": "the desire for income increase"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "the diversification of business", "content": "the diversification of business"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "the emergence of tipflation", "content": "the emergence of tipflation"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］因果细节题（新行业索要小费诱因）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 creeping into new kinds of services 定位至第四段。该段开篇明晰因果：“数字支付设备的普及让商家向顾客索要小费变得更轻而易举（The prevalence of digital payment devices has made it easier to ask customers for a tip）；这也解释了为什么如今连以往从未收过小费的新型服务也纷纷出现小费请求。”由此可知正是收银支付科技进步催生了这一蔓延现象，故［A］the advancement of technology 正确。\n［错项排除］［B］增加收入的愿望只是商家/雇员潜在动因，原文归因句 That helps explain 明确指向前句的数字设备硬件普及；［C］业务多元化及［D］小费膨胀现象出现系本末倒置（tipflation 本身正是第四段描述的现象统称而非深层原因）。' WHERE id = 'aa0bef16-5605-565f-a744-465b27b0e200'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The movement toward no-tipping services was intended to ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "promote consumption", "content": "promote consumption"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "enrich income sources", "content": "enrich income sources"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "maintain reasonable prices", "content": "maintain reasonable prices"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "guarantee income fairness", "content": "guarantee income fairness"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］目的意图题（取消小费改革初衷定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 movement toward no-tipping services 定位至第六段。文章在此揭示餐饮业内部矛盾：高额小费大多落入前台服务员口袋，而后厨厨师和洗碗工却常被排除在外；“为了确保全体员工都能获得公平报酬（To ensure that all employees were paid fair wages），一些餐馆全面禁止小费并相应提高菜品定价”。可见取消小费运动旨在保障员工收入公平，故［D］guarantee income fairness 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］刺激消费、［B］丰富收入来源及［C］维持合理价格均偏离第六段核心——实际上该举措甚至需要“提高菜单价格（increased prices）”而非降价保价。' WHERE id = '3c5d01d8-179c-5417-95a3-2baa9f6c2998'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'It can be learned from the last paragraph that tipping ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "is becoming a burden for customers", "content": "is becoming a burden for customers"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "helps encourage quality service", "content": "helps encourage quality service"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "is vital to business development", "content": "is vital to business development"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "reflects the need to reduce prices", "content": "reflects the need to reduce prices"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］段落主旨推断题（末段消费者体验定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 last paragraph 与 tipping 定位至文章最后一段。末段指出，民众并不拒绝给努力服务的侍者合适小费，问题在于当今普遍让人窝火的“小费膨胀（tipflation）”——“许多顾客倍感沮丧，因为他们觉得索要的小费比例过高、频率太勤，甚至在尚未享受任何服务前便遭伸手讨要”，导致给小费显得愈发具有强制压迫感（more coercive）。这清晰反映出小费正日益沦为消费者的心理及财务负担，故［A］is becoming a burden for customers 正确。\n［错项排除］［B］有助于激励优质服务恰被末句“与服务质量完全脱钩”反驳；［C］对商业发展至关重要与前段不少餐馆试水去小费引发争议及流失不符；［D］反映降价需要毫无依据。' WHERE id = 'fd278c89-208f-5748-9272-45359bc0fb92'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to the first two paragraphs, the NHS ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "is troubled by funding deficiencies", "content": "is troubled by funding deficiencies"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "can hardly satisfy people\'s needs", "content": "can hardly satisfy people\'s needs"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "can barely retain its current employees", "content": "can barely retain its current employees"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "is rivalled by private medical services", "content": "is rivalled by private medical services"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］细节理解题（前两段机构困境概括）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 first two paragraphs 与 the NHS 定位至第一、二段。第一段指出 NHS 正面临空前严重的困境，第二段以具体数据展开论证：“超过 680 万人仍在排队候诊名单上，医疗服务变得愈发可望而不可及（healthcare is becoming increasingly inaccessible）；无论患者还是员工均苦不堪言”，而且整体健康指标也落后于同等国家。可见 NHS 当下已难以满足民众的正常医疗需求，故［B］can hardly satisfy people\'s needs 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］资金短缺困扰偏颇，首段强调投入经费早已大增（Even with... the budget growing significantly）但表现依旧乏力，即并非单纯差钱；［C］难以留住现有员工在原文两段未曾重点提及（只言 staff suffering 压力大）；［D］受到私营医疗冲击在前两段全无影子。' WHERE id = '04e960f5-948f-5c25-ba7d-2f80fb6af646'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'One answer to the crisis in health and care is to ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "boost the efficiency of hospitals", "content": "boost the efficiency of hospitals"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "lighten the burden on social care", "content": "lighten the burden on social care"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "increase resources for primary care", "content": "increase resources for primary care"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "reduce the pressure on communities", "content": "reduce the pressure on communities"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］细节事实题（医疗危机解决对策定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 answer to the crisis in health and care 定位至第三段。针对医院人满为患的危机，作者提出切实方向：“要在医院与社区之间重新平衡投入，必须在基层社区和初级保健上投入更多（Much more needs to be invested in communities and primary care），以降低我们对大型医院体系的过度依赖。”选项［C］increase resources for primary care（增加初级医疗保健资源）准确复现核心对策，故正确。\n［错项排除］［A］提升大医院内部效率及［B］减轻社会护理负担偏离作者核心提议“分流至初级社区医疗而非继续独木难支堆高大医院投入”；［D］减轻社区压力正好反向——原文主张向社区倾注资源强化社区分担能力。' WHERE id = '05a5a235-32a5-57e1-9a52-dda6b8175db4'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'"Reimagining health" is aimed to ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "reinforce hospital management", "content": "reinforce hospital management"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "readjust healthcare regulations", "content": "readjust healthcare regulations"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "restructure the health system", "content": "restructure the health system"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "resume suspended health reforms", "content": "resume suspended health reforms"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］主旨目标题（专栏项目意图定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 Reimagining health 定位至第四段。文中提到智库 Reform 发起该项目，旨在呼吁“对我们延续至今的以医院为核心的模式进行紧迫反思（urgent rethink of the hospital-centric model）”；并围绕一个关键问题展开探索：在医疗卫生体制内部应当如何重新分配权力与资源（how power and resources should be distributed in our health system）。由此可见该项目志在重塑与重构整个医疗体系，故［C］restructure the health system 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］强化医院管理仍停留在被批评的“以医院为中心”旧框架内；［B］调整医疗行业法规及［D］重启搁置的医疗改革在第四段均未作为该项目的根本目标出现。' WHERE id = '2e9e89df-6d1d-5a7c-b345-992644fc1251'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'To maximise the nation\'s health, the author suggests ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "introducing relevant taxation policies", "content": "introducing relevant taxation policies"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "paying due attention to social factors", "content": "paying due attention to social factors"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "reevaluating major health outcomes", "content": "reevaluating major health outcomes"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "enhancing the quality of health care", "content": "enhancing the quality of health care"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］细节建议题（国民健康决定因素定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 maximise the nation\'s health 与 author suggests 定位至第五段。作者明确指出医疗救治其实只决定了约 20% 的健康结果（only accounts for around 20 per cent of health outcomes）；“远比医疗本身更为重要的是我们生活、工作、社交的地点以及饮食质量——然而公共政策几乎没有关注改善这些健康的社会决定因素（improving these social determinants of health）”。作者意在呼吁正视并着力改善这些社会影响因子，故［B］paying due attention to social factors 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］出台相关税收政策（原文仅批评预算和政策忽视了社会因素）；［C］重新评估主要健康指标与［D］提升医疗服务质量均错把占比仅 20% 的传统医疗环节当作最大抓手。' WHERE id = 'c058ac06-d0f9-579f-8b49-2ef0b2da11d0'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'It can be inferred that local leaders should ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "exercise their power more reasonably", "content": "exercise their power more reasonably"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "develop a stronger sense of responsibility", "content": "develop a stronger sense of responsibility"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "play a bigger role in the health system", "content": "play a bigger role in the health system"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "understand people\'s health needs better", "content": "understand people\'s health needs better"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］推理判断题（末段权力下放诉求定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 local leaders should 定位至最后一段。末段末尾以设问作结，直言重构系统时必须直面“哪些卫生职能应留在中央，而哪些应该下放给最了解当地民众真实需求的市级、地区及社区领导人（what should be given to local leaders... with a much better understanding of the needs of their populations）”。言下之意正是倡导赋权地方、让地方领导在医疗卫生体系中扮演更重要的角色，故［C］play a bigger role in the health system 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］更合理地行使手中现有权力回避了“中央向地方放权”的核心；［B］培养更高责任感偏离体制权责分配；［D］更好了解民众需求其实原文已肯定地方原本就“much better understanding”，关键在于能否获权落实。' WHERE id = 'e454c0d2-c406-53c4-bf61-847680304d36'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to Paragraph 1, Nagpur\'s plan proposes measures to ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "tackle extreme weather", "content": "tackle extreme weather"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "ensure construction quality", "content": "ensure construction quality"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "monitor emergency warnings", "content": "monitor emergency warnings"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "address excessive workloads", "content": "address excessive workloads"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］细节事实题（首段地方应对措施定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 Paragraph 1 与 Nagpur\'s plan 定位至第一段。作为印度高温重镇，那格浦尔市早在 2016 年便出台行动计划：例如要求医院在夏季专为救治中暑病例预留“降温病房（cold wards）”，并建议建筑工地在酷暑日停工休整。不难看出这一系列举措都是为了积极应对高温等极端天气事件，故［A］tackle extreme weather 正确。\n［错项排除］［B］保证建筑质量篡改了“工地在酷暑日停工防暑”的主旨；［C］监测紧急警报在第一段尚未触及（属于第二段全印计划争议）；［D］解决超负荷工作量把极端热天临时停工曲解为日常劳工工时改革。' WHERE id = 'db7465ad-7eba-5c00-a08d-75554b76a20f'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'One problem with existing HAPs is that they ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "prove too costly to be implemented", "content": "prove too costly to be implemented"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "lack localized alert-issuing criteria", "content": "lack localized alert-issuing criteria"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "give delayed responses to heat waves", "content": "give delayed responses to heat waves"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "keep hospitals under great pressure", "content": "keep hospitals under great pressure"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］事实细节题（既有计划短板定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 problem with existing HAPs 定位至第二段。2023 年一项针对全印 37 份现存高温行动计划的评估报告发现其落实情况参差不齐，直指两大症结之一在于“其触发预警的门槛阈值往往未能结合当地具体气候特征加以量身定制（triggering thresholds often are not customized to the local climate）”，例如沿海高湿地区照搬了干燥内陆的标准。这正说明现行 HAPs 缺乏因地制宜的本地化预警标准，故［B］lack localized alert-issuing criteria 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］实施成本过于高昂与原文提及“缺乏足够资金（underfunded）”不是一回事；［C］对热浪响应滞后与［D］令医院承压过重均不是第二段报告指出的触发机制标准漏洞。' WHERE id = '876d1d26-7368-5134-8c99-752e604fbb30'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Mumbai\'s case shows that India\'s heat alert systems need to ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "include other factors besides temperature", "content": "include other factors besides temperature"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "take subtle weather changes into account", "content": "take subtle weather changes into account"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "prioritize potentially disastrous heat waves", "content": "prioritize potentially disastrous heat waves"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "draw further support from local authorities", "content": "draw further support from local authorities"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］例证目的题（个案折射制度缺陷定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 Mumbai\'s case 与 heat alert systems 定位至第三段。2023 年 4 月孟买发生中暑死亡悲剧当天，当地气温约 36℃，甚至还比国家气象局划定的热浪预警线低了 1℃；研究人员复盘指明致命真凶：“高温的危害被高湿度（humidity）——预警系统中常被忽视的一个因子——以及缺乏遮荫处急剧放大”。由此可知高温预警体系不能唯温度论，急需纳入温度以外的其他环境风险要素，故［A］include other factors besides temperature 正确。\n［错项排除］［B］把微妙天气变化算入偏离“湿度/遮阳等跨维度指标”；［C］优先关注潜在灾难级热浪忽视了“未达传统温度门槛却因高湿照样夺命”；［D］争取地方政府进一步支持偏离个案揭示的气象技术标准缺失。' WHERE id = '464bf9b3-9bd6-5eda-b781-de5601264385'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Kotharkar holds that a vulnerability map can help ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "prevent the harm of high humidity", "content": "prevent the harm of high humidity"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "target areas needing special attention", "content": "target areas needing special attention"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "expand the Nagpur project\'s coverage", "content": "expand the Nagpur project\'s coverage"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "make relief plans for heat-stricken people", "content": "make relief plans for heat-stricken people"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［考点提炼］人物观点题（科研学者建议工具作用定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干人名 Kotharkar 与关键词 vulnerability map 定位至第四、五段。学者 Kotharkar 在第四段末尾建议绘制脆弱性分布图，以便“帮助将应急响应资源精准集中到风险最高的人群（focus responses on the populations most at risk）”；紧接第五段展开他在那格浦尔的实践成效：那份结合了收入水平、供水管道与遮荫状况的多指标地图“能清晰告知官员究竟应当重点关照哪些街区（tell officials which neighborhoods to focus on）”。选项［B］target areas needing special attention（锁定并瞄准最需要特别关注的区域）贴切概括，故正确。\n［错项排除］［A］杜绝高湿伤害（地图主要用于精准筛选高危区域配置资源而非直接改变大气湿度）；［C］扩大那格浦尔项目覆盖面及［D］为中暑者制定具体医疗救治方案皆非脆弱性地图的直接定位功能。' WHERE id = '4786a54f-027b-5f2d-be5d-b1f59145e6f5'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to the last paragraph, researchers suggest that HAPs should ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "focus more on the heatstroke treatment", "content": "focus more on the heatstroke treatment"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "invite wider public participation", "content": "invite wider public participation"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "apply for more government grants", "content": "apply for more government grants"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "serve a broader range of purposes", "content": "serve a broader range of purposes"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］段落推断题（末段未来改进愿景定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 last paragraph 与 researchers suggest that HAPs should 定位至最后一段。研究人员主张高温行动计划不能仅仅停留在“短期应急抢救（short-term emergency responses）”（如发预警避暑减死），更应纳入“让社区长久凉爽下来的中长期举措（medium-to-long-term measures）”，并且应当“指导房屋节能翻新或修订建筑规范（guide efforts to retrofit homes or modify building regulations）”，涵盖种植城市行道树与防热屋顶绿化等。可见学界呼吁 HAPs 服务于更广泛深远的目标，故［D］serve a broader range of purposes 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］把更多精力集中在现症中暑救治恰与呼吁突破短期医疗救急相反；［B］吸引更广泛公众参与及［C］申请更多政府经费虽可能重要，但偏离末段强调功能从短期避险延伸至建筑、城市规划等长远用途。' WHERE id = '0b6fa875-e999-5c45-9255-87c13e76bd6e'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'According to Paragraph 1, desire paths are a result of ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "the curiosity to explore surrounding hills", "content": "the curiosity to explore surrounding hills"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "the necessity to preserve green spaces", "content": "the necessity to preserve green spaces"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "the tendency to pursue convenience", "content": "the tendency to pursue convenience"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "the wish to find comfort in solitude", "content": "the wish to find comfort in solitude"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［考点提炼］细节理解题（首段现象定义定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 Paragraph 1 与 desire paths 定位至第一段。文章定义“欲望路径（desire paths）”为社区留下的非官方足迹、公开秘而不宣的共同偏好与大家踩出来的捷径（shared shortcuts），并进一步解释它们“代表了人类（以及部分动物）沿着阻力最小路径从 A 点最高效抵达 B 点的自然天性（most effectively, following the path of least resistance）”。追求高效直达少走弯路正反映了人们图方便的天性倾向，故［C］the tendency to pursue convenience 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］探索周围山丘的好奇心、［B］保护绿地的必要性（恰恰相反，踩踏草地往往被认为破坏绿地）以及［D］在独处中寻找慰藉均非首段揭示的捷径动因。' WHERE id = '460727d4-5002-5ad2-bfe3-0aa3c012edd5'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'It can be inferred that Ohio State University ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "intends to improve its desire paths", "content": "intends to improve its desire paths"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "leads in the research on desire paths", "content": "leads in the research on desire paths"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "guides the creation of its desire paths", "content": "guides the creation of its desire paths"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "takes a positive view of desire paths", "content": "takes a positive view of desire paths"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］推理判断题（高校案例体现校方态度）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 Ohio State University 定位至第二段中间。文章描述俄亥俄州立大学面对学生踩踏椭圆大草坪的行为并未一味设障惩罚，而是“先允许学生自由穿行校园草地，随后顺势将他们踏出的小路直接铺设成正规硬化路面（proceeded to pave the desire paths），从而打造出一张高效实用的通路网”。校方这种顺应尊重学生自然行进需求并予以硬化转正的做法，彰显了校方对欲望路径持肯定积极态度，故［D］takes a positive view of desire paths 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］打算改良自身现有欲望路径曲解时态与语义（学校当年并非觉得欲望路径不好要改造它，而是认可并铺平固化学生走出的路线）；［B］引领欲望路径学术研究属无中生有；［C］主动引导规定欲望路径的形成正好与“允许自由走踏（navigate... freely）”之后再顺应铺路相反。' WHERE id = '42bbfdb8-497a-578b-997b-a442893f2883'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The images on the Reddit webpage reflect ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "conflicting opinions on the use of desire paths", "content": "conflicting opinions on the use of desire paths"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "the call to upgrade the designing of public spaces", "content": "the call to upgrade the designing of public spaces"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "the demand for proper planning of desire paths", "content": "the demand for proper planning of desire paths"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "growing concerns over the loss of public spaces", "content": "growing concerns over the loss of public spaces"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［考点提炼］细节理解题（网络图集所折射的社会冲突）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 images on the Reddit webpage 定位至第三段。文中提到 Reddit 论坛专题页面收集了无数对比鲜明的照片：人们踏出的斜向泥土捷径旁边，偏偏竖着冷冰冰要求绕行官方铺砖步道的警示牌。作者随后直接点破其深意：“这种冲突凸显了使用者自发需求与追求整齐规划的城市审美愿景之间持续不断的博弈（This clash highlights an ongoing struggle...）”。可见照片反映出关于如何使用与看待欲望路径的分歧对立观点，故［A］conflicting opinions on the use of desire paths 正确。\n［错项排除］［B］呼吁全面升级公共空间设计及［C］要求妥善规划欲望路径皆把作者后续反思拔高为图片自带的单一呼吁；［D］对绿地/公共空间丧失的担忧片面夸大了规范派的单方立场，未能反映照片展示的“双方冲突（clash/struggle）”。' WHERE id = 'fe281eea-4982-5682-9756-aac43a75b294'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'The example of the Wickquasgeck Trail illustrates ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "the growth of New York City", "content": "the growth of New York City"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "the Dutch origin of desire paths", "content": "the Dutch origin of desire paths"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "the importance of urban planning", "content": "the importance of urban planning"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "the recognition of desire paths", "content": "the recognition of desire paths"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］例证目的题（历史著名案例作用定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 Wickquasgeck Trail 定位至第四段。前句指出有些看似草率的捷径最终会突破城市严整的网格规划获得官方的正式认可与永久接纳（permanently recognized）；紧接作者就以美洲原住民在曼哈顿森林穿行踏出的 Wickquasgeck Trail 为例，说明这条泥土小径后来直接演变成为了世界闻名的纽约百老汇大道（Broadway），至今仍斜穿曼哈顿棋盘网格。该知名实例有力论证了民间欲望路径被正式接纳承认的真实历程，故［D］the recognition of desire paths 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］说明纽约城市发展扩张与［B］说明欲望路径源自荷兰（原文称荷兰殖民者当年也借用了原住民早就踩出的通道）均系次要背景信息；［C］说明正规城市规划的重要性恰与百老汇打破正交网格格局相悖。' WHERE id = 'c4065de4-7282-5b92-8e3c-b7ad64d4b981'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'It can be learned from the last paragraph that desire paths ______.', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "reveal humans\' deep respect for nature", "content": "reveal humans\' deep respect for nature"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "are crucial to humans\' mental well-being", "content": "are crucial to humans\' mental well-being"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "are a human imitation of animal behaviour", "content": "are a human imitation of animal behaviour"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "show a shared trait in humans and animals", "content": "show a shared trait in humans and animals"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'D', explanation = E'［考点提炼］段落推断题（末段人类与动物共性定位）。\n［精准定位］根据题干关键词 last paragraph 与 desire paths 定位至最后一段。作者首先拓展视角指出欲望路径并非人类专属（not exclusively human），继而举出鸭子踏穿结冰池塘、家犬在花园抄近道的生动实例（Animal desire paths...），并在首尾呼应指出：这些现象凸显了无论是人类还是动物体验中共通的适应能力与直觉捷径天性（highlight the adaptability of these trails in both human and animal experiences）。这揭示了人与动物在趋利避害、追求阻力最小路径上的共有特征，故［D］show a shared trait in humans and animals 正确。\n［错项排除］［A］揭示人类对自然的深切敬畏及［B］对人类心理健康至关重要在末段全无依据；［C］称欲望路径是人类刻意模仿动物行为将并列“共同本能”歪曲成了“模仿借鉴”。' WHERE id = 'dff32c1d-b50d-5722-bc56-455157190a1b'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the most suitable subheading from A-G for paragraph [41]:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Stay positive", "content": "Stay positive"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Respect the past", "content": "Respect the past"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Use channels", "content": "Use channels"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Give it time", "content": "Give it time"}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "Invite resistance", "content": "Invite resistance"}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "Be a salesman", "content": "Be a salesman"}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "Be humble", "content": "Be humble"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'F', explanation = E'［定位/考点］段落小标题匹配（第[41]段）。\n［解题思路］本段开篇点破痛点：“绝妙的点子绝不会孤立自明（Great ideas don\'t stand alone）”——仅仅提一次建议绝不足以让别人拍板采纳。为此作者要求提案者“积极维护推广自己的方案并大力兜售其优势价值（champion your plan and sell its merits）”，同时做好准备面对挑剔审视，针对不同听众群体的关切以多样化方式反复阐释新想法。像推销员一样主动推广创意、打消受众疑虑正是本段核心，故［F］Be a salesman（做一名推销员）完全契合。\n［错项排除］干扰项如［E］Invite resistance 看似与 scrutiny and criticism 沾边，但本段重点在于用多元宣讲主动推销长处并扛住质疑，而非主动邀请反对派提意见（后文第 43 段讲到倾听异议，且那也是保持谦逊）。' WHERE id = '01cd911d-bcae-51e0-b129-41885658c725'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the most suitable subheading from A-G for paragraph [42]:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Stay positive", "content": "Stay positive"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Respect the past", "content": "Respect the past"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Use channels", "content": "Use channels"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Give it time", "content": "Give it time"}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "Invite resistance", "content": "Invite resistance"}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "Be a salesman", "content": "Be a salesman"}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "Be humble", "content": "Be humble"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'C', explanation = E'［定位/考点］段落小标题匹配（第[42]段）。\n［解题思路］本段着重探讨推动变革落地的具体社交与组织路径选择：有时先找直属上司单线沟通顺理成章，而另一些时候则适合先联合平级同事及其他利益相关方结成同盟（build a coalition among your co-workers or other stakeholders）；比如预先私下对接技术部沟通工作量与可行性，再有备无患地应对 stubborn supervisor 的反对。这正是在阐述善于打通上下级及跨部门多方人脉路径来助力提案，故［C］Use channels（善用各方渠道）精准对应。\n［错项排除］切勿将［F］的推销优势与本段专门讲求“找准先去找老板还是先找部门同事串联借力”的沟通渠道艺术相混淆。' WHERE id = 'f8994764-ed67-5c19-82e0-201db7b83926'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the most suitable subheading from A-G for paragraph [43]:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Stay positive", "content": "Stay positive"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Respect the past", "content": "Respect the past"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Use channels", "content": "Use channels"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Give it time", "content": "Give it time"}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "Invite resistance", "content": "Invite resistance"}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "Be a salesman", "content": "Be a salesman"}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "Be humble", "content": "Be humble"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'G', explanation = E'［定位/考点］段落小标题匹配（第[43]段）。\n［解题思路］本段深刻揭示提案推进中最致命的障碍之一：提案人给众人留下“好斗、死不认错、听不进建议、自以为无所不知（argumentative, defensive, or close-minded / No one likes a know-it-all）”的傲慢观感。因此作者告诫千万不要被反对就恼羞成怒（don\'t be indignant），而是应当充分倾听顾虑、设身处地理解他人的立足点并将各方建议及补救措施纳入后续探讨。与自满傲慢相对的“虚心接纳、收敛锋芒”，正是［G］Be humble（保持谦逊），故正确。\n［错项排除］注意区分［G］的“放下‘万事通’身段虚心倾听改进”与下段［B］的“向老一辈历史方案致意”之间的界限；虽同有尊重意味，但本段反讽“know-it-all”直指个人处事须谦卑（humble）。' WHERE id = 'efdf2f1c-ee7a-5c3f-9428-44dd85889847'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the most suitable subheading from A-G for paragraph [44]:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Stay positive", "content": "Stay positive"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Respect the past", "content": "Respect the past"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Use channels", "content": "Use channels"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Give it time", "content": "Give it time"}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "Invite resistance", "content": "Invite resistance"}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "Be a salesman", "content": "Be a salesman"}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "Be humble", "content": "Be humble"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'B', explanation = E'［定位/考点］段落小标题匹配（第[44]段）。\n［解题思路］本段借比喻指出：“新点子都是旧点子的隔代子孙（New ideas are the grandchildren of old ones）”，警示推行创新万不可为了凸显自己方案高明而将过去的旧做法贬得一文不值（don\'t throw old solutions under the bus）。作者提醒我们：当年旧系统能解决（哪怕近期失效的）特定问题，在彼时也曾是一桩了不起的良策；在提出未来革新的同时珍视前人的既往贡献，不仅有助赢得体谅，还能增强新方案本身的可信度（Appreciating the older contributions as you suggest future innovations helps bolster the credibility of your idea）。由此明显对应［B］Respect the past（尊重过去），故正确。\n［错项排除］［D］Give it time 虽偶涉旧制度曾经存续的时间感，但全段旨在表达“对前人成果保持敬意以免树敌”，绝非等待时机。' WHERE id = 'a14f6641-6815-58ab-b258-17f17771fab7'::uuid;
UPDATE public.questions SET stem = E'Choose the most suitable subheading from A-G for paragraph [45]:', options = E'[{"key": "A", "value": "A", "text": "Stay positive", "content": "Stay positive"}, {"key": "B", "value": "B", "text": "Respect the past", "content": "Respect the past"}, {"key": "C", "value": "C", "text": "Use channels", "content": "Use channels"}, {"key": "D", "value": "D", "text": "Give it time", "content": "Give it time"}, {"key": "E", "value": "E", "text": "Invite resistance", "content": "Invite resistance"}, {"key": "F", "value": "F", "text": "Be a salesman", "content": "Be a salesman"}, {"key": "G", "value": "G", "text": "Be humble", "content": "Be humble"}]'::jsonb, correct_answer = E'A', explanation = E'［定位/考点］段落小标题匹配（第[45]段）。\n［解题思路］本段最后谈论游说变革时的语言表达基调：推销新构想时应当多用“充盈积极的词汇（the language of abundance）”，取代挑刺指责的“匮乏负向词句（language of deficit）”；少盯着“哪里出错、破败、次优（wrong, broken, or suboptimal）”做文章，多谈论“什么是可行、可修补或理想状态（right, fixable, or ideal）”，做到乐观而务实（Be optimistic but realistic）。全文紧扣正面积极的心态与措辞，故［A］Stay positive（保持积极乐观）完美收尾，故选 A。\n［错项排除］［F］Be a salesman 已分配给专门强调阐释产品优点的第 41 段；本段虽也用 pitching 一词，但其独一无二的重心完全集中在正负用语对比与“optimistic（乐观）”态度上。' WHERE id = 'af83eca4-d09c-5a35-acef-7f54dff2d6dc'::uuid;
COMMIT;
